window.QI18N={"Arabiyyah": "Arabiyyah", "Beginner {0}": "Mafari {0}", "Lesson {0}": "Darasi na {0}", "Sound": "Sauti", "Close": "Rufe", "Welcome to the Arabic class. In this course you will learn to understand, read and speak Arabic, the language of the Qur'an, step by step.": "Barka da zuwa ajin Larabci. A wannan kwas za ka koyi fahimta, karatu da magana da Larabci, harshen Alƙur'ani, mataki-mataki.", "We follow the famous book, Lessons in Arabic Language, by Dr. V.": "Muna bin shahararren littafin nan, Darussan Harshen Larabci, na Dr. V.", "taught at the Islamic University of Madinah.": "wanda aka koyar a Jami'ar Musulunci ta Madina.", "The course has four levels. Beginner 1 is Book 1. Beginner 2 is the first half of Book 2. Beginner 3 is the second half of Book 2. Beginner 4 is Book 3. Each level ends with a final exam and a certificate.": "Kwas ɗin yana da matakai huɗu. Mafari 1 shi ne Littafi na 1. Mafari 2 shi ne rabin farko na Littafi na 2. Mafari 3 shi ne rabi na biyu na Littafi na 2. Mafari 4 shi ne Littafi na 3. Kowane mataki yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida.", "In this lesson you will learn": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi", "which means this. You will ask": "wanda ma'anarsa wannan. Za ka tambaya", "what is this, and": "mene ne wannan, da", "who is this. You will ask yes or no questions, and answer with": "wane ne wannan. Za ka yi tambayoyin i ko a'a, ka amsa da", "yes, and": "i, da", "no. You will also learn twenty four new words.": "a'a. Za ka kuma koyi sababbin kalmomi ashirin da huɗu.", "In each lesson you learn the new rule and the new words, you read sentences aloud and the app checks you, you practise with short exercises, and you finish with an exam. You need 90 percent to pass, and you can retake it as many times as you like.": "A kowane darasi za ka koyi sabuwar ƙa'ida da sababbin kalmomi, za ka karanta jumloli da ƙarfi kuma manhajar za ta duba ka, za ka yi atisaye da gajerun ayyuka, sannan ka gama da jarrabawa. Kana buƙatar kashi casa'in cikin ɗari don ka ci, kuma za ka iya sake yin ta sau duk yadda kake so.", "Listen carefully and repeat everything aloud.": "Saurara da kyau ka maimaita komai da ƙarfi.", "Let's begin.": "Mu fara.", "means this. We use it to point at something or someone near us.": "ma'anarsa wannan. Muna amfani da shi don nuna wani abu ko wani mutum da ke kusa da mu.", "The ending": "Ƙarshen", "written with two": "wanda ake rubutawa da damma biyu", "means a or an.": "ma'anarsa wani ko wata.", "means a house. Notice there is no word for is.": "ma'anarsa wani gida. Ka lura babu kalmar \"ne\" a Larabci a nan.", "means what. We use it to ask about things and animals.": "ma'anarsa mene. Muna amfani da shi don tambaya game da abubuwa da dabbobi.", "means who. We use it to ask about people.": "ma'anarsa wane. Muna amfani da shi don tambaya game da mutane.", "Do not mix them up.": "Kada ka haɗa su.", "is for things and animals.": "na abubuwa ne da dabbobi.", "is only for people.": "na mutane ne kawai.", "Put": "Sanya", "at the start of a sentence to make a yes or no question.": "a farkon jumla don yin tambayar i ko a'a.", "becomes": "ya zama", "is this a house?": "shin wannan gida ne?", "Answer with": "Ka amsa da", "yes, or": "i, ko", "no. Then say what it is.": "a'a. Sannan ka faɗi abin da yake.", "This is…": "Wannan…", "📗 Lessons in Arabic Language, Book {0}": "📗 Darussan Harshen Larabci, Littafi na {0}", "Lesson {0}, pp. {1}–{2}": "Darasi na {0}, shafi na {1} zuwa {2}", "Intro": "Gabatarwa", "Learn": "Koyo", "Words: things": "Kalmomi: abubuwa", "Words: people": "Kalmomi: mutane", "Match pictures": "Haɗa hotuna", "Match meanings": "Haɗa ma'anoni", "Maa or man?": "Maa ko man?", "Read & repeat": "Karanta ka maimaita", "What is this?": "Mene ne wannan?", "Is this…?": "Shin wannan…?", "Listen": "Saurara", "Meaning": "Ma'ana", "Build": "Gina", "Write": "Rubuta", "Exam": "Jarrabawa", "Start lesson": "Fara darasi", "These words are people. For people we ask": "Waɗannan kalmomi mutane ne. Ga mutane muna tambaya", "who is this. Tap every picture to hear the word.": "wane ne wannan. Taɓa kowane hoto don jin kalmar.", "Step {0} of {1}": "Mataki na {0} cikin {1}", "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Welcome to the Arabic class. In this course you will learn to understand, read and speak Arabic, the language of the Qur'an, step by step.": "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Barka da zuwa ajin Larabci. A wannan kwas za ka koyi fahimta, karatu da magana da Larabci, harshen Alƙur'ani, mataki-mataki.", "Start the lesson →": "Fara darasi →", "Pause": "Dakata", "Replay": "Sake kunnawa", "Skip": "Tsallake", "The rule": "Ƙa'ida", "Read each card and tap the examples to hear them.": "Karanta kowane kati ka taɓa misalan don jin su.", "haadhaa": "haadhaa", "this": "wannan", "Use": "Yi amfani da", "to point at something or someone near you. (It is for masculine words; you will learn the feminine later.)": "don nuna wani abu ko wani mutum da ke kusa da kai. Na kalmomin namiji ne; za ka koyi na mace daga baya.", "This is a house.": "Wannan gida ne.", "This is a mosque.": "Wannan masallaci ne.", "This is a door.": "Wannan ƙofa ce.", "Next rule →": "Ƙa'ida ta gaba →", "bayt-un": "bayt-un", "-un = a / an": "-un yana nufin wani ko wata", "-un": "-un", "(two dammas on the last letter) means": "damma biyu a kan harafin ƙarshe, ma'anarsa", "or": "ko", "an": "wata", "= a house. Arabic has no word for": "yana nufin wani gida. Larabci ba shi da kalmar", "is": "ne", "here:": "a nan:", "= this (is) a house.": "yana nufin wannan gida ne.", "a house": "wani gida", "a pen": "wani alƙalami", "a boy": "wani yaro", "← Back": "← Koma baya", "maa haadhaa?": "maa haadhaa?", "means": "ma'anarsa", "what": "mene", ". Use it to ask about things and animals.": ". Yi amfani da shi don tambaya game da abubuwa da dabbobi.", "This is a book.": "Wannan littafi ne.", "This is a camel.": "Wannan raƙumi ne.", "man haadhaa?": "man haadhaa?", "Who is this?": "Wane ne wannan?", "who": "wane", ". Use it to ask about people.": ". Yi amfani da shi don tambaya game da mutane.", "This is a doctor.": "Wannan likita ne.", "This is a boy.": "Wannan yaro ne.", "maa": "maa", "man": "man", "Don't mix them up:": "Kada ka haɗa su:", "is for things and animals,": "na abubuwa ne da dabbobi,", "What is this? This is a cat.": "Mene ne wannan? Wannan mage ce.", "Who is this? This is a man.": "Wane ne wannan? Wannan namiji ne.", "What is this? This is a door.": "Mene ne wannan? Wannan ƙofa ce.", "Who is this? This is a teacher.": "Wane ne wannan? Wannan malami ne.", "Is…? (a yes / no question)": "Shin…? Tambayar i ko a'a", "at the start of a sentence to make a yes or no question:": "a farkon jumla don yin tambayar i ko a'a:", "Is this a house?": "Shin wannan gida ne?", "Is this a pen?": "Shin wannan alƙalami ne?", "na'am": "na'am", "yes": "i", "laa": "laa", "no": "a'a", "(yes) or": "wato i, ko", "(no), then say what it is.": "wato a'a, sannan ka faɗi abin da yake.", "Yes, this is a house.": "I, wannan gida ne.", "Is this a bed?": "Shin wannan gado ne?", "No, this is a chair.": "A'a, wannan kujera ce.", "Next →": "Na gaba →", "Tap every picture to hear the word. Say it aloud.": "Taɓa kowane hoto don jin kalmar. Faɗe ta da ƙarfi.", "a mosque": "wani masallaci", "a door": "wata ƙofa", "a book": "wani littafi", "a key": "wani mabuɗi", "a desk": "wani teburin karatu", "a bed": "wani gado", "a chair": "wata kujera", "a shirt": "wata riga", "a star": "wani tauraro", "a handkerchief": "wani hankici", "a dog": "wani kare", "a cat": "wata mage", "a donkey": "wani jaki", "a horse": "wani doki", "a camel": "wani raƙumi", "a rooster": "wani zakara", "New words: things and animals": "Sababbin kalmomi: abubuwa da dabbobi", "baytun": "baytun", "masjidun": "masjidun", "baabun": "baabun", "kitaabun": "kitaabun", "qalamun": "qalamun", "miftaaḥun": "miftaaḥun", "maktabun": "maktabun", "sareerun": "sareerun", "kursiyyun": "kursiyyun", "qameeṣun": "qameeṣun", "najmun": "najmun", "mindeelun": "mindeelun", "kalbun": "kalbun", "qiṭṭun": "qiṭṭun", "ḥimaarun": "ḥimaarun", "ḥiṣaanun": "ḥiṣaanun", "jamalun": "jamalun", "deekun": "deekun", "▶ Read all": "▶ Karanta duka", "{0} / {1} heard": "{0} cikin {1} an ji", "a doctor": "wani likita", "a student": "wani ɗalibi", "a man": "wani namiji", "a merchant": "wani ɗan kasuwa", "a teacher": "wani malami", "New words: people": "Sababbin kalmomi: mutane", "ṭabeebun": "ṭabeebun", "waladun": "waladun", "ṭaalibun": "ṭaalibun", "rajulun": "rajulun", "taajirun": "taajirun", "mudarrisun": "mudarrisun", "Tap a picture, then tap its Arabic word.": "Taɓa hoto, sannan ka taɓa kalmarsa ta Larabci.", "Match the picture to the word": "Haɗa hoton da kalmar", "Round {0} / {1}": "Zagaye na {0} cikin {1}", "Mumtaz! Excellent!": "Mumtaz! Madalla!", "Masha'Allah!": "Masha'Allah!", "Barakallahu feekum!": "Barakallahu feekum!", "All pairs matched": "An haɗa dukan biyu-biyu", "No mistakes. Masha'Allah!": "Babu kuskure. Masha'Allah!", "Tap an Arabic word, then tap its meaning.": "Taɓa kalmar Larabci, sannan ka taɓa ma'anarta.", "Match the word to its meaning": "Haɗa kalmar da ma'anarta", "Things and animals: use": "Abubuwa da dabbobi: yi amfani da", "Things and animals →": "Abubuwa da dabbobi →", ". People →": ". Mutane →", "Which question do we ask?": "Wace tambaya muke yi?", "People: use": "Mutane: yi amfani da", "{0} / {1} right first time": "{0} cikin {1} daidai a karon farko", "Every answer is now correct.": "Yanzu kowace amsa daidai ce.", "Listen, then tap the mic and read the sentence aloud. The app checks you.": "Saurara, sannan ka taɓa makirufo ka karanta jumlar da ƙarfi. Manhajar za ta duba ka.", "What is this? This is a book.": "Mene ne wannan? Wannan littafi ne.", "🔊 Listen": "🔊 Saurara", "▶ My voice": "▶ Muryata", "Tap the mic and read it aloud": "Taɓa makirufo ka karanta da ƙarfi", "Listening… tap again to stop": "Ina sauraro… sake taɓawa don tsayawa", "Microphone not available. Read it aloud, then continue.": "Babu makirufo. Ka karanta da ƙarfi, sannan ka ci gaba.", "Try again": "Sake gwadawa", "I read it correctly": "Na karanta daidai", "Is this a house? Yes, this is a house.": "Shin wannan gida ne? I, wannan gida ne.", "Is this a bed? No, this is a chair.": "Shin wannan gado ne? A'a, wannan kujera ce.", "Who is this? This is a doctor.": "Wane ne wannan? Wannan likita ne.", "Is this a boy? No, this is a man.": "Shin wannan yaro ne? A'a, wannan namiji ne.", "Is this a dog? No, this is a cat.": "Shin wannan kare ne? A'a, wannan mage ce.", "What is this? This is a camel.": "Mene ne wannan? Wannan raƙumi ne.", "Is this a shirt? No, this is a handkerchief.": "Shin wannan riga ce? A'a, wannan hankici ne.", "{0} / {1} read correctly": "{0} cikin {1} an karanta daidai", "Look at the picture and choose the right answer.": "Duba hoton ka zaɓi amsar da ta dace.", "What is this? Who is this?": "Mene ne wannan? Wane ne wannan?", "Answer the question.": "Amsa tambayar.", "Play": "Kunna", "(no).": "wato a'a.", "Look at the picture and answer.": "Duba hoton ka amsa.", "Listen to the word, then tap its picture.": "Saurari kalmar, sannan ka taɓa hotonta.", "Listen and choose": "Saurara ka zaɓa", "Which picture is it?": "Wane hoto ne?", "🔊 Play": "🔊 Kunna", "Choose the meaning of the Arabic.": "Zaɓi ma'anar Larabcin.", "What does it mean?": "Mece ce ma'anarsa?", "What does this word mean?": "Mece ce ma'anar wannan kalma?", "Is this a book?": "Shin wannan littafi ne?", "What does this mean?": "Mece ce ma'anar wannan?", "Tap the words in the right order (Arabic goes from right to left).": "Taɓa kalmomin bisa tsarin da ya dace. Larabci yana tafiya daga dama zuwa hagu.", "Build the sentence": "Gina jumlar", "Is this a dog?": "Shin wannan kare ne?", "Check": "Duba", "{0} sentences built": "An gina jumloli {0}", "Listen, then tap the letters to write the word.": "Saurara, sannan ka taɓa haruffan don rubuta kalmar.", "Read & write": "Karanta ka rubuta", "{0} words written": "An rubuta kalmomi {0}", "Lesson {0} exam": "Jarrabawar darasi na {0}", "15 questions": "Tambayoyi 15", "{0} minutes": "Minti {0}", "pass mark 90%": "maki na ci kashi 90%", "Start the exam": "Fara jarrabawa", "Question {0} / {1} ·": "Tambaya ta {0} cikin {1} ·", "Listen, then write the word. (a star)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato wani tauraro.", "مَا or مَنْ?": "مَا ko مَنْ?", "Passed. Lesson complete": "Ka ci. An gama darasi", "Masha'Allah": "Masha'Allah", "Barakallahu feekum": "Barakallahu feekum", "15 of 15 correct": "15 cikin 15 daidai", "Retake exam": "Sake jarrabawa", "Answer review": "Duba amsoshi", "✅ Look at the picture and answer.": "✅ Duba hoton ka amsa.", "✅ Answer the question.": "✅ Amsa tambayar.", "✅ Write: a star": "✅ Rubuta: wani tauraro", "✅ Which question do we ask?": "✅ Wace tambaya muke yi?", "✅ What does this word mean?": "✅ Mece ce ma'anar wannan kalma?", "✅ What is this?": "✅ Mene ne wannan?", "✅ Is this a dog?": "✅ Shin wannan kare ne?", "✅ Which picture is it?": "✅ Wane hoto ne?", "which means that, for something far away. You will compare": "wanda ma'anarsa wancan, don abin da ke nesa. Za ka kwatanta", "this, and": "wannan, da", "that, and ask": "wancan, ka tambaya", "what is that, and": "mene ne wancan, da", "who is that. You will also learn four new words.": "wane ne wancan. Za ka kuma koyi sababbin kalmomi huɗu.", "means that. We use it for something or someone far from us.": "ma'anarsa wancan. Muna amfani da shi don wani abu ko wani mutum da ke nesa da mu.", "is for something near you.": "na abin da ke kusa da kai ne.", "is for something far away.": "na abin da ke nesa ne.", "Just like Lesson 1.": "Kamar yadda yake a Darasi na 1.", "for things and animals,": "don abubuwa da dabbobi,", "for people.": "don mutane.", "means and. It is joined to the next word, like": "ma'anarsa da. Ana haɗa shi da kalmar da ke biye, kamar", "and that.": "da wancan.", "Add": "Ƙara", "at the start for a yes or no question, as in Lesson 1.": "a farko don tambayar i ko a'a, kamar a Darasi na 1.", "That is…": "Wancan…", "SUGAR": "SUKARI", "New words": "Sababbin kalmomi", "Near or far?": "Kusa ko nesa?", "What is that?": "Mene ne wancan?", "Is that…?": "Shin wancan…?", "In this lesson you will learn ذٰلِكَ, which means that, for something far away. You will compare هٰذَا, this, and ذٰلِكَ, that, and ask مَا ذٰلِكَ, what is that, and مَنْ ذٰلِكَ, who is that. You will also learn four new words.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi ذٰلِكَ, wanda ma'anarsa wancan, don abin da ke nesa. Za ka kwatanta هٰذَا, wannan, da ذٰلِكَ, wancan, ka tambaya مَا ذٰلِكَ, mene ne wancan, da مَنْ ذٰلِكَ, wane ne wancan. Za ka kuma koyi sababbin kalmomi huɗu.", "dhaalika": "dhaalika", "that": "wancan", "for something or someone": "don wani abu ko wani mutum da ke", "far": "nesa", "from you. (In the book it is written": "da kai. A cikin littafin ana rubuta shi", ", without the small alif; we read it dhaalika.)": ", ba tare da ƙaramin alif ba; muna karanta shi dhaalika.", "That is a star.": "Wancan tauraro ne.", "That is a bed.": "Wancan gado ne.", "That is an imam.": "Wancan liman ne.", "this (near)": "wannan, na kusa", "that (far)": "wancan, na nesa", "points to something near you.": "yana nuna abin da ke kusa da kai.", "points to something far away.": "yana nuna abin da ke nesa.", "near": "kusa", "This is a mosque and that is a house.": "Wannan masallaci ne kuma wancan gida ne.", "This is a horse and that is a donkey.": "Wannan doki ne kuma wancan jaki ne.", "This is sugar and that is milk.": "Wannan sukari ne kuma wancan madara ce.", "maa dhaalika?": "maa dhaalika?", "man dhaalika?": "man dhaalika?", "Who is that?": "Wane ne wancan?", "Like Lesson 1:": "Kamar Darasi na 1:", "What is that? That is a stone.": "Mene ne wancan? Wancan dutse ne.", "Who is this and who is that?": "Wane ne wannan kuma wane ne wancan?", "This is a teacher and that is an imam.": "Wannan malami ne kuma wancan liman ne.", "wa": "wa", "and": "da", ". It is written joined to the next word:": ". Ana rubuta shi a haɗe da kalmar da ke biye:", "(and that).": "wato da wancan.", "This is a pen and that is a book.": "Wannan alƙalami ne kuma wancan littafi ne.", "a-dhaalika…?": "a-dhaalika…?", "for a yes or no question, as in Lesson 1.": "don tambayar i ko a'a, kamar a Darasi na 1.", "Is that a dog?": "Shin wancan kare ne?", "No, that is a cat.": "A'a, wancan mage ce.", "Tap every word to hear it. Say it aloud.": "Taɓa kowace kalma don jin ta. Faɗe ta da ƙarfi.", "an imam": "wani liman", "a stone": "wani dutse", "sugar": "sukari", "milk": "madara", "imaamun": "imaamun", "ḥajarun": "ḥajarun", "sukkarun": "sukkarun", "labanun": "labanun", "What is that? That is a star.": "Mene ne wancan? Wancan tauraro ne.", "Is that a dog? No, that is a cat.": "Shin wancan kare ne? A'a, wancan mage ce.", "Near: use": "Kusa: yi amfani da", "Near →": "Kusa →", ". Far →": ". Nesa →", "👇 It is": "👇 Yana", "you. Choose the right sentence.": "da kai. Zaɓi jumlar da ta dace.", "Far: use": "Nesa: yi amfani da", "👉 It is": "👉 Yana", "from you. Choose the right sentence.": "da kai. Zaɓi jumlar da ta dace.", "Look at the picture and answer the question.": "Duba hoton ka amsa tambayar.", "What is that? Who is that?": "Mene ne wancan? Wane ne wancan?", "That is a stone.": "Wancan dutse ne.", "هٰذَا or ذٰلِكَ?": "هٰذَا ko ذٰلِكَ?", "Listen, then write the word. (an imam)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato wani liman.", "✅ 👇 It is": "✅ 👇 Yana", "✅ That is a stone.": "✅ Wancan dutse ne.", "✅ 👉 It is": "✅ 👉 Yana", "✅ This is a teacher and that is an imam.": "✅ Wannan malami ne kuma wancan liman ne.", "✅ Write: an imam": "✅ Rubuta: wani liman", "which means the. You will make simple sentences like": "wanda ma'anarsa \"the\" na Turanci, wato sanin abu. Za ka yi jumloli masu sauƙi kamar", "the pen is broken, with many new describing words. You will also learn the moon letters and the sun letters, which tell you when the": "alƙalamin ya karye, tare da sababbin kalmomi masu siffantawa da yawa. Za ka kuma koyi haruffan wata da haruffan rana, waɗanda ke gaya maka lokacin da ake karanta", "of": "na", "is read and when it is silent.": "da lokacin da ake yin shiru da shi.", "before a word to mean the. Then the ending": "a gaban kalma don nufin \"the\", wato sanannen abu. Sannan ƙarshen", "a house, becomes": "wato wani gida, ya zama", "the house.": "gidan, wato sanannen gida.", "A simple sentence: the thing, with": "Jumla mai sauƙi: abin, da", "then what it is like, with": "sannan yadda yake, da", "There is no word for is.": "Babu kalmar \"ne\" a nan.", "Join two sentences with": "Haɗa jumloli biyu da", "Before": "A gaban", "it is joined, like": "ana haɗa shi, kamar", "With the moon letters, the": "Da haruffan wata, ana furta", "is pronounced:": ":", "With the sun letters, the": "Da haruffan rana, ana rubuta", "is written but not read, and the next letter is doubled:": "amma ba a karanta shi, kuma harafin da ke biye ana ninka shi:", "The pen is broken": "Alƙalamin ya karye", "Words {0}": "Kalmomi {0}", "Add الْ": "Ƙara الْ", "Moon or sun?": "Wata ko rana?", "Opposites": "Kishiyoyi", "Say it in Arabic": "Faɗe shi da Larabci", "In this lesson you will learn الْ, which means the. You will make simple sentences like الْقَلَمُ مَكْسُورٌ, the pen is broken, with many new describing words. You will also learn the moon letters and the sun letters, which tell you when the لَامْ of الْ is read and when it is silent.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi الْ, wanda ma'anarsa \"the\" na Turanci, wato sanin abu. Za ka yi jumloli masu sauƙi kamar الْقَلَمُ مَكْسُورٌ, alƙalamin ya karye, tare da sababbin kalmomi masu siffantawa da yawa. Za ka kuma koyi haruffan wata da haruffan rana, waɗanda ke gaya maka lokacin da ake karanta لَامْ na الْ da lokacin da ake yin shiru da shi.", "al-": "al-", "the": "sanannen abu, kamar \"-n\" a gidan", "before a word to mean": "a gaban kalma don nufin", ". The ending": ". Sannan ƙarshen", "then becomes a single damma": "ya zama damma ɗaya", "(a house) →": "wato wani gida, ya zama →", "(the house).": "wato gidan.", "a house → the house": "wani gida → gidan", "a book → the book": "wani littafi → littafin", "a pen → the pen": "wani alƙalami → alƙalamin", "al-qalamu maksuurun": "al-qalamu maksuurun", "The pen is broken.": "Alƙalamin ya karye.", "A sentence:": "Jumla:", "the thing": "abin", "(with": "da", "what it is like": "yadda yake", "(with -un). There is no word for": "da -un. Babu kalmar", "The door is open.": "Ƙofar a buɗe take.", "The water is cold.": "Ruwan yana da sanyi.", ". Before": ". A gaban", "we say": "muna cewa", "wal-": "wal-", "The boy is sitting and the teacher is standing.": "Yaron yana zaune kuma malamin yana tsaye.", "The house is near and the mosque is far.": "Gidan yana kusa kuma masallacin yana nesa.", "al-qamaru": "al-qamaru", "Moon letters: the ل is read": "Haruffan wata: ana karanta ل", "With 14 letters, the": "Da haruffa 14, ana furta", "al-baabu": "al-baabu", "the moon": "watan", "the door": "ƙofar", "the dog": "karen", "the boy": "yaron", "ash-shamsu": "ash-shamsu", "Sun letters: the ل is silent": "Haruffan rana: ba a karanta ل", "With the other 14 letters, the": "Da sauran haruffa 14, ana rubuta", "is written but not read, and the next letter is doubled (it has a shadda):": "amma ba a karanta shi, kuma harafin da ke biye ana ninka shi, wato yana da shadda:", "ar-rajulu": "ar-rajulu", "an-najmu": "an-najmu", "the man": "mutumin", "the star": "tauraron", "the merchant": "ɗan kasuwar", "the rooster": "zakaran", "a moon": "wani wata", "water": "ruwa", "paper": "takarda", "a shop": "wani shago", "apples": "tuffa", "a notebook": "wani littafin rubutu", "New words: things": "Sababbin kalmomi: abubuwa", "qamarun": "qamarun", "maa'un": "maa'un", "waraqun": "waraqun", "dukkaanun": "dukkaanun", "tuffaaḥun": "tuffaaḥun", "daftarun": "daftarun", "new": "sabo", "old": "tsoho", "broken": "karyayye", "open": "buɗaɗɗe", "dirty": "datti", "clean": "mai tsabta", "cold": "mai sanyi", "hot": "mai zafi", "big": "babba", "small": "ƙarami", "New words: describing words {0}": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin siffantawa {0}", "jadeedun": "jadeedun", "qadeemun": "qadeemun", "maksuurun": "maksuurun", "maftuuḥun": "maftuuḥun", "wasikhun": "wasikhun", "naẓeefun": "naẓeefun", "baaridun": "baaridun", "ḥaarrun": "ḥaarrun", "kabeerun": "kabeerun", "ṣagheerun": "ṣagheerun", "heavy": "mai nauyi", "light (not heavy)": "mara nauyi", "beautiful": "kyakkyawa", "sitting": "zaune", "standing": "tsaye", "sweet": "mai zaƙi", "delicious": "mai daɗi", "thaqeelun": "thaqeelun", "khafeefun": "khafeefun", "jameelun": "jameelun", "qareebun": "qareebun", "ba'eedun": "ba'eedun", "jaalisun": "jaalisun", "waaqifun": "waaqifun", "ḥulwun": "ḥulwun", "ladheedhun": "ladheedhun", "sick": "mara lafiya", "rich": "mawadaci", "poor": "matalauci", "tall, long": "dogo", "short": "gajere", "mareeḍun": "mareeḍun", "ghaniyyun": "ghaniyyun", "faqeerun": "faqeerun", "ṭaweelun": "ṭaweelun", "qaṣeerun": "qaṣeerun", "The book is new and the pen is old.": "Littafin sabo ne kuma alƙalamin tsoho ne.", "The donkey is small and the horse is big.": "Jakin ƙarami ne kuma dokin babba ne.", "The stone is heavy and the paper is light.": "Dutsen yana da nauyi kuma takardar ba ta da nauyi.", "The apples are delicious.": "Tuffar tana da daɗi.", "Make it “the …”": "Mayar da shi sanannen abu", "and change the ending to a single damma.": "ka canza ƙarshen zuwa damma ɗaya.", "How do you say “the …”?": "Yaya ake faɗar sanannen abu?", "and change the ending to a single": "ka canza ƙarshen zuwa", "Listen: is the": "Saurara: shin ana karanta", "No: sun letter, the ل is silent": "A'a: harafin rana ne, ba a karanta ل", "Yes: moon letter, the ل is read": "I: harafin wata ne, ana karanta ل", "Moon letter or sun letter?": "Harafin wata ne ko harafin rana?", "read?": "?", "Is the ل pronounced here?": "Shin ana furta ل a nan?", "Choose the word with the opposite meaning.": "Zaɓi kalmar da ke da kishiyar ma'ana.", "What is the opposite?": "Mene ne kishiyarsa?", "Choose the Arabic sentence that means the same.": "Zaɓi jumlar Larabci da ke da ma'ana ɗaya.", "“The horse is big.”": "“Dokin babba ne.”", "“The doctor is tall.”": "“Likitan dogo ne.”", "“The house is near.”": "“Gidan yana kusa.”", "“The apples are delicious.”": "“Tuffar tana da daɗi.”", "“The pen is old.”": "“Alƙalamin tsoho ne.”", "“The moon is beautiful.”": "“Watan kyakkyawa ne.”", "“The student is sick.”": "“Ɗalibin ba shi da lafiya.”", "“The stone is heavy.”": "“Dutsen yana da nauyi.”", "“The merchant is rich.”": "“Ɗan kasuwar mawadaci ne.”", "“The chair is broken.”": "“Kujerar ta karye.”", "Listen, then write the word. (big)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato babba.", "“The man is standing.”": "“Mutumin yana tsaye.”", "✅ The boy is sitting and the teacher is standing.": "✅ Yaron yana zaune kuma malamin yana tsaye.", "✅ How do you say “the …”?": "✅ Yaya ake faɗar sanannen abu?", "✅ What is the opposite?": "✅ Mene ne kishiyarsa?", "✅ The door is open.": "✅ Ƙofar a buɗe take.", "✅ Is the ل pronounced here?": "✅ Shin ana furta ل a nan?", "✅ Write: big": "✅ Rubuta: babba", "✅ “The man is standing.”": "✅ “Mutumin yana tsaye.”", "✅ “The moon is beautiful.”": "✅ “Watan kyakkyawa ne.”", "In this lesson you will ask": "A wannan darasi za ka tambaya", "where, and answer with": "ina, ka amsa da", "in, and": "a cikin, da", "on. You will learn": "a kan. Za ka koyi", "he, and": "shi, da", "she. Then you will learn": "ita. Sannan za ka koyi", "from, and": "daga, da", "to, ask": "zuwa, ka tambaya", "where are you from, and say": "daga ina kake, ka ce", "he went, and": "ya tafi, da", "he went out.": "ya fita.", "means in.": "ma'anarsa a cikin.", "means on. After them, the last vowel changes to a": "ma'anarsa a kan. Bayan su, wasalin ƙarshe yana canzawa zuwa", "in the house.": "a cikin gidan.", "Ask": "Tambaya", "is for a man or a masculine word.": "na namiji ne ko kalmar namiji, wato muzakkari.", "is for a woman or a feminine word. Words ending in": "na mace ne ko kalmar mace, wato mu'annasi. Kalmomin da ke ƙarewa da", "are usually feminine.": "yawanci na mace ne.", "Boys' names usually end in": "Sunayen maza yawanci suna ƙarewa da", "like": "kamar", "Most girls' names end in": "Yawancin sunayen mata suna ƙarewa da", "with no": "ba tare da", "means from.": "ma'anarsa daga.", "means to. They also change the last vowel to a": "ma'anarsa zuwa. Su ma suna canza wasalin ƙarshe zuwa", "means, where are you from? Answer:": "ma'anarsa, daga ina kake? Amsa:", "I am from.": "Ni daga.", "Where is it?": "Ina yake?", "He or she?": "Shi ko ita?", "In, on, from, to": "A cikin, a kan, daga, zuwa", "Where from?": "Daga ina?", "In this lesson you will ask أَيْنَ, where, and answer with فِي, in, and عَلَى, on. You will learn هُوَ, he, and هِيَ, she. Then you will learn مِنْ, from, and إِلَى, to, ask مِنْ أَيْنَ أَنْتَ, where are you from, and say ذَهَبَ, he went, and خَرَجَ, he went out.": "A wannan darasi za ka tambaya أَيْنَ, ina, ka amsa da فِي, a cikin, da عَلَى, a kan. Za ka koyi هُوَ, shi, da هِيَ, ita. Sannan za ka koyi مِنْ, daga, da إِلَى, zuwa, ka tambaya مِنْ أَيْنَ أَنْتَ, daga ina kake, ka ce ذَهَبَ, ya tafi, da خَرَجَ, ya fita.", "fee": "fee", "in": "a cikin", "'alaa": "'alaa", "on": "a kan", "After": "Bayan", "(in) and": "wato a cikin, da", "(on), the last vowel changes to": "wato a kan, wasalin ƙarshe yana canzawa zuwa", "kasra -i": "kasra -i", "the house → in the house": "gidan → a cikin gidan", "the mosque → in the mosque": "masallacin → a cikin masallacin", "the desk → on the desk": "teburin → a kan teburin", "the bed → on the bed": "gadon → a kan gadon", "ayna?": "ayna?", "Where?": "Ina?", "and answer with": "ka amsa da", "Where is Muhammad?": "Ina Muhammadu yake?", "He is in the room.": "Yana cikin ɗakin.", "Where is the book?": "Ina littafin yake?", "It is on the desk.": "Yana kan teburin.", "huwa": "huwa", "he": "shi", "hiya": "hiya", "she": "ita", "for a man or a masculine word.": "na namiji ne ko kalmar namiji, wato muzakkari.", "for a woman or a feminine word. Words ending in": "na mace ne ko kalmar mace, wato mu'annasi. Kalmomin da ke ƙarewa da", "are usually feminine:": "yawanci na mace ne:", "it": "shi ko ita, ga abu", "Where is Aminah? She is in the kitchen.": "Ina Aminatu take? Tana cikin kicin.", "Where is the watch? It is on the bed.": "Ina agogon yake? Yana kan gadon.", "Where is Yasir? He is in the bathroom.": "Ina Yasir yake? Yana cikin banɗaki.", "names": "sunaye", "Boys' and girls' names": "Sunayen maza da na mata", ". Most girls' names end in a single damma with no -un:": ". Yawancin sunayen mata suna ƙarewa da damma ɗaya ba tare da -un ba:", "boys": "maza", "girls": "mata", "Hamid": "Hamid", "Ammar": "Ammar", "Aishah": "A'isha", "Khadijah": "Khadija", "min": "min", "from": "daga", "ilaa": "ilaa", "to": "zuwa", "(from) and": "wato daga, da", "(to) also change the last vowel to -i. Before": "wato zuwa, su ma suna canza wasalin ƙarshe zuwa -i. A gaban", "from the house": "daga gidan", "to the mosque": "zuwa masallacin", "He went to the principal.": "Ya tafi wurin shugaban makarantar.", "He went out of the classroom.": "Ya fita daga ajin.", "min ayna anta?": "min ayna anta?", "Where are you from?": "Daga ina kake?", "Answer:": "Amsa:", "… (I am from …).": "… wato ni daga … nake.", "I am from Japan.": "Ni daga Japan nake.", "He is from China.": "Shi daga China yake.", "He is from India.": "Shi daga Indiya yake.", "the school": "makarantar", "the classroom": "ajin", "the room": "ɗakin", "the kitchen": "kicin ɗin", "the bathroom": "banɗakin wanka", "the toilet": "banɗakin bayan gida", "the university": "jami'ar", "the market": "kasuwar", "the watch, the clock": "agogon", "New words: places": "Sababbin kalmomi: wurare", "al-madrasatu": "al-madrasatu", "al-faṣlu": "al-faṣlu", "al-ghurfatu": "al-ghurfatu", "al-maṭbakhu": "al-maṭbakhu", "al-ḥammaamu": "al-ḥammaamu", "al-mirḥaaḍu": "al-mirḥaaḍu", "al-jaami'atu": "al-jaami'atu", "as-suuqu": "as-suuqu", "as-saa'atu": "as-saa'atu", "Japan": "Japan", "China": "China", "India": "Indiya", "the Philippines": "Filifin", "the principal (director)": "shugaban makarantar, wato darakta", "he went": "ya tafi", "he went out": "ya fita", "New words: countries and people": "Sababbin kalmomi: ƙasashe da mutane", "al-yaabaanu": "al-yaabaanu", "aṣ-ṣeenu": "aṣ-ṣeenu", "al-hindu": "al-hindu", "al-filibbeenu": "al-filibbeenu", "al-mudeeru": "al-mudeeru", "dhahaba": "dhahaba", "kharaja": "kharaja", "she, it": "ita, ga mace ko abu na mace", "you (a man)": "kai, ga namiji", "he, it": "shi, ga namiji ko abu na namiji", "where?": "ina?", "Where is Muhammad? He is in the room.": "Ina Muhammadu yake? Yana cikin ɗakin.", "And where is Aminah? She is in the kitchen.": "Kuma ina Aminatu take? Tana cikin kicin.", "Where is the book? It is on the desk.": "Ina littafin yake? Yana kan teburin.", "And where is the watch? It is on the bed.": "Kuma ina agogon yake? Yana kan gadon.", "Where are you from? I am from Japan.": "Daga ina kake? Ni daga Japan nake.", "And where is Ammar from? He is from China.": "Kuma daga ina Ammar yake? Shi daga China yake.", "Where did he go? He went to the principal.": "Ina ya tafi? Ya tafi wurin shugaban makarantar.", "The teacher went out of the classroom and went to the principal.": "Malamin ya fita daga ajin kuma ya tafi wurin shugaban makarantar.", "Read the English, then choose the right answer to the question.": "Karanta Turancin, sannan ka zaɓi amsar da ta dace da tambayar.", "“Fatimah is in the school.”": "“Faɗimatu tana cikin makarantar.”", "“Zaynab is in the room.”": "“Zainab tana cikin ɗakin.”", "“The watch is on the bed.”": "“Agogon yana kan gadon.”", "“Muhammad is in the room.”": "“Muhammadu yana cikin ɗakin.”", "“The teacher is in the classroom.”": "“Malamin yana cikin ajin.”", "“The student is at the university.”": "“Ɗalibin yana jami'ar.”", "“Yasir is in the bathroom.”": "“Yasir yana cikin banɗakin.”", "“The man is in the mosque.”": "“Mutumin yana cikin masallacin.”", "Choose": "Zaɓi", "for masculine,": "don namiji,", "for feminine.": "don mace.", "Which word do we use?": "Wace kalma muke amfani da ita?", "Choose the word that fits.": "Zaɓi kalmar da ta dace.", "Choose the word that fits the gap.": "Zaɓi kalmar da ta dace da gurbin.", "These words change the last vowel to": "Waɗannan kalmomi suna canza wasalin ƙarshe zuwa", "The ending after": "Ƙarshen da ke bayan", "These words change the last vowel to kasra (-i).": "Waɗannan kalmomi suna canza wasalin ƙarshe zuwa kasra, wato -i.", "Which is correct?": "Wanne ne daidai?", "Choose the right answer.": "Zaɓi amsar da ta dace.", "Ammar is from India.": "Ammar daga Indiya yake.", "You are from China.": "Kai daga China kake.", "You are from Japan.": "Kai daga Japan kake.", "Ammar is from the Philippines.": "Ammar daga Filifin yake.", "You are from India.": "Kai daga Indiya kake.", "You are from the Philippines.": "Kai daga Filifin kake.", "The teacher went out of the classroom.": "Malamin ya fita daga ajin.", "It (the watch) is on the bed.": "Shi, wato agogon, yana kan gadon.", "هُوَ or هِيَ?": "هُوَ ko هِيَ?", "The ending after فِي": "Ƙarshen da ke bayan فِي", "Ammar is from Japan.": "Ammar daga Japan yake.", "Listen, then write the word. (from)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato daga.", "✅ It (the watch) is on the bed.": "✅ Shi, wato agogon, yana kan gadon.", "✅ Which word do we use?": "✅ Wace kalma muke amfani da ita?", "✅ Choose the word that fits the gap.": "✅ Zaɓi kalmar da ta dace da gurbin.", "✅ I am from Japan.": "✅ Ni daga Japan nake.", "✅ “The teacher is in the classroom.”": "✅ “Malamin yana cikin ajin.”", "✅ Which is correct?": "✅ Wanne ne daidai?", "✅ “The student is at the university.”": "✅ “Ɗalibin yana jami'ar.”", "✅ Ammar is from Japan.": "✅ Ammar daga Japan yake.", "✅ Write: from": "✅ Rubuta: daga", "In this lesson you will learn to say whose something is, by putting two words together, like": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi faɗar wanda yake da abu, ta hanyar haɗa kalmomi biyu, kamar", "Muhammad's book. You will ask": "littafin Muhammadu. Za ka tambaya", "whose book is this. You will learn": "littafin wane ne wannan. Za ka koyi", "under, and how to call someone with": "a ƙarƙashin, da yadda ake kiran mutum da", "Put two nouns together to show whose something is. First the thing, then the owner.": "Haɗa sunaye biyu don nuna wanda yake da abu. Na farko abin, sannan mai shi. Ana kiran wannan idafa.", "means Muhammad's book.": "ma'anarsa littafin Muhammadu.", "The first word never has": "Kalma ta farko ba ta taɓa samun", "and never has": "kuma ba ta taɓa samun", "The second word ends in a": "Kalma ta biyu tana ƙarewa da", "After a first word,": "Bayan kalma ta farko,", "the House of Allah.": "Ɗakin Allah.", "where the owner goes, to ask whose.": "a wurin mai abin, don tambayar na wane ne.", "means under. Like": "ma'anarsa a ƙarƙashin. Kamar", "it changes the next ending to a": "yana canza ƙarshen kalmar da ke biye zuwa", "means there.": "ma'anarsa can.", "To call someone, say": "Don kiran mutum, ka ce", "then the name with one": "sannan sunan da damma ɗaya", "The first alif of": "Alif na farko na", "is only read at the start. In the middle it is silent, like": "ana karanta shi ne a farko kawai. A tsakiya ba a karanta shi, kamar", "Muhammad's book": "Littafin Muhammadu", "Whose is it?": "Na wane ne?", "Correct it": "Gyara shi", "Calling": "Kira", "Under, on, in": "A ƙarƙashin, a kai, a ciki", "In this lesson you will learn to say whose something is, by putting two words together, like كِتَابُ مُحَمَّدٍ, Muhammad's book. You will ask كِتَابُ مَنْ هٰذَا, whose book is this. You will learn تَحْتَ, under, and how to call someone with يَا.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi faɗar wanda yake da abu, ta hanyar haɗa kalmomi biyu, kamar كِتَابُ مُحَمَّدٍ, littafin Muhammadu. Za ka tambaya كِتَابُ مَنْ هٰذَا, littafin wane ne wannan. Za ka koyi تَحْتَ, a ƙarƙashin, da yadda ake kiran mutum da يَا.", "kitaabu muḥammadin": "kitaabu muḥammadin", "Put two nouns together to show whose something is:": "Haɗa sunaye biyu don nuna wanda yake da abu:", "first, then": "na farko, sannan", "the owner": "mai shi", ". Arabic says “book Muhammad”.": ". Larabci yana cewa “littafi Muhammadu”, kamar yadda Hausa ke cewa littafin Muhammadu.", "Hamid's pen": "alƙalamin Hamid", "the principal's car": "motar shugaban makarantar", "the two endings": "ƙarshe biyun", "How the endings change": "Yadda ƙarshen kalmomi ke canzawa", "The": "Ita", "first word": "kalma ta farko", "never has": "ba ta taɓa samun", "or -un:": "ko -un:", ". The": ". Ita", "second word": "kalma ta biyu", "ends in -i (or -in):": "tana ƙarewa da -i ko -in:", "1st: no الْ, no -un": "Ta 1: babu الْ, babu -un", "2nd: ends in -i": "Ta 2: tana ƙarewa da -i", "the teacher's book": "littafin malamin", "the door of the mosque": "ƙofar masallacin", "the teacher's bag": "jakar malamin", "baytullaahi": "baytullaahi", "the House of Allah": "Ɗakin Allah", "The Kaaba is the House of Allah.": "Ka'aba ita ce Ɗakin Allah.", "The Qur'an is the Book of Allah.": "Alƙur'ani shi ne Littafin Allah.", "Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.": "Muhammadu shi ne Manzon Allah.", "kitaabu man haadhaa?": "kitaabu man haadhaa?", "Whose book is this?": "Littafin wane ne wannan?", "where the owner goes to ask “whose?”.": "a wurin mai abin don tambayar “na wane ne?”.", "Whose pen is this?": "Alƙalamin wane ne wannan?", "This is the teacher's pen.": "Wannan alƙalamin malamin ne.", "Whose son are you?": "Kai ɗan wane ne?", "I am the teacher's son.": "Ni ɗan malamin ne.", "taḥta": "taḥta", "under": "a ƙarƙashin", "hunaaka": "hunaaka", "there": "can", "changes the next word's ending to -i, like": "yana canza ƙarshen kalmar da ke biye zuwa -i, kamar", "The bag is under the desk.": "Jakar tana ƙarƙashin teburin.", "The dog is under the car.": "Karen yana ƙarƙashin motar.", "It is on the desk over there.": "Yana kan teburin can.", "yaa muḥammadu": "yaa muḥammadu", "O Muhammad! (calling)": "Ya Muhammadu! Wato kira", "and the name with a single damma (no -un):": "da sunan da damma ɗaya, ba tare da -un ba:", "O Muhammad!": "Ya Muhammadu!", "O teacher!": "Ya malam!", "O Khalid!": "Ya Khalid!", "O boy!": "Ya yaro!", "ismun": "ismun", "ibnun": "ibnun", "The hamza you don't always say": "Hamzar da ba a koyaushe ake faɗa ba", "is only read at the start. In the middle it is silent:": "ana karanta shi ne a farko kawai. A tsakiya ba a karanta shi:", "wasmu": "wasmu", "wabnu": "wabnu", "The boy's name is Muhammad and the girl's name is Zaynab.": "Sunan yaron Muhammadu ne kuma sunan yarinyar Zainab ne.", "Khalid's son is at school and Hamid's son is at university.": "Ɗan Khalid yana makaranta kuma ɗan Hamid yana jami'a.", "the Messenger": "Manzon", "the Kaaba": "Ka'aba", "the name": "sunan", "the son": "ɗan", "the daughter, the girl": "'yar, yarinyar", "the uncle (father's brother)": "baffan, wato ɗan'uwan uba", "the uncle (mother's brother)": "kawun, wato ɗan'uwan uwa", "the engineer": "injiniyan", "New words: words 1": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomi 1", "ar-rasuulu": "ar-rasuulu", "al-ka'batu": "al-ka'batu", "al-ismu": "al-ismu", "al-ibnu": "al-ibnu", "al-bintu": "al-bintu", "al-'ammu": "al-'ammu", "al-khaalu": "al-khaalu", "al-muhandisu": "al-muhandisu", "the bag": "jakar", "the car": "motar", "the street": "titin", "closed": "rufaffe", "the teacher (ustadh)": "malamin, wato ustaz", "New words: words 2": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomi 2", "al-ḥaqeebatu": "al-ḥaqeebatu", "as-sayyaaratu": "as-sayyaaratu", "ash-shaari'u": "ash-shaari'u", "mughlaqun": "mughlaqun", "al-ustaadhu": "al-ustaadhu", "O … (calling someone)": "Ya … wato kiran mutum", "Allah": "Allah", "Is this Muhammad's book, Yasir?": "Shin wannan littafin Muhammadu ne, Yasir?", "No, this is Hamid's book.": "A'a, wannan littafin Hamid ne.", "Whose pen is this, Ali?": "Alƙalamin wane ne wannan, Ali?", "Where is the teacher's bag? It is under the desk.": "Ina jakar malamin take? Tana ƙarƙashin teburin.", "The mosque door is open and the school door is closed.": "Ƙofar masallacin a buɗe take kuma ƙofar makarantar a rufe take.", "Abbas's car is in the street.": "Motar Abbas tana cikin titin.", "First word: no": "Kalma ta farko: babu", ", no -un. Second word: ends in -i.": ", babu -un. Kalma ta biyu: tana ƙarewa da -i.", "How do you say “the doctor's daughter”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'yar likitan”?", "Second word: ends in": "Kalma ta biyu: tana ƙarewa da", "How do you say “the car key”?": "Yaya ake cewa “mabuɗin motar”?", "How do you say “the principal's desk”?": "Yaya ake cewa “teburin shugaban makarantar”?", "How do you say “the teacher's car”?": "Yaya ake cewa “motar malamin”?", "How do you say “the teacher's bag”?": "Yaya ake cewa “jakar malamin”?", "How do you say “Ali's house”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gidan Ali”?", "How do you say “the engineer's son”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗan injiniyan”?", "How do you say “the merchant's shop”?": "Yaya ake cewa “shagon ɗan kasuwar”?", "Each phrase has one mistake. Choose the correct one.": "Kowace kalma tana da kuskure ɗaya. Zaɓi wadda ta yi daidai.", "Correct the mistake": "Gyara kuskuren", "This is wrong. What is correct?": "Wannan ba daidai ba ne. Mene ne daidai?", "Choose the meaning.": "Zaɓi ma'anar.", "the boy's name": "sunan yaron", "the doctor's daughter": "'yar likitan", "the principal's son": "ɗan shugaban makarantar", "the engineer's car": "motar injiniyan", "the car door": "ƙofar motar", "the Book of Allah": "Littafin Allah", "the student's uncle (father's brother)": "baffan ɗalibin, wato ɗan'uwan uba", "Hamid's uncle (mother's brother)": "kawun Hamid, wato ɗan'uwan uwa", "the Messenger of Allah": "Manzon Allah", "Calling someone with": "Kiran mutum da", "+ the name with a single damma.": "tare da sunan da damma ɗaya.", "Call the doctor.": "Kira likitan.", "plus the name with a single": "tare da sunan da", "Call the teacher.": "Kira malamin.", "Call the boy.": "Kira yaron.", "Call Yasir.": "Kira Yasir.", "Call Ammar.": "Kira Ammar.", "Call the man.": "Kira mutumin.", "Read the English, then choose the answer.": "Karanta Turancin, sannan ka zaɓi amsar.", "“The book is on the desk.”": "“Littafin yana kan teburin.”", "“The cat is under the bed.”": "“Magen tana ƙarƙashin gadon.”", "“The watch is under the book.”": "“Agogon yana ƙarƙashin littafin.”", "“The dog is under the car.”": "“Karen yana ƙarƙashin motar.”", "“The bag is under the desk.”": "“Jakar tana ƙarƙashin teburin.”", "“The car is in the street.”": "“Motar tana cikin titin.”", "Listen, then write the word. (O … (calling someone))": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato Ya …, kiran mutum.", "Calling someone with يَا": "Kiran mutum da يَا", "Call the shaykh.": "Kira shehin.", "How do you say “Hamid's pen”?": "Yaya ake cewa “alƙalamin Hamid”?", "✅ How do you say “the engineer's son”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗan injiniyan”?", "✅ This is wrong. What is correct?": "✅ Wannan ba daidai ba ne. Mene ne daidai?", "✅ What does this mean?": "✅ Mece ce ma'anar wannan?", "✅ Write: O … (calling someone)": "✅ Rubuta: Ya …, kiran mutum", "✅ This is the teacher's pen.": "✅ Wannan alƙalamin malamin ne.", "✅ Call the shaykh.": "✅ Kira shehin.", "✅ The Kaaba is the House of Allah.": "✅ Ka'aba ita ce Ɗakin Allah.", "✅ “The bag is under the desk.”": "✅ “Jakar tana ƙarƙashin teburin.”", "✅ How do you say “Hamid's pen”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “alƙalamin Hamid”?", "✅ Call the man.": "✅ Kira mutumin.", "which means this, for feminine words. You will see how": "wanda ma'anarsa wannan, don kalmomin mace. Za ka ga yadda", "makes a word feminine, like": "ke mayar da kalma ta mace, kamar", "and learn the feminine words that have no": "kuma za ka koyi kalmomin mace waɗanda ba su da", "You will also ask": "Za ka kuma tambaya", "whose is this, and learn many words for things and the body.": "na wane ne wannan, ka koyi kalmomi da yawa na abubuwa da na jiki.", "for masculine words, and": "don kalmomin namiji, da", "for feminine words.": "don kalmomin mace.", "Most feminine words end in": "Yawancin kalmomin mace suna ƙarewa da", "Add it to make a word feminine:": "Ƙara shi don mayar da kalma ta mace:", "a male student, becomes": "wato ɗalibi namiji, ya zama", "a female student.": "wato ɗaliba mace.", "Some words are feminine without": "Wasu kalmomi na mace ne ba tare da", "mother, and parts of the body that come in pairs, like ear, eye, hand and foot. But nose and mouth are masculine.": "wato uwa, da sassan jiki da ke zuwa biyu-biyu, kamar kunne, ido, hannu da ƙafa. Amma hanci da baki na namiji ne.", "When the thing is feminine, the describing word also gets": "Idan abin na mace ne, kalmar siffantawa ma tana samun", "means for, or belongs to. The name after it ends in a": "ma'anarsa na, ko mallakar wani. Sunan da ke bayansa yana ƙarewa da", "it is Khalid's.": "na Khalid ne.", "plus": "tare da", "makes a question:": "yana yin tambaya:", "is she?": "shin ita ce?", "means also.": "ma'anarsa kuma, ko shi ma.", "This (feminine)": "Wannan, na mace", "This (m or f)?": "Wannan, namiji ko mace?", "Make it feminine": "Mayar da shi na mace", "In this lesson you will learn هٰذِهِ, which means this, for feminine words. You will see how تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ makes a word feminine, like طَالِبٌ and طَالِبَةٌ, and learn the feminine words that have no تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ. You will also ask لِمَنْ هٰذِهِ, whose is this, and learn many words for things and the body.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi هٰذِهِ, wanda ma'anarsa wannan, don kalmomin mace. Za ka ga yadda تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ ke mayar da kalma ta mace, kamar طَالِبٌ da طَالِبَةٌ, kuma za ka koyi kalmomin mace waɗanda ba su da تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ. Za ka kuma tambaya لِمَنْ هٰذِهِ, na wane ne wannan, ka koyi kalmomi da yawa na abubuwa da na jiki.", "haadhihi": "haadhihi", "this (feminine)": "wannan, na mace", "for masculine words and": "don kalmomin namiji da", "masculine": "namiji, wato muzakkari", "feminine": "mace, wato mu'annasi", "This is Hamid's son and this is Yasir's daughter.": "Wannan ɗan Hamid ne kuma wannan 'yar Yasir ce.", "What is this? This is an iron.": "Mene ne wannan? Wannan dutsen guga ne.", "Whose car is this?": "Motar wane ne wannan?", "-atun": "-atun", "taa marbuutah: a feminine word": "taa marbuutah: alamar kalmar mace", ". Add": ". Ƙara", "to make a word feminine:": "don mayar da kalma ta mace:", "(a male student) →": "wato ɗalibi namiji →", "(a female student).": "wato ɗaliba mace.", "a student (m) → a student (f)": "ɗalibi namiji → ɗaliba mace", "an engineer (m → f)": "injiniya namiji → mace", "a doctor (m → f)": "likita namiji → mace", "no ة, but feminine": "babu ة, amma ta mace ce", "Feminine words without ة": "Kalmomin mace da ba su da ة", "Some words are feminine with no": "Wasu kalmomi na mace ne ba tare da", "(mother), and parts of the body that come in pairs:": "wato uwa, da sassan jiki da ke zuwa biyu-biyu:", ". But": ". Amma", "are masculine.": "na namiji ne.", "This is an ear and this is an eye.": "Wannan kunne ne kuma wannan ido ne.", "And this is a hand and this is a foot.": "Kuma wannan hannu ne kuma wannan ƙafa ce.", "This is a nose and this is a mouth.": "Wannan hanci ne kuma wannan baki ne.", "This is Yasir's mother.": "Wannan mahaifiyar Yasir ce.", "hiya jameelatun": "hiya jameelatun", "The describing word becomes feminine too": "Kalmar siffantawa ma tana zama ta mace", "When the thing is feminine, the describing word gets": "Idan abin na mace ne, kalmar siffantawa tana samun", "too.": "ita ma.", "Hamid's son is sitting and Yasir's daughter is standing.": "Ɗan Hamid yana zaune kuma 'yar Yasir tana tsaye.", "This is Ali's watch. It is very beautiful.": "Wannan agogon Ali ne. Yana da kyau sosai.", "This is Ammar's bicycle. This one is new.": "Wannan keken Ammar ne. Wannan sabo ne.", "liman haadhihi?": "liman haadhihi?", "Whose is this?": "Na wane ne wannan?", "for / belongs to": "na, ko mallakar", ", and the name ends in -i:": ", kuma sunan yana ƙarewa da -i:", "(Khalid's).": "wato na Khalid.", "Whose is this? This is Khalid's.": "Na wane ne wannan? Wannan na Khalid ne.", "Whose is this? This is Yasir's.": "Na wane ne wannan? Wannan na Yasir ne.", "a-hiya…?": "a-hiya…?", "Is she…?": "Shin ita ce…?", "ayḍan": "ayḍan", "also": "kuma, shi ma", "makes a question.": "yana yin tambaya.", "Who is this? This is the engineer's sister.": "Wace ce wannan? Wannan 'yar'uwar injiniyan ce.", "Is she also an engineer?": "Shin ita ma injiniya ce?", "No, she is a doctor.": "A'a, ita likita ce.", "an iron": "dutsen guga", "a bicycle": "keke", "a spoon": "cokali", "a pot": "tukunya", "a fridge": "firji", "a window": "taga", "tea": "shayi", "coffee": "kofi", "a cow": "saniya", "a hen": "kaza", "mikwaatun": "mikwaatun", "darraajatun": "darraajatun", "mil'aqatun": "mil'aqatun", "qidrun": "qidrun", "thallaajatun": "thallaajatun", "naafidhatun": "naafidhatun", "shaayun": "shaayun", "qahwatun": "qahwatun", "baqaratun": "baqaratun", "dajaajatun": "dajaajatun", "a nose": "hanci", "a mouth": "baki", "an ear": "kunne", "an eye": "ido", "a hand": "hannu", "a foot, a leg": "ƙafa", "New words: the body": "Sababbin kalmomi: jiki", "anfun": "anfun", "famun": "famun", "udhunun": "udhunun", "'aynun": "'aynun", "yadun": "yadun", "rijlun": "rijlun", "a mother": "uwa", "a sister": "'yar'uwa", "a farmer": "manomi", "fast": "mai sauri", "ummun": "ummun", "ukhtun": "ukhtun", "fallaaḥun": "fallaaḥun", "saree'un": "saree'un", "very": "sosai", "whose? (for whom?)": "na wane? Wato mallakar wa?", "Is she also an engineer? No, she is a doctor.": "Shin ita ma injiniya ce? A'a, ita likita ce.", "Whose car is this? This is the principal's car.": "Motar wane ne wannan? Wannan motar shugaban makarantar ce.", "This is a spoon and this is a pot.": "Wannan cokali ne kuma wannan tukunya ce.", "This is the farmer's cow.": "Wannan saniyar manomin ce.", "Masculine: use": "Namiji: yi amfani da", "Masculine →": "Namiji →", ". Feminine →": ". Mace →", "Choose the right sentence.": "Zaɓi jumlar da ta dace.", "Feminine: use": "Mace: yi amfani da", "Read the first sentence, then complete the second one.": "Karanta jumla ta farko, sannan ka cika ta biyu.", "Now say the same about": "Yanzu ka faɗi haka game da", "+ the name ending in -i.": "tare da sunan da ke ƙarewa da -i.", "It is Khalid's.": "Na Khalid ne.", "plus the name ending in": "tare da sunan da ke ƙarewa da", "It is Hamid's.": "Na Hamid ne.", "It is Yasir's.": "Na Yasir ne.", "It is Muhammad's.": "Na Muhammadu ne.", "It is Sa'eed's.": "Na Sa'idu ne.", "Each sentence has one mistake. Choose the correct one.": "Kowace jumla tana da kuskure ɗaya. Zaɓi wadda ta yi daidai.", "This is Yasir's daughter.": "Wannan 'yar Yasir ce.", "Listen, then write the word. (a mouth)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato baki.", "هٰذَا or هٰذِهِ?": "هٰذَا ko هٰذِهِ?", "This is the principal's car.": "Wannan motar shugaban makarantar ce.", "✅ Write: a mouth": "✅ Rubuta: baki", "✅ It is Khalid's.": "✅ Na Khalid ne.", "✅ Choose the right sentence.": "✅ Zaɓi jumlar da ta dace.", "✅ This is Yasir's daughter.": "✅ Wannan 'yar Yasir ce.", "✅ It is Muhammad's.": "✅ Na Muhammadu ne.", "✅ This is the principal's car.": "✅ Wannan motar shugaban makarantar ce.", "which means that, for feminine words far away. Then you will know all four pointing words:": "wanda ma'anarsa waccan, don kalmomin mace da ke nesa. Sannan za ka san dukan kalmomin nuni huɗu:", "for near,": "don kusa,", "for far.": "don nesa.", "means that, for a feminine person or thing that is far away.": "ma'anarsa waccan, don mutum ko abu na mace da ke nesa.", "Both mean that, for something far.": "Dukansu ma'anarsu wancan ko waccan, don abin da ke nesa.", "Near:": "Kusa:", "for feminine. Far:": "don mace. Nesa:", "for a yes or no question.": "don tambayar i ko a'a.", "That (feminine)": "Waccan, na mace", "Which pointing word?": "Wace kalmar nuni?", "ذٰلِكَ or تِلْكَ?": "ذٰلِكَ ko تِلْكَ?", "In this lesson you will learn تِلْكَ, which means that, for feminine words far away. Then you will know all four pointing words: هٰذَا and هٰذِهِ for near, ذٰلِكَ and تِلْكَ for far.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi تِلْكَ, wanda ma'anarsa waccan, don kalmomin mace da ke nesa. Sannan za ka san dukan kalmomin nuni huɗu: هٰذَا da هٰذِهِ don kusa, ذٰلِكَ da تِلْكَ don nesa.", "tilka": "tilka", "that (feminine)": "waccan, na mace", "for a feminine person or thing that is": "don mutum ko abu na mace da ke", "away.": ".", "Who is this? This is Aminah.": "Wace ce wannan? Wannan Aminatu ce.", "And who is that? That is Fatimah.": "Kuma wace ce waccan? Waccan Faɗimatu ce.", "What is that? That is an egg.": "Mene ne waccan? Waccan ƙwai ne.", "that (m)": "wancan, namiji", "that (f)": "waccan, mace", "Both mean": "Dukansu ma'anarsu", "(far).": "wato na nesa.", "That is a rooster and that is a hen.": "Wancan zakara ne kuma waccan kaza ce.", "This is a camel and that is a she-camel.": "Wannan raƙumi ne kuma waccan taguwa ce.", "This is a dog and that is a cat.": "Wannan kare ne kuma waccan mage ce.", "the four pointing words": "kalmomin nuni huɗu", "near and far, masculine and feminine": "kusa da nesa, namiji da mace", "Far:": "Nesa:", "near (m": "kusa, namiji", "far (m": "nesa, namiji", "This is Muhammad.": "Wannan Muhammadu ne.", "This is Aminah.": "Wannan Aminatu ce.", "That is Hamid.": "Wancan Hamid ne.", "That is Zaynab.": "Waccan Zainab ce.", "a-tilka…?": "a-tilka…?", "Is that (f)…?": "Shin waccan…? Na mace", "Is that a hen?": "Shin waccan kaza ce?", "No, that is a duck.": "A'a, waccan agwagwa ce.", "Is this Abbas's watch?": "Shin wannan agogon Abbas ne?", "No, this is Hamid's watch. That is Abbas's watch.": "A'a, wannan agogon Hamid ne. Wancan agogon Abbas ne.", "a nurse (f)": "ma'aikaciyar jinya", "a muezzin (who calls the adhan)": "ladan, wato mai kiran sallah", "a garden": "lambu", "a duck": "agwagwa", "a she-camel": "taguwa", "an egg": "ƙwai", "mumarriḍatun": "mumarriḍatun", "mu'adhdhinun": "mu'adhdhinun", "ḥadeeqatun": "ḥadeeqatun", "baṭṭatun": "baṭṭatun", "naaqatun": "naaqatun", "bayḍatun": "bayḍatun", "that (masculine)": "wancan, na namiji", "This is a doctor and that is a nurse.": "Wannan likita ne kuma waccan ma'aikaciyar jinya ce.", "Is that a hen? No, that is a duck.": "Shin waccan kaza ce? A'a, waccan agwagwa ce.", "This is the teacher's car and that is the principal's car.": "Wannan motar malamin ce kuma waccan motar shugaban makarantar ce.", "Near or far? Masculine or feminine?": "Kusa ko nesa? Namiji ko mace?", ". Choose the right sentence.": ". Zaɓi jumlar da ta dace.", "Point far away:": "Nuni zuwa nesa:", ". Feminine: use": ". Mace: yi amfani da", "It is far away. Which word do you use?": "Yana nesa. Wace kalma za ka yi amfani da ita?", "“This is the teacher's car and that is the principal's car.”": "“Wannan motar malamin ce kuma waccan motar shugaban makarantar ce.”", "“This is a camel and that is a she-camel.”": "“Wannan raƙumi ne kuma waccan taguwa ce.”", "“This is the muezzin's house and that is the merchant's garden.”": "“Wannan gidan ladan ne kuma waccan lambun ɗan kasuwar ne.”", "“That is a rooster and that is a hen.”": "“Wancan zakara ne kuma waccan kaza ce.”", "“That is a donkey and that is a cow.”": "“Wancan jaki ne kuma waccan saniya ce.”", "“This is a dog and that is a cat.”": "“Wannan kare ne kuma waccan mage ce.”", "What is that? (f)": "Mene ne waccan? Na mace", "Who is that? (f)": "Wace ce waccan? Na mace", "That is an egg.": "Waccan ƙwai ne.", "What is this? (f)": "Mene ne wannan? Na mace", "That is Fatimah.": "Waccan Faɗimatu ce.", "Who is this? (f)": "Wace ce wannan? Na mace", "This is a school and that is a university.": "Wannan makaranta ce kuma waccan jami'a ce.", "Point far away: ذٰلِكَ or تِلْكَ?": "Nuni zuwa nesa: ذٰلِكَ ko تِلْكَ?", "Listen, then write the word. (a duck)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato agwagwa.", "✅ This is a school and that is a university.": "✅ Wannan makaranta ce kuma waccan jami'a ce.", "✅ It is far away. Which word do you use?": "✅ Yana nesa. Wace kalma za ka yi amfani da ita?", "✅ “This is a dog and that is a cat.”": "✅ “Wannan kare ne kuma waccan mage ce.”", "✅ That is a rooster and that is a hen.": "✅ Wancan zakara ne kuma waccan kaza ce.", "✅ Write: a duck": "✅ Rubuta: agwagwa", "✅ “This is the teacher's car and that is the principal's car.”": "✅ “Wannan motar malamin ce kuma waccan motar shugaban makarantar ce.”", "In this lesson you will learn the difference between": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi bambanci tsakanin", "this is a man, and": "wannan namiji ne, da", "this man. You will say that something belongs to someone with": "wannan mutumin. Za ka faɗi cewa abu mallakar wani ne da", "learn": "za ka koyi", "in front of, and": "a gaban, da", "behind, and the names of some countries.": "a bayan, da sunayen wasu ƙasashe.", "Without": "Ba tare da", "it is a full sentence: this is a man. With": "jumla ce cikakkiya: wannan namiji ne. Da", "it is only a part: this man.": "wani sashe ne kawai: wannan mutumin.", "It works the same way with": "Haka yake da", "When": "Idan", "comes before": "ya zo kafin", "the alif drops:": "alif ɗin yana faɗuwa:", "it belongs to the merchant.": "mallakar ɗan kasuwar ne.", "means in front of.": "ma'anarsa a gaban.", "means behind. Like": "ma'anarsa a bayan. Kamar", "they change the next ending to a": "suna canza ƙarshen kalmar da ke biye zuwa", "Names like America, Germany and France, and the word": "Sunaye kamar Amurka, Jamus da Faransa, da kalmar", "end in a long vowel, so their ending never changes.": "suna ƙarewa da dogon wasali, don haka ƙarshensu ba ya canzawa.", "This man": "Wannan mutumin", "A man or this man?": "Wani mutum ko wannan mutumin?", "In front, behind": "A gaba, a baya", "In this lesson you will learn the difference between هٰذَا رَجُلٌ, this is a man, and هٰذَا الرَّجُلُ, this man. You will say that something belongs to someone with لِ, learn أَمَامَ, in front of, and خَلْفَ, behind, and the names of some countries.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi bambanci tsakanin هٰذَا رَجُلٌ, wannan namiji ne, da هٰذَا الرَّجُلُ, wannan mutumin. Za ka faɗi cewa abu mallakar wani ne da لِ, za ka koyi أَمَامَ, a gaban, da خَلْفَ, a bayan, da sunayen wasu ƙasashe.", "haadhaa rajulun": "haadhaa rajulun", "This is a man.": "Wannan namiji ne.", "haadhaa ar-rajulu": "haadhaa ar-rajulu", "this man": "wannan mutumin", "it is a full sentence:": "jumla ce cikakkiya:", "With": "Da", "it is only part of a sentence:": "wani sashe ne kawai na jumla:", "this man …": "wannan mutumin …", "This man is a merchant.": "Wannan mutumin ɗan kasuwa ne.", "And that man is a doctor.": "Kuma wancan mutumin likita ne.", "haadhihis-sayyaaratu": "haadhihis-sayyaaratu", "this car": "wannan motar", "The same with": "Haka ma da", "This car is from Japan.": "Wannan motar daga Japan take.", "And that car is from America.": "Kuma waccan motar daga Amurka take.", "This book is new and that book is old.": "Wannan littafin sabo ne kuma wancan littafin tsoho ne.", "li + al = lil": "li da al suna zama lil", "belongs to the …": "mallakar …", ", the alif drops:": ", alif ɗin yana faɗuwa:", "(the merchant's).": "wato na ɗan kasuwar.", "This house belongs to the merchant.": "Wannan gidan mallakar ɗan kasuwar ne.", "And that house belongs to the doctor.": "Kuma wancan gidan mallakar likitan ne.", "Whose is this car?": "Wannan motar ta wane ce?", "This car belongs to the doctor.": "Wannan motar mallakar likitan ce.", "amaama": "amaama", "in front of": "a gaban", "khalfa": "khalfa", "behind": "a bayan", "Like": "Kamar", ", they change the next word's ending to -i.": ", suna canza ƙarshen kalmar da ke biye zuwa -i.", "The merchant's house is in front of the mosque.": "Gidan ɗan kasuwar yana gaban masallacin.", "And the doctor's house is behind the school.": "Kuma gidan likitan yana bayan makarantar.", "The blackboard is in front of the student.": "Allon rubutun yana gaban ɗalibin.", "fee amreekaa": "fee amreekaa", "Words that never change": "Kalmomin da ba sa canzawa", "Names like": "Sunaye kamar", "and the word": "da kalmar", "end in a long vowel, so their ending never changes:": "suna ƙarewa da dogon wasali, don haka ƙarshensu ba ya canzawa:", "in America": "a Amurka", "from Germany": "daga Jamus", "to France": "zuwa Faransa", "Mahmud is sick. He is in the hospital now.": "Mahmud ba shi da lafiya. Yana asibitin yanzu.", "the hospital": "asibitin", "the blackboard": "allon rubutun", "the mihrab (prayer niche)": "mihirabin, wato wurin limami a masallaci", "the knife": "wuƙar", "al-mustashfaa": "al-mustashfaa", "as-sabbuuratu": "as-sabbuuratu", "al-miḥraabu": "al-miḥraabu", "as-sikkeenu": "as-sikkeenu", "America": "Amurka", "Germany": "Jamus", "England": "Ingila", "Switzerland": "Suwizalan", "France": "Faransa", "New words: countries": "Sababbin kalmomi: ƙasashe", "amreekaa": "amreekaa", "almaaniyaa": "almaaniyaa", "inkiltaraa": "inkiltaraa", "suweesraa": "suweesraa", "faransaa": "faransaa", "he sat": "ya zauna", "now": "yanzu", "This man is a merchant and that man is a doctor.": "Wannan mutumin ɗan kasuwa ne kuma wancan mutumin likita ne.", "The merchant's name is Mahmud and the doctor's name is Sa'eed.": "Sunan ɗan kasuwar Mahmud ne kuma sunan likitan Sa'idu ne.", "This house belongs to the merchant and that house belongs to the doctor.": "Wannan gidan mallakar ɗan kasuwar ne kuma wancan gidan mallakar likitan ne.", "The merchant's house is in front of the mosque and the doctor's house is behind the school.": "Gidan ɗan kasuwar yana gaban masallacin kuma gidan likitan yana bayan makarantar.", "Whose is this car and whose is that one?": "Wannan motar ta wane ce kuma waccan ta wane ce?", "This car is from Japan and that one is from America.": "Wannan motar daga Japan take kuma waccan daga Amurka take.", "Read the English, then choose the Arabic.": "Karanta Turancin, sannan ka zaɓi Larabcin.", "“That book is old.”": "“Wancan littafin tsoho ne.”", "“This boy is Khalid.”": "“Wannan yaron Khalid ne.”", "“This man is a merchant.”": "“Wannan mutumin ɗan kasuwa ne.”", "“This is a man.”": "“Wannan namiji ne.”", "“That man is a doctor.”": "“Wancan mutumin likita ne.”", "“This is a door.”": "“Wannan ƙofa ce.”", "“This door is open.”": "“Wannan ƙofar a buɗe take.”", "“This car is from Japan.”": "“Wannan motar daga Japan take.”", "plus a name ending in -i. Before": "tare da suna mai ƙarewa da -i. A gaban", "it becomes": "yana zama", "It belongs to the doctor.": "Mallakar likitan ne.", "plus a name ending in": "tare da suna mai ƙarewa da", "It belongs to Ammar.": "Mallakar Ammar ne.", "It belongs to the principal.": "Mallakar shugaban makarantar ne.", "It belongs to the student.": "Mallakar ɗalibin ne.", "It belongs to Abbas.": "Mallakar Abbas ne.", "It belongs to the teacher.": "Mallakar malamin ne.", "“The doctor's house is behind the school.”": "“Gidan likitan yana bayan makarantar.”", "“The teacher's car is in front of the school.”": "“Motar malamin tana gaban makarantar.”", "“The blackboard is in front of the student.”": "“Allon rubutun yana gaban ɗalibin.”", "“The imam's house is behind the mosque.”": "“Gidan limamin yana bayan masallacin.”", "“The blackboard is behind the teacher.”": "“Allon rubutun yana bayan malamin.”", "“Ammar sat in front of the mihrab.”": "“Ammar ya zauna a gaban mihirabin.”", "Where is it from?": "Daga ina yake?", "The spoon is from Japan.": "Cokalin daga Japan yake.", "The doctor is from Switzerland.": "Likitan daga Suwizalan yake.", "The engineer is from England.": "Injiniyan daga Ingila yake.", "The knife is from Germany.": "Wuƙar daga Jamus take.", "The watch is from America.": "Agogon daga Amurka yake.", "He is in the hospital now.": "Yana asibitin yanzu.", "هٰذَا رَجُلٌ or هٰذَا الرَّجُلُ?": "هٰذَا رَجُلٌ ko هٰذَا الرَّجُلُ?", "The car is from France.": "Motar daga Faransa take.", "Listen, then write the word. (France)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato Faransa.", "The imam's house is behind the mosque.": "Gidan limamin yana bayan masallacin.", "“This book is new.”": "“Wannan littafin sabo ne.”", "✅ “This car is from Japan.”": "✅ “Wannan motar daga Japan take.”", "✅ The car is from France.": "✅ Motar daga Faransa take.", "✅ “The imam's house is behind the mosque.”": "✅ “Gidan limamin yana bayan masallacin.”", "✅ “The blackboard is in front of the student.”": "✅ “Allon rubutun yana gaban ɗalibin.”", "✅ Write: France": "✅ Rubuta: Faransa", "✅ The imam's house is behind the mosque.": "✅ Gidan limamin yana bayan masallacin.", "✅ It belongs to Abbas.": "✅ Mallakar Abbas ne.", "✅ It belongs to the teacher.": "✅ Mallakar malamin ne.", "✅ The spoon is from Japan.": "✅ Cokalin daga Japan yake.", "✅ Whose is this car?": "✅ Wannan motar ta wane ce?", "✅ “This book is new.”": "✅ “Wannan littafin sabo ne.”", "In this lesson you will put a describing word after a noun, like": "A wannan darasi za ka sanya kalmar siffantawa bayan suna, kamar", "a rich merchant, and": "wani ɗan kasuwa mawadaci, da", "the new teacher. The describing word copies the noun: masculine or feminine, with": "sabon malamin. Kalmar siffantawa tana bin sunan: namiji ko mace, da", "or without. You will also learn": "ko ba tare da shi ba. Za ka kuma koyi", "who or which,": "wanda ko wadda,", "with or at, and words like hungry, thirsty and angry.": "tare da, ko a wurin, da kalmomi kamar mai yunwa, mai ƙishirwa da mai fushi.", "A describing word can come after a noun. It copies the noun's ending.": "Kalmar siffantawa, wato na'at, tana iya zuwa bayan suna. Tana bin ƙarshen sunan.", "a rich merchant.": "wani ɗan kasuwa mawadaci.", "If the noun is feminine, the describing word also gets": "Idan sunan na mace ne, kalmar siffantawa ma tana samun", "If the noun has": "Idan sunan yana da", "the describing word also gets": "kalmar siffantawa ma tana samun", "on the describing word, it is a full sentence: the teacher is new. With": "a kan kalmar siffantawa, jumla ce cikakkiya: malamin sabo ne. Da", "it is only a part: the new teacher.": "wani sashe ne kawai: sabon malamin.", "means who or which. It joins extra information to a masculine word: the man who went out.": "ma'anarsa wanda ko wadda. Yana haɗa ƙarin bayani da kalmar namiji: mutumin da ya fita.", "Words like": "Kalmomi kamar", "never take": "ba sa taɓa samun", "They end in one": "Suna ƙarewa da", "A rich merchant": "Ɗan kasuwa mawadaci", "Copy the noun": "Bi sunan", "Sentence or phrase?": "Jumla ko sashe?", "Fill the gap": "Cika gurbin", "In this lesson you will put a describing word after a noun, like تَاجِرٌ غَنِيٌّ, a rich merchant, and الْمُدَرِّسُ الْجَدِيدُ, the new teacher. The describing word copies the noun: masculine or feminine, with الْ or without. You will also learn الَّذِي, who or which, عِنْدَ, with or at, and words like hungry, thirsty and angry.": "A wannan darasi za ka sanya kalmar siffantawa bayan suna, kamar تَاجِرٌ غَنِيٌّ, wani ɗan kasuwa mawadaci, da الْمُدَرِّسُ الْجَدِيدُ, sabon malamin. Kalmar siffantawa tana bin sunan: namiji ko mace, da الْ ko ba tare da shi ba. Za ka kuma koyi الَّذِي, wanda ko wadda, عِنْدَ, tare da ko a wurin, da kalmomi kamar mai yunwa, mai ƙishirwa da mai fushi.", "taajirun ghaniyyun": "taajirun ghaniyyun", "a rich merchant": "wani ɗan kasuwa mawadaci", "A describing word can come": "Kalmar siffantawa tana iya zuwa", "after": "bayan", "a noun. It copies the noun's ending: both end in": "suna. Tana bin ƙarshen sunan: dukansu suna ƙarewa da", "Abbas is a rich merchant.": "Abbas ɗan kasuwa ne mawadaci.", "Hamid is a new teacher.": "Hamid sabon malami ne.", "The sparrow is a small bird.": "Gwara ƙaramin tsuntsu ne.", "lughatun sahlatun": "lughatun sahlatun", "an easy language": "wani harshe mai sauƙi", "If the noun is feminine, the describing word gets": "Idan sunan na mace ne, kalmar siffantawa tana samun", "Arabic is an easy language.": "Larabci harshe ne mai sauƙi.", "Apples are a delicious fruit.": "Tuffa 'ya'yan itace ne masu daɗi.", "Cairo is a big city.": "Alƙahira babban birni ce.", "al-mudarrisu al-jadeedu": "al-mudarrisu al-jadeedu", "the new teacher": "sabon malamin", ", the describing word gets": ", kalmar siffantawa tana samun", "Where is the new teacher?": "Ina sabon malamin yake?", "He is with the principal.": "Yana wurin shugaban makarantar.", "Where is the small spoon? It is in the glass.": "Ina ƙaramin cokalin yake? Yana cikin kofin.", "al-mudarrisu jadeedun": "al-mudarrisu jadeedun", "The teacher is new.": "Malamin sabo ne.", "on the describing word, it is a sentence:": "a kan kalmar siffantawa, jumla ce:", "it is only": "sashe ne kawai", "the new teacher …": "sabon malamin …", "The book is big.": "Littafin babba ne.", "the big book …": "babban littafin …", "Whose is this big book?": "Wannan babban littafin na wane ne?", "alladhee": "alladhee", "who, which": "wanda, wadda", "joins extra information to a masculine word:": "yana haɗa ƙarin bayani da kalmar namiji:", "(the man": "wato mutumin", "went out).": "ya fita.", "Who is that tall man who just went out of the school?": "Wane ne wannan dogon mutumin da ya fita daga makarantar yanzu?", "He is the new principal.": "Shi ne sabon shugaban makarantar.", "The book which is on the desk is the teacher's.": "Littafin da ke kan teburin na malamin ne.", "jaw'aanu": "jaw'aanu", "hungry": "mai yunwa", "'aṭshaanu": "'aṭshaanu", "thirsty": "mai ƙishirwa", "Words ending in": "Kalmomin da ke ƙarewa da", "never take -un. They end in a single damma.": "ba sa taɓa samun -un. Suna ƙarewa da damma ɗaya.", "I am hungry.": "Ina jin yunwa.", "Are you hungry? No, I am thirsty.": "Kana jin yunwa? A'a, ina jin ƙishirwa.", "Why is the teacher angry today?": "Me ya sa malamin yake fushi yau?", "The glass is full.": "Kofin ya cika.", "a language": "harshe", "fruit": "'ya'yan itace", "a bird": "tsuntsu", "a sparrow": "gwara", "a city": "birni", "a cup, a glass": "kofi", "easy": "mai sauƙi", "difficult": "mai wuya", "hardworking": "mai ƙwazo", "lughatun": "lughatun", "faakihatun": "faakihatun", "ṭaa'irun": "ṭaa'irun", "'uṣfuurun": "'uṣfuurun", "madeenatun": "madeenatun", "kuubun": "kuubun", "sahlun": "sahlun", "ṣa'bun": "ṣa'bun", "mujtahidun": "mujtahidun", "lazy": "malalaci", "angry": "mai fushi", "full": "cike", "famous": "shahararre", "sharp": "mai kaifi", "New words: how someone feels": "Sababbin kalmomi: yadda mutum yake ji", "kaslaanu": "kaslaanu", "ghaḍbaanu": "ghaḍbaanu", "mal'aanu": "mal'aanu", "shaheerun": "shaheerun", "ḥaaddun": "ḥaaddun", "a library, a bookshop": "ɗakin karatu, ko shagon littattafai", "a fan": "fanka", "a clinic": "asibiti ƙarami, wato shan magani", "a minister": "minista", "the secondary school": "makarantar sakandare", "Arabic (the language)": "Larabci, harshen", "English (the language)": "Turanci, harshen", "Cairo": "Alƙahira", "New words: places and people": "Sababbin kalmomi: wurare da mutane", "maktabatun": "maktabatun", "mirwaḥatun": "mirwaḥatun", "mustawṣafun": "mustawṣafun", "wazeerun": "wazeerun", "al-madrasatuth-thaanawiyyatu": "al-madrasatuth-thaanawiyyatu", "al-'arabiyyatu": "al-'arabiyyatu", "al-inkileeziyyatu": "al-inkileeziyyatu", "al-qaahiratu": "al-qaahiratu", "who, which (for a masculine word)": "wanda, ga kalmar namiji", "today": "yau", "with, at (someone's place)": "tare da, a wurin wani", "Ammar is a hardworking student and Mahmud is a lazy student.": "Ammar ɗalibi ne mai ƙwazo kuma Mahmud ɗalibi ne malalaci.", "Are you a new student? Yes, I am a new student.": "Kai sabon ɗalibi ne? I, ni sabon ɗalibi ne.", "Where is the new teacher? He is with the principal.": "Ina sabon malamin yake? Yana wurin shugaban makarantar.", "Whose is that beautiful car? It is the new principal's.": "Waccan kyakkyawar motar ta wane ce? Ta sabon shugaban makarantar ce.", "Masculine or feminine, with": "Namiji ko mace, da", "The describing word copies the noun": "Kalmar siffantawa tana bin sunan", "or without.": "ko ba tare da shi ba.", "How do you say “a small bird”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ƙaramin tsuntsu”?", "How do you say “a big city”?": "Yaya ake cewa “babban birni”?", "How do you say “a famous doctor”?": "Yaya ake cewa “shahararren likita”?", "How do you say “the beautiful car”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kyakkyawar motar”?", "How do you say “the big room”?": "Yaya ake cewa “babban ɗakin”?", "How do you say “a difficult language”?": "Yaya ake cewa “harshe mai wuya”?", "How do you say “the small spoon”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ƙaramin cokalin”?", "How do you say “an easy language”?": "Yaya ake cewa “harshe mai sauƙi”?", "the broken pen": "karyayyen alƙalamin", "A sentence or a phrase?": "Jumla ce ko sashe?", "The boy is tall.": "Yaron dogo ne.", "the tall boy": "dogon yaron", "the big book": "babban littafin", "the beautiful car": "kyakkyawar motar", "The car is beautiful.": "Motar kyakkyawa ce.", "Look at the noun before the gap.": "Duba sunan da ke kafin gurbin.", "Choose the right describing word": "Zaɓi kalmar siffantawa da ta dace", "“I am thirsty.”": "“Ina jin ƙishirwa.”", "“I am hungry.”": "“Ina jin yunwa.”", "“Mahmud is a lazy student.”": "“Mahmud ɗalibi ne malalaci.”", "“Are you hungry?”": "“Kana jin yunwa?”", "“The glass is full.”": "“Kofin ya cika.”", "“Why is the teacher angry today?”": "“Me ya sa malamin yake fushi yau?”", "How do you say “a delicious fruit”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'ya'yan itace masu daɗi”?", "Listen, then write the word. (with, at (someone's place))": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato tare da, a wurin wani.", "✅ Where is the new teacher?": "✅ Ina sabon malamin yake?", "✅ How do you say “a big city”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “babban birni”?", "✅ Arabic is an easy language.": "✅ Larabci harshe ne mai sauƙi.", "✅ “Mahmud is a lazy student.”": "✅ “Mahmud ɗalibi ne malalaci.”", "✅ How do you say “a delicious fruit”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “'ya'yan itace masu daɗi”?", "✅ “Why is the teacher angry today?”": "✅ “Me ya sa malamin yake fushi yau?”", "✅ Write: with, at (someone's place)": "✅ Rubuta: tare da, a wurin wani", "In this lesson you will learn the endings that mean my, your, his and her, like": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi ƙarshen kalmomi masu ma'anar nawa, naka, nasa da nata, kamar", "my house, and": "gidana, da", "your house. You will say I have with": "gidanka. Za ka faɗi ina da shi da", "and with with": "da kuma tare da, da", "You will also meet a dialogue between two students.": "Za ka kuma ga tattaunawa tsakanin ɗalibai biyu.", "Add an ending to a noun:": "Ƙara ƙarshe ga suna:", "my house.": "gidana.", "your house.": "gidanka.", "his house.": "gidansa.", "her house. The noun then has no": "gidanta. Sannan sunan ba shi da", "and no": "kuma ba shi da", "what is your name?": "mene ne sunanka?", "my name is Muhammad. A word ending in": "sunana Muhammadu. Kalmar da ke ƙarewa da", "changes it to": "tana canza shi zuwa", "my car.": "motata.", "get a long u before an ending:": "suna samun dogon u kafin ƙarshen:", "But my is short:": "Amma nawa gajere ne:", "For things, say": "Ga abubuwa, ka ce", "I have a pen. For family, say": "ina da alƙalami. Ga 'yan'uwa, ka ce", "I have a brother. For I don't have, put": "ina da ɗan'uwa. Don ka ce ba ni da shi, sanya", "first.": "a farko.", "means with. It takes the same endings:": "ma'anarsa tare da. Yana ɗaukar ƙarshe iri ɗaya:", "with me.": "tare da ni.", "with you.": "tare da kai.", "with him.": "tare da shi.", "Some boys' names end in": "Wasu sunayen maza suna ƙarewa da", "They never take": "Ba sa taɓa samun", "My, your, his, her": "Nawa, naka, nasa, nata", "Father and brother": "Uba da ɗan'uwa", "I have": "Ina da", "His or her?": "Nasa ko nata?", "In this lesson you will learn the endings that mean my, your, his and her, like بَيْتِي, my house, and بَيْتُكَ, your house. You will say I have with عِنْدِي and لِي, and with with مَعَ. You will also meet a dialogue between two students.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi ƙarshen kalmomi masu ma'anar nawa, naka, nasa da nata, kamar بَيْتِي, gidana, da بَيْتُكَ, gidanka. Za ka faɗi ina da shi da عِنْدِي da لِي, da kuma tare da, da مَعَ. Za ka kuma ga tattaunawa tsakanin ɗalibai biyu.", "baytee": "baytee", "my house": "gidana", "baytuka": "baytuka", "your house": "gidanka", "baytuhu": "baytuhu", "his house": "gidansa", "baytuhaa": "baytuhaa", "her house": "gidanta", "(my),": "wato nawa,", "(your),": "wato naka,", "(his),": "wato nasa,", "(her). The noun then has no": "wato nata. Sannan sunan ba shi da", "and no -un.": "kuma ba shi da -un.", "ismee": "ismee", "my name": "sunana", "ismuka": "ismuka", "your name": "sunanka", "(What is your name?) →": "wato mene ne sunanka? →", "(My name is Muhammad). A word ending in": "wato sunana Muhammadu. Kalmar da ke ƙarewa da", "What is your name? My name is Muhammad.": "Mene ne sunanka? Sunana Muhammadu.", "What is your language? My language is Urdu.": "Mene ne harshenka? Harshena Urdu ne.", "my car": "motata", "his car": "motarsa", "abee": "abee", "my father": "babana", "abuuka": "abuuka", "your father": "babanka", "abuuhu": "abuuhu", "his father": "babansa", "my": "nawa", "is short:": "gajere ne:", "Where is your father, Muhammad?": "Ina babanka yake, Muhammadu?", "My father is in Kuwait. He is a famous doctor.": "Babana yana Kuwait. Shi shahararren likita ne.", "Her brother is in Taif and her father is in Madinah.": "Ɗan'uwanta yana Ɗa'if kuma babanta yana Madina.", "'indee": "'indee", "I have (things)": "ina da shi, ga abubuwa", "lee": "lee", "I have (family)": "ina da shi, ga 'yan'uwa", "For": "Ga", "things": "abubuwa", "say": "ka ce", ". For": ". Ga", "family": "'yan'uwa", ". To say “I don't have”, put": ". Don ka ce “ba ni da shi”, sanya", "first:": "a farko:", "Do you have a car?": "Kana da mota?", "No, I don't have a car. I have a bicycle.": "A'a, ba ni da mota. Ina da keke.", "Do you have a brother? Yes, I have one brother.": "Kana da ɗan'uwa? I, ina da ɗan'uwa ɗaya.", "Hamzah has a car.": "Hamza yana da mota.", "ma'a": "ma'a", "with": "tare da", "takes the same endings:": "yana ɗaukar ƙarshe iri ɗaya:", "(with me),": "wato tare da ni,", "(with you),": "wato tare da kai,", "(with him),": "wato tare da shi,", "(with her).": "wato tare da ita.", "Who is this young man with you?": "Wane ne wannan saurayin da ke tare da kai?", "He is my classmate.": "Shi abokin ajina ne.", "Hamid went out with Khalid.": "Hamid ya fita tare da Khalid.", "Hamzah": "Hamza", "Usamah": "Usama", "Boys' names with ة": "Sunayen maza masu ة", ". Like girls' names, they never take -un:": ". Kamar sunayen mata, ba sa taɓa samun -un:", "Talhah": "Ɗalha", "Mu'awiyah": "Mu'awiya", "a father": "uba", "a brother": "ɗan'uwa", "a husband": "miji", "a child": "jariri, ƙaramin yaro", "a young man": "saurayi", "a classmate, a colleague": "abokin aji, abokin aiki", "one": "ɗaya", "New words: family": "Sababbin kalmomi: iyali", "abun": "abun", "akhun": "akhun", "zawjun": "zawjun", "ṭiflun": "ṭiflun", "fatan": "fatan", "zameelun": "zameelun", "waaḥidun": "waaḥidun", "Kuwait": "Kuwait", "Iraq": "Iraƙi", "Urdu (the language)": "Urdu, harshen", "Japanese (the language)": "Japananci, harshen", "New words: places and languages": "Sababbin kalmomi: wurare da harsuna", "al-kuwaytu": "al-kuwaytu", "al-'iraaqu": "al-'iraaqu", "al-urdiyyatu": "al-urdiyyatu", "al-yaabaaniyyatu": "al-yaabaaniyyatu", "here": "nan", "Who are you? I am a student at the university.": "Wane ne kai? Ni ɗalibi ne a jami'a.", "Where are you from? I am from India.": "Daga ina kake? Ni daga Indiya nake.", "And who is this young man with you? He is my classmate.": "Kuma wane ne wannan saurayin da ke tare da kai? Shi abokin ajina ne.", "What is your language, Muhammad? My language is Urdu.": "Mene ne harshenka, Muhammadu? Harshena Urdu ne.", "Where is your father? My father is in Kuwait.": "Ina babanka yake? Babana yana Kuwait.", "Do you have a car? No, I don't have a car. I have a bicycle.": "Kana da mota? A'a, ba ni da mota. Ina da keke.", "Choose the right ending.": "Zaɓi ƙarshen da ya dace.", "My": "Nawa", "your": "naka", "his": "nasa", "her": "nata", "How do you say “my name”?": "Yaya ake cewa “sunana”?", "How do you say “his book”?": "Yaya ake cewa “littafinsa”?", "How do you say “her house”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gidanta”?", "How do you say “his handkerchief”?": "Yaya ake cewa “hankicinsa”?", "How do you say “his hand”?": "Yaya ake cewa “hannunsa”?", "How do you say “my bed”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gadona”?", "How do you say “your house”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gidanka”?", "How do you say “my pen”?": "Yaya ake cewa “alƙalamina”?", "How do you say “his pen”?": "Yaya ake cewa “alƙalaminsa”?", "How do you say “your name”?": "Yaya ake cewa “sunanka”?", "Father and brother get a long u before an ending.": "Uba da ɗan'uwa suna samun dogon u kafin ƙarshen kalma.", "How do you say “her father”?": "Yaya ake cewa “babanta”?", "How do you say “your brother”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗan'uwanka”?", "How do you say “your father”?": "Yaya ake cewa “babanka”?", "How do you say “my brother”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗan'uwana”?", "How do you say “my father”?": "Yaya ake cewa “babana”?", "How do you say “his brother”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗan'uwansa”?", "Things: use": "Abubuwa: yi amfani da", ". Family: use": ". 'Yan'uwa: yi amfani da", "“Hamzah has a car.”": "“Hamza yana da mota.”", "Family: use": "'Yan'uwa: yi amfani da", "“I don't have a brother.”": "“Ba ni da ɗan'uwa.”", "“I have one sister.”": "“Ina da 'yar'uwa ɗaya.”", "“I have a brother.”": "“Ina da ɗan'uwa.”", "“I have a pen.”": "“Ina da alƙalami.”", "“Do you have a sister?”": "“Kana da 'yar'uwa?”", "His: use": "Nasa: yi amfani da", ". Her: use": ". Nata: yi amfani da", "Her: use": "Nata: yi amfani da", "Where is your father?": "Ina babanka yake?", "عِنْدِي or لِي?": "عِنْدِي ko لِي?", "Listen, then write the word. (a husband)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato miji.", "How do you say “his father”?": "Yaya ake cewa “babansa”?", "How do you say “your bed”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gadonka”?", "ـهُ or ـهَا?": "ـهُ ko ـهَا?", "I don't have a car.": "Ba ni da mota.", "✅ “I have one sister.”": "✅ “Ina da 'yar'uwa ɗaya.”", "✅ “Hamzah has a car.”": "✅ “Hamza yana da mota.”", "✅ Write: a husband": "✅ Rubuta: miji", "✅ How do you say “my bed”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “gadona”?", "✅ How do you say “his father”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “babansa”?", "✅ How do you say “your bed”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “gadonka”?", "✅ How do you say “his brother”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗan'uwansa”?", "✅ He is my classmate.": "✅ Shi abokin ajina ne.", "✅ How do you say “your house”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “gidanka”?", "✅ “I don't have a brother.”": "✅ “Ba ni da ɗan'uwa.”", "✅ I don't have a car.": "✅ Ba ni da mota.", "In this lesson you will read a short text called": "A wannan darasi za ka karanta gajeren rubutu mai suna", "my house. You will practise the ending for my with many words, learn": "gidana. Za ka yi atisayen ƙarshen nawa da kalmomi da yawa, ka koyi", "in it, and say": "a cikinsa, ka kuma ce", "I love.": "ina so.", "Listen to the whole text, called": "Saurari dukan rubutun, mai suna", "my house. Tap any sentence to hear it again, and see its meaning.": "gidana. Taɓa kowace jumla don sake jin ta, ka ga ma'anarta.", "Remember:": "Ka tuna:", "before an ending:": "kafin ƙarshen kalma:", "means in it, for a masculine word.": "ma'anarsa a cikinsa, don kalmar namiji.", "is for a feminine word.": "na kalmar mace ne.", "means there is no one in it.": "ma'anarsa babu kowa a cikinsa.", "means I love.": "ma'anarsa ina so.", "My house": "Gidana", "About the text": "Game da rubutun", "In it": "A cikinsa", "My …": "Nawa …", "I love": "Ina so", "In this lesson you will read a short text called بَيْتِي, my house. You will practise the ending for my with many words, learn فِيهِ and فِيهَا, in it, and say أُحِبُّ, I love.": "A wannan darasi za ka karanta gajeren rubutu mai suna بَيْتِي, gidana. Za ka yi atisayen ƙarshen nawa da kalmomi da yawa, ka koyi فِيهِ da فِيهَا, a cikinsa ko a cikinta, ka kuma ce أُحِبُّ, ina so.", "My house (the text)": "Gidana, rubutun", "Listen to the whole text. Tap any sentence to hear it again.": "Saurari dukan rubutun. Taɓa kowace jumla don sake jin ta.", "This is my house. My house is in front of the mosque.": "Wannan gidana ne. Gidana yana gaban masallaci.", "My house is beautiful. In it there is a small garden.": "Gidana yana da kyau. A cikinsa akwai ƙaramin lambu.", "This is my room. In it there is a big window and a beautiful fan.": "Wannan ɗakina ne. A cikinsa akwai babbar taga da kyakkyawar fanka.", "This is my bed, this is my chair and this is my desk.": "Wannan gadona ne, wannan kujerata ce kuma wannan teburina ne.", "My watch, my pen and my book are on the desk.": "Agogona, alƙalamina da littafina suna kan teburin.", "And my bag is under the desk. My room's window is open.": "Kuma jakata tana ƙarƙashin teburin. Tagar ɗakina a buɗe take.", "This is my brother's room and that is my sister's room.": "Wannan ɗakin ɗan'uwana ne kuma waccan ɗakin 'yar'uwata ne.", "My brother's room is big and my sister's room is small.": "Ɗakin ɗan'uwana babba ne kuma ɗakin 'yar'uwata ƙarami ne.", "I have one brother, his name is Usamah, and one sister, her name is Su'ad.": "Ina da ɗan'uwa ɗaya, sunansa Usama, da 'yar'uwa ɗaya, sunanta Su'ad.", "My father and my mother are in that big room.": "Babana da mamata suna cikin wancan babban ɗakin.", "I love my father and my mother, and I love my brother and my sister.": "Ina son babana da mamata, kuma ina son ɗan'uwana da 'yar'uwata.", "ghurfatun": "ghurfatun", "a room": "ɗaki", "ghurfatee": "ghurfatee", "my room": "ɗakina", "my watch": "agogona", "my bag": "jakata", "My room's window is open.": "Tagar ɗakina a buɗe take.", "feehi": "feehi", "in it (m)": "a cikinsa, na namiji", "feehaa": "feehaa", "in it (f)": "a cikinta, na mace", "(in him / in it).": "wato a cikinsa.", "(in her / in it).": "wato a cikinta.", "= There is no one in it.": "yana nufin babu kowa a cikinsa.", "Who is in this house? Hamid is in it.": "Wane ne a cikin wannan gidan? Hamid yana cikinsa.", "What is in the bag? My book and my pen are in it.": "Me ke cikin jakar? Littafina da alƙalamina suna cikinta.", "Who is in the university mosque now? No one is in it.": "Wane ne a cikin masallacin jami'ar yanzu? Babu kowa a cikinsa.", "uḥibbu": "uḥibbu", "+ the person or thing you love.": "tare da mutumin ko abin da kake so.", "I love my father and my mother.": "Ina son babana da mamata.", "I love Allah.": "Ina son Allah.", "I love the Arabic language.": "Ina son harshen Larabci.", "my bed": "gadona", "my chair": "kujerata", "my desk": "teburina", "my pen": "alƙalamina", "New words: my things": "Sababbin kalmomi: kayana", "sareeree": "sareeree", "kursiyyee": "kursiyyee", "maktabee": "maktabee", "saa'atee": "saa'atee", "qalamee": "qalamee", "ḥaqeebatee": "ḥaqeebatee", "my mother": "mamata", "my brother": "ɗan'uwana", "my sister": "'yar'uwata", "New words: my family": "Sababbin kalmomi: iyalina", "ummee": "ummee", "akhee": "akhee", "ukhtee": "ukhtee", "anyone, one person": "kowa, wani mutum ɗaya", "in it (masculine)": "a cikinsa, na namiji", "in it (feminine)": "a cikinta, na mace", "Answer from the text": "Amsa daga rubutun", "Questions about the text": "Tambayoyi game da rubutun", "Answer from the text.": "Amsa daga rubutun.", "No": "Babu", "How do you say “my …”?": "Yaya ake cewa “nawa …”?", ", no -un, and": ", babu -un, kuma", "How do you say “my room”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗakina”?", "How do you say “my sister”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'yar'uwata”?", "How do you say “my house”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gidana”?", "How do you say “my bag”?": "Yaya ake cewa “jakata”?", "How do you say “my watch”?": "Yaya ake cewa “agogona”?", "“I love my brother and my sister.”": "“Ina son ɗan'uwana da 'yar'uwata.”", "“I love my father and my mother.”": "“Ina son babana da mamata.”", "“I love the Arabic language.”": "“Ina son harshen Larabci.”", "“I love Allah.”": "“Ina son Allah.”", "In it there is a small garden.": "A cikinsa akwai ƙaramin lambu.", "فِيهِ or فِيهَا?": "فِيهِ ko فِيهَا?", "Listen, then write the word. (my mother)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato mamata.", "There is no one in it.": "Babu kowa a cikinsa.", "✅ Answer from the text.": "✅ Amsa daga rubutun.", "✅ In it there is a small garden.": "✅ A cikinsa akwai ƙaramin lambu.", "✅ How do you say “my room”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗakina”?", "✅ “I love my father and my mother.”": "✅ “Ina son babana da mamata.”", "✅ Write: my mother": "✅ Rubuta: mamata", "✅ How do you say “my watch”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “agogona”?", "✅ There is no one in it.": "✅ Babu kowa a cikinsa.", "✅ “I love Allah.”": "✅ “Ina son Allah.”", "In this lesson you will learn how to talk to a woman or a girl:": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi yadda ake magana da mace ko yarinya:", "you, and the ending for your, like": "ke, da ƙarshen kalma mai ma'anar naki, kamar", "You will greet with": "Za ka yi gaisuwa da", "and ask": "ka tambaya", "how are you. You will also learn": "yaya kike. Za ka kuma koyi", "she went, and": "ta tafi, da", "who or which for a feminine word, and the words for aunts.": "wadda, don kalmar mace, da kalmomin gwaggo.", "To greet a woman, say": "Don gaishe da mace, ka ce", "She answers": "Tana amsawa", "Talking to a man, say": "Idan kana magana da namiji, ka ce", "Talking to a woman, say": "Idan kana magana da mace, ka ce", "to say she did it:": "don faɗar cewa ita ce ta yi:", "she went. Before": "ta tafi. Kafin", "it gets a": "yana samun", "the student sat.": "ɗalibar ta zauna.", "after a masculine word, and": "bayan kalmar namiji, da", "after a feminine word.": "bayan kalmar mace.", "is the father's brother.": "shi ne ɗan'uwan uba, wato baffa.", "is the father's sister.": "ita ce 'yar'uwar uba, wato gwaggo.", "is the mother's brother.": "shi ne ɗan'uwan uwa, wato kawu.", "is the mother's sister.": "ita ce 'yar'uwar uwa, wato inna.", "Talking to a woman": "Magana da mace", "To a man or a woman?": "Ga namiji ko ga mace?", "She went": "Ta tafi", "Who, which": "Wanda, wadda", "to the verb, like": "ga fi'ili, kamar", "it is read with a": "ana karanta shi da", "In this lesson you will learn how to talk to a woman or a girl: أَنْتِ, you, and the ending for your, like اسْمُكِ. You will greet with السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ and ask كَيْفَ حَالُكِ, how are you. You will also learn ذَهَبَتْ, she went, and الَّتِي, who or which for a feminine word, and the words for aunts.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi yadda ake magana da mace ko yarinya: أَنْتِ, ke, da ƙarshen kalma mai ma'anar naki, kamar اسْمُكِ. Za ka yi gaisuwa da السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكِ ka tambaya كَيْفَ حَالُكِ, yaya kike. Za ka kuma koyi ذَهَبَتْ, ta tafi, da الَّتِي, wadda, don kalmar mace, da kalmomin gwaggo.", "as-salaamu 'alayki": "as-salaamu 'alayki", "Peace be upon you (to a woman)": "Aminci ya tabbata a gare ki, ga mace", "To greet a woman:": "Don gaishe da mace:", ". She answers:": ". Tana amsawa:", "Peace be upon you, and Allah's mercy and blessings.": "Aminci ya tabbata a gare ki, da rahamar Allah da albarkarsa.", "And upon you be peace, and Allah's mercy and blessings.": "A gare ka ma aminci ya tabbata, da rahamar Allah da albarkarsa.", "How are you, girl?": "Yaya kike, yarinya?", "I am well, praise be to Allah.": "Lafiya lau, godiya ta tabbata ga Allah.", "anta": "anta", "anti": "anti", "you (a woman)": "ke, ga mace", "Talking to a man:": "Magana da namiji:", "and the ending": "da ƙarshen", ". Talking to a woman:": ". Magana da mace:", "to a man": "ga namiji", "to a woman": "ga mace", "Where are you from (f)? I am from Riyadh.": "Daga ina kike? Ni daga Riyadh nake.", "What is your name (f)? My name is Aminah.": "Mene ne sunanki? Sunana Aminatu.", "Where is your father? My father is here in Madinah.": "Ina babanki yake? Babana yana nan Madina.", "Are you a doctor, my sister? No, I am a teacher.": "Ke likita ce, 'yar'uwata? A'a, ni malama ce.", "dhahabat": "dhahabat", "she went": "ta tafi", "-at": "-at", "to say": "don faɗar cewa", "did it:": "ita ce ta yi:", "it is read": "ana karanta shi", "-ati": "-ati", "Muhammad went out of the house.": "Muhammadu ya fita daga gidan.", "Aminah went out of the house.": "Aminatu ta fita daga gidan.", "Is your mother at home now? No, she went to the hospital.": "Mamarki tana gida yanzu? A'a, ta tafi asibiti.", "The student (f) sat down.": "Ɗalibar ta zauna.", "who, which (m)": "wanda, na namiji", "allatee": "allatee", "who, which (f)": "wadda, na mace", "after a masculine word and": "bayan kalmar namiji da", "the young man who": "saurayin da", "the girl who": "yarinyar da", "Who is the young man who just left your house? He is my cousin.": "Wane ne saurayin da ya fita daga gidanki yanzu? Shi ɗan baffana ne.", "Who is the girl who just left your house? She is my cousin.": "Wace ce yarinyar da ta fita daga gidanki yanzu? Ita 'yar baffana ce.", "Whose is the watch which is on the bed?": "Agogon da ke kan gadon na wane ne?", "uncles and aunts": "baffanni da gwaggonni", "father's side": "ɓangaren uba", "mother's side": "ɓangaren uwa", "The 'amm is the father's brother.": "'Amm shi ne ɗan'uwan uba.", "The 'ammah is the father's sister.": "'Ammah ita ce 'yar'uwar uba.", "The khaal is the mother's brother.": "Khaal shi ne ɗan'uwan uwa.", "The khaalah is the mother's sister.": "Khaalah ita ce 'yar'uwar uwa.", "a girl, a young woman": "yarinya, budurwa", "a teacher (f)": "malama", "a supervisor (in a school)": "mai kula, a makaranta", "a friend": "aboki", "an aunt (father's sister)": "gwaggo, 'yar'uwar uba", "an aunt (mother's sister)": "inna, 'yar'uwar uwa", "fataatun": "fataatun", "mudarrisatun": "mudarrisatun", "muwajjihun": "muwajjihun", "ṣadeequn": "ṣadeequn", "'ammatun": "'ammatun", "khaalatun": "khaalatun", "a tree": "bishiya", "the maternity hospital": "asibitin haihuwa", "the middle school": "makarantar tsakiya", "Riyadh": "Riyadh", "shajaratun": "shajaratun", "mustashfal-wilaadati": "mustashfal-wilaadati", "al-madrasatul-mutawassiṭatu": "al-madrasatul-mutawassiṭatu", "ar-riyaaḍu": "ar-riyaaḍu", "who, which (for a feminine word)": "wadda, ga kalmar mace", "well, fine": "lafiya, lau", "how?": "yaya?", "How are you, girl? I am well, praise be to Allah.": "Yaya kike, yarinya? Lafiya lau, godiya ta tabbata ga Allah.", "Where are you from? I am from Riyadh.": "Daga ina kike? Ni daga Riyadh nake.", "What is your name? My name is Aminah.": "Mene ne sunanki? Sunana Aminatu.", "And where is your mother? She is here too. She is a doctor at the maternity hospital.": "Kuma ina mamarki take? Ita ma tana nan. Ita likita ce a asibitin haihuwa.", "And who is this girl with you? Is she your sister?": "Kuma wace ce wannan yarinyar da ke tare da ke? 'Yar'uwarki ce?", "No, she is my cousin. Her name is Fatimah.": "A'a, ita 'yar baffana ce. Sunanta Faɗimatu.", "To a man: use": "Ga namiji: yi amfani da", "Talking to a man or a woman?": "Magana da namiji ko da mace?", ". To a woman: use": ". Ga mace: yi amfani da", "Ask Fatimah: Where are you from?": "Tambayi Faɗimatu: Daga ina kike?", "To a woman: use": "Ga mace: yi amfani da", "Ask your father: How are you?": "Tambayi babanka: Yaya kake?", "Ask Aminah: What is your name?": "Tambayi Aminatu: Mene ne sunanki?", "Greet a woman.": "Gaishe da mace.", "Ask Khalid: Where are you from?": "Tambayi Khalid: Daga ina kake?", "Ask Hamid: What is your name?": "Tambayi Hamid: Mene ne sunanka?", "Ask Zaynab: Where is your son?": "Tambayi Zainab: Ina ɗanki yake?", "Ask Aminah: Do you have a sister?": "Tambayi Aminatu: Kina da 'yar'uwa?", "Now say it about a woman": "Yanzu ka faɗe shi game da mace", "Add -at to the verb:": "Ƙara -at ga fi'ilin:", "it is read -ati.": "ana karanta shi -ati.", "Now say it about a woman:": "Yanzu ka faɗe shi game da mace:", "Where are you from? (to a woman)": "Daga ina kike? Ga mace", "What is your name? (to a woman)": "Mene ne sunanki? Ga mace", "Where is your mother?": "Ina mamarka take?", "How are you? (to a woman)": "Yaya kike? Ga mace", "She went to the hospital.": "Ta tafi asibiti.", "الَّذِي or الَّتِي?": "الَّذِي ko الَّتِي?", "Ask Muhammad: Is this your pen?": "Tambayi Muhammadu: Wannan alƙalaminka ne?", "She is my cousin (my uncle's daughter).": "Ita 'yar baffana ce.", "Listen, then write the word. (after)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato bayan.", "✅ Ask Muhammad: Is this your pen?": "✅ Tambayi Muhammadu: Wannan alƙalaminka ne?", "✅ Ask Zaynab: Where is your son?": "✅ Tambayi Zainab: Ina ɗanki yake?", "✅ She is my cousin (my uncle's daughter).": "✅ Ita 'yar baffana ce.", "✅ What is your name? (to a woman)": "✅ Mene ne sunanki? Ga mace", "✅ Ask Aminah: Do you have a sister?": "✅ Tambayi Aminatu: Kina da 'yar'uwa?", "✅ Write: after": "✅ Rubuta: bayan", "In this lesson you will learn plurals, more than two people or things. You will meet": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi jam'i, wato fiye da mutum biyu ko abu biyu. Za ka haɗu da", "these, and": "waɗannan, da", "those,": "waɗancan,", "they, and verbs like": "su, da fi'iloli kamar", "they went. You will learn the three ways to make a plural: the broken plural, the ending for men, and the ending for women.": "sun tafi. Za ka koyi hanyoyi uku na yin jam'i: jam'in taksiri, ƙarshen jam'i na maza, da ƙarshen jam'i na mata.", "For more than two people, use": "Ga mutane fiye da biyu, yi amfani da", "they. Many plurals change the inside of the word. This is a broken plural:": "su. Jam'i da yawa suna canza cikin kalmar. Wannan shi ne jam'in taksiri:", "There is no single rule for broken plurals, so learn each plural together with its word.": "Babu ƙa'ida ɗaya ta jam'in taksiri, don haka ka koyi kowane jam'i tare da kalmarsa.", "Some words for men just add an ending:": "Wasu kalmomin maza suna ƙara ƙarshe kawai:", "usually change it to": "yawanci suna canza shi zuwa", "For women, use": "Ga mata, yi amfani da", "they:": "su:", "For men,": "Ga maza,", "they went. For women,": "sun tafi. Ga mata,", "Both are used for men or women.": "Dukansu ana amfani da su ga maza ko mata.", "is for near,": "na kusa ne,", "is for far.": "na nesa ne.", "means some of them, for men.": "ma'anarsa wasunsu, ga maza.", "is for women.": "na mata ne.", "Plurals": "Jam'i", "Plural": "Jam'i", "He, she, they": "Shi, ita, su", "They went": "Sun tafi", "This, these, those": "Wannan, waɗannan, waɗancan", "In this lesson you will learn plurals, more than two people or things. You will meet هٰؤُلَاءِ, these, and أُولٰئِكَ, those, هُمْ and هُنَّ, they, and verbs like ذَهَبُوا, they went. You will learn the three ways to make a plural: the broken plural, the ending for men, and the ending for women.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi jam'i, wato fiye da mutum biyu ko abu biyu. Za ka haɗu da هٰؤُلَاءِ, waɗannan, da أُولٰئِكَ, waɗancan, هُمْ da هُنَّ, su, da fi'iloli kamar ذَهَبُوا, sun tafi. Za ka koyi hanyoyi uku na yin jam'i: jam'in taksiri, ƙarshen jam'i na maza, da ƙarshen jam'i na mata.", "haadhaa ṭaalibun": "haadhaa ṭaalibun", "This is a student.": "Wannan ɗalibi ne.", "haa'ulaa'i ṭullaabun": "haa'ulaa'i ṭullaabun", "These are students.": "Waɗannan ɗalibai ne.", "For more than two people use": "Ga mutane fiye da biyu yi amfani da", "(these) and": "wato waɗannan, da", "(they). Many plurals change the inside of the word. This is called a": "wato su. Jam'i da yawa suna canza cikin kalmar. Ana kiran wannan", "broken plural": "jam'in taksiri", "Who are these tall young men, Ali?": "Su wane ne waɗannan dogayen samari, Ali?", "They are new students.": "Su sababbin ɗalibai ne.", "Where are they from? They are from America.": "Daga ina suke? Su daga Amurka suke.", "And who are these short men? They are pilgrims.": "Kuma su wane ne waɗannan gajerun mutane? Su alhazai ne.", "broken plurals": "jam'in taksiri", "Learn each plural with its word": "Koyi kowane jam'i tare da kalmarsa", "There is no single rule for broken plurals, so learn each one with its word.": "Babu ƙa'ida ɗaya ta jam'in taksiri, don haka ka koyi kowanne tare da kalmarsa.", "a man → men": "namiji → maza", "a boy → boys": "yaro → yara", "a merchant → merchants": "ɗan kasuwa → 'yan kasuwa", "a friend → friends": "aboki → abokai", "a brother → brothers": "ɗan'uwa → 'yan'uwa", "big (one) → big (many)": "babba, ɗaya → manya, da yawa", "mudarrisuuna": "mudarrisuuna", "Men: add ـُونَ": "Maza: ƙara ـُونَ", "Some words for men just add": "Wasu kalmomin maza suna ƙara", "(-uuna):": "wato -uuna:", "teacher → teachers": "malami → malamai", "engineer → engineers": "injiniya → injiniyoyi", "Are they hardworking? Yes, they are hardworking.": "Su masu ƙwazo ne? I, su masu ƙwazo ne.", "ṭaalibatun": "ṭaalibatun", "ṭaalibaatun": "ṭaalibaatun", "Women: ة becomes ـَاتٌ": "Mata: ة tana zama ـَاتٌ", "(-aatun). For women use": "wato -aatun. Ga mata yi amfani da", "(they):": "wato su:", "This is a girl → these are girls": "Wannan yarinya ce → waɗannan 'yan mata ne", "Who are these girls, Maryam? They are my classmates.": "Su wane ne waɗannan 'yan matan, Maryam? Su abokan ajina ne.", "Are they sisters? Yes, they are sisters.": "Su 'yan'uwa ne? I, su 'yan'uwa ne.", "dhahabuu": "dhahabuu", "they went (men)": "sun tafi, maza", "dhahabna": "dhahabna", "they went (women)": "sun tafi, mata", "Men:": "Maza:", "Women:": "Mata:", "Muhammad, Hamid and Ali went.": "Muhammadu, Hamid da Ali sun tafi.", "Maryam, Aminah and Fatimah went.": "Maryam, Aminatu da Faɗimatu sun tafi.", "Where are Musa and his friends? They went to the restaurant.": "Ina Musa da abokansa suke? Sun tafi gidan abinci.", "haa'ulaa'i": "haa'ulaa'i", "these (near)": "waɗannan, na kusa", "ulaa'ika": "ulaa'ika", "those (far)": "waɗancan, na nesa", "Both are for men or women.": "Dukansu na maza ne ko na mata.", "these": "waɗannan", "those": "waɗancan", "These are my brothers and those are my friends.": "Waɗannan 'yan'uwana ne kuma waɗancan abokaina ne.", "Who are those women? They are the students' mothers.": "Su wane ne waɗancan matan? Su iyayen ɗaliban ne mata.", "These men are poor and those are rich.": "Waɗannan mutanen matalauta ne kuma waɗancan mawadata ne.", "ba'ḍuhum": "ba'ḍuhum", "some of them": "wasunsu", "= some of them (men).": "yana nufin wasunsu, maza.", "= some of them (women).": "yana nufin wasunsu, mata.", "Some of them are from China and some are from Japan.": "Wasunsu daga China suke kuma wasu daga Japan suke.", "I have young sons. Some of them are in primary school.": "Ina da ƙananan 'ya'ya maza. Wasunsu suna makarantar firamare.", "a guest": "baƙo", "an old man, a shaykh": "tsoho, shehi", "a pilgrim (Hajj)": "alhaji, mai aikin Hajji", "a woman": "mace", "people": "mutane", "a relative": "dangi", "a scholar": "malami masani, wato alim", "New words: new words": "Sababbin kalmomi: sababbin kalmomi", "ḍayfun (pl. ḍuyuufun)": "ḍayfun (pl. ḍuyuufun)", "shaykhun (pl. shuyuukhun)": "shaykhun (pl. shuyuukhun)", "ḥaajjun (pl. ḥujjaajun)": "ḥaajjun (pl. ḥujjaajun)", "imra'atun (pl. nisaa'un)": "imra'atun (pl. nisaa'un)", "an-naasu": "an-naasu", "qareebun (pl. aqribaa'u)": "qareebun (pl. aqribaa'u)", "'aalimun (pl. 'ulamaa'u)": "'aalimun (pl. 'ulamaa'u)", "a field (farm)": "gona", "a village": "ƙauye", "a restaurant, a dining hall": "gidan abinci, ɗakin cin abinci", "the primary school": "makarantar firamare", "strong": "mai ƙarfi", "weak": "mara ƙarfi", "ḥaqlun (pl. ḥuquulun)": "ḥaqlun (pl. ḥuquulun)", "qaryatun": "qaryatun", "maṭ'amun": "maṭ'amun", "al-madrasatul-ibtidaa'iyyatu": "al-madrasatul-ibtidaa'iyyatu", "qawiyyun (pl. aqwiyaa'u)": "qawiyyun (pl. aqwiyaa'u)", "ḍa'eefun (pl. ḍi'aafun)": "ḍa'eefun (pl. ḍi'aafun)", "these (people)": "waɗannan, mutane", "those (people)": "waɗancan, mutane", "they (men)": "su, maza", "some of": "wasu daga", "they (women)": "su, mata", "Who are these tall young men, Ali? They are new students.": "Su wane ne waɗannan dogayen samari, Ali? Su sababbin ɗalibai ne.", "Are they your classmates? Yes, they are my classmates. They are in my class.": "Su abokan ajinka ne? I, su abokan ajina ne. Suna ajina.", "What are their names? Their names are Yasir, Zakariyya, Musa and Abdullah.": "Mene ne sunayensu? Sunayensu Yasir, Zakariyya, Musa da Abdullahi.", "Who is their father? Their father is Shaykh Bilal. Their mother is my teacher.": "Wane ne babansu? Babansu Shehu Bilal ne. Mamarsu malamata ce.", "Where are the new students? They went out and went to the library.": "Ina sababbin ɗaliban suke? Sun fita sun tafi ɗakin karatu.", "Choose the plural of the word.": "Zaɓi jam'in kalmar.", "What is the plural?": "Mene ne jam'insa?", "One man:": "Namiji ɗaya:", ". One woman:": ". Mace ɗaya:", ". Men:": ". Maza:", ". Women:": ". Mata:", "One woman:": "Mace ɗaya:", "Make it plural": "Mayar da shi jam'i", "Now make it plural:": "Yanzu ka mayar da shi jam'i:", ". Far:": ". Nesa:", "Point to them: they are 👇": "Nuna su: suna 👇", "Point to them: they are 👉": "Nuna su: suna 👉", "Those are students.": "Waɗancan ɗalibai ne.", "They went.": "Sun tafi.", "They (f) are my classmates.": "Su, mata, abokan ajina ne.", "They went to the restaurant.": "Sun tafi gidan abinci.", "Listen, then write the word. (they (women))": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato su, mata.", "Those men are rich.": "Waɗancan mutanen mawadata ne.", "✅ What is the plural?": "✅ Mene ne jam'insa?", "✅ Point to them: they are 👉": "✅ Nuna su: suna 👉", "✅ They went to the restaurant.": "✅ Sun tafi gidan abinci.", "✅ Write: they (women)": "✅ Rubuta: su, mata", "✅ Those men are rich.": "✅ Waɗancan mutanen mawadata ne.", "In this lesson you will talk to a group of men with": "A wannan darasi za ka yi magana da rukunin maza da", "you all, and talk about yourself and others with": "ku, ka kuma yi magana game da kanka da wasu da", "we. You will learn": "mu. Za ka koyi", "your house, and": "gidanku, da", "our house, the verbs": "gidanmu, da fi'iloli", "you all went, and": "kun tafi, da", "we went, and the question word": "mun tafi, da kalmar tambaya", "which.": "wane ko wace.", "Talking to a group of men, say": "Idan kana magana da rukunin maza, ka ce", "you all. For yourself and others, say": "ku. Game da kanka da wasu, ka ce", "we.": "mu.", "New endings:": "Sababbin ƙarshe:", "your house, for a group of men, and": "gidanku, ga rukunin maza, da", "our house.": "gidanmu.", "we went.": "mun tafi.", "means which. The noun after it ends in a": "ma'anarsa wane ko wace. Sunan da ke bayansa yana ƙarewa da", "which day?": "wace rana?", "Say": "Ka ce", "to welcome a guest. When someone is sick, say": "don maraba da baƙo. Idan wani ba shi da lafiya, ka ce", "may Allah cure him.": "Allah ya ba shi lafiya.", "You all, we": "Ku, mu", "Answer for all of you": "Amsa a madadinku duka", "Your and our": "Naku da namu", "You all went": "Kun tafi", "Which?": "Wane?", "In this lesson you will talk to a group of men with أَنْتُمْ, you all, and talk about yourself and others with نَحْنُ, we. You will learn بَيْتُكُمْ, your house, and بَيْتُنَا, our house, the verbs ذَهَبْتُمْ, you all went, and ذَهَبْنَا, we went, and the question word أَيُّ, which.": "A wannan darasi za ka yi magana da rukunin maza da أَنْتُمْ, ku, ka kuma yi magana game da kanka da wasu da نَحْنُ, mu. Za ka koyi بَيْتُكُمْ, gidanku, da بَيْتُنَا, gidanmu, da fi'iloli ذَهَبْتُمْ, kun tafi, da ذَهَبْنَا, mun tafi, da kalmar tambaya أَيُّ, wane ko wace.", "antum": "antum", "you all (men)": "ku, maza", "naḥnu": "naḥnu", "we": "mu", "Talking to a group of men:": "Magana da rukunin maza:", ". Talking about yourself and others:": ". Magana game da kanka da wasu:", "(for men or women).": "ga maza ko mata.", "Who are you (all)?": "Ku su wane ne?", "We are the sons of Doctor Musa.": "Mu 'ya'yan Likita Musa ne.", "Are you (all) in secondary school?": "Kuna makarantar sakandare?", "No, we are at the university.": "A'a, muna jami'a.", "baytukum": "baytukum", "your house (all of you)": "gidanku, na dukanku", "baytunaa": "baytunaa", "our house": "gidanmu", "(your, for a group of men) and": "wato naku, ga rukunin maza, da", "(our).": "wato namu.", "Where is your new house?": "Ina sabon gidanku yake?", "Our new house is near the airport.": "Sabon gidanmu yana kusa da filin jirgin sama.", "Your father is my friend.": "Babanku abokina ne.", "She is our sister.": "Ita 'yar'uwarmu ce.", "dhahabtum": "dhahabtum", "you all went": "kun tafi", "dhahabnaa": "dhahabnaa", "we went": "mun tafi", "(you all went) →": "wato kun tafi →", "(we went).": "wato mun tafi.", "Did you go to the hospital to visit your uncle today?": "Kun tafi asibiti don duba baffanku yau?", "Yes, we went.": "I, mun tafi.", "Where did you go, brothers? We went to the market.": "Ina kuka tafi, 'yan'uwa? Mun tafi kasuwa.", "ayyu?": "ayyu?", "which?": "wane?", "+ a noun ending in -i:": "tare da suna mai ƙarewa da -i:", "(which day?)": "wato wace rana?", "(which month?)": "wato wane wata?", "Which day is this? This is Saturday.": "Wace rana ce wannan? Wannan Asabar ce.", "Which faculty is this? This is the faculty of commerce.": "Wace kwaleji ce wannan? Wannan kwalejin kasuwanci ce.", "Which country are you from, brother? I am from Greece.": "Daga wace ƙasa kake, ɗan'uwa? Ni daga Girka nake.", "ahlan wa sahlan": "ahlan wa sahlan", "Welcome!": "Maraba!", "(May Allah cure him).": "wato Allah ya ba shi lafiya.", "He is sick. He is in the hospital now.": "Ba shi da lafiya. Yana asibiti yanzu.", "May Allah cure him.": "Allah ya ba shi lafiya.", "a grandson": "jika", "a Christian": "Kirista", "a college, a faculty": "kwaleji, sashen jami'a", "the faculty of medicine": "kwalejin likitanci", "the faculty of engineering": "kwalejin injiniyanci", "the faculty of Shari'ah": "kwalejin Shari'a", "the faculty of commerce": "kwalejin kasuwanci", "a court (of law)": "kotu", "an airport": "filin jirgin sama", "a country, a town": "ƙasa, gari", "Greece": "Girka", "New words: people and places": "Sababbin kalmomi: mutane da wurare", "ḥafeedun (pl. ḥafadatun)": "ḥafeedun (pl. ḥafadatun)", "naṣraaniyyun (pl. naṣaaraa)": "naṣraaniyyun (pl. naṣaaraa)", "kulliyyatun (pl. kulliyyaatun)": "kulliyyatun (pl. kulliyyaatun)", "kulliyyatuṭ-ṭibbi": "kulliyyatuṭ-ṭibbi", "kulliyyatul-handasati": "kulliyyatul-handasati", "kulliyyatush-sharee'ati": "kulliyyatush-sharee'ati", "kulliyyatut-tijaarati": "kulliyyatut-tijaarati", "maḥkamatun": "maḥkamatun", "maṭaarun": "maṭaarun", "baladun (pl. bilaadun)": "baladun (pl. bilaadun)", "al-yuunaanu": "al-yuunaanu", "a day": "rana", "a month": "wata", "Saturday": "Asabar", "New words: time": "Sababbin kalmomi: lokaci", "yawmun": "yawmun", "shahrun": "shahrun", "as-sabtu": "as-sabtu", "welcome!": "maraba!", "Peace be upon you. And upon you be peace, and Allah's mercy and blessings.": "Assalamu alaikum. Wa alaikumus salam wa rahmatullahi wa barakatuh.", "How are you, uncle? I am well, praise be to Allah.": "Yaya kake, baffa? Lafiya lau, godiya ta tabbata ga Allah.", "Who are you? We are the sons of Doctor Musa.": "Ku su wane ne? Mu 'ya'yan Likita Musa ne.", "Welcome! Your father is my friend.": "Maraba! Babanku abokina ne.", "Where is your new house? Our new house is near the airport.": "Ina sabon gidanku yake? Sabon gidanmu yana kusa da filin jirgin sama.", "I am in the faculty of engineering and Mahmud is in the faculty of medicine.": "Ina kwalejin injiniyanci kuma Mahmud yana kwalejin likitanci.", "We are Muslims. Allah is our Lord and Islam is our religion.": "Mu Musulmi ne. Allah ne Ubangijinmu kuma Musulunci ne addininmu.", "The question uses": "Tambayar tana amfani da", ". Answer about yourselves.": ". Amsa game da kanku.", "Answer about yourselves.": "Amsa game da kanku.", "Choose the right word.": "Zaɓi kalmar da ta dace.", "(your, all of you) ·": "wato naku, na dukanku ·", "(our)": "wato namu", "How do you say “our uncle”?": "Yaya ake cewa “baffanmu”?", "How do you say “your mother” (to a group)?": "Yaya ake cewa “mamarku”, ga rukuni?", "How do you say “our language”?": "Yaya ake cewa “harshenmu”?", "How do you say “your brother” (to a group)?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗan'uwanku”, ga rukuni?", "How do you say “our school”?": "Yaya ake cewa “makarantarmu”?", "How do you say “your language” (to a group)?": "Yaya ake cewa “harshenku”, ga rukuni?", "How do you say “your sister” (to a group)?": "Yaya ake cewa “'yar'uwarku”, ga rukuni?", "How do you say “our brother”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗan'uwanmu”?", "Talk to a group": "Yi magana da rukuni", "Now say it about a group:": "Yanzu ka faɗe shi game da rukuni:", "use": "yi amfani da", "Choose the Arabic question.": "Zaɓi tambayar Larabci.", "(which?)": "wato wane?", "“Which school are you in?”": "“A wace makaranta kake?”", "“Which month is this?”": "“Wane wata ne wannan?”", "“Which country are you from?”": "“Daga wace ƙasa kake?”", "“Which faculty is this?”": "“Wace kwaleji ce wannan?”", "“Which day is this?”": "“Wace rana ce wannan?”", "Listen, then write the word. (an airport)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato filin jirgin sama.", "أَيُّ؟ (which?)": "أَيُّ؟ Wato wane?", "“Which street is your house in?”": "“A wane titi gidanka yake?”", "Answer with نَحْنُ and ـنَا": "Amsa da نَحْنُ da ـنَا", "We went to the market.": "Mun tafi kasuwa.", "ـكُمْ (your, all of you)": "ـكُمْ, wato naku, na dukanku", "ـنَا (our)": "ـنَا, wato namu", "How do you say “your uncle” (to a group)?": "Yaya ake cewa “baffanku”, ga rukuni?", "How do you say “our father”?": "Yaya ake cewa “babanmu”?", "✅ Write: an airport": "✅ Rubuta: filin jirgin sama", "✅ “Which street is your house in?”": "✅ “A wane titi gidanka yake?”", "✅ Who are you (all)?": "✅ Ku su wane ne?", "✅ We went to the market.": "✅ Mun tafi kasuwa.", "✅ How do you say “your uncle” (to a group)?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “baffanku”, ga rukuni?", "✅ How do you say “our father”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “babanmu”?", "✅ “Which faculty is this?”": "✅ “Wace kwaleji ce wannan?”", "In this lesson you will talk to a group of women with": "A wannan darasi za ka yi magana da rukunin mata da", "You will complete the past tense:": "Za ka kammala lokacin da ya wuce, wato madi:", "when, and answer with": "yaushe, ka amsa da", "before, and": "kafin, da", "after. Finally you will see all the pronouns together.": "bayan. A ƙarshe za ka ga dukan wakilan suna, wato damiru, tare.", "Talking to a group of women, say": "Idan kana magana da rukunin mata, ka ce", "you all, and": "ku, da", "we, is for women too.": "mu, na mata ma ne.", "For one person:": "Ga mutum ɗaya:", "you went, to a man.": "ka tafi, ga namiji.", "to a woman.": "ga mace.", "I went.": "na tafi.", "For groups:": "Ga rukuni:", "you all went, for men.": "kun tafi, ga maza.", "for women.": "ga mata.", "when. Answer with": "yaushe. Amsa da", "before, or": "kafin, ko", "after.": "bayan.", "Here are all the pronouns. For one person:": "Ga dukan wakilan suna. Ga mutum ɗaya:", "For many people:": "Ga mutane da yawa:", "You all (women), when?": "Ku mata, yaushe?", "Which you?": "Wane ku?", "Your (women)": "Naku, mata", "He went, I went": "Ya tafi, na tafi", "When?": "Yaushe?", "In this lesson you will talk to a group of women with أَنْتُنَّ and بَيْتُكُنَّ. You will complete the past tense: ذَهَبْتَ، ذَهَبْتِ، ذَهَبْتُ، ذَهَبْتُمْ، ذَهَبْتُنَّ and ذَهَبْنَا. You will also ask مَتَى, when, and answer with قَبْلَ, before, and بَعْدَ, after. Finally you will see all the pronouns together.": "A wannan darasi za ka yi magana da rukunin mata da أَنْتُنَّ da بَيْتُكُنَّ. Za ka kammala lokacin da ya wuce, wato madi: ذَهَبْتَ، ذَهَبْتِ، ذَهَبْتُ، ذَهَبْتُمْ، ذَهَبْتُنَّ da ذَهَبْنَا. Za ka kuma tambaya مَتَى, yaushe, ka amsa da قَبْلَ, kafin, da بَعْدَ, bayan. A ƙarshe za ka ga dukan wakilan suna, wato damiru, tare.", "antunna": "antunna", "you all (women)": "ku, mata", "-kunna": "-kunna", "your (women)": "naku, mata", "Talking to a group of women:": "Magana da rukunin mata:", "(you all) and the ending": "wato ku, da ƙarshen", "(your). We (women) is also": "wato naku. Mu, na mata, ma shi ne", "Who are you, sisters?": "Ku su wace ne, 'yan'uwa mata?", "We are the daughters of Shaykh Abbas.": "Mu 'ya'yan Shehu Abbas ne mata.", "Your mother is my teacher. How is she?": "Mamarku malamata ce. Yaya take?", "Which school are you in? We are in middle school.": "A wace makaranta kuke? Muna makarantar tsakiya.", "dhahabta": "dhahabta", "you went (m)": "ka tafi, namiji", "dhahabti": "dhahabti", "you went (f)": "kin tafi, mace", "dhahabtu": "dhahabtu", "I went": "na tafi", "One person:": "Mutum ɗaya:", "(you, m) ·": "wato kai, namiji ·", "(you, f) ·": "wato ke, mace ·", "Where did you go, my brother?": "Ina ka tafi, ɗan'uwana?", "Where did you go, my sister?": "Ina kika tafi, 'yar'uwata?", "I went to the mosque.": "Na tafi masallaci.", "you all went (m)": "kun tafi, maza", "dhahabtunna": "dhahabtunna", "you all went (f)": "kun tafi, mata", "Groups:": "Rukuni:", "(you all, men) ·": "wato ku, maza ·", "(you all, women) ·": "wato ku, mata ·", "(we).": "wato mu.", "Where did you go, my brothers?": "Ina kuka tafi, 'yan'uwana maza?", "Where did you go, my sisters?": "Ina kuka tafi, 'yan'uwana mata?", "Did you go to school today? Yes, we went and came back.": "Kun tafi makaranta yau? I, mun tafi mun dawo.", "mataa?": "mataa?", ". Answer with": ". Amsa da", "(before) or": "wato kafin, ko", "(after) and a noun ending in -i.": "wato bayan, da suna mai ƙarewa da -i.", "before": "kafin", "When did she go? She went a week ago.": "Yaushe ta tafi? Ta tafi mako ɗaya da ya wuce.", "When did you leave the class, Muhammad? I left after the lesson.": "Yaushe ka fita daga ajin, Muhammadu? Na fita bayan darasin.", "I went to the mosque before the adhan.": "Na tafi masallaci kafin kiran sallah.", "When is your exam? Our exam is in a month.": "Yaushe jarrabawarku take? Jarrabawarmu bayan wata ɗaya ce.", "all the pronouns": "dukan wakilan suna", "one person": "mutum ɗaya", "many people": "mutane da yawa", "Here are all the pronouns. The right box is for": "Ga dukan wakilan suna. Akwatin dama na", ", the left box for": "ne, akwatin hagu na", ". Tap the examples.": "ne. Taɓa misalan.", "They (m) are students.": "Su, maza, ɗalibai ne.", "They (f) are students.": "Su, mata, ɗalibai ne.", "You (all, m) are students.": "Ku, maza, ɗalibai ne.", "You (all, f) are students.": "Ku, mata, ɗalibai ne.", "We are students.": "Mu ɗalibai ne.", "a week": "mako", "the adhan (call to prayer)": "kiran sallah, wato adhan", "the prayer": "sallah", "an exam, a test": "jarrabawa, gwaji", "he returned, came back": "ya dawo", "usbuu'un": "usbuu'un", "al-adhaanu": "al-adhaanu", "aṣ-ṣalaatu": "aṣ-ṣalaatu", "ikhtibaarun": "ikhtibaarun", "raja'a": "raja'a", "when?": "yaushe?", "Who are you, sisters? We are the daughters of Shaykh Abbas.": "Ku su wace ne, 'yan'uwa mata? Mu 'ya'yan Shehu Abbas ne mata.", "Welcome! Your mother is my teacher. How is she?": "Maraba! Mamarku malamata ce. Yaya take?", "Where is she now? She is in Riyadh now.": "Ina take yanzu? Tana Riyadh yanzu.", "Who went with her? Our brother Ibrahim went with her.": "Wane ne ya tafi tare da ita? Ɗan'uwanmu Ibrahim ne ya tafi tare da ita.", "Who are you talking to?": "Da wa kake magana?", "Ask a woman: Are you sick?": "Tambayi mace: Ba ki da lafiya?", "Ask some women: Are you doctors?": "Tambayi wasu mata: Ku likitoci ne?", "Ask a woman: Are you the teacher's daughter?": "Tambayi mace: Ke 'yar malamin ce?", "Ask a man: Are you a Muslim?": "Tambayi namiji: Kai Musulmi ne?", "Say: I am a Muslim (a man).": "Ka ce: Ni Musulmi ne, namiji.", "Ask some women: Are you Abbas's sisters?": "Tambayi wasu mata: Ku 'yan'uwan Abbas ne mata?", "Ask some men: Are you merchants?": "Tambayi wasu maza: Ku 'yan kasuwa ne?", "Change": "Canza", "Now talk to sisters": "Yanzu ka yi magana da 'yan'uwa mata", "Now ask some sisters:": "Yanzu ka tambayi wasu 'yan'uwa mata:", "Choose the right form of": "Zaɓi siffar da ta dace ta", "Who went?": "Wane ne ya tafi?", "How do you say “we went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “mun tafi”?", "How do you say “you all (women) went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kun tafi”, mata?", "How do you say “you all (men) went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kun tafi”, maza?", "How do you say “they (women) went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “sun tafi”, mata?", "How do you say “he went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ya tafi”?", "How do you say “you (a man) went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ka tafi”, ga namiji?", "How do you say “you (a woman) went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kin tafi”, ga mace?", "How do you say “she went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ta tafi”?", "Choose the Arabic sentence.": "Zaɓi jumlar Larabci.", "“My father went to Cairo a week ago.”": "“Babana ya tafi Alƙahira mako ɗaya da ya wuce.”", "“I went to the mosque before the adhan.”": "“Na tafi masallaci kafin kiran sallah.”", "“Our exam is in a month.”": "“Jarrabawarmu bayan wata ɗaya ce.”", "“I left the class after the lesson.”": "“Na fita daga ajin bayan darasin.”", "“He went to Riyadh a month ago.”": "“Ya tafi Riyadh wata ɗaya da ya wuce.”", "Listen, then write the word. (when?)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato yaushe?", "I left after the lesson.": "Na fita bayan darasin.", "✅ How do you say “you (a man) went”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ka tafi”, ga namiji?", "✅ “I went to the mosque before the adhan.”": "✅ “Na tafi masallaci kafin kiran sallah.”", "✅ How do you say “you (a woman) went”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “kin tafi”, ga mace?", "✅ How do you say “you all (women) went”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “kun tafi”, mata?", "✅ Ask a woman: Are you the teacher's daughter?": "✅ Tambayi mace: Ke 'yar malamin ce?", "✅ Who are you, sisters?": "✅ Ku su wace ne, 'yan'uwa mata?", "✅ Ask some women: Are you doctors?": "✅ Tambayi wasu mata: Ku likitoci ne?", "✅ Write: when?": "✅ Rubuta: yaushe?", "✅ Ask a man: Are you a Muslim?": "✅ Tambayi namiji: Kai Musulmi ne?", "✅ I left after the lesson.": "✅ Na fita bayan darasin.", "✅ “Our exam is in a month.”": "✅ “Jarrabawarmu bayan wata ɗaya ce.”", "In this lesson you will learn an important rule: the plural of things and animals is treated like one feminine word. So we say": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi wata muhimmiyar ƙa'ida: jam'in abubuwa da na dabbobi ana ɗaukar sa kamar kalmar mace ɗaya. Don haka muna cewa", "these are books, and": "waɗannan littattafai ne, da", "not": "ba", "You will also learn many new plurals.": "ba. Za ka kuma koyi sababbin jam'i da yawa.", "For a plural of people, use": "Ga jam'in mutane, yi amfani da", "For a plural of things or animals, use the feminine singular:": "Ga jam'in abubuwa ko dabbobi, yi amfani da tilon mace:", "Even for many pens, books or notebooks, say": "Ko da alƙalami da yawa ne, ko littattafai, ko littattafan rubutu, ka ce", "Far away:": "Nesa:", "those are houses. For people it is": "waɗancan gidaje ne. Ga mutane kuwa", "Here are more plurals to learn. Words with": "Ga ƙarin jam'i da za ka koya. Kalmomin da ke da", "usually end in": "yawanci suna ƙarewa da", "Plural of things": "Jam'in abubuwa", "هٰذِهِ or هٰؤُلَاءِ?": "هٰذِهِ ko هٰؤُلَاءِ?", "هِيَ or هُمْ?": "هِيَ ko هُمْ?", "In this lesson you will learn an important rule: the plural of things and animals is treated like one feminine word. So we say هٰذِهِ كُتُبٌ, these are books, and هِيَ, not هُمْ. You will also learn many new plurals.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi wata muhimmiyar ƙa'ida: jam'in abubuwa da na dabbobi ana ɗaukar sa kamar kalmar mace ɗaya. Don haka muna cewa هٰذِهِ كُتُبٌ, waɗannan littattafai ne, da هِيَ, ba هُمْ ba. Za ka kuma koyi sababbin jam'i da yawa.", "haadhihi kutubun": "haadhihi kutubun", "These are books.": "Waɗannan littattafai ne.", "For a plural of": "Ga jam'in", ". For a plural of": ". Ga jam'in", "things or animals": "abubuwa ko dabbobi", "use the feminine singular:": "yi amfani da tilon mace:", "This is a new student. He is from Belgium.": "Wannan sabon ɗalibi ne. Shi daga Beljiyam yake.", "These are new students. They are from Belgium.": "Waɗannan sababbin ɗalibai ne. Su daga Beljiyam suke.", "This is a new book. It is from Belgium.": "Wannan sabon littafi ne. Daga Beljiyam yake.", "These are new books. They are from Belgium.": "Waɗannan sababbin littattafai ne. Daga Beljiyam suke.", "liman haadhihil-aqlaamu?": "liman haadhihil-aqlaamu?", "Whose are these pens?": "Waɗannan alƙaluman na wane ne?", "Whose are these pens, Muhammad? They are mine, teacher.": "Waɗannan alƙaluman na wane ne, Muhammadu? Nawa ne, malam.", "And these new books, are they yours? No, they are Hamid's.": "Kuma waɗannan sababbin littattafan, naku ne? A'a, na Hamid ne.", "Where are your notebooks, brothers? They are here on this desk.": "Ina littattafan rubutunku suke, 'yan'uwa? Suna nan a kan wannan teburin.", "tilka buyuutun": "tilka buyuutun", "Those are houses.": "Waɗancan gidaje ne.", ". For people it is": ". Ga mutane kuwa", "plural of things": "jam'in abubuwa", "plural of people": "jam'in mutane", "This is a house → these are houses": "Wannan gida ne → waɗannan gidaje ne", "That is a house → those are houses": "Wancan gida ne → waɗancan gidaje ne", "That is a car → those are cars": "Waccan mota ce → waɗancan motoci ne", "new plurals": "sababbin jam'i", "Learn these plurals": "Koyi waɗannan jam'i", "More broken plurals. Words with": "Ƙarin jam'in taksiri. Kalmomin da ke da", "usually take": "yawanci suna ɗaukar", "star → stars": "tauraro → taurari", "pen → pens": "alƙalami → alƙaluma", "door → doors": "ƙofa → ƙofofi", "dog → dogs": "kare → karnuka", "notebook → notebooks": "littafin rubutu → littattafan rubutu", "bed → beds": "gado → gadaje", "a lesson": "darasi", "a river": "kogi", "a mountain": "dutse, tsauni", "a sea": "teku", "a hotel": "otal", "an airplane": "jirgin sama", "Belgium": "Beljiyam", "darsun (pl. duruusun)": "darsun (pl. duruusun)", "nahrun (pl. anhaarun)": "nahrun (pl. anhaarun)", "jabalun (pl. jibaalun)": "jabalun (pl. jibaalun)", "baḥrun (pl. biḥaarun)": "baḥrun (pl. biḥaarun)", "funduqun (pl. fanaadiqu)": "funduqun (pl. fanaadiqu)", "ṭaa'iratun (pl. ṭaa'iraatun)": "ṭaa'iratun (pl. ṭaa'iraatun)", "baljeekaa": "baljeekaa", "They are very beautiful. And these new books, are they yours?": "Suna da kyau sosai. Kuma waɗannan sababbin littattafan, naku ne?", "No, they are Hamid's.": "A'a, na Hamid ne.", ". People: use": ". Mutane: yi amfani da", "Which word points to them (near)?": "Wace kalma ce ke nuna su, a kusa?", "(men) or": "wato maza, ko", "(women).": "wato mata.", "“Those are houses.”": "“Waɗancan gidaje ne.”", "“They (the notebooks) are on the desk.”": "“Su, wato littattafan rubutun, suna kan teburin.”", "“These are new books.”": "“Waɗannan sababbin littattafai ne.”", "“These are new students.”": "“Waɗannan sababbin ɗalibai ne.”", "“These are cars.”": "“Waɗannan motoci ne.”", "They (the students) are from Belgium.": "Su, wato ɗaliban, daga Beljiyam suke.", "“Whose are these pens?”": "“Waɗannan alƙaluman na wane ne?”", "“Those are students.”": "“Waɗancan ɗalibai ne.”", "Listen, then write the word. (a river)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato kogi.", "✅ “Whose are these pens?”": "✅ “Waɗannan alƙaluman na wane ne?”", "✅ Which word points to them (near)?": "✅ Wace kalma ce ke nuna su, a kusa?", "✅ Whose are these pens?": "✅ Waɗannan alƙaluman na wane ne?", "✅ “Those are students.”": "✅ “Waɗancan ɗalibai ne.”", "✅ Write: a river": "✅ Rubuta: kogi", "✅ They (the students) are from Belgium.": "✅ Su, wato ɗaliban, daga Beljiyam suke.", "In this lesson you will use the rule from Lesson 16 with describing words. A plural of things is described with a feminine singular word:": "A wannan darasi za ka yi amfani da ƙa'idar Darasi na 16 tare da kalmomin siffantawa. Jam'in abubuwa ana siffanta shi da kalmar tilon mace:", "the doors are open. You will also learn the words for company, cheap and many.": "ƙofofin a buɗe suke. Za ka kuma koyi kalmomin kamfani, mai arha da mai yawa.", "A plural of things takes a describing word in the feminine singular, with": "Jam'in abubuwa yana ɗaukar kalmar siffantawa a tilon mace, tare da", "the doors are open.": "ƙofofin a buɗe suke.", "For people, the describing word is plural too:": "Ga mutane, kalmar siffantawa ma jam'i ce:", "For things, it is feminine singular:": "Ga abubuwa, tilon mace ce:", "many, follows the same rule:": "wato mai yawa, yana bin ƙa'ida iri ɗaya:", "many languages.": "harsuna da yawa.", "The doors are open": "Ƙofofin a buɗe suke", "In this lesson you will use the rule from Lesson 16 with describing words. A plural of things is described with a feminine singular word: الْأَبْوَابُ مَفْتُوحَةٌ, the doors are open. You will also learn the words for company, cheap and many.": "A wannan darasi za ka yi amfani da ƙa'idar Darasi na 16 tare da kalmomin siffantawa. Jam'in abubuwa ana siffanta shi da kalmar tilon mace: الْأَبْوَابُ مَفْتُوحَةٌ, ƙofofin a buɗe suke. Za ka kuma koyi kalmomin kamfani, mai arha da mai yawa.", "al-baabu maftuuḥun": "al-baabu maftuuḥun", "al-abwaabu maftuuḥatun": "al-abwaabu maftuuḥatun", "The doors are open.": "Ƙofofin a buɗe suke.", "A plural of": "Jam'in", "takes a describing word in the": "yana ɗaukar kalmar siffantawa a", "feminine singular": "tilon mace", ", with": ", tare da", "The doors of the mosque are open.": "Ƙofofin masallacin a buɗe suke.", "The stars are beautiful.": "Taurarin suna da kyau.", "These lessons are easy.": "Waɗannan darussan suna da sauƙi.", "Those beds are broken.": "Waɗancan gadajen sun karye.", "aṭ-ṭullaabu judud": "aṭ-ṭullaabu judud", "The students are new.": "Ɗaliban sababbi ne.", "al-kutubu jadeedatun": "al-kutubu jadeedatun", "The books are new.": "Littattafan sababbi ne.", "the describing word is plural too:": "kalmar siffantawa ma jam'i ce:", "it is feminine singular:": "tilon mace ce:", "plural": "jam'i", "Where are the new books? They are in the library.": "Ina sababbin littattafan suke? Suna ɗakin karatu.", "Whose are these new houses? They belong to the company director.": "Waɗannan sababbin gidajen na wane ne? Mallakar daraktan kamfanin ne.", "In this street there are big hotels.": "A wannan titin akwai manyan otal-otal.", "lughaatun katheeratun": "lughaatun katheeratun", "many languages": "harsuna da yawa", "(many) follows the same rule:": "wato mai yawa, yana bin ƙa'ida iri ɗaya:", "(many languages).": "wato harsuna da yawa.", "In India there are many languages.": "A Indiya akwai harsuna da yawa.", "The Japanese watch is cheap.": "Agogon Japan yana da arha.", "These donkeys belong to the farmer.": "Waɗannan jakunan mallakar manomin ne.", "a company": "kamfani", "the company director": "daraktan kamfanin", "cheap": "mai arha", "many, a lot": "mai yawa, da yawa", "shirts": "riguna", "sharikatun (pl. sharikaatun)": "sharikatun (pl. sharikaatun)", "mudeerush-sharikati": "mudeerush-sharikati", "rakheeṣun": "rakheeṣun", "katheerun": "katheerun", "qumṣaanun": "qumṣaanun", "Where are your books, sisters? They are in the classroom.": "Ina littattafanku suke, 'yan'uwa mata? Suna cikin ajin.", "These are my books and those are my sister's books.": "Waɗannan littattafaina ne kuma waɗancan littattafan 'yar'uwata ne.", "Things: feminine singular describing word. People: plural describing word.": "Abubuwa: kalmar siffantawa ta tilon mace. Mutane: kalmar siffantawa ta jam'i.", "Make it plural:": "Mayar da shi jam'i:", "Is it a plural of things or of people?": "Jam'in abubuwa ne ko na mutane?", "Choose the describing word": "Zaɓi kalmar siffantawa", "“In this street there are big hotels.”": "“A wannan titin akwai manyan otal-otal.”", "“In India there are many languages.”": "“A Indiya akwai harsuna da yawa.”", "“The Japanese watch is cheap.”": "“Agogon Japan yana da arha.”", "“Those beds are broken.”": "“Waɗancan gadajen sun karye.”", "“These lessons are easy.”": "“Waɗannan darussan suna da sauƙi.”", "Listen, then write the word. (cheap)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato mai arha.", "“The doors of the mosque are open.”": "“Ƙofofin masallacin a buɗe suke.”", "✅ “The Japanese watch is cheap.”": "✅ “Agogon Japan yana da arha.”", "✅ Write: cheap": "✅ Rubuta: mai arha", "✅ “The doors of the mosque are open.”": "✅ “Ƙofofin masallacin a buɗe suke.”", "✅ The stars are beautiful.": "✅ Taurarin suna da kyau.", "✅ These lessons are easy.": "✅ Waɗannan darussan suna da sauƙi.", "✅ “In this street there are big hotels.”": "✅ “A wannan titin akwai manyan otal-otal.”", "In this lesson you will learn the special Arabic form for exactly two, like": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi siffar Larabci ta musamman don abu biyu daidai, wato tasniya, kamar", "two books. You will learn": "littattafai biyu. Za ka koyi", "these two, and": "waɗannan biyun, da", "they two. You will also ask": "su biyun. Za ka kuma tambaya", "how many, and learn the two Eids.": "nawa, ka koyi Sallolin Idi biyu.", "Arabic has a special form for two.": "Larabci yana da siffa ta musamman don abu biyu.", "two books. A word with": "littattafai biyu. Kalmar da ke da", "two cars.": "motoci biyu.", "is for two masculine things,": "na abubuwa biyu ne na namiji,", "for two feminine things. For they two, say": "na abubuwa biyu na mace. Don su biyun, ka ce", "how many, use one noun with two": "nawa, yi amfani da suna ɗaya mai fatha biyu", "how many brothers?": "'yan'uwa maza nawa?", "how many cars?": "motoci nawa?", "The two Eids are": "Idodin biyu su ne", "Note that one and two come after the noun.": "Ka lura cewa ɗaya da biyu suna zuwa bayan sunan.", "Two of them": "Biyu daga cikinsu", "هٰذَانِ or هٰتَانِ?": "هٰذَانِ ko هٰتَانِ?", "How many?": "Nawa?", "Answer with two": "Amsa da biyu", "To make two:": "Don yin biyu:", "A word with": "Kalmar da ke da", "In this lesson you will learn the special Arabic form for exactly two, like كِتَابَانِ, two books. You will learn هٰذَانِ and هٰتَانِ, these two, and هُمَا, they two. You will also ask كَمْ, how many, and learn the two Eids.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi siffar Larabci ta musamman don abu biyu daidai, wato tasniya, kamar كِتَابَانِ, littattafai biyu. Za ka koyi هٰذَانِ da هٰتَانِ, waɗannan biyun, da هُمَا, su biyun. Za ka kuma tambaya كَمْ, nawa, ka koyi Sallolin Idi biyu.", "kitaabaani": "kitaabaani", "two books": "littattafai biyu", "Arabic has a special form for": "Larabci yana da siffa ta musamman don", "two": "biyu", ": add": ": ƙara", "(-aani) to the word. A word with": "wato -aani, ga kalmar. Kalmar da ke da", "a book → two books": "littafi → littattafai biyu", "a car → two cars": "mota → motoci biyu", "a sister → two sisters": "'yar'uwa → 'yan'uwa mata biyu", "an Eid → two Eids": "Idi → Idodi biyu", "haadhaani": "haadhaani", "these two (m)": "waɗannan biyun, namiji", "haataani": "haataani", "these two (f)": "waɗannan biyun, mace", "for two masculine things,": "don abubuwa biyu na namiji,", "for two feminine things. For “they two” say": "don abubuwa biyu na mace. Don “su biyun” ka ce", "(m and f).": "ga namiji da mace.", "these two notebooks": "waɗannan littattafan rubutu biyu", "these two rulers": "waɗannan rulan biyu", "Whose are these two notebooks? They are mine.": "Waɗannan littattafan rubutu biyu na wane ne? Nawa ne.", "Whose are these two rulers? They are mine.": "Waɗannan rulan biyu na wane ne? Nawa ne.", "Whose are these two cows? They belong to the farmer.": "Waɗannan shanu biyu na wane ne? Mallakar manomin ne.", "kam akhan laka?": "kam akhan laka?", "How many brothers do you have?": "'Yan'uwa maza nawa kake da su?", "noun ending in": "suna mai ƙarewa da", "-an": "-an", "ends in": "yana ƙarewa da", "How many brothers do you have, Muhammad? I have one brother.": "'Yan'uwa maza nawa kake da su, Muhammadu? Ina da ɗan'uwa ɗaya.", "And how many sisters do you have? I have two sisters.": "Kuma 'yan'uwa mata nawa kake da su? Ina da 'yan'uwa mata biyu.", "How many wheels does a bicycle have? It has two wheels.": "Keke yana da tayoyi nawa? Yana da tayoyi biyu.", "How many Eids are in a year? There are two Eids in a year.": "Idi nawa ne a shekara? Akwai Idi biyu a shekara.", "'eedul-fiṭri": "'eedul-fiṭri", "Eid al-Fitr": "Ƙaramar Sallah, wato Idin Fiddu", "'eedul-aḍḥaa": "'eedul-aḍḥaa", "Eid al-Adha": "Babbar Sallah, wato Idin Layya", "The two Eids of the year.": "Idodin biyu na shekara.", "One": "Ɗaya", "come after the noun:": "suna zuwa bayan sunan:", "(one brother),": "wato ɗan'uwa ɗaya,", "(two big stores).": "wato manyan shaguna biyu.", "They are Eid al-Fitr and Eid al-Adha.": "Su ne Ƙaramar Sallah da Babbar Sallah.", "He has two big stores.": "Yana da manyan shaguna biyu.", "The Fajr prayer is two rak'ahs.": "Sallar Asuba raka'a biyu ce.", "I have two eyes, two ears, two hands and two feet.": "Ina da idanu biyu, kunnuwa biyu, hannaye biyu da ƙafafu biyu.", "the Eid (festival)": "Idin, wato sallah", "the year": "shekarar", "a wheel": "taya", "a neighbourhood": "unguwa", "a riyal (money)": "riyal, wato kuɗi", "a rak'ah (unit of prayer)": "raka'a, wato sashen sallah", "a ruler (for lines)": "rula, don zana layi", "a store, a shop": "shago, kanti", "al-'eedu (pl. a'yaadun)": "al-'eedu (pl. a'yaadun)", "as-sanatu (pl. sanawaatun)": "as-sanatu (pl. sanawaatun)", "'ajalatun (pl. 'ajalaatun)": "'ajalatun (pl. 'ajalaatun)", "ḥayyun (pl. aḥyaa'un)": "ḥayyun (pl. aḥyaa'un)", "riyaalun (pl. riyaalaatun)": "riyaalun (pl. riyaalaatun)", "rak'atun (pl. raka'aatun)": "rak'atun (pl. raka'aatun)", "misṭaratun (pl. masaaṭiru)": "misṭaratun (pl. masaaṭiru)", "matjarun": "matjarun", "they two": "su biyun", "how many?": "nawa?", "How many wheels does a bicycle have, Hamid? It has two wheels.": "Keke yana da tayoyi nawa, Hamid? Yana da tayoyi biyu.", "Your father is a big merchant. How many stores does he have? He has two big stores.": "Babanka babban ɗan kasuwa ne. Shaguna nawa yake da su? Yana da manyan shaguna biyu.", "Make it “two”": "Mayar da shi “biyu”", "Add -aani:": "Ƙara -aani:", ". With": ". Da", "How do you say two of them?": "Yaya ake cewa biyu daga cikinsu?", "Now say it about two:": "Yanzu ka faɗe shi game da biyu:", "Choose the correct question.": "Zaɓi tambayar da ta dace.", "+ one noun ending in -an": "tare da suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da -an", "“How many mosques are in your village?”": "“Masallatai nawa ne a ƙauyenku?”", "“How many cars are at the university?”": "“Motoci nawa ne a jami'ar?”", "“How many pens do you have?”": "“Alƙaluma nawa kake da su?”", "“How many books do you have?”": "“Littattafai nawa kake da su?”", "“How many windows are in your room?”": "“Tagogi nawa ne a ɗakinka?”", "“How many brothers do you have?”": "“'Yan'uwa maza nawa kake da su?”", "Answer with the form for two.": "Amsa da siffar biyu.", "Answer the question": "Amsa tambayar", "I have two sisters.": "Ina da 'yan'uwa mata biyu.", "There are two Eids in a year.": "Akwai Idi biyu a shekara.", "كَمْ + one noun ending in -an": "كَمْ tare da suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da -an", "Listen, then write the word. (how many?)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato nawa?", "✅ There are two Eids in a year.": "✅ Akwai Idi biyu a shekara.", "✅ “How many windows are in your room?”": "✅ “Tagogi nawa ne a ɗakinka?”", "✅ Write: how many?": "✅ Rubuta: nawa?", "✅ “How many cars are at the university?”": "✅ “Motoci nawa ne a jami'ar?”", "✅ Choose the right answer.": "✅ Zaɓi amsar da ta dace.", "✅ I have two sisters.": "✅ Ina da 'yan'uwa mata biyu.", "✅ How do you say two of them?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa biyu daga cikinsu?", "In this lesson you will count from three to ten with masculine words, like": "A wannan darasi za ka ƙirga daga uku zuwa goma da kalmomin namiji, kamar", "three students. The number comes first, and the word after it is plural, ending in a": "ɗalibai uku. Lambar tana zuwa farko, kuma kalmar da ke bayanta jam'i ce, mai ƙarewa da", "You will also learn words for price, bus, passenger and question.": "Za ka kuma koyi kalmomin farashi, bas, fasinja da tambaya.", "Here are the numbers from three to ten, used with masculine words.": "Ga lambobi daga uku zuwa goma, waɗanda ake amfani da su da kalmomin namiji.", "The number comes first. The word after it is plural and ends in": "Lambar tana zuwa farko. Kalmar da ke bayanta jam'i ce kuma tana ƙarewa da", "three students.": "ɗalibai uku.", "Remember: after": "Ka tuna: bayan", "use one noun with two fathas. Answer with the number and the plural.": "yi amfani da suna ɗaya mai fatha biyu. Ka amsa da lambar da jam'in.", "Listen to this short text about students from different countries.": "Saurari wannan gajeren rubutu game da ɗalibai daga ƙasashe daban-daban.", "Numbers 3–10 (masculine)": "Lambobi 3 zuwa 10, na namiji", "Which number?": "Wace lamba?", "Count them": "Ƙirga su", "Answer": "Amsa", "In this lesson you will count from three to ten with masculine words, like ثَلَاثَةُ طُلَّابٍ, three students. The number comes first, and the word after it is plural, ending in a كَسْرَةْ. You will also learn words for price, bus, passenger and question.": "A wannan darasi za ka ƙirga daga uku zuwa goma da kalmomin namiji, kamar ثَلَاثَةُ طُلَّابٍ, ɗalibai uku. Lambar tana zuwa farko, kuma kalmar da ke bayanta jam'i ce, mai ƙarewa da كَسْرَةْ. Za ka kuma koyi kalmomin farashi, bas, fasinja da tambaya.", "the numbers 3 to 10": "lambobi 3 zuwa 10", "These are the numbers you use with": "Waɗannan su ne lambobin da kake amfani da su da kalmomin", "words. Tap each one to hear it.": "namiji. Taɓa kowace ɗaya don jin ta.", "thalaathatu ṭullaabin": "thalaathatu ṭullaabin", "three students": "ɗalibai uku", "The number comes": "Lambar tana zuwa", "first": "farko", ". The word after it is": ". Kalmar da ke bayanta", "and ends in a kasra (": "ce, kuma tana ƙarewa da kasra (", "-in": "-in", "five books": "littattafai biyar", "six sons": "'ya'ya maza shida", "ten students": "ɗalibai goma", "kam kitaaban 'indaka?": "kam kitaaban 'indaka?", "How many books do you have?": "Littattafai nawa kake da su?", "Remember Lesson 18: after": "Ka tuna Darasi na 18: bayan", "noun ending in -an. Answer with the number + plural.": "suna mai ƙarewa da -an. Ka amsa da lambar tare da jam'i.", "How many books do you have? I have three books.": "Littattafai nawa kake da su? Ina da littattafai uku.", "How many brothers do you have, Aminah? I have four brothers.": "'Yan'uwa maza nawa kike da su, Aminatu? Ina da 'yan'uwa maza huɗu.", "What is the price of this book? Its price is seven and a half riyals.": "Nawa ne farashin wannan littafi? Farashinsa riyal bakwai da rabi ne.", "old students": "tsofaffin ɗalibai", "new students": "sababbin ɗalibai", "A reading: our class": "Karatu: ajinmu", "How many new students are in your class, Shaykh?": "Sababbin ɗalibai nawa ne a ajinka, Malam?", "There are ten new students in it.": "Akwai sababbin ɗalibai goma a cikinsa.", "They are from different countries. Three students are from the Philippines and four students from Japan.": "Sun fito daga ƙasashe daban-daban. Ɗalibai uku daga Filifin suke kuma ɗalibai huɗu daga Japan.", "And there are seven students from America. Are they new? No, they are old students.": "Kuma akwai ɗalibai bakwai daga Amurka. Shin sababbi ne? A'a, su tsofaffin ɗalibai ne.", "How many students are from Europe? Five from England and eight from Germany.": "Ɗalibai nawa ne daga Turai? Biyar daga Ingila da takwas daga Jamus.", "a price": "farashi", "a half": "rabi", "a piastre (small coin)": "kwabo, wato ƙaramin kuɗi", "a bus": "bas", "a passenger": "fasinja", "a question": "tambaya", "a pocket": "aljihu", "Europe": "Turai", "Malaysia": "Malaysia", "different": "daban-daban", "thamanun": "thamanun", "niṣfun": "niṣfun", "qirshun (pl. quruushun)": "qirshun (pl. quruushun)", "ḥaafilatun (pl. ḥaafilaatun)": "ḥaafilatun (pl. ḥaafilaatun)", "raakibun (pl. rukkaabun)": "raakibun (pl. rukkaabun)", "su'aalun (pl. as'ilatun)": "su'aalun (pl. as'ilatun)", "jaybun (pl. juyuubun)": "jaybun (pl. juyuubun)", "uurubbaa": "uurubbaa", "maaleeziyaa": "maaleeziyaa", "mukhtalifun": "mukhtalifun", "three students, four students, five students": "ɗalibai uku, ɗalibai huɗu, ɗalibai biyar", "six students, seven students, eight students": "ɗalibai shida, ɗalibai bakwai, ɗalibai takwas", "nine students, ten students": "ɗalibai tara, ɗalibai goma", "I have five books and three pens.": "Ina da littattafai biyar da alƙaluma uku.", "There are seven days in a week.": "Akwai kwanaki bakwai a mako.", "What is the price of this book? Seven and a half riyals.": "Nawa ne farashin wannan littafi? Riyal bakwai da rabi.", "Listen and choose the number.": "Saurara ka zaɓi lambar.", "Which number is it?": "Wace lamba ce?", "Which number is this?": "Wace lamba ce wannan?", "The number has": "Lambar tana da", "Count with masculine words": "Ƙirga da kalmomin namiji", ". The word after it is plural with a kasra.": ". Kalmar da ke bayanta jam'i ce mai kasra.", "How do you say “9 houses”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gidaje 9”?", "The word after it is plural with a": "Kalmar da ke bayanta jam'i ce mai", "How do you say “5 piastres”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kwabo 5”?", "How do you say “6 sons”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'ya'ya maza 6”?", "How do you say “{0} students”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai {0}”?", "How do you say “7 days”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kwanaki 7”?", "How do you say “4 pens”?": "Yaya ake cewa “alƙaluma 4”?", "How do you say “5 books”?": "Yaya ake cewa “littattafai 5”?", "Choose the answer with the right number.": "Zaɓi amsar da ke da lambar da ta dace.", "Answer with the number": "Amsa da lambar", "Answer: {0}": "Amsa: {0}", "“I have five books and three pens.”": "“Ina da littattafai biyar da alƙaluma uku.”", "“In this neighbourhood there are nine new houses.”": "“A wannan unguwa akwai sababbin gidaje tara.”", "“On this bus there are ten passengers.”": "“A cikin wannan bas akwai fasinjoji goma.”", "“Khalid has six sons.”": "“Khalid yana da 'ya'ya maza shida.”", "“This car has four doors.”": "“Wannan mota tana da ƙofofi huɗu.”", "I have three books.": "Ina da littattafai uku.", "“There are seven days in a week.”": "“Akwai kwanaki bakwai a mako.”", "Listen, then write the word. (a question)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato tambaya.", "How do you say “8 riyals”?": "Yaya ake cewa “riyal 8”?", "✅ “On this bus there are ten passengers.”": "✅ “A cikin wannan bas akwai fasinjoji goma.”", "✅ Which number is this?": "✅ Wace lamba ce wannan?", "✅ Answer: {0}": "✅ Amsa: {0}", "✅ How do you say “5 piastres”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “kwabo 5”?", "✅ There are ten new students in it.": "✅ Akwai sababbin ɗalibai goma a cikinsa.", "✅ “There are seven days in a week.”": "✅ “Akwai kwanaki bakwai a mako.”", "✅ Write: a question": "✅ Rubuta: tambaya", "✅ How do you say “8 riyals”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “riyal 8”?", "✅ There are seven days in a week.": "✅ Akwai kwanaki bakwai a mako.", "In this lesson you will count from three to ten with feminine words, like": "A wannan darasi za ka ƙirga daga uku zuwa goma da kalmomin mace, kamar", "three female students. Here the number has no": "ɗalibai mata uku. A nan lambar ba ta da", "It is the opposite of Lesson 19. You will also learn words for magazine, letter and word.": "Wannan akasin Darasi na 19 ne. Za ka kuma koyi kalmomin mujalla, harafi da kalma.", "With feminine words, the number has no": "Da kalmomin mace, lambar ba ta da", "three female students.": "ɗalibai mata uku.", "It is the opposite. A masculine word takes the number with": "Akasin haka ne. Kalmar namiji tana ɗaukar lamba mai", "A feminine word takes the number without it. Look at the singular word to decide.": "Kalmar mace tana ɗaukar lamba ba tare da ita ba. Ka duba kalmar a tilo don ka yanke shawara.", "Listen to the dialogue between": "Saurari tattaunawa tsakanin", "Numbers 3–10 (feminine)": "Lambobi 3 zuwa 10, na mace", "With or without ة?": "Da ة ko ba tare da ita ba?", "In this lesson you will count from three to ten with feminine words, like ثَلَاثُ طَالِبَاتٍ, three female students. Here the number has no تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ. It is the opposite of Lesson 19. You will also learn words for magazine, letter and word.": "A wannan darasi za ka ƙirga daga uku zuwa goma da kalmomin mace, kamar ثَلَاثُ طَالِبَاتٍ, ɗalibai mata uku. A nan lambar ba ta da تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ. Wannan akasin Darasi na 19 ne. Za ka kuma koyi kalmomin mujalla, harafi da kalma.", "thalaathu ṭaalibaatin": "thalaathu ṭaalibaatin", "three female students": "ɗalibai mata uku", "words the number has": "kalmomin, lambar tana da", ". Tap each number to hear it.": ". Taɓa kowace lamba don jin ta.", "{0} students (f)": "ɗalibai mata {0}", "thalaathatu ikhwatin": "thalaathatu ikhwatin", "three brothers": "'yan'uwa maza uku", "thalaathu akhawaatin": "thalaathu akhawaatin", "three sisters": "'yan'uwa mata uku", "It is the": "Shi ne", "opposite": "akasi", ": masculine word → number": ": kalmar namiji → lamba", ". Feminine word → number": ". Kalmar mace → lamba", "without": "ba tare da ita ba", ". Look at the": ". Ka duba kalmar a", "singular": "tilo", "word to decide:": "don ka yanke shawara:", "is masculine,": "na namiji ne,", "is feminine.": "na mace ne.", "masculine word → number with ة": "kalmar namiji → lamba mai ة", "feminine word → number without ة": "kalmar mace → lamba ba tare da ة ba", "I have three sisters and five brothers.": "Ina da 'yan'uwa mata uku da 'yan'uwa maza biyar.", "I have four brothers and four sisters.": "Ina da 'yan'uwa maza huɗu da 'yan'uwa mata huɗu.", "She has eight brothers and eight sisters.": "Tana da 'yan'uwa maza takwas da 'yan'uwa mata takwas.", "a dialogue": "tattaunawa", "Two students talk about their class": "Ɗalibai mata biyu suna magana game da ajinsu", "Salma, are there students from China and Japan in your class?": "Salma, akwai ɗalibai daga China da Japan a ajinki?", "Yes. In our class there are five from China, four from Japan and eight from Indonesia.": "I. A ajinmu akwai biyar daga China, huɗu daga Japan da takwas daga Indonesiya.", "And in our class there are three from India, six from the Philippines and seven from Turkey.": "Kuma a ajinmu akwai uku daga Indiya, shida daga Filifin da bakwai daga Turkiyya.", "How many sisters do you have, Layla? I have three sisters.": "'Yan'uwa mata nawa kike da su, Laila? Ina da 'yan'uwa mata uku.", "And how many brothers? I have five brothers.": "Kuma 'yan'uwa maza nawa? Ina da 'yan'uwa maza biyar.", "a magazine": "mujalla", "a letter (of the alphabet)": "harafi, na baƙaƙe", "a word": "kalma", "Indonesia": "Indonesiya", "Turkey": "Turkiyya", "majallatun (pl. majallaatun)": "majallatun (pl. majallaatun)", "ḥarfun (pl. ḥuruufun)": "ḥarfun (pl. ḥuruufun)", "kalimatun (pl. kalimaatun)": "kalimatun (pl. kalimaatun)", "indooneesiyaa": "indooneesiyaa", "turkiyaa": "turkiyaa", "{0} (with feminine words)": "{0}, da kalmomin mace", "three, four, five students (f)": "ɗalibai mata uku, huɗu, biyar", "six, seven, eight students (f)": "ɗalibai mata shida, bakwai, takwas", "nine, ten students (f)": "ɗalibai mata tara, goma", "You have three sisters and five brothers.": "Kana da 'yan'uwa mata uku da 'yan'uwa maza biyar.", "In our house there are three rooms.": "A gidanmu akwai ɗakuna uku.", "In that lesson there are eight new words.": "A wancan darasin akwai sababbin kalmomi takwas.", "Masculine word: number with": "Kalmar namiji: lamba mai", "Masculine or feminine word?": "Kalmar namiji ce ko ta mace?", ". Feminine word: number without": ". Kalmar mace: lamba ba tare da", "How do you say “8 words”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kalmomi 8”?", "One of them:": "Ɗaya daga cikinsu:", "Feminine word: number without": "Kalmar mace: lamba ba tare da", "How do you say “4 books”?": "Yaya ake cewa “littattafai 4”?", "How do you say “3 female students”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai mata 3”?", "How do you say “10 magazines”?": "Yaya ake cewa “mujallu 10”?", "How do you say “8 female teachers”?": "Yaya ake cewa “malamai mata 8”?", "How do you say “5 brothers”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'yan'uwa maza 5”?", "How do you say “{0} cars”?": "Yaya ake cewa “motoci {0}”?", "How do you say “5 sisters”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'yan'uwa mata 5”?", "“At the university there are ten buses.”": "“A jami'ar akwai bas goma.”", "“In our house there are three rooms.”": "“A gidanmu akwai ɗakuna uku.”", "“I have three magazines.”": "“Ina da mujallu uku.”", "“In that lesson there are eight new words.”": "“A wancan darasin akwai sababbin kalmomi takwas.”", "“Abbas has seven daughters.”": "“Abbas yana da 'ya'ya mata bakwai.”", "I have five brothers.": "Ina da 'yan'uwa maza biyar.", "How do you say “7 daughters”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'ya'ya mata 7”?", "Listen, then write the word. (a letter (of the alphabet))": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato harafi, na baƙaƙe.", "✅ I have five brothers.": "✅ Ina da 'yan'uwa maza biyar.", "✅ How do you say “7 daughters”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “'ya'ya mata 7”?", "✅ Write: a letter (of the alphabet)": "✅ Rubuta: harafi, na baƙaƙe", "✅ “I have three magazines.”": "✅ “Ina da mujallu uku.”", "✅ “In our house there are three rooms.”": "✅ “A gidanmu akwai ɗakuna uku.”", "✅ In our house there are three rooms.": "✅ A gidanmu akwai ɗakuna uku.", "✅ How do you say “4 books”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “littattafai 4”?", "✅ How do you say “7 days”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “kwanaki 7”?", "In this lesson you will read a text called": "A wannan darasi za ka karanta rubutu mai suna", "my school. It brings together much of what you have learned. You will learn the words for colour and qiblah,": "makarantata. Ya tattaro yawancin abin da ka koya. Za ka koyi kalmomin launi da alƙibla,", "another word for that, and": "wata kalma ta wancan, da", "but. You will also learn which countries are in Asia, Africa and Europe.": "amma. Za ka kuma koyi ƙasashen da ke Asiya, Afirka da Turai.", "my school. Tap any sentence to hear it again and see its meaning.": "makarantata. Taɓa kowace jumla don sake jin ta ka ga ma'anarta.", "is another way to say": "wata hanya ce ta faɗar", "that.": "wancan.", "means but. It joins two ideas that are different.": "ma'anarsa amma. Yana haɗa ra'ayoyi biyu da suka bambanta.", "Plurals like": "Jam'i kamar", "You will learn why in Lesson 22.": "Za ka koyi dalilin a Darasi na 22.", "My school": "Makarantata", "True or false?": "Gaskiya ko ƙarya?", "Continents": "Nahiyoyi", "In this lesson you will read a text called مَدْرَسَتِي, my school. It brings together much of what you have learned. You will learn the words for colour and qiblah, ذَاكَ, another word for that, and لٰكِنْ, but. You will also learn which countries are in Asia, Africa and Europe.": "A wannan darasi za ka karanta rubutu mai suna مَدْرَسَتِي, makarantata. Ya tattaro yawancin abin da ka koya. Za ka koyi kalmomin launi da alƙibla, ذَاكَ, wata kalma ta wancan, da لٰكِنْ, amma. Za ka kuma koyi ƙasashen da ke Asiya, Afirka da Turai.", "madrasatee": "madrasatee", "My school (the text)": "Makarantata, rubutun", "Listen to the whole text. Tap any sentence to hear it again and see its meaning.": "Saurari dukan rubutun. Taɓa kowace jumla don sake jin ta ka ga ma'anarta.", "This is my school. It is near the mosque.": "Wannan makarantata ce. Tana kusa da masallaci.", "It is a big school with three doors. Its doors are open now.": "Babbar makaranta ce mai ƙofofi uku. Ƙofofinta a buɗe suke yanzu.", "In the school there are many classrooms. This is our classroom, and it is spacious.": "A makarantar akwai ajujuwa da yawa. Wannan ajinmu ne, kuma yana da faɗi.", "It has two big windows, desks and chairs, and a big blackboard.": "Yana da manyan tagogi biyu, tebura da kujeru, da babban allon rubutu.", "This is the teacher's desk and that is his chair. And those are the students' desks and chairs.": "Wannan teburin malamin ne kuma wancan kujerarsa ce. Kuma waɗancan teburan ɗalibai ne da kujerunsu.", "The teacher's desk is big and the students' desks are small.": "Teburin malamin babba ne kuma teburan ɗaliban ƙanana ne.", "In our class there are ten students, and they are from different countries.": "A ajinmu akwai ɗalibai goma, kuma sun fito daga ƙasashe daban-daban.", "This is Muhammad, from Japan. This is Ibrahim, from Ghana. This is Isma'il, from Nigeria.": "Wannan Muhammadu ne, daga Japan. Wannan Ibrahim ne, daga Ghana. Wannan Isma'ila ne, daga Najeriya.", "They are from different countries, their languages are different and their colours are different.": "Sun fito daga ƙasashe daban-daban, harsunansu sun bambanta kuma launukansu sun bambanta.", "But their religion is one, their Lord is one, their Prophet is one, and their qiblah is one.": "Amma addininsu ɗaya ne, Ubangijinsu ɗaya ne, Annabinsu ɗaya ne, kuma alƙiblarsu ɗaya ce.", "They are Muslims, and Muslims are brothers.": "Su Musulmi ne, kuma Musulmi 'yan'uwa ne.", "This is our teacher, Shaykh Bilal. He is from Madinah, and he is a righteous man. We love him very much.": "Wannan malaminmu ne, Shehu Bilal. Shi daga Madina yake, kuma mutum ne nagari. Muna son sa sosai.", "dhaaka": "dhaaka", "(that).": "wato wancan.", "This is the teacher's desk and that is his chair.": "Wannan teburin malamin ne kuma wancan kujerarsa ce.", "laakin": "laakin", "but": "amma", "(but) joins two ideas that are different.": "wato amma, yana haɗa ra'ayoyi biyu da suka bambanta.", "Their languages are different, but their religion is one.": "Harsunansu sun bambanta, amma addininsu ɗaya ne.", "desk": "tebur", "makaatibu": "makaatibu", "desks": "tebura", "never take -un. You will learn why in Lesson 22.": "ba sa taɓa samun -un. Za ka koyi dalilin a Darasi na 22.", "desk → desks": "tebur → tebura", "chair → chairs": "kujera → kujeru", "colour → colours": "launi → launuka", "desks (plural of مَكْتَبٌ)": "tebura, jam'in مَكْتَبٌ", "chairs (plural of كُرْسِيٌّ)": "kujeru, jam'in كُرْسِيٌّ", "a colour": "launi", "the qiblah (direction of prayer)": "alƙibla, wato inda ake fuskanta a sallah", "wide, spacious": "mai faɗi", "righteous, good": "nagari, salihi", "karaasiyyu": "karaasiyyu", "lawnun (pl. alwaanun)": "lawnun (pl. alwaanun)", "qiblatun": "qiblatun", "waasi'un": "waasi'un", "ṣaaliḥun": "ṣaaliḥun", "Ghana": "Ghana", "Nigeria": "Najeriya", "Asia": "Asiya", "Africa": "Afirka", "ghaanaa": "ghaanaa", "nayjeeriyaa": "nayjeeriyaa", "aasiyaa": "aasiyaa", "ifreeqiyaa": "ifreeqiyaa", "we love": "muna so", "that (= ذٰلِكَ)": "wancan, kamar ذٰلِكَ", "Read the sentence. Is it true, according to the text?": "Karanta jumlar. Shin gaskiya ce, bisa ga rubutun?", "✓ Correct": "✓ Daidai ne", "✗ Not correct": "✗ Ba daidai ba ne", "Is it correct?": "Shin daidai ne?", "According to the text:": "Bisa ga rubutun:", "Where are they from?": "Daga ina suke?", "Which continent is the country in?": "A wace nahiya ƙasar take?", "Asia, Africa or Europe?": "Asiya, Afirka ko Turai?", "Which continent is it in?": "A wace nahiya take?", "But their religion is one.": "Amma addininsu ɗaya ne.", "Listen, then write the word. (the qiblah (direction of prayer))": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato alƙibla.", "We love him very much.": "Muna son sa sosai.", "✅ Write: the qiblah (direction of prayer)": "✅ Rubuta: alƙibla", "✅ According to the text:": "✅ Bisa ga rubutun:", "✅ Which continent is it in?": "✅ A wace nahiya take?", "✅ We love him very much.": "✅ Muna son sa sosai.", "✅ But their religion is one.": "✅ Amma addininsu ɗaya ne.", "In this lesson you will learn the colours, and an important group of words that never take": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi launuka, da wani muhimmin rukuni na kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun", "red, and": "ja, da", "mosques. You will also learn": "masallatai. Za ka kuma koyi", "he said, and": "ya ce, da", "she said.": "ta ce.", "Here are the colours. Tap each one to hear it.": "Ga launuka. Taɓa kowanne don jin sa.", "Colours never take": "Launuka ba sa taɓa samun", "a red pen.": "jan alƙalami.", "These words never take": "Waɗannan kalmomi ba sa taɓa samun", "girls' names, names with": "sunayen mata, sunaye masu", "words ending in": "kalmomin da ke ƙarewa da", "the pattern": "tsarin", "foreign names, and plurals like": "sunayen baƙi, da jam'i kamar", "means he said.": "ma'anarsa ya ce.", "means she said, just like": "ma'anarsa ta ce, kamar", "Colours, words without -un": "Launuka, kalmomin da ba su da -un", "Which colour?": "Wane launi?", "A red pen": "Jan alƙalami", "Never -un": "Babu -un har abada", "Correct ending": "Ƙarshen da ya dace", "In this lesson you will learn the colours, and an important group of words that never take أُنْ, like أَحْمَرُ, red, and مَسَاجِدُ, mosques. You will also learn قَالَ, he said, and قَالَتْ, she said.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi launuka, da wani muhimmin rukuni na kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun أُنْ, kamar أَحْمَرُ, ja, da مَسَاجِدُ, masallatai. Za ka kuma koyi قَالَ, ya ce, da قَالَتْ, ta ce.", "colours": "launuka", "red": "ja", "green": "kore", "blue": "shuɗi", "Colours (masculine) follow the pattern": "Launuka na namiji suna bin tsarin", ". Tap each colour to hear it.": ". Taɓa kowane launi don jin sa.", "white": "fari", "black": "baƙi", "yellow": "rawaya", "qalamun aḥmaru": "qalamun aḥmaru", "a red pen": "jan alƙalami", "Colours": "Launuka", "never take -un": "ba sa taɓa samun -un", ". They end in a single damma:": ". Suna ƙarewa da damma ɗaya:", "I have five pens: this is a red pen, and this is a blue pen.": "Ina da alƙaluma biyar: wannan jan alƙalami ne, kuma wannan shuɗin alƙalami ne.", "This is a green pen, this is a black pen, and this is a yellow pen.": "Wannan koren alƙalami ne, wannan baƙin alƙalami ne, kuma wannan alƙalami mai rawaya ne.", "Do you have a green handkerchief? No, I don't have a green handkerchief.": "Kana da koren hankici? A'a, ba ni da koren hankici.", "words that never take -un": "kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun -un", "Who are they?": "Su wane ne?", "These never take -un:": "Waɗannan ba sa taɓa samun -un:", "Girls' names:": "Sunayen mata:", "Names ending in": "Sunaye masu ƙarewa da", "The pattern": "Tsarin", "Foreign names:": "Sunayen baƙi:", "girls' names": "sunayen mata", "ending in ـَانُ": "masu ƙarewa da ـَانُ", "pattern أَفْعَلُ": "tsarin أَفْعَلُ", "foreign names": "sunayen baƙi", "plurals ending in ـَاءُ": "jam'i masu ƙarewa da ـَاءُ", "plurals like مَسَاجِدُ": "jam'i kamar مَسَاجِدُ", "qaala": "qaala", "he said": "ya ce", "qaalat": "qaalat", "she said": "ta ce", "Yusuf said: I have five pens.": "Yusuf ya ce: Ina da alƙaluma biyar.", "Zaynab said: I have many handkerchiefs.": "Zainab ta ce: Ina da hankici da yawa.", "Talhah said: I have many keys.": "Ɗalha ya ce: Ina da mabuɗai da yawa.", "Sufyan said: In our country there are many mosques and schools.": "Sufyan ya ce: A ƙasarmu akwai masallatai da makarantu da yawa.", "New words: colours": "Sababbin kalmomi: launuka", "abyaḍu": "abyaḍu", "aswadu": "aswadu", "aḥmaru": "aḥmaru", "akhḍaru": "akhḍaru", "azraqu": "azraqu", "aṣfaru": "aṣfaru", "a cup": "kofi", "a minute": "minti", "finjaanun (pl. fanaajeenu)": "finjaanun (pl. fanaajeenu)", "daqeeqatun (pl. daqaa'iqu)": "daqeeqatun (pl. daqaa'iqu)", "Hamid is a doctor. His wife is a teacher. Her name is Aminah.": "Hamid likita ne. Matarsa malama ce. Sunanta Aminatu.", "Hamid has four sons: Hamzah, Uthman, Ahmad and Ibrahim.": "Hamid yana da 'ya'ya maza huɗu: Hamza, Usman, Ahmad da Ibrahim.", "This is a red pen, and this is a blue pen.": "Wannan jan alƙalami ne, kuma wannan shuɗin alƙalami ne.", "Are these doctors? No, they are teachers, and they are great scholars.": "Shin waɗannan likitoci ne? A'a, su malamai ne, kuma manyan malamai ne masana.", "Listen, then tap the colour.": "Saurara, sannan ka taɓa launin.", "Which colour is it?": "Wane launi ne?", "Choose the correct phrase.": "Zaɓi kalmomin da suka dace.", "Colours never take -un": "Launuka ba sa taɓa samun -un", "How do you say “a red shirt”?": "Yaya ake cewa “jar riga”?", "How do you say “a black handkerchief”?": "Yaya ake cewa “baƙin hankici”?", "How do you say “a green door”?": "Yaya ake cewa “koriyar ƙofa”?", "How do you say “a yellow cup”?": "Yaya ake cewa “kofi mai rawaya”?", "How do you say “a white pen”?": "Yaya ake cewa “farin alƙalami”?", "Choose the word that never takes": "Zaɓi kalmar da ba ta taɓa samun", "Which one never takes -un?": "Wacce ce ba ta taɓa samun -un?", "Choose the word that never takes -un.": "Zaɓi kalmar da ba ta taɓa samun -un.", "Which word never takes -un?": "Wace kalma ce ba ta taɓa samun -un?", "With -un or without?": "Da -un ko ba tare da shi ba?", "How do you write “Khalid”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “Khalid”?", "or without?": "ko ba tare da shi ba?", "How do you write “Uthman”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “Usman”?", "How do you write “Yusuf”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “Yusuf”?", "How do you write “Ahmad”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “Ahmad”?", "How do you write “red”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “ja”?", "How do you write “Fatimah”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “Faɗimatu”?", "This is a red pen.": "Wannan jan alƙalami ne.", "How do you say “a blue book”?": "Yaya ake cewa “shuɗin littafi”?", "In our country there are many mosques.": "A ƙasarmu akwai masallatai da yawa.", "Listen, then write the word. (red)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato ja.", "✅ Which word never takes -un?": "✅ Wace kalma ce ba ta taɓa samun -un?", "✅ How do you say “a black handkerchief”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “baƙin hankici”?", "✅ How do you write “Yusuf”?": "✅ Yaya ake rubuta “Yusuf”?", "✅ How do you write “Fatimah”?": "✅ Yaya ake rubuta “Faɗimatu”?", "✅ How do you say “a blue book”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “shuɗin littafi”?", "✅ This is a red pen.": "✅ Wannan jan alƙalami ne.", "✅ In our country there are many mosques.": "✅ A ƙasarmu akwai masallatai da yawa.", "✅ Which colour is it?": "✅ Wane launi ne?", "✅ Write: red": "✅ Rubuta: ja", "In this last lesson of Beginner 1 you will see what happens to words that never take": "A wannan darasi na ƙarshe na Mafari 1 za ka ga abin da ke faruwa ga kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun", "Instead of a": "Maimakon", "they take a": "suna samun", "You will also learn the names of some cities.": "Za ka kuma koyi sunayen wasu birane.", "most words end in": "yawancin kalmomi suna ƙarewa da", "Words that never take": "Kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun", "end in": "suna ƙarewa da", "instead:": "a maimakon haka:", "The same happens to every word on the list from Lesson 22.": "Haka yake faruwa ga kowace kalma a jerin Darasi na 22.", "means give it to me, or bring it.": "ma'anarsa ba ni shi, ko kawo shi.", "From Zaynab, to Ahmad": "Daga Zainab, zuwa ga Ahmad", "-in or -a?": "-in ko -a?", "The dialogue": "Tattaunawar", "Normal words end in": "Kalmomi na yau da kullum suna ƙarewa da", "Look carefully at the name, then choose the correct ending.": "Duba sunan da kyau, sannan ka zaɓi ƙarshen da ya dace.", "In this last lesson of Beginner 1 you will see what happens to words that never take أُنْ after مِنْ, إِلَى and لِ. Instead of a كَسْرَةْ, they take a فَتْحَةْ: مِنْ زَيْنَبَ, لِأَحْمَدَ, إِلَى مَكَّةَ. You will also learn the names of some cities.": "A wannan darasi na ƙarshe na Mafari 1 za ka ga abin da ke faruwa ga kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun أُنْ bayan مِنْ, إِلَى da لِ. Maimakon كَسْرَةْ, suna samun فَتْحَةْ: مِنْ زَيْنَبَ, لِأَحْمَدَ, إِلَى مَكَّةَ. Za ka kuma koyi sunayen wasu birane.", "min muḥammadin": "min muḥammadin", "from Muhammad": "daga Muhammadu", "min zaynaba": "min zaynaba", "from Zaynab": "daga Zainab", "(and as an owner), most words end in": "da kuma idan mai abu ne, yawancin kalmomi suna ƙarewa da", ". Words that never take -un end in a": ". Kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun -un suna ƙarewa da", "fatha": "fatha", "normal word: -in": "kalma ta yau da kullum: -in", "never -un: -a": "ba ta taɓa samun -un: -a", "Muhammad → from, to, for Muhammad": "Muhammadu → daga, zuwa, don Muhammadu", "Zaynab → from, to, for Zaynab": "Zainab → daga, zuwa, don Zainab", "Zaynab's book": "littafin Zainab", "ilaa makkata": "ilaa makkata", "to Makkah": "zuwa Makka", "li-aḥmada": "li-aḥmada", "for Ahmad": "don Ahmad", "The same happens to every word on the list from Lesson 22: names,": "Haka yake faruwa ga kowace kalma a jerin Darasi na 22: sunaye,", ", foreign names and plurals like": ", sunayen baƙi da jam'i kamar", "My father went to Makkah and my uncle went to Jeddah.": "Babana ya tafi Makka kuma baffana ya tafi Jidda.", "This book is Muhammad's and that one is Zaynab's.": "Wannan littafin na Muhammadu ne kuma wancan na Zainab ne.", "Khalid went to Ahmad.": "Khalid ya tafi wurin Ahmad.", "In Istanbul there are many mosques.": "A Istanbul akwai masallatai da yawa.", "haati": "haati", "give me! bring!": "ba ni! kawo!", "The teacher says": "Malamin yana cewa", "when he wants something given to him.": "idan yana son a ba shi wani abu.", "I have seven notebooks. Whose are they?": "Ina da littattafan rubutu bakwai. Na wane ne?", "Give them to me, teacher. This is mine, this is Muhammad's, this is Hamid's, this is Ibrahim's and this is Uthman's.": "Ba ni su, malam. Wannan nawa ne, wannan na Muhammadu ne, wannan na Hamid ne, wannan na Ibrahim ne kuma wannan na Usman ne.", "Makkah": "Makka", "Jeddah": "Jidda", "Baghdad": "Bagadaza", "London": "Landan", "Paris": "Faris", "Istanbul": "Istanbul", "Pakistan": "Pakistan", "New words: cities": "Sababbin kalmomi: birane", "makkatu": "makkatu", "juddatu": "juddatu", "baghdaadu": "baghdaadu", "landanu": "landanu", "baareesu": "baareesu", "isṭanbuulu": "isṭanbuulu", "baakistaanu": "baakistaanu", "give me! (bring!)": "ba ni! kawo!", "Who are you, brother? I am a new student.": "Wane ne kai, ɗan'uwa? Ni sabon ɗalibi ne.", "What is your name? My name is Ahmad.": "Mene ne sunanka? Sunana Ahmad.", "Where are you from? I am from Pakistan.": "Daga ina kake? Ni daga Pakistan nake.", "Is this your book, Muhammad? No, this is Hamzah's book.": "Wannan littafinka ne, Muhammadu? A'a, wannan littafin Hamza ne.", "Where is Ali, brothers? He went to Riyadh.": "Ina Ali yake, 'yan'uwa? Ya tafi Riyadh.", "And where is Ya'qub? He went to Makkah.": "Kuma ina Ya'aƙub yake? Ya tafi Makka.", "Where is Ishaq? He went out to the principal, five minutes ago.": "Ina Ishaƙ yake? Ya fita wurin shugaban makaranta, minti biyar da suka wuce.", "Normal words: -in. Words that never take -un: -a.": "Kalmomi na yau da kullum: -in. Kalmomin da ba sa taɓa samun -un: -a.", "Choose the correct ending": "Zaɓi ƙarshen da ya dace", "Look carefully at the name.": "Duba sunan da kyau.", "Answer like in the dialogue": "Amsa kamar a tattaunawar", "This book is Zaynab's.": "Wannan littafin na Zainab ne.", "I am from Pakistan.": "Ni daga Pakistan nake.", "He went out five minutes ago.": "Ya fita minti biyar da suka wuce.", "Listen, then write the word. (Baghdad)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato Bagadaza.", "✅ I am from Pakistan.": "✅ Ni daga Pakistan nake.", "✅ He went out five minutes ago.": "✅ Ya fita minti biyar da suka wuce.", "✅ Write: Baghdad": "✅ Rubuta: Bagadaza", "Final exam": "Jarrabawar ƙarshe", "This is the final exam of Beginner 1. It has forty questions from all twenty three lessons of Book 1, and you have thirty minutes. You need eighty five percent to pass and open Beginner 2.": "Wannan ita ce jarrabawar ƙarshe ta Mafari 1. Tana da tambayoyi arba'in daga dukan darussa ashirin da uku na Littafi na 1, kuma kana da minti talatin. Kana buƙatar kashi tamanin da biyar cikin ɗari don ka ci ka buɗe Mafari 2.", "Take your time and read each question carefully.": "Ka natsu ka karanta kowace tambaya da kyau.", "Good luck.": "Allah ya ba da sa'a.", "Lessons {0}–{1}": "Darussa {0} zuwa {1}", "40 questions": "Tambayoyi 40", "pass mark 85%": "maki na ci kashi 85%", "She, they, I went": "Ta tafi, sun tafi, na tafi", "How do you say “I went”?": "Yaya ake cewa “na tafi”?", "Numbers": "Lambobi", "The, describing words": "Sanin abu, kalmomin siffantawa", "How do you say “The doors are open.”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ƙofofin a buɗe suke.”?", "Meanings": "Ma'anoni", "Words without -un": "Kalmomin da ba su da -un", "How do you say “from Zaynab”?": "Yaya ake cewa “daga Zainab”?", "Where, whose": "Ina, na wane", "How do you say “This house belongs to the merchant.”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Wannan gidan mallakar ɗan kasuwar ne.”?", "How do you say “The student (f) sat.”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ɗalibar ta zauna.”?", "Plurals and two": "Jam'i da biyu", "This, that, what, who": "Wannan, wancan, mene, wane", ". 🐪 (a camel)": ". 🐪 Wato raƙumi", ". 🐔 (a hen)": ". 🐔 Wato kaza", "“He went to the mosque.”": "“Ya tafi masallaci.”", "How do you say “for Muhammad”?": "Yaya ake cewa “don Muhammadu”?", "My, your, his, our": "Nawa, naka, nasa, namu", "How do you say “her name”?": "Yaya ake cewa “sunanta”?", "How do you say “many mosques”?": "Yaya ake cewa “masallatai da yawa”?", "How do you say “I have a brother.”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ina da ɗan'uwa.”?", "How do you say “the moon”?": "Yaya ake cewa “watan”?", "Is the ل pronounced?": "Shin ana furta ل?", "Ask a woman: What is your name?": "Tambayi mace: Mene ne sunanki?", "How do you say “my car”?": "Yaya ake cewa “motata”?", "How do you say “The students are new.”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ɗaliban sababbi ne.”?", ". 🔑 (a key)": ". 🔑 Wato mabuɗi", "How do you say “they went” (men)?": "Yaya ake cewa “sun tafi”, maza?", "🪑 The picture shows a chair.": "🪑 Hoton yana nuna kujera.", "Which question fits? 🐈": "Wace tambaya ta dace? 🐈", "40 of 40 correct": "40 cikin 40 daidai", "✅ How do you say “I went”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “na tafi”?", "✅ How do you say “{0} students”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai {0}”?", "✅ How do you say “The doors are open.”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ƙofofin a buɗe suke.”?", "✅ How do you say “from Zaynab”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “daga Zainab”?", "✅ How do you say “she went”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ta tafi”?", "✅ How do you say “This house belongs to the merchant.”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Wannan gidan mallakar ɗan kasuwar ne.”?", "✅ How do you say “The student (f) sat.”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ɗalibar ta zauna.”?", "✅ How many brothers do you have?": "✅ 'Yan'uwa maza nawa kake da su?", "✅ “He went to the mosque.”": "✅ “Ya tafi masallaci.”", "✅ How do you say “for Muhammad”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “don Muhammadu”?", "✅ How do you say “we went”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “mun tafi”?", "✅ How do you say “her name”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “sunanta”?", "✅ How do you say “many mosques”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “masallatai da yawa”?", "✅ How do you say “10 cars”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “motoci 10”?", "✅ How do you say “I have a brother.”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ina da ɗan'uwa.”?", "✅ How do you say “the moon”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “watan”?", "✅ these two rulers": "✅ waɗannan rulan biyu", "✅ Is the ل pronounced?": "✅ Shin ana furta ل?", "✅ Ask a woman: What is your name?": "✅ Tambayi mace: Mene ne sunanki?", "✅ How do you say “my car”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “motata”?", "✅ How do you say “The students are new.”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ɗaliban sababbi ne.”?", "✅ “The book is on the desk.”": "✅ “Littafin yana kan teburin.”", "✅ How do you say “the teacher's car”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “motar malamin”?", "✅ How do you say “they went” (men)?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “sun tafi”, maza?", "✅ These are books.": "✅ Waɗannan littattafai ne.", "✅ 🪑 The picture shows a chair.": "✅ 🪑 Hoton yana nuna kujera.", "✅ Which question fits? 🐈": "✅ Wace tambaya ta dace? 🐈", "Welcome to Beginner 2. In this level you will study the first half of Book 2, lessons 1 to 15. It ends with a final exam and a certificate.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 2. A wannan mataki za ka karanta rabin farko na Littafi na 2, darussa 1 zuwa 15. Yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida.", "you have come far. Keep going.": "ka yi nisa. Ka ci gaba.", "which gives a sentence strength, like indeed. After it the first word ends in": "wanda ke ƙarfafa jumla, kamar lalle. Bayansa kalmar farko tana ƙarewa da", "You will also learn": "Za ka kuma koyi", "perhaps,": "watakila,", "or,": "ko,", "having, and the numbers": "ma'abocin, da lambobi", "a hundred, and": "ɗari, da", "a thousand.": "dubu.", "makes a sentence stronger. The first word after it ends in": "yana ƙarfafa jumla. Kalmar farko da ke bayansa tana ƙarewa da", "With pronouns,": "Da wakilan suna,", "joins the ending:": "yana haɗuwa da ƙarshen:", "he.": "shi.", "she.": "ita.", "you.": "kai.", "they.": "su.", "means perhaps, or I hope. It works like": "ma'anarsa watakila, ko ina fata. Yana aiki kamar", "means I hope you are well.": "ma'anarsa ina fata kana lafiya.", "In a question with": "A tambaya mai", "for or.": "don ko.", "means having.": "ma'anarsa ma'abocin, wato mai.", "is a student with good character. For a woman,": "ɗalibi ne mai kyawawan halaye. Ga mace,", "For women,": "Ga mata,", "use one noun ending in": "yi amfani da suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da", "a hundred men.": "maza ɗari.", "a thousand riyals.": "riyal dubu.", "إِنَّ (indeed)": "إِنَّ, wato lalle", "Add إِنَّ": "Ƙara إِنَّ", "إِنَّ + pronoun": "إِنَّ tare da wakilin suna", "Or?": "Ko?", "Hundred, thousand": "Ɗari, dubu", "· Book 1": "· Littafi na 1", "· Book 2, lessons 1 to 15": "· Littafi na 2, darussa 1 zuwa 15", "· Book 2, lessons 16 to 31": "· Littafi na 2, darussa 16 zuwa 31", "· Book 3": "· Littafi na 3", "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Welcome to Beginner 2. In this level you will study the first half of Book 2, lessons 1 to 15. It ends with a final exam and a certificate. مَا شَاءَ اللهُ, you have come far. Keep going.": "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Barka da zuwa Mafari 2. A wannan mataki za ka karanta rabin farko na Littafi na 2, darussa 1 zuwa 15. Yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida. مَا شَاءَ اللهُ, ka yi nisa. Ka ci gaba.", "inna l-mudarrisa jadeedun": "inna l-mudarrisa jadeedun", "Indeed, the teacher is new.": "Lalle, malamin sabo ne.", "makes a sentence stronger. The": "yana ƙarfafa jumla. Kalmar", "after it ends in a": "da ke bayansa tana ƙarewa da", "(-a). With -un it becomes": "wato -a. Da -un tana zama", "Indeed the teacher is new.": "Lalle malamin sabo ne.", "Indeed Fatimah is a doctor.": "Lalle Faɗimatu likita ce.", "Indeed Hamid is married.": "Lalle Hamid yana da aure.", "innahu": "innahu", "innahaa": "innahaa", "innaka": "innaka", "you": "kai", "innee": "innee", "(he),": "wato shi,", "(she),": "wato ita,", "(you, m),": "wato kai, namiji,", "(you, f),": "wato ke, mace,", "(they, m),": "wato su, maza,", "(they, f),": "wato su, mata,", "(you all),": "wato ku,", "You are an intelligent student, Hashim.": "Lalle kai ɗalibi ne mai hazaƙa, Hashim.", "I am from India.": "Lalle ni daga Indiya nake.", "It is very cheap.": "Lalle yana da arha sosai.", "They are teachers (f).": "Lalle su malamai ne mata.", "la'alla": "la'alla", "perhaps, I hope": "watakila, ina fata", "works like": "yana aiki kamar", ": the next word ends in a fatha.": ": kalmar da ke biye tana ƙarewa da fatha.", "= I hope you are well.": "yana nufin ina fata kana lafiya.", "How are you, teacher? I hope you are well.": "Yaya kake, malam? Ina fata kana lafiya.", "Perhaps the principal is in his room.": "Watakila shugaban makarantar yana ɗakinsa.", "am": "am", "or (in a question)": "ko, a tambaya", ", use": ", yi amfani da", "for “or”.": "don “ko”.", "Are you from Pakistan or from India?": "Kai daga Pakistan kake ko daga Indiya?", "Is it expensive or cheap?": "Yana da tsada ko arha?", "Are you a doctor or an engineer?": "Kai likita ne ko injiniya?", "dhuu": "dhuu", "having (m)": "ma'abocin, namiji", "dhaatu": "dhaatu", "having (f)": "ma'abociyar, mace", "means having, and is followed by a noun ending in -i:": "ma'anarsa ma'abocin, wato mai, kuma suna mai ƙarewa da -i yana biye da shi:", "(a student of good character). For a woman": "wato ɗalibi mai kyawawan halaye. Ga mace", ", for men": ", ga maza", ", for women": ", ga mata", "You are an intelligent, hardworking student with good character.": "Kai ɗalibi ne mai hazaƙa, mai ƙwazo, mai kyawawan halaye.", "This student (f) has good character.": "Wannan ɗalibar tana da kyawawan halaye.", "This shirt has a short sleeve.": "Wannan rigar tana da gajeren hannu.", "This man has a lot of money.": "Wannan mutumin yana da kuɗi da yawa.", "mi'atu riyaalin": "mi'atu riyaalin", "100 riyals": "riyal 100", "alfu riyaalin": "alfu riyaalin", "1000 riyals": "riyal 1000", "noun ending in -i:": "suna mai ƙarewa da -i:", ". The alif in": ". Alif ɗin da ke cikin", "is not read:": "ba a karanta shi:", "mi'atun": "mi'atun", "(expensive) ends in -in, but the feminine is": "wato mai tsada, yana ƙarewa da -in, amma na macensa shi ne", "It costs only a hundred rupees.": "Kuɗinsa rupi ɗari ne kawai.", "I have a thousand dollars.": "Ina da dala dubu.", "In this book there are a hundred pages.": "A cikin wannan littafi akwai shafuka ɗari.", "This pen is expensive, and this watch is expensive.": "Wannan alƙalami yana da tsada, kuma wannan agogo yana da tsada.", "intelligent": "mai hazaƙa", "stupid": "dakiki, mara wayo", "character, manners": "hali, ɗabi'a", "married": "mai aure", "single (not married)": "gwauro, wanda bai yi aure ba", "successful (passed)": "wanda ya ci jarrabawa", "expensive": "mai tsada", "a Jew": "Bayahude", "New words: describing words": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin siffantawa", "dhakiyyun (pl. adhkiyaa'u)": "dhakiyyun (pl. adhkiyaa'u)", "ghabiyyun (pl. aghbiyaa'u)": "ghabiyyun (pl. aghbiyaa'u)", "khuluqun (pl. akhlaaqun)": "khuluqun (pl. akhlaaqun)", "mutazawwijun": "mutazawwijun", "'azabun (pl. a'zaabun)": "'azabun (pl. a'zaabun)", "naajiḥun (pl. naajiḥuuna)": "naajiḥun (pl. naajiḥuuna)", "ghaalin": "ghaalin", "yahuudiyyun (pl. yahuud)": "yahuudiyyun (pl. yahuud)", "a hundred": "ɗari", "a thousand": "dubu", "a rupee": "rupi", "a dollar": "dala", "a dictionary": "ƙamus", "a page": "shafi", "a sleeve": "hannun riga", "New words: things and numbers": "Sababbin kalmomi: abubuwa da lambobi", "alfun": "alfun", "ruubiyyatun": "ruubiyyatun", "duulaarun": "duulaarun", "mu'jamun (pl. ma'aajimu)": "mu'jamun (pl. ma'aajimu)", "ṣafḥatun": "ṣafḥatun", "kummun (pl. akmaamun)": "kummun (pl. akmaamun)", "only": "kawai", "having, with": "ma'abocin, mai", "indeed, certainly": "lalle, haƙiƙa", "Praise be to Allah. And how are you, Hashim? I like you very much.": "Godiya ta tabbata ga Allah. Kai kuma yaya kake, Hashim? Ina son ka sosai.", "Are you from Pakistan or India? I am from India.": "Kai daga Pakistan kake ko Indiya? Ni daga Indiya nake.", "Your watch is beautiful, Hashim. Is it from Japan?": "Agogonka yana da kyau, Hashim. Daga Japan yake?", "Is it expensive or cheap? It is very cheap, only a hundred rupees.": "Yana da tsada ko arha? Yana da arha sosai, rupi ɗari kawai.", "Are they students? No, they are merchants.": "Shin su ɗalibai ne? A'a, su 'yan kasuwa ne.", "The first word after": "Kalmar farko da ke bayan", "ends in a fatha.": "tana ƙarewa da fatha.", "Add إِنَّ:": "Ƙara إِنَّ:", "ends in a": "tana ƙarewa da", "Join": "Haɗa", "to the pronoun.": "da wakilin sunan.", "(or)": "wato ko", "“Are you hardworking or lazy?”": "“Kai mai ƙwazo ne ko malalaci?”", "“Is it expensive or cheap?”": "“Yana da tsada ko arha?”", "“Are you a doctor or an engineer?”": "“Kai likita ne ko injiniya?”", "“Is she from China or Japan?”": "“Ita daga China take ko Japan?”", "“Are you from India or from Pakistan?”": "“Kai daga Indiya kake ko daga Pakistan?”", "How do you say “a shirt with a short sleeve”?": "Yaya ake cewa “riga mai gajeren hannu”?", "How do you say “a student (m) with good character”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibi mai kyawawan halaye”?", "How do you say “a man with a lot of money”?": "Yaya ake cewa “mutum mai kuɗi da yawa”?", "How do you say “students (f) with good character”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai mata masu kyawawan halaye”?", "How do you say “students (m) with good character”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai maza masu kyawawan halaye”?", "After a hundred or a thousand: one noun ending in": "Bayan ɗari ko dubu: suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da", "After a hundred or a thousand: one noun ending in -i.": "Bayan ɗari ko dubu: suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da -i.", "How do you say “100 riyals”?": "Yaya ake cewa “riyal 100”?", "How do you say “1000 rupees”?": "Yaya ake cewa “rupi 1000”?", "How do you say “100 women”?": "Yaya ake cewa “mata 100”?", "How do you say “1000 dollars”?": "Yaya ake cewa “dala 1000”?", "You are an intelligent student.": "Lalle kai ɗalibi ne mai hazaƙa.", "أَمْ (or)": "أَمْ, wato ko", "Listen, then write the word. (intelligent)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato mai hazaƙa.", "I hope you are well.": "Ina fata kana lafiya.", "✅ You are an intelligent student.": "✅ Lalle kai ɗalibi ne mai hazaƙa.", "✅ “Is it expensive or cheap?”": "✅ “Yana da tsada ko arha?”", "✅ How do you say “a student (m) with good character”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibi mai kyawawan halaye”?", "✅ Write: intelligent": "✅ Rubuta: mai hazaƙa", "✅ How do you say “1000 dollars”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “dala 1000”?", "✅ I hope you are well.": "✅ Ina fata kana lafiya.", "✅ How do you say “students (m) with good character”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai maza masu kyawawan halaye”?", "which means is not. It changes with the person, like": "wanda ma'anarsa ba … ba, wato korewa. Yana canzawa da mutum, kamar", "she is not, and": "ita ba … ba, da", "I am not, and the word after it often comes with": "ni ba … ba, kuma kalmar da ke bayansa sau da yawa tana zuwa da", "indeed I have.": "lalle ina da.", "means is not. The word after it often has": "ma'anarsa ba … ba. Kalmar da ke bayansa sau da yawa tana da", "and then ends in": "sannan ta ƙare da", "changes like a past verb.": "yana canzawa kamar fi'ilin da ya wuce.", "and other short words,": "da wasu gajerun kalmomi,", "comes without": "yana zuwa ba tare da", "When the subject comes after": "Idan abin da ake magana a kai ya zo bayan", "still gives it": "har yanzu yana ba shi", "لَيْسَ (is not)": "لَيْسَ, wato ba … ba", "Make it negative": "Mayar da shi korewa", "Answer no": "Amsa da a'a", "In this lesson you will learn لَيْسَ, which means is not. It changes with the person, like لَيْسَتْ, she is not, and لَسْتُ, I am not, and the word after it often comes with بِ. You will also learn إِنَّ لِي, indeed I have.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi لَيْسَ, wanda ma'anarsa ba … ba, wato korewa. Yana canzawa da mutum, kamar لَيْسَتْ, ita ba … ba, da لَسْتُ, ni ba … ba, kuma kalmar da ke bayansa sau da yawa tana zuwa da بِ. Za ka kuma koyi إِنَّ لِي, lalle ina da.", "ḥaamidun ṭaalibun": "ḥaamidun ṭaalibun", "Hamid is a student.": "Hamid ɗalibi ne.", "ḥaamidun laysa biṭaalibin": "ḥaamidun laysa biṭaalibin", "Hamid is not a student.": "Hamid ba ɗalibi ba ne.", "is not": "ba … ba", ". The word after it often has": ". Kalmar da ke bayansa sau da yawa tana da", "and then ends in -i:": "sannan ta ƙare da -i:", "Is your father a Muslim? No, he is not a Muslim.": "Babanka Musulmi ne? A'a, shi ba Musulmi ba ne.", "The door is not closed.": "Ƙofar ba a rufe take ba.", "laysa": "laysa", "laysat": "laysat", "laysuu": "laysuu", "they (m)": "su, maza", "lasna": "lasna", "they (f)": "su, mata", "changes like a past verb:": "yana canzawa kamar fi'ilin da ya wuce:", "Aminah is not a doctor.": "Aminatu ba likita ba ce.", "The students are not young.": "Ɗaliban ba yara ƙanana ba ne.", "The girls are not married.": "'Yan matan ba su da aure.", "lasta": "lasta", "you (m)": "kai, namiji", "lasti": "lasti", "you (f)": "ke, mace", "lastu": "lastu", "lasnaa": "lasnaa", "You are not old.": "Kai ba tsoho ba ne.", "I am not a teacher.": "Ni ba malami ba ne.", "No, I am not from Washington. I am from New York.": "A'a, ni ba daga Washington nake ba. Ni daga New York nake.", "We are not students.": "Mu ba ɗalibai ba ne.", "without بِ": "ba tare da بِ ba", "is not from Japan": "ba daga Japan yake ba", "He is not from Japan.": "Shi ba daga Japan yake ba.", "She is not at home.": "Ita ba ta gida.", "I have no brothers.": "Ba ni da 'yan'uwa maza.", "inna lee thalaatha akhawaatin": "inna lee thalaatha akhawaatin", "Indeed, I have three sisters.": "Lalle, ina da 'yan'uwa mata uku.", "When the subject comes": "Idan abin da ake magana a kai ya zo", "still gives it a fatha:": "har yanzu yana ba shi fatha:", "Do you have brothers? No, I have no brothers. I have three sisters.": "Kana da 'yan'uwa maza? A'a, ba ni da 'yan'uwa maza. Ina da 'yan'uwa mata uku.", "There are five new students in the class.": "Akwai sababbin ɗalibai biyar a ajin.", "We have a good teacher.": "Muna da malami nagari.", "a meeting": "saduwa, haɗuwa", "good": "mai kyau", "sleeping": "mai barci", "glad, happy": "mai farin ciki", "a telegram": "talgiram, wato saƙon waya na gaggawa", "a bank": "banki", "the post office": "gidan waya", "the United States": "Amurka, wato Haɗaɗɗiyar Daular Amurka", "liqaa'un": "liqaa'un", "jayyidun": "jayyidun", "naa'imun": "naa'imun", "masruurun": "masruurun", "barqiyyatun": "barqiyyatun", "maṣrifun (pl. maṣaarifu)": "maṣrifun (pl. maṣaarifu)", "maktabul-bareedi": "maktabul-bareedi", "al-wilaayaatul-muttaḥidatu": "al-wilaayaatul-muttaḥidatu", "I am not": "ni ba … ba", "I am a new engineer. My name is Hisham. I am from the United States.": "Ni sabon injiniya ne. Sunana Hisham. Ni daga Amurka nake.", "Welcome, brother. I am glad to meet you.": "Maraba, ɗan'uwa. Na yi farin cikin saduwa da kai.", "Are you from Washington? No, I am not from Washington. I am from New York.": "Kai daga Washington kake? A'a, ni ba daga Washington nake ba. Ni daga New York nake.", "Are they students? No, they are not students.": "Su ɗalibai ne? A'a, su ba ɗalibai ba ne.", "Are they married (f)? No, they are not married.": "Su masu aure ne, mata? A'a, ba su da aure.", "Choose the correct form of": "Zaɓi siffar da ta dace ta", "and the ending.": "da ƙarshen.", "Make it negative:": "Mayar da shi korewa:", "Answer the question with": "Amsa tambayar da", "Answer with no.": "Amsa da a'a.", "The subject after": "Abin da ake magana a kai bayan", "I am not from Washington.": "Ni ba daga Washington nake ba.", "She is not a Muslim.": "Ita ba Musulma ba ce.", "Add لَيْسَ": "Ƙara لَيْسَ", "Answer with لَا": "Amsa da لَا", "Listen, then write the word. (a bank)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato banki.", "✅ She is not a Muslim.": "✅ Ita ba Musulma ba ce.", "✅ Answer with no.": "✅ Amsa da a'a.", "✅ Write: a bank": "✅ Rubuta: banki", "✅ Indeed, I have three sisters.": "✅ Lalle, ina da 'yan'uwa mata uku.", "In this lesson you will count from eleven to nineteen, like": "A wannan darasi za ka ƙirga daga goma sha ɗaya zuwa goma sha tara, kamar", "You will compare things with": "Za ka kwatanta abubuwa da", "taller, and": "ya fi tsawo, da", "the tallest student. You will learn": "ɗalibin da ya fi kowa tsawo. Za ka koyi", "but,": "amma,", "as if,": "kamar dai,", "isn't it so, and the order words": "ba haka ba ne, da kalmomin jeri", "first, to": "na farko, zuwa", "tenth.": "na goma.", "From eleven to nineteen the number is two words, and the noun after it is one, ending in -an:": "Daga goma sha ɗaya zuwa goma sha tara lambar kalmomi biyu ce, kuma sunan da ke bayanta ɗaya ne, mai ƙarewa da -an:", "To compare, use the pattern": "Don kwatanta, yi amfani da tsarin", "before a noun to say the most.": "kafin suna don faɗar mafi.", "is the tallest student in our class.": "shi ne ɗalibin da ya fi kowa tsawo a ajinmu.", "but, and": "amma, da", "as if, are sisters of": "kamar dai, 'yan'uwan", "The next word ends in": "Kalmar da ke biye tana ƙarewa da", "To agree with a question that has not in it, answer": "Don yarda da tambayar da ke da korewa a cikinta, ka amsa", "for which of the two.": "don wanne daga cikin biyun.", "Order words come after the noun:": "Kalmomin jeri suna zuwa bayan suna:", "For feminine add": "Ga mace ƙara", "But first, feminine, is": "Amma na farko, na mace, shi ne", "أَطْوَلُ (taller)": "أَطْوَلُ, wato ya fi tsawo", "{0} to {1}": "{0} zuwa {1}", "Number + noun": "Lamba tare da suna", "Taller than": "Ya fi tsawo", "The most": "Mafi", "First, second": "Na farko, na biyu", "In this lesson you will count from eleven to nineteen, like أَرْبَعَةَ عَشَرَ طَالِبًا. You will compare things with أَطْوَلُ, taller, and أَطْوَلُ طَالِبٍ, the tallest student. You will learn لٰكِنَّ, but, كَأَنَّ, as if, أَلَيْسَ كَذٰلِكَ, isn't it so, and the order words الْأَوَّلُ, first, to الْعَاشِرُ, tenth.": "A wannan darasi za ka ƙirga daga goma sha ɗaya zuwa goma sha tara, kamar أَرْبَعَةَ عَشَرَ طَالِبًا. Za ka kwatanta abubuwa da أَطْوَلُ, ya fi tsawo, da أَطْوَلُ طَالِبٍ, ɗalibin da ya fi kowa tsawo. Za ka koyi لٰكِنَّ, amma, كَأَنَّ, kamar dai, أَلَيْسَ كَذٰلِكَ, ba haka ba ne, da kalmomin jeri الْأَوَّلُ, na farko, zuwa الْعَاشِرُ, na goma.", "aḥada 'ashara ṭaaliban … tis'ata 'ashara ṭaaliban": "aḥada 'ashara ṭaaliban … tis'ata 'ashara ṭaaliban", "11 students … 19 students": "ɗalibai 11 … ɗalibai 19", "From 11 to 19 the number is two words, both ending in": "Daga 11 zuwa 19 lambar kalmomi biyu ce, dukansu suna ƙarewa da", ". The noun after it is": ". Sunan da ke bayanta", ", ending in": ", mai ƙarewa da", ". Twelve is": ". Goma sha biyu ita ce", ". Twenty is": ". Ashirin ita ce", "How many students are in your class? In our class there are fourteen students.": "Ɗalibai nawa ne a ajinku? A ajinmu akwai ɗalibai goma sha huɗu.", "tall": "dogo", "aṭwalu min": "aṭwalu min", "taller than": "ya fi tsawo", ". It is the same for a man or a woman:": ". Iri ɗaya ne ga namiji ko mace:", "Hashim is tall, and Hamid is taller than him.": "Hashim dogo ne, kuma Hamid ya fi shi tsawo.", "Aminah is young, and Zainab is younger than her.": "Aminatu yarinya ce, kuma Zainab ta fi ta ƙanƙanta.", "My house is farther from the school than your house.": "Gidana ya fi gidanka nisa da makarantar.", "aṭwalu ṭaalibin": "aṭwalu ṭaalibin", "the tallest student": "ɗalibin da ya fi kowa tsawo", "a noun ending in -i to say": "suna mai ƙarewa da -i don faɗar", "the most": "mafi", "= the tallest student in our class.": "yana nufin ɗalibin da ya fi kowa tsawo a ajinmu.", "The tallest student in our class is Ibrahim.": "Ɗalibin da ya fi kowa tsawo a ajinmu shi ne Ibrahim.", "Muhammad is the best student in the class.": "Muhammadu shi ne ɗalibin da ya fi kowa kyau a ajin.", "Al-Azhar is the oldest university in the world.": "Azhar ita ce jami'ar da ta fi kowace tsufa a duniya.", "laakinna": "laakinna", "ka-anna": "ka-anna", "as if": "kamar dai", "(but) and": "wato amma, da", "(as if) are sisters of": "wato kamar dai, 'yan'uwan", "The students are many but the class is small.": "Ɗaliban suna da yawa amma ajin ƙarami ne.", "Hamid is hardworking but his friend is lazy.": "Hamid mai ƙwazo ne amma abokinsa malalaci ne.", "Who is this boy? It seems he is your brother.": "Wane ne wannan yaron? Kamar dai ɗan'uwanka ne.", "a-laysa kadhaalika?": "a-laysa kadhaalika?", "Isn't it so?": "Ba haka ba ne?", "balaa": "balaa", "Yes, it is.": "I, haka ne.", "To agree with a question that has": "Don yarda da tambayar da ke da", "in it, answer": "a cikinta, ka amsa", "(yes, it is), not": "wato i, haka ne, ba", ". Use": "ba. Yi amfani da", "for “which of the two”.": "don “wanne daga cikin biyun”.", "He is very tall, isn't he? Yes, he is.": "Dogo ne sosai, ko ba haka ba? I, haka ne.", "You are from India, aren't you? Yes.": "Kai daga Indiya kake, ko ba haka ba? I.", "These are two books. Which of them is more beautiful?": "Waɗannan littattafai biyu ne. Wanne ne ya fi kyau daga cikinsu?", "al-awwalu": "al-awwalu", "ath-thaanee": "ath-thaanee", "second": "na biyu", "ath-thaalithu … al-'aashiru": "ath-thaalithu … al-'aashiru", "third … tenth": "na uku … na goma", "Order words follow the noun:": "Kalmomin jeri suna bin sunan:", ". For feminine add": ". Ga mace ƙara", ". But first (f) is": ". Amma na farko, na mace, shi ne", "I am in the fifth dormitory.": "Ina ɗakin kwana na biyar.", "I came back after the first period.": "Na dawo bayan lokacin darasi na farko.", "a dormitory": "ɗakin kwanan ɗalibai", "a team": "ƙungiya", "a player": "ɗan wasa", "a full brother": "shaƙiƙi, wato ɗan'uwa uwa ɗaya uba ɗaya", "the world": "duniya", "Al-Azhar": "Azhar", "mahja'un (pl. mahaaji'u)": "mahja'un (pl. mahaaji'u)", "fareequn (pl. furaqaa'u)": "fareequn (pl. furaqaa'u)", "laa'ibun (pl. laa'ibuuna)": "laa'ibun (pl. laa'ibuuna)", "shaqeequn (pl. ashiqqaa'u)": "shaqeequn (pl. ashiqqaa'u)", "al-'aalamu": "al-'aalamu", "al-azharu": "al-azharu", "a star, a planet": "tauraro, duniyar sama", "in a dream": "a mafarki", "New words: other words": "Sababbin kalmomi: wasu kalmomi", "kawkabun (pl. kawaakibu)": "kawkabun (pl. kawaakibu)", "shahrun (pl. shuhuurun, ashhurun)": "shahrun (pl. shuhuurun, ashhurun)", "fil-manaami": "fil-manaami", "which of the two": "wanne daga cikin biyun", "yes (it is so)": "i, haka ne", "as if, it seems": "kamar dai, da alama", "How many students are in your class, Ali? In our class there are fourteen students.": "Ɗalibai nawa ne a ajinku, Ali? A ajinmu akwai ɗalibai goma sha huɗu.", "The students in our class are more. There are nineteen students in it.": "Ɗaliban ajinmu sun fi yawa. Akwai ɗalibai goma sha tara a cikinsa.", "He is very tall, isn't he? Yes, he is very tall, but Hamid is taller than him.": "Dogo ne sosai, ko ba haka ba? I, dogo ne sosai, amma Hamid ya fi shi tsawo.", "Your handwriting is very beautiful, ma sha Allah. My handwriting is beautiful, and yours is more beautiful.": "Rubutun hannunka yana da kyau sosai, ma sha Allah. Rubutun hannuna yana da kyau, kuma naka ya fi kyau.", "Who is this boy with you? It seems he is your brother. Yes, he is my full brother.": "Wane ne wannan yaron da ke tare da kai? Kamar dai ɗan'uwanka ne. I, shi shaƙiƙina ne.", "I am in the eighth dormitory, and it is farther than your dormitory.": "Ina ɗakin kwana na takwas, kuma ya fi ɗakin kwananka nisa.", "Choose the number in words.": "Zaɓi lambar a rubuce da kalmomi.", "Count 11 to 19": "Ƙirga 11 zuwa 19", "How do you say it?": "Yaya ake faɗar sa?", "One noun ending in": "Suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da", "The noun after 11–19": "Sunan da ke bayan 11 zuwa 19", "One noun ending in -an.": "Suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da -an.", "Choose the": "Zaɓi siffar", "Make the comparing word": "Yi kalmar kwatanta", "form.": "da ta dace.", "More / -er:": "Fiye da:", "Compare with": "Kwatanta da", "“This car is more beautiful than that.”": "“Wannan motar ta fi waccan kyau.”", "“Zainab is younger than Aminah.”": "“Zainab ta fi Aminatu ƙanƙanta.”", "“Hamid is taller than Hashim.”": "“Hamid ya fi Hashim tsawo.”", "“Cairo is bigger than Riyadh.”": "“Alƙahira ta fi Riyadh girma.”", "“Milk is better than tea.”": "“Madara ta fi shayi kyau.”", "The best, the tallest": "Mafi kyau, mafi tsawo", "+ one noun ending in -i.": "tare da suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da -i.", "Aminah is a young student.": "Aminatu ɗaliba ce ƙarama.", "Say it is the best / most:": "Ka ce shi ne mafi kyau ko mafi …:", "plus one noun ending in": "tare da suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da", "Al-Azhar is an old university.": "Azhar jami'a ce tsohuwa.", "This is a cheap watch.": "Wannan agogo ne mai arha.", "This is a beautiful house.": "Wannan gida ne mai kyau.", "The word after them ends in a": "Kalmar da ke bayansu tana ƙarewa da", "The word after them ends in a fatha.": "Kalmar da ke bayansu tana ƙarewa da fatha.", "Join or add كَأَنَّ:": "Haɗa ko ƙara كَأَنَّ:", "Choose the order word.": "Zaɓi kalmar jeri.", "How do you say “the second room”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗaki na biyu”?", "How do you say “the fifth dormitory”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗakin kwana na biyar”?", "How do you say “the eighth house”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gida na takwas”?", "How do you say “the third lesson”?": "Yaya ake cewa “darasi na uku”?", "How do you say “the first student (f)”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗaliba ta farko”?", "Hamid is taller than him.": "Hamid ya fi shi tsawo.", "How do you say “the tenth page”?": "Yaya ake cewa “shafi na goma”?", "It seems he is your brother.": "Kamar dai ɗan'uwanka ne.", "Compare with مِنْ": "Kwatanta da مِنْ", "Listen, then write the word. ()": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. ()", "✅ How do you say “the tenth page”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “shafi na goma”?", "✅ It seems he is your brother.": "✅ Kamar dai ɗan'uwanka ne.", "✅ “This car is more beautiful than that.”": "✅ “Wannan motar ta fi waccan kyau.”", "✅ Aminah is a young student.": "✅ Aminatu ɗaliba ce ƙarama.", "✅ Write:": "✅ Rubuta:", "✅ Hamid is taller than him.": "✅ Hamid ya fi shi tsawo.", "In this lesson you will learn the past verb": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi fi'ilin da ya wuce", "he went, with every person:": "ya tafi, da kowane mutum:", "she went,": "ta tafi,", "they went,": "sun tafi,", "I went, and more. You will say did not with": "na tafi, da ƙari. Za ka faɗi bai yi ba da", "answer": "ka amsa", "and give a reason with": "ka kuma ba da dalili da", "because.": "saboda.", "The past verb changes its ending with the person.": "Fi'ilin da ya wuce yana canza ƙarshensa da mutum.", "For you:": "Ga kai ko ku:", "Careful:": "Ka kula:", "is I went, and": "shi ne na tafi, kuma", "is you went.": "shi ne ka tafi.", "before a past verb to say did not:": "kafin fi'ilin da ya wuce don faɗar bai yi ba:", "For a question with not, the yes answer is": "Ga tambaya mai korewa, amsar i ita ce", "means because. It is a sister of": "ma'anarsa saboda. 'Yar'uwar", "With pronouns:": "Da wakilan suna:", "ذَهَبَ (he went)": "ذَهَبَ, wato ya tafi", "Did not": "Bai yi ba", "نَعَمْ or بَلَى": "نَعَمْ ko بَلَى", "Because": "Saboda", "In this lesson you will learn the past verb ذَهَبَ, he went, with every person: ذَهَبَتْ, she went, ذَهَبُوا, they went, ذَهَبْتُ, I went, and more. You will say did not with مَا, answer بَلَى, and give a reason with لِأَنَّ, because.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi fi'ilin da ya wuce ذَهَبَ, ya tafi, da kowane mutum: ذَهَبَتْ, ta tafi, ذَهَبُوا, sun tafi, ذَهَبْتُ, na tafi, da ƙari. Za ka faɗi bai yi ba da مَا, ka amsa بَلَى, ka kuma ba da dalili da لِأَنَّ, saboda.", "they (m) went": "sun tafi, maza", "they (f) went": "sun tafi, mata", "The past verb changes its": "Fi'ilin da ya wuce yana canza", "ending": "ƙarshensa", "with the person:": "da mutum:", "Where is your father? He went to the market.": "Ina babanka yake? Ya tafi kasuwa.", "And where is your mother? She went to my aunt Zainab.": "Kuma ina mamarka take? Ta tafi wurin innata Zainab.", "And your brothers? They went to the university.": "Kuma 'yan'uwanka maza? Sun tafi jami'a.", "And your sisters? They went to the school.": "Kuma 'yan'uwanka mata? Sun tafi makaranta.", "you went (m": "ka tafi, namiji", "m pl": "jam'in maza", "f pl)": "jam'in mata", "For “you”:": "Ga “kai”:", ". Before these endings the letter": ". Kafin waɗannan ƙarshe harafin", "has a sukun.": "yana da sukun.", "Did you go to the doctor?": "Ka tafi wurin likita?", "Where did you go, Aminah?": "Ina kika tafi, Aminatu?", "When did you all come back from Makkah?": "Yaushe kuka dawo daga Makka?", ". Careful:": ". Ka kula:", "(I) and": "wato na, da", "(you) differ only in the last vowel.": "wato ka, sun bambanta ne kawai a wasalin ƙarshe.", "I went and came back after the first period.": "Na tafi kuma na dawo bayan lokacin darasi na farko.", "We went to the mosque.": "Mun tafi masallaci.", "maa dhahaba": "maa dhahaba", "he did not go": "bai tafi ba", "before a past verb to say": "kafin fi'ilin da ya wuce don faɗar", "did not": "bai yi ba", "(I did not go). For a question with “not”, the “yes” answer is": "wato ban tafi ba. Ga tambaya mai korewa, amsar “i” ita ce", "Did you go to school yesterday? No, I did not go.": "Ka tafi makaranta jiya? A'a, ban tafi ba.", "Didn't you go to school today? Yes, I went.": "Ba ka tafi makaranta yau ba? I, na tafi.", "Ibrahim did not go to the doctor.": "Ibrahim bai tafi wurin likita ba.", "li-anna": "li-anna", "because": "saboda", ", a sister of": ", 'yar'uwar", ". With pronouns:": ". Da wakilan suna:", "Why did you come back? I came back because I am sick.": "Me ya sa ka dawo? Na dawo saboda ba ni da lafiya.", "Hamid came back from school because he is sick.": "Hamid ya dawo daga makaranta saboda ba shi da lafiya.", "Aminah came back because she is sick.": "Aminatu ta dawo saboda ba ta da lafiya.", "he came back": "ya dawo", "New words: verbs": "Sababbin kalmomi: fi'iloli", "a maternal aunt": "inna, 'yar'uwar uwa", "a maternal uncle": "kawu, ɗan'uwan uwa", "the class period": "lokacin darasi, wato hissa", "the doctor": "likitan", "New words: words in the dialogue": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin tattaunawar", "khaalun": "khaalun", "al-ḥiṣṣatu": "al-ḥiṣṣatu", "aṭ-ṭabeebu": "aṭ-ṭabeebu", "no problem, never mind": "ba komai, ba damuwa", "why": "me ya sa", "Welcome, uncle. How are you? I hope you are well.": "Maraba, kawu. Yaya kake? Ina fata kana lafiya.", "Where is your father, Ibrahim? He went to the market.": "Ina babanka yake, Ibrahim? Ya tafi kasuwa.", "And where are your brothers? They went to the university.": "Kuma ina 'yan'uwanka maza suke? Sun tafi jami'a.", "Didn't you go to school today? Yes, I went and came back after the first period.": "Ba ka tafi makaranta yau ba? I, na tafi kuma na dawo bayan lokacin darasi na farko.", "Why did you come back? Because I am sick. Never mind. Did you go to the doctor? Yes, I went.": "Me ya sa ka dawo? Saboda ba ni da lafiya. Ba damuwa. Ka tafi wurin likita? I, na tafi.", "Choose the verb for the pronoun.": "Zaɓi fi'ilin da ya dace da wakilin sunan.", "with each person": "da kowane mutum", "Choose the verb:": "Zaɓi fi'ilin:", "Same endings, new verb.": "Ƙarshe iri ɗaya, sabon fi'ili.", "One verb has the wrong ending.": "Fi'ili ɗaya yana da ƙarshen da bai dace ba.", "Correct the sentence": "Gyara jumlar", "Choose the correct sentence:": "Zaɓi jumlar da ta yi daidai:", "Say no, with": "Ka ce a'a, da", "before the verb.": "kafin fi'ilin.", "Answer no.": "Amsa da a'a.", "After a question with not, say": "Bayan tambaya mai korewa, ka ce", "Answer yes.": "Amsa da i.", "+ pronoun": "tare da wakilin suna", "to the right pronoun.": "da wakilin sunan da ya dace.", "رَجَعُوا لِأَنَّ … مَرْضَى (they)": "رَجَعُوا لِأَنَّ … مَرْضَى, wato su", "رَجَعَ حَامِدٌ لِأَنَّ … مَرِيضٌ (he)": "رَجَعَ حَامِدٌ لِأَنَّ … مَرِيضٌ, wato shi", "رَجَعَتْ آمِنَةُ لِأَنَّ … مَرِيضَةٌ (she)": "رَجَعَتْ آمِنَةُ لِأَنَّ … مَرِيضَةٌ, wato ita", "They went to the university.": "Sun tafi jami'a.", "لِأَنَّ + pronoun": "لِأَنَّ tare da wakilin suna", "رَجَعَ with each person": "رَجَعَ da kowane mutum", "ذَهَبَ with each person": "ذَهَبَ da kowane mutum", "نَعَمْ or بَلَى?": "نَعَمْ ko بَلَى?", "Answer with مَا": "Amsa da مَا", "My mother went to my aunt.": "Mamata ta tafi wurin innata.", "My father went to the market.": "Babana ya tafi kasuwa.", "✅ Answer yes.": "✅ Amsa da i.", "✅ Answer no.": "✅ Amsa da a'a.", "✅ My mother went to my aunt.": "✅ Mamata ta tafi wurin innata.", "✅ My father went to the market.": "✅ Babana ya tafi kasuwa.", "In this lesson you will learn the parts of a verb sentence. The doer,": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi sassan jumlar fi'ili. Fa'ili, wato mai aikatawa,", "and the object,": "da maf'uli bihi, wato wanda aka yi wa aikin,", "You will see that a verb before a plural doer stays singular, and you will join the object to the verb, like": "Za ka ga cewa fi'ili da ke kafin fa'ili na jam'i yana zama tilo, kuma za ka haɗa maf'uli da fi'ilin, kamar", "I opened it.": "na buɗe ta.", "A verb sentence has the verb, then the doer,": "Jumlar fi'ili tana da fi'ili, sannan fa'ili, wato mai aikatawa,", "ending in": "mai ƙarewa da", "then the object,": "sannan maf'uli, wato wanda aka yi wa aikin,", "When the verb comes before a plural doer, it stays singular:": "Idan fi'ilin ya zo kafin fa'ili na jam'i, yana zama tilo:", "For women:": "Ga mata:", "The object can be a pronoun joined to the verb.": "Maf'uli yana iya zama wakilin suna da aka haɗa da fi'ilin.", "I opened it, for a feminine word or things.": "na buɗe ta, ga kalmar mace ko abubuwa.", "Put it all together.": "Haɗa duka tare.", "I did not break it.": "Ban karya shi ba.", "because I did not understand the questions.": "saboda ban fahimci tambayoyin ba.", "the doer and the object": "fa'ili da maf'uli", "Find the doer": "Nemo fa'ili", "Find the object": "Nemo maf'uli", "Endings": "Ƙarshe", "Verb first": "Fi'ili a farko", "It, them": "Shi, su", "In this lesson you will learn the parts of a verb sentence. The doer, الْفَاعِلُ, ends in ضَمَّةْ, and the object, الْمَفْعُولُ بِهِ, ends in فَتْحَةْ: قَرَأَ الطَّالِبُ الْقُرْآنَ. You will see that a verb before a plural doer stays singular, and you will join the object to the verb, like فَتَحْتُهُ, I opened it.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi sassan jumlar fi'ili. Fa'ili, الْفَاعِلُ, wato mai aikatawa, yana ƙarewa da ضَمَّةْ, kuma maf'uli bihi, الْمَفْعُولُ بِهِ, wato wanda aka yi wa aikin, yana ƙarewa da فَتْحَةْ: قَرَأَ الطَّالِبُ الْقُرْآنَ. Za ka ga cewa fi'ili da ke kafin fa'ili na jam'i yana zama tilo, kuma za ka haɗa maf'uli da fi'ilin, kamar فَتَحْتُهُ, na buɗe ta.", "qara'a": "qara'a", "read (verb)": "ya karanta, fi'ili", "aṭ-ṭaalibu": "aṭ-ṭaalibu", "the student (doer)": "ɗalibin, fa'ili", "al-qur'aana": "al-qur'aana", "the Qur'an (object)": "Alƙur'anin, maf'uli", "A verb sentence: the": "Jumlar fi'ili:", "verb": "fi'ili", ", then the": ", sannan", "doer": "fa'ili", ") ending in": ") mai ƙarewa da", "object": "maf'uli", "The student read the Qur'an.": "Ɗalibin ya karanta Alƙur'ani.", "The guest drank the coffee.": "Baƙon ya sha gahawar.", "The teacher wrote the lesson.": "Malamin ya rubuta darasin.", "Aminah opened the door.": "Aminatu ta buɗe ƙofar.", "aṭ-ṭullaabu dhahabuu": "aṭ-ṭullaabu dhahabuu", "dhahaba ṭ-ṭullaabu": "dhahaba ṭ-ṭullaabu", "The students went. (both)": "Ɗaliban sun tafi. Dukansu biyu.", "When the verb comes": "Idan fi'ilin ya zo", "a plural doer, it stays": "fa'ili na jam'i, yana zama", ". For women:": ". Ga mata:", ". When the doer comes first:": ". Idan fa'ili ya zo farko:", "The students went to the playground.": "Ɗaliban sun tafi filin wasa.", "The students (f) went to the library.": "Ɗalibai matan sun tafi ɗakin karatu.", "The new students went out and went to the principal.": "Sababbin ɗaliban sun fita sun tafi wurin shugaban makaranta.", "fataḥtu + hu": "fataḥtu + hu", "fataḥtuhu": "fataḥtuhu", "I opened it (m)": "na buɗe shi, namiji", "The object can be a pronoun joined to the verb:": "Maf'uli yana iya zama wakilin suna da aka haɗa da fi'ilin:", "(I opened it, m),": "wato na buɗe shi, namiji,", "(I opened it, f, or them, things),": "wato na buɗe ta, mace, ko na buɗe su, abubuwa,", "(I memorised it).": "wato na haddace shi.", "Who opened the classroom door? I opened it.": "Wane ne ya buɗe ƙofar ajin? Ni na buɗe ta.", "And who opened the windows? I opened them.": "Kuma wane ne ya buɗe tagogin? Ni na buɗe su.", "Did you memorise Surat al-Fajr? Yes, I memorised it.": "Ka haddace Suratul Fajr? I, na haddace ta.", "Did you understand the lesson? Yes, I understood it well.": "Ka fahimci darasin? I, na fahimce shi sosai.", "innee maa kasartuhu": "innee maa kasartuhu", "I did not break it": "ban karya shi ba", "Put it all together:": "Haɗa duka tare:", "+ verb + pronoun object.": "tare da fi'ili da wakilin suna na maf'uli.", "= because I did not understand the questions.": "yana nufin saboda ban fahimci tambayoyin ba.", "Who broke this desk? Did you break it, Hashim? No, I did not break it.": "Wane ne ya karya wannan teburin? Kai ne ka karya shi, Hashim? A'a, ban karya shi ba.", "Did you write the answers, Faisal? No, I did not write them.": "Ka rubuta amsoshin, Faisal? A'a, ban rubuta su ba.", "Why? Because I did not understand the questions.": "Me ya sa? Saboda ban fahimci tambayoyin ba.", "he opened": "ya buɗe", "he broke": "ya karya", "he understood": "ya fahimta", "he wrote": "ya rubuta", "he memorised": "ya haddace", "he heard": "ya ji", "he drank": "ya sha", "fataḥa": "fataḥa", "kasara": "kasara", "fahima": "fahima", "kataba": "kataba", "ḥafiẓa": "ḥafiẓa", "sami'a": "sami'a", "shariba": "shariba", "grapes": "inabi", "bananas": "ayaba", "figs": "ɓaure", "the stick": "sandar", "a snake": "maciji", "al-'inabu": "al-'inabu", "al-mawzu": "al-mawzu", "at-teenu": "at-teenu", "al-'aṣaa": "al-'aṣaa", "ḥayyatun (pl. ḥayyaatun)": "ḥayyatun (pl. ḥayyaatun)", "an answer": "amsa", "the grocer": "mai shagon kayan abinci", "dawn, Surat al-Fajr": "alfijir, Suratul Fajr", "New words: school words": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin makaranta", "jawaabun (pl. ajwibatun)": "jawaabun (pl. ajwibatun)", "al-baqqaalu": "al-baqqaalu", "al-fajru": "al-fajru", "the object": "maf'uli, wato wanda aka yi wa aiki", "the doer (subject)": "fa'ili, wato mai aikatawa", "Did Zakariyya, Hamzah and Uthman come back from Makkah? No, they did not.": "Shin Zakariyya, Hamza da Usman sun dawo daga Makka? A'a, ba su dawo ba.", "Teacher, the new students went out and went to the principal.": "Malam, sababbin ɗaliban sun fita sun tafi wurin shugaban makaranta.", "Did you write the answers, Faisal? No, because I did not understand the questions.": "Ka rubuta amsoshin, Faisal? A'a, saboda ban fahimci tambayoyin ba.", "Did you memorise Surat al-Fajr, Ibrahim? Yes, and I memorised Surat at-Teen too.": "Ka haddace Suratul Fajr, Ibrahim? I, kuma na haddace Suratut Tin ma.", "Who did the action? It ends in -u.": "Wane ne ya yi aikin? Yana ƙarewa da -u.", "Find the doer (": "Nemo fa'ili (", "Which word is the doer?": "Wace kalma ce fa'ili?", "What received the action? It ends in -a.": "Me aka yi wa aikin? Yana ƙarewa da -a.", "Find the object (": "Nemo maf'uli (", "Which word is the object?": "Wace kalma ce maf'uli?", "Choose the sentence with the right endings.": "Zaɓi jumlar da ke da ƙarshe masu kyau.", "-u for the doer, -a for the object": "-u ga fa'ili, -a ga maf'uli", "“The man killed the snake.”": "“Mutumin ya kashe macijin.”", "“The grocer opened the shop.”": "“Mai shagon kayan abinci ya buɗe shagon.”", "“Hamzah memorised the Qur'an.”": "“Hamza ya haddace Alƙur'ani.”", "“Bilal heard the adhan.”": "“Bilal ya ji kiran sallah.”", "“Yusuf drank the coffee.”": "“Yusuf ya sha gahawar.”", "“The child broke the pen.”": "“Yaron ya karya alƙalamin.”", "Before a plural doer the verb stays singular.": "Kafin fa'ili na jam'i fi'ilin yana zama tilo.", "Put the verb first": "Sanya fi'ilin a farko", "Put the verb first:": "Sanya fi'ilin a farko:", "for a masculine word,": "ga kalmar namiji,", "for a feminine word or things.": "ga kalmar mace ko abubuwa.", "Answer with a pronoun.": "Amsa da wakilin suna.", "Find the doer (الْفَاعِلُ)": "Nemo fa'ili (الْفَاعِلُ)", "Find the object (الْمَفْعُولُ بِهِ)": "Nemo maf'uli (الْمَفْعُولُ بِهِ)", "Listen, then write the word. (bananas)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato ayaba.", "✅ The students went to the playground.": "✅ Ɗaliban sun tafi filin wasa.", "✅ “Hamzah memorised the Qur'an.”": "✅ “Hamza ya haddace Alƙur'ani.”", "✅ Write: bananas": "✅ Rubuta: ayaba", "✅ Answer with a pronoun.": "✅ Amsa da wakilin suna.", "✅ The guest drank the coffee.": "✅ Baƙon ya sha gahawar.", "In this lesson you will join it and them to a verb, like": "A wannan darasi za ka haɗa shi, ita da su da fi'ili, kamar", "I saw him, and": "na gan shi, da", "I saw her. You will learn": "na gan ta. Za ka koyi", "that, as in": "cewa, kamar a cikin", "and count eleven to nineteen with a feminine noun. You will also learn words like": "ka kuma ƙirga goma sha ɗaya zuwa goma sha tara da sunan mace. Za ka kuma koyi kalmomi kamar", "hungry, and": "mai yunwa, da", "for a woman,": "ga mace,", "why, and": "me ya sa, da", "give me.": "ba ni.", "Join the object to the verb.": "Haɗa maf'uli da fi'ilin.", "I saw him.": "Na gan shi.", "I saw her.": "Na gan ta.", "I saw them.": "Na gan su.", "I saw them, for women.": "Na gan su, ga mata.", "means that. It is another sister of": "ma'anarsa cewa. Wata 'yar'uwar", "and joins two sentences:": "ce kuma tana haɗa jumloli biyu:", "I think that he is sick.": "Ina tsammani cewa ba shi da lafiya.", "With a feminine noun,": "Da sunan mace,", "and three to nine lose the": "kuma uku zuwa tara suna rasa", "Words on the pattern": "Kalmomi a kan tsarin", "have no tanween, and the feminine is": "ba su da tanwini, kuma na macensu shi ne", "means why, the same as": "ma'anarsa me ya sa, daidai da", "Alone it is said": "Idan shi kaɗai ne ana cewa", "means give me. To a woman,": "ma'anarsa ba ni. Ga mace,", "To men,": "Ga maza,", "To women,": "Ga mata,", "أَنَّ (that)": "أَنَّ, wato cewa", "جَوْعَانُ (hungry)": "جَوْعَانُ, wato mai yunwa", "Him, her, them": "Shi, ita, su", "Give me": "Ba ni", "In this lesson you will join it and them to a verb, like رَأَيْتُهُ, I saw him, and رَأَيْتُهَا, I saw her. You will learn أَنَّ, that, as in أَظُنُّ أَنَّهُ مَرِيضٌ, and count eleven to nineteen with a feminine noun. You will also learn words like جَوْعَانُ, hungry, and جَوْعَى for a woman, لِمَ, why, and هَاتِ, give me.": "A wannan darasi za ka haɗa shi, ita da su da fi'ili, kamar رَأَيْتُهُ, na gan shi, da رَأَيْتُهَا, na gan ta. Za ka koyi أَنَّ, cewa, kamar a cikin أَظُنُّ أَنَّهُ مَرِيضٌ, ka kuma ƙirga goma sha ɗaya zuwa goma sha tara da sunan mace. Za ka kuma koyi kalmomi kamar جَوْعَانُ, mai yunwa, da جَوْعَى ga mace, لِمَ, me ya sa, da هَاتِ, ba ni.", "ra'aytuhu": "ra'aytuhu", "I saw him": "na gan shi", "ra'aytuhaa": "ra'aytuhaa", "ra'aytuhum": "ra'aytuhum", "them (m)": "su, maza", "ra'aytuhunna": "ra'aytuhunna", "them (f)": "su, mata", "Join the object to the verb:": "Haɗa maf'uli da fi'ilin:", "(him, it),": "wato shi,", "(her, it, or things),": "wato ita, ko abubuwa,", "(them, m),": "wato su, maza,", "(them, f).": "wato su, mata.", "Did you see Hamid? Yes, I saw him.": "Ka ga Hamid? I, na gan shi.", "Where is your sister Maryam? I don't know. I did not see her.": "Ina 'yar'uwarka Maryam take? Ban sani ba. Ban gan ta ba.", "Did you see Hamid, Hisham and Ali? Yes, I saw them.": "Ka ga Hamid, Hisham da Ali? I, na gan su.", "Where are your classmates? I did not see them after the prayer.": "Ina abokan ajinka suke? Ban gan su ba bayan sallah.", "inna": "inna", "indeed": "lalle", "anna": "anna", "(that) is another sister of": "wato cewa, wata 'yar'uwar", ". It joins two sentences:": "ce. Tana haɗa jumloli biyu:", "(I think that he is sick). The word after it ends in a fatha.": "wato ina tsammani cewa ba shi da lafiya. Kalmar da ke bayansa tana ƙarewa da fatha.", "I think that the teacher did not come.": "Ina tsammani cewa malamin bai zo ba.", "I think that she went to Makkah.": "Ina tsammani cewa ta tafi Makka.", "I heard that Bilal is sick.": "Na ji cewa Bilal ba shi da lafiya.", "iḥdaa 'ashrata ṭaalibatan … tis'a 'ashrata ṭaalibatan": "iḥdaa 'ashrata ṭaalibatan … tis'a 'ashrata ṭaalibatan", "11 students (f) … 19 students (f)": "ɗalibai mata 11 … ɗalibai mata 19", "With a": "Da sunan", "noun, 11 to 19 change:": "mace, 11 zuwa 19 suna canzawa:", ", and 3 to 9 lose the": ", kuma 3 zuwa 9 suna rasa", ". 11 is": ". 11 ita ce", ", 12 is": ", 12 ita ce", "hungry (m)": "mai yunwa, namiji", "jaw'aa": "jaw'aa", "hungry (f)": "mai yunwa, mace", "have": "ba su da", "-un ending, and the feminine is": "ƙarshen -un, kuma na macensu shi ne", ". Plurals:": ". Jam'i:", "(hungry),": "wato masu yunwa,", "(lazy).": "wato malalata.", "Hamid is hungry.": "Hamid yana jin yunwa.", "Maryam is hungry.": "Maryam tana jin yunwa.", "The students are hungry.": "Ɗaliban suna jin yunwa.", "The teacher is angry.": "Malamin yana fushi.", "lima": "lima", "why?": "me ya sa?", "give me": "ba ni", "(why). Alone it is said": "wato me ya sa. Idan shi kaɗai ne ana cewa", "means give me (to a man),": "ma'anarsa ba ni, ga namiji,", "(to a woman),": "ga mace,", "(to men),": "ga maza,", "(to women).": "ga mata.", "Why did you go out of the class?": "Me ya sa ka fita daga ajin?", "No, she did not come today. Why?": "A'a, ba ta zo yau ba. Me ya sa?", "Bring the tea, Layla.": "Kawo shayin, Laila.", "Give me that one, mother. That is more beautiful than this.": "Ba ni waccan, mama. Waccan ta fi wannan kyau.", "a surah": "sura", "a tooth, age": "haƙori, shekaru", "suuratun (pl. suwarun)": "suuratun (pl. suwarun)", "sinnun (pl. asnaanun)": "sinnun (pl. asnaanun)", "a building": "gini", "a flat, an apartment": "gida a bene, wato fulat", "'imaaratun (pl. 'amaa'iru)": "'imaaratun (pl. 'amaa'iru)", "shaqqatun (pl. shiqaqun)": "shaqqatun (pl. shiqaqun)", "he came": "ya zo", "he ironed": "ya yi guga", "full (not hungry)": "ƙoshi, wanda ba ya jin yunwa", "New words: verbs and feelings": "Sababbin kalmomi: fi'iloli da yadda ake ji", "jaa'a": "jaa'a", "kawaa": "kawaa", "jaw'aanu (f. jaw'aa)": "jaw'aanu (f. jaw'aa)", "'aṭshaanu (f. 'aṭshaa)": "'aṭshaanu (f. 'aṭshaa)", "shab'aanu (f. shab'aa)": "shab'aanu (f. shab'aa)", "ghaḍbaanu (f. ghaḍbaa)": "ghaḍbaanu (f. ghaḍbaa)", "I think": "ina tsammani", "he saw": "ya gani", "When did you come back from school, son? I came back half an hour ago.": "Yaushe ka dawo daga makaranta, ɗana? Na dawo rabin awa da ya wuce.", "Where is your sister Maryam? Hasn't she come back? I don't know. I did not see her.": "Ina 'yar'uwarka Maryam take? Ba ta dawo ba? Ban sani ba. Ban gan ta ba.", "What did you read today? I read a new lesson in fiqh. Did you understand it? Yes, I understood it well.": "Me ka karanta yau? Na karanta sabon darasi a fiƙihu. Ka fahimce shi? I, na fahimce shi sosai.", "I read Surat ar-Rahman and memorised it. The teacher was very happy with me.": "Na karanta Suratur Rahman kuma na haddace ta. Malamin ya yi farin ciki da ni sosai.", "Ma sha Allah. May Allah increase you in knowledge, my son.": "Ma sha Allah. Allah ya ƙara maka ilimi, ɗana.", "Where are your classmates Aminah, Fatimah and Suad? I did not see them after the prayer.": "Ina abokan ajinki Aminatu, Faɗimatu da Su'ad suke? Ban gan su ba bayan sallah.", "I think that she went to Makkah. Bring a piece of bread too, Layla. I am hungry.": "Ina tsammani cewa ta tafi Makka. Kawo guntun burodi ma, Laila. Ina jin yunwa.", "Answer with the right pronoun.": "Amsa da wakilin sunan da ya dace.", "Join with": "Haɗa da", ". The word after it ends in a fatha.": ". Kalmar da ke bayansa tana ƙarewa da fatha.", "Begin with أَظُنُّ:": "Fara da أَظُنُّ:", "The word after it ends in a": "Kalmar da ke bayansa tana ƙarewa da", "11–19 with a feminine noun": "11 zuwa 19 da sunan mace", "for feminine,": "ga mace,", "for masculine.": "ga namiji.", "The feminine of": "Na macen", "Choose the right form.": "Zaɓi siffar da ta dace.", "Say “give” to men:": "Ka ce “ba ni” ga maza:", "Say “give” to a man:": "Ka ce “ba ni” ga namiji:", "Say “give” to women:": "Ka ce “ba ni” ga mata:", "Say “give” to a woman:": "Ka ce “ba ni” ga mace:", "In the class there are thirteen students (f).": "A ajin akwai ɗalibai mata goma sha uku.", "Listen, then write the word. (a flat, an apartment)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato gida a bene, fulat.", "✅ I think that he is sick.": "✅ Ina tsammani cewa ba shi da lafiya.", "✅ In the class there are thirteen students (f).": "✅ A ajin akwai ɗalibai mata goma sha uku.", "✅ Write: a flat, an apartment": "✅ Rubuta: gida a bene, fulat", "✅ Say “give” to a man:": "✅ Ka ce “ba ni” ga namiji:", "In this lesson you will talk to a group:": "A wannan darasi za ka yi magana da rukuni:", "you men went, and": "ku maza kun tafi, da", "you women went. You will join it to these verbs, like": "ku mata kun tafi. Za ka haɗa shi da waɗannan fi'iloli, kamar", "did you see it. You will learn": "kun gan shi. Za ka koyi", "was, the helping vowel before": "ya kasance, wasalin taimako kafin", "and the fractions": "da rabe-raben lamba", "half,": "rabi,", "a third, and": "sulusi, wato kashi ɗaya cikin uku, da", "a quarter.": "rubu'i, wato kashi ɗaya cikin huɗu.", "To a group of men, -": "Ga rukunin maza, -", "To a group of women, -": "Ga rukunin mata, -", "They answer with": "Suna amsawa da", "When an object pronoun joins -": "Idan wakilin suna na maf'uli ya haɗu da -", "comes in between.": "yana shiga tsakani.", "make": "suna yin", "means was. For a woman,": "ma'anarsa ya kasance. Ga mace,", "A word ending in a sukun gets a vowel before": "Kalmar da ke ƙarewa da sukun tana samun wasali kafin", "When the noun has": "Idan sunan yana da", "the word after": "kalmar da ke bayan", "also takes": "ita ma tana ɗaukar", "Fractions:": "Rabe-raben lamba:", "half.": "rabi.", "a third.": "sulusi.", "a fifth.": "humusi, wato kashi ɗaya cikin biyar.", "a sixth.": "sudusi, wato kashi ɗaya cikin shida.", "a tenth.": "ushuri, wato kashi ɗaya cikin goma.", "ذَهَبْتُمْ (you all went)": "ذَهَبْتُمْ, wato kun tafi", "كَانَ (was)": "كَانَ, wato ya kasance", "-تُمْ or -تُنَّ": "تُمْ ko تُنَّ", "Say it to women": "Ka faɗe shi ga mata", "Helping vowel": "Wasalin taimako", "ذُو with الْ": "ذُو tare da الْ", "Fractions": "Rabe-raben lamba", "In this lesson you will talk to a group: ذَهَبْتُمْ, you men went, and ذَهَبْتُنَّ, you women went. You will join it to these verbs, like رَأَيْتُمُوهُ, did you see it. You will learn كَانَ, was, the helping vowel before الْ, ذُو with الْ, and the fractions نِصْفٌ, half, ثُلُثٌ, a third, and رُبْعٌ, a quarter.": "A wannan darasi za ka yi magana da rukuni: ذَهَبْتُمْ, ku maza kun tafi, da ذَهَبْتُنَّ, ku mata kun tafi. Za ka haɗa shi da waɗannan fi'iloli, kamar رَأَيْتُمُوهُ, kun gan shi. Za ka koyi كَانَ, ya kasance, wasalin taimako kafin الْ, ذُو tare da الْ, da rabe-raben lamba نِصْفٌ, rabi, ثُلُثٌ, sulusi, da رُبْعٌ, rubu'i.", "you (men) went": "ku maza kun tafi", "you (women) went": "ku mata kun tafi", "To a group of men:": "Ga rukunin maza:", ". To a group of women:": ". Ga rukunin mata:", ". The answer from the group:": ". Amsar rukunin:", "Where did you go after the lesson, my sons? We went to the playground.": "Ina kuka tafi bayan darasin, 'ya'yana? Mun tafi filin wasa.", "Where did you go, my daughters? We went to visit the headmistress.": "Ina kuka tafi, 'ya'yana mata? Mun tafi ziyarar shugabar makaranta.", "Did you walk or go by car?": "Kun tafi a ƙafa ne ko a mota?", "ra'aytum + hu": "ra'aytum + hu", "you all saw + him": "kun gani tare da shi", "ra'aytumuuhu": "ra'aytumuuhu", "you all saw him": "kun gan shi", "When an object pronoun joins": "Idan wakilin suna na maf'uli ya haɗu da", "comes in between:": "yana shiga tsakani:", ". With other endings nothing changes:": ". Da sauran ƙarshe babu abin da ke canzawa:", "Where is the book? Did you see it?": "Ina littafin yake? Kun gan shi?", "This is an easy lesson. Did you understand it?": "Wannan darasi ne mai sauƙi. Kun fahimce shi?", "Where is the snake? Did you kill it?": "Ina macijin yake? Kun kashe shi?", "kaana l-mudarrisu fil-faṣli": "kaana l-mudarrisu fil-faṣli", "The teacher is in the class.": "Malamin yana cikin ajin.", "The teacher was in the class.": "Malamin ya kasance a cikin ajin.", "was": "ya kasance", ". For a woman": ". Ga mace", ". Before a plural it stays": ". Kafin jam'i yana zama", "The teacher was in the class five minutes ago.": "Malamin ya kasance a cikin ajin minti biyar da suka wuce.", "The students were in the library half an hour ago.": "Ɗaliban sun kasance a ɗakin karatu rabin awa da ya wuce.", "My mother was in the kitchen a little while ago.": "Mamata ta kasance a kicin ɗan lokaci kaɗan da ya wuce.", "Where is the magazine that was under that book?": "Ina mujallar da ta kasance a ƙarƙashin wancan littafin?", "a-qara'tumu l-qur'aana": "a-qara'tumu l-qur'aana", "Did you read the Qur'an?": "Kun karanta Alƙur'ani?", "A word ending in a": "Kalmar da ke ƙarewa da", "sukun": "sukun", "gets a vowel before": "tana samun wasali kafin", "; other letters →": "; sauran haruffa →", "The alif of": "Alif na", "is not read.": "ba a karanta shi.", "Did you see the teacher?": "Ka ga malamin?", "Is the house yours?": "Gidan naka ne?", "The girl went out.": "Yarinyar ta fita.", "Who is the boy?": "Wane ne yaron?", "al-kitaabu dhul-ghilaafil-aḥmari": "al-kitaabu dhul-ghilaafil-aḥmari", "a book with a red cover": "littafi mai jan bango", "the book with the red cover": "littafin mai jan bango", ", the word after": ", kalmar da ke bayan", ". For feminine:": ". Ga mace:", "Where is the book with the red cover?": "Ina littafin mai jan bango yake?", "No, the magazine with the yellow cover.": "A'a, mujallar mai bangon rawaya.", "That man with the glasses is our principal.": "Wancan mutumin mai tabarau shi ne shugaban makarantarmu.", "thuluthun": "thuluthun", "rub'un": "rub'un", "= we sat with her for a third of an hour.": "yana nufin mun zauna tare da ita kashi ɗaya cikin uku na awa.", "a broom": "tsintsiya", "a ladder, stairs": "tsani, matakala", "glasses": "tabarau", "soap": "sabulu", "a picture": "hoto", "juice": "ruwan 'ya'yan itace, wato jus", "oranges": "lemu", "miknasatun (pl. makaanisu)": "miknasatun (pl. makaanisu)", "sullamun (pl. salaalimu)": "sullamun (pl. salaalimu)", "naẓẓaaratun (pl. naẓẓaaraatun)": "naẓẓaaratun (pl. naẓẓaaraatun)", "'ajalatun (pl. 'ajalun)": "'ajalatun (pl. 'ajalun)", "ṣaabuunun": "ṣaabuunun", "ṣuuratun (pl. ṣuwarun)": "ṣuuratun (pl. ṣuwarun)", "'aṣeerun": "'aṣeerun", "burtuqaalun": "burtuqaalun", "a minaret": "hasumiyar masallaci", "a radio station": "gidan rediyo", "football": "ƙwallon ƙafa", "basketball": "ƙwallon kwando", "a beard": "gemu", "New words: places and sport": "Sababbin kalmomi: wurare da wasanni", "manaaratun (pl. manaa'iru)": "manaaratun (pl. manaa'iru)", "idhaa'atun (pl. idhaa'aatun)": "idhaa'atun (pl. idhaa'aatun)", "kuratul-qadami": "kuratul-qadami", "kuratus-sallati": "kuratus-sallati", "liḥyatun (pl. liḥan)": "liḥyatun (pl. liḥan)", "he took": "ya ɗauka", "he put": "ya ajiye", "he found": "ya samu", "he looked for": "ya nema", "he walked": "ya yi tafiya a ƙafa", "akhadha": "akhadha", "waḍa'a": "waḍa'a", "wajada": "wajada", "baḥatha 'an": "baḥatha 'an", "mashaa": "mashaa", "yesterday evening": "jiya da daddare", "morning": "safiya", "New words: time words": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin lokaci", "al-baariḥata": "al-baariḥata", "ṣabaaḥun": "ṣabaaḥun", "he was": "ya kasance", "a quarter": "rubu'i, kashi ɗaya cikin huɗu", "a third": "sulusi, kashi ɗaya cikin uku", "Did you play football or basketball? Today we played football.": "Kun buga ƙwallon ƙafa ko ƙwallon kwando? Yau mun buga ƙwallon ƙafa.", "Did you hear the news on the radio today? Yes, we heard it.": "Kun ji labarai a rediyo yau? I, mun ji su.", "I heard that Bilal is sick and in hospital. Is it true? Yes, it is true. May Allah cure him.": "Na ji cewa Bilal ba shi da lafiya kuma yana asibiti. Gaskiya ne? I, gaskiya ne. Allah ya ba shi lafiya.", "Where is the book with the red cover that was in my room? Did you see it?": "Ina littafin mai jan bango da ya kasance a ɗakina? Kun gan shi?", "Where did you go, my daughters? We went to visit the headmistress. We sat with her a third of an hour.": "Ina kuka tafi, 'ya'yana mata? Mun tafi ziyarar shugabar makaranta. Mun zauna tare da ita kashi ɗaya cikin uku na awa.", "Mother, is there cold water in the fridge? We are thirsty. Good news, there is cold water and orange juice.": "Mama, akwai ruwan sanyi a firji? Muna jin ƙishirwa. Albishir, akwai ruwan sanyi da ruwan lemu.", "Men: -": "Maza: -", ". Women: -": ". Mata: -", "Fill the gap:": "Cika gurbin:", "Women: -": "Mata: -", "Change -": "Canza -", "to -": "zuwa -", "Say it to women:": "Ka faɗe shi ga mata:", "After -": "Bayan -", "Join the object": "Haɗa maf'uli", "add": "ƙara", "before the pronoun.": "kafin wakilin sunan.", "for a woman;": "ga mace;", "before men.": "kafin maza.", "Say it was, earlier:": "Ka ce ya kasance, a da:", "The helping vowel before": "Wasalin taimako kafin", "becomes -": "yana zama -", "; other letters take -": "; sauran haruffa suna ɗaukar -", "other letters take -": "sauran haruffa suna ɗaukar -", "After a noun with": "Bayan suna mai", ", the words after": ", kalmomin da ke bayan", "also take": "su ma suna ɗaukar", "عِنْدِي كِتَابٌ ذُو …… (a red cover)": "عِنْدِي كِتَابٌ ذُو …… Wato mai jan bango", "the words after": "kalmomin da ke bayan", "مَنْ ذٰلِكَ الْوَلَدُ ذُو …… ؟ (a red shirt)": "مَنْ ذٰلِكَ الْوَلَدُ ذُو …… ؟ Wato mai jar riga", "هٰذِهِ الدَّرَّاجَةُ ذَاتُ …… (three wheels)": "هٰذِهِ الدَّرَّاجَةُ ذَاتُ …… Wato mai tayoyi uku", "مَنْ ذٰلِكَ الْفَتَى ذُو …… ؟ (small glasses)": "مَنْ ذٰلِكَ الْفَتَى ذُو …… ؟ Wato mai ƙananan tabarau", "Choose the fraction word.": "Zaɓi kalmar rabon lamba.", "Where did you go, my sons?": "Ina kuka tafi, 'ya'yana?", "We went to the playground.": "Mun tafi filin wasa.", "ذَهَبْتُمْ or ذَهَبْتُنَّ?": "ذَهَبْتُمْ ko ذَهَبْتُنَّ?", "Add كَانَ": "Ƙara كَانَ", "The helping vowel before الْ": "Wasalin taimako kafin الْ", "Listen, then write the word. (a ladder, stairs)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato tsani, matakala.", "✅ We went to the playground.": "✅ Mun tafi filin wasa.", "✅ The teacher was in the class.": "✅ Malamin ya kasance a cikin ajin.", "✅ Write: a ladder, stairs": "✅ Rubuta: tsani, matakala", "This is a review lesson. You will put together the whole past verb table, from": "Wannan darasi ne na bita. Za ka haɗa dukan teburin fi'ilin da ya wuce, daga", "he went, to": "ya tafi, zuwa", "we went. You will also find the doer inside the verb: the endings": "mun tafi. Za ka kuma nemo fa'ili a cikin fi'ilin: ƙarshen", "and the hidden doer in": "da fa'ili ɓoyayye a cikin", "The absent person.": "Wanda ba ya nan, wato gha'ib.", "The person spoken to.": "Wanda ake magana da shi, wato mukhatab.", "The speaker:": "Mai magana, wato mutakallim:", "In these verbs the ending is the doer: the": "A cikin waɗannan fi'iloli ƙarshen shi ne fa'ili:", "In": "A cikin", "the doer is hidden. The": "fa'ili ɓoyayye ne. Harafin", "is not the doer. It only shows that the doer is a woman.": "ba fa'ili ba ne. Yana nuna kawai cewa fa'ili mace ce.", "the past verb table (review)": "teburin fi'ilin da ya wuce, bita", "The table": "Teburin", "ذَهَبَ in a sentence": "ذَهَبَ a cikin jumla", "Other verbs": "Wasu fi'iloli", "Hidden doer": "Fa'ili ɓoyayye", "This is a review lesson. You will put together the whole past verb table, from ذَهَبَ, he went, to ذَهَبْنَا, we went. You will also find the doer inside the verb: the endings تَاءْ, وَاوْ, نُونْ and نَا, and the hidden doer in ذَهَبَ and ذَهَبَتْ.": "Wannan darasi ne na bita. Za ka haɗa dukan teburin fi'ilin da ya wuce, daga ذَهَبَ, ya tafi, zuwa ذَهَبْنَا, mun tafi. Za ka kuma nemo fa'ili a cikin fi'ilin: ƙarshen تَاءْ, وَاوْ, نُونْ da نَا, da fa'ili ɓoyayye a cikin ذَهَبَ da ذَهَبَتْ.", "The absent person (": "Wanda ba ya nan (", "). Men:": "). Maza:", "Hamid went.": "Hamid ya tafi.", "Hamid, Hashim and Ali went.": "Hamid, Hashim da Ali sun tafi.", "Aminah went.": "Aminatu ta tafi.", "Aminah, Zainab and Maryam went.": "Aminatu, Zainab da Maryam sun tafi.", "you went (m pl)": "kun tafi, jam'in maza", "The person spoken to (": "Wanda ake magana da shi (", ". The speaker (": ". Mai magana (", ", the same for men and women.": ", iri ɗaya ne ga maza da mata.", "you all (m)": "ku, maza", "you all (f)": "ku, mata", "You (m) went.": "Kai ka tafi.", "You all (m) went.": "Ku maza kun tafi.", "You (f) went.": "Ke kin tafi.", "You all (f) went.": "Ku mata kun tafi.", "We went.": "Mun tafi.", "In these verbs the": "A cikin waɗannan fi'iloli", "ending is the doer": "ƙarshen shi ne fa'ili", "): -tu in": "): -tu a cikin", ", -uu in": ", -uu a cikin", ", -na in": ", -na a cikin", ", -naa in": ", -naa a cikin", ". It is the same in": ". Haka yake a cikin", "the ending -tu is the doer: I": "ƙarshen -tu shi ne fa'ili: ni", "the ending -uu is the doer: they": "ƙarshen -uu shi ne fa'ili: su", "the ending -na is the doer: they (f)": "ƙarshen -na shi ne fa'ili: su, mata", "the ending -naa is the doer: we": "ƙarshen -naa shi ne fa'ili: mu", "kharajat": "kharajat", "she went out": "ta fita", "the doer is": "fa'ilin", "hidden": "ɓoyayye ne", "): he or she. The": "): shi ko ita. Harafin", "the doer; it only shows the doer is feminine.": "fa'ili ba ne; yana nuna kawai cewa fa'ili mace ce.", "Where is Hamid? He went out.": "Ina Hamid yake? Ya fita.", "Where is Aminah? She went out.": "Ina Aminatu take? Ta fita.", "he entered": "ya shiga", "he ate": "ya ci", "he washed": "ya wanke", "he played": "ya yi wasa", "he hit": "ya buga, ya daka", "he killed": "ya kashe", "New words: verbs to review": "Sababbin kalmomi: fi'ilolin bita", "dakhala": "dakhala", "jalasa": "jalasa", "akala": "akala", "ghasala": "ghasala", "la'iba": "la'iba", "ḍaraba": "ḍaraba", "qatala": "qatala", "Hamid went, and Hamid, Hashim and Ali went.": "Hamid ya tafi, kuma Hamid, Hashim da Ali sun tafi.", "Aminah went, and Aminah, Zainab and Maryam went.": "Aminatu ta tafi, kuma Aminatu, Zainab da Maryam sun tafi.", "You (m) went, and you all (m) went.": "Kai ka tafi, kuma ku maza kun tafi.", "You (f) went, and you all (f) went.": "Ke kin tafi, kuma ku mata kun tafi.", "I went, and we went.": "Na tafi, kuma mun tafi.", "I looked for my pen but I did not find it.": "Na nemi alƙalamina amma ban same shi ba.", "Match each pronoun to its verb.": "Haɗa kowane wakilin suna da fi'ilinsa.", "The whole table": "Dukan teburin", "Fill in": "Cika", "Look at who is doing it.": "Duba wanda yake yin aikin.", "Fill in the verb": "Cika fi'ilin", "Which part is the doer?": "Wane sashe ne fa'ili?", "at the end is the doer.": "a ƙarshe shi ne fa'ili.", "Hidden or showing?": "Ɓoyayye ko a bayyane?", "the doer is hidden.": "fa'ili ɓoyayye ne.", "Where is the doer of the last verb?": "Ina fa'ilin fi'ili na ƙarshe yake?", "hidden (he)": "ɓoyayye, wato shi", "the فَ": "harafin فَ", "the تْ": "harafin تْ", "hidden (she)": "ɓoyayye, wato ita", "the تُ": "harafin تُ", "Listen, then write the word. (he sat)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato ya zauna.", "Fill in ذَهَبَ": "Cika ذَهَبَ", "I looked for my pen and did not find it.": "Na nemi alƙalamina kuma ban same shi ba.", "✅ Write: he sat": "✅ Rubuta: ya zauna", "✅ Hamid, Hashim and Ali went.": "✅ Hamid, Hashim da Ali sun tafi.", "✅ I looked for my pen and did not find it.": "✅ Na nemi alƙalamina kuma ban same shi ba.", "In this lesson you will say how wonderful something is:": "A wannan darasi za ka faɗi yadda abu yake da ban mamaki:", "how easy this lesson is. You will call people the right way, like": "kai, wannan darasi akwai sauƙi. Za ka kira mutane ta hanyar da ta dace, kamar", "and see the plural object ending,": "ka kuma ga ƙarshen jam'i na maf'uli,", "You will learn": "Za ka koyi", "he created me, the short question words": "ya halicce ni, gajerun kalmomin tambaya", "and the joining words": "da kalmomin haɗawa", "To say how wonderful, use": "Don faɗar ban mamaki, yi amfani da", "a single name ends in": "suna guda yana ƙarewa da", "A two-word name ends in": "Suna mai kalmomi biyu yana ƙarewa da", "A plural ending in": "Jam'i mai ƙarewa da", "takes": "yana ɗaukar", "as an object, never": "a matsayin maf'uli, ba", "The object me on a verb is": "Maf'uli ni a kan fi'ili shi ne", "he created me. Us is": "ya halicce ni. Mu shi ne", "You is": "Kai shi ne", "after a short word becomes short.": "bayan gajeriyar kalma yana zama gajere.", "These words join a noun to a sentence about it.": "Waɗannan kalmomi suna haɗa suna da jumla game da shi.", "for a man.": "ga namiji.", "for men.": "ga maza.", "for a woman.": "ga mace.", "الَّذِي (who, which)": "الَّذِي, wato wanda, wadda", "How …!": "Kai, … !", "Plural ـَاتٍ": "Jam'i ـَاتٍ", "Me, us": "Ni, mu", "In this lesson you will say how wonderful something is: مَا أَسْهَلَ هٰذَا الدَّرْسَ, how easy this lesson is. You will call people the right way, like يَا عَبْدَ اللهِ, and see the plural object ending, رَأَيْتُ سَيَّارَاتٍ. You will learn خَلَقَنِي, he created me, the short question words مِمَّ, بِمَ and عَمَّ, and the joining words الَّذِي, الَّذِينَ, الَّتِي and اللَّاتِي.": "A wannan darasi za ka faɗi yadda abu yake da ban mamaki: مَا أَسْهَلَ هٰذَا الدَّرْسَ, kai, wannan darasi akwai sauƙi. Za ka kira mutane ta hanyar da ta dace, kamar يَا عَبْدَ اللهِ, ka kuma ga ƙarshen jam'i na maf'uli, رَأَيْتُ سَيَّارَاتٍ. Za ka koyi خَلَقَنِي, ya halicce ni, gajerun kalmomin tambaya مِمَّ, بِمَ da عَمَّ, da kalmomin haɗawa الَّذِي, الَّذِينَ, الَّتِي da اللَّاتِي.", "maa as-hala haadha d-darsa": "maa as-hala haadha d-darsa", "This lesson is easy.": "Wannan darasi yana da sauƙi.", "How easy this lesson is!": "Kai, wannan darasi akwai sauƙi!", "To say “how …!”, use": "Don faɗar “kai, … !”, yi amfani da", "(ending in -a) + the noun ending in": "mai ƙarewa da -a, tare da sunan mai ƙarewa da", "How tall this man is!": "Kai, wannan mutumin akwai tsawo!", "How beautiful this car is!": "Kai, wannan motar akwai kyau!", "How big this house is!": "Kai, wannan gidan akwai girma!", "O Muhammad": "Ya Muhammadu", "yaa 'abda llaahi": "yaa 'abda llaahi", "O Abdullah": "Ya Abdullahi", "without -un:": "ba tare da -un ba:", ". A two-word name (idafa) ends in": ". Suna mai kalmomi biyu, wato idafa, yana ƙarewa da", "O Muhammad, O Hamid, O teacher": "Ya Muhammadu, ya Hamid, ya malam", "O Abdullah, O Abdur-Rahman": "Ya Abdullahi, ya Abdurrahman", "Well done, Abu Bakr.": "Madalla, Abubakar.", "O imam of the mosque": "Ya limamin masallaci", "ra'aytu sayyaaratan": "ra'aytu sayyaaratan", "I saw a car": "na ga mota", "ra'aytu sayyaaraatin": "ra'aytu sayyaaraatin", "I saw cars": "na ga motoci", "takes a": "yana ɗaukar", "kasra": "kasra", "(-i, -in) as an object, never a fatha:": "wato -i, -in, a matsayin maf'uli, ba fatha ba:", "I saw cars.": "Na ga motoci.", "The headmistress asked the students.": "Shugabar makarantar ta tambayi ɗaliban mata.", "I read the magazines.": "Na karanta mujallun.", "Allah created the heavens and the earth.": "Allah ya halicci sammai da ƙasa.", "khalaqanee": "khalaqanee", "he created me": "ya halicce ni", "khalaqanaa": "khalaqanaa", "us": "mu", "khalaqaka": "khalaqaka", "The object": "Maf'uli", "me": "ni", "on a verb is": "a kan fi'ili shi ne", "(not just -": "ba kawai -", ". Us:": ". Mu:", ". You:": ". Kai:", "Who created you, Ibrahim? Allah created me.": "Wane ne ya halicce ka, Ibrahim? Allah ne ya halicce ni.", "Who created you, my sons? Allah created us.": "Wane ne ya halicce ku, 'ya'yana? Allah ne ya halicce mu.", "Did the teacher see you in the mosque? Yes, he saw me.": "Malamin ya gan ka a masallaci? I, ya gan ni.", "mimma": "mimma", "from what?": "daga me?", "bima": "bima", "with what?": "da me?", "'amma": "'amma", "about what?": "game da me?", "after a short word becomes short:": "bayan gajeriyar kalma yana zama gajere:", "From what did Allah create man? He created him from clay.": "Daga me Allah ya halicci mutum? Ya halicce shi daga taɓo.", "From what did Allah create the jinn? From fire.": "Daga me Allah ya halicci aljanu? Daga wuta.", "With what did you kill the snake? With a stone.": "Da me ka kashe macijin? Da dutse.", "What did you look for at school? I looked for my watch.": "Me ka nema a makaranta? Na nemi agogona.", "who/which: m": "wanda, wadda: namiji", "alladheena": "alladheena", "allaatee": "allaatee", "f pl": "jam'in mata", "These join a noun with": "Waɗannan suna haɗa suna mai", "to a sentence about it:": "da jumla game da shi:", "Who is the boy who entered the class just now?": "Wane ne yaron da ya shiga ajin yanzu-yanzu?", "Who are the boys who entered the class just now?": "Su wane ne yaran da suka shiga ajin yanzu-yanzu?", "Who is the girl who entered the class just now?": "Wace ce yarinyar da ta shiga ajin yanzu-yanzu?", "Who are the girls who entered the class just now?": "Su wace ne 'yan matan da suka shiga ajin yanzu-yanzu?", "he created": "ya halitta", "he raised": "ya ɗaga", "he attended, came": "ya halarta, ya zo", "it rang": "ya yi ƙara", "he returned": "ya koma", "khalaqa": "khalaqa", "rafa'a": "rafa'a", "ḥaḍara": "ḥaḍara", "ranna": "ranna", "'aada": "'aada", "clay": "taɓo, laka", "fire": "wuta", "a sky, a heaven": "sama", "a bell": "ƙararrawa", "a list": "jeri, lissafi", "a meaning": "ma'ana", "a connection": "alaƙa", "a moment": "ɗan lokaci, lokaci kaɗan", "the grandfather": "kakan", "New words: nouns": "Sababbin kalmomi: sunaye", "ṭeenun": "ṭeenun", "naarun": "naarun", "samaa'un (pl. samaawaatun)": "samaa'un (pl. samaawaatun)", "jarasun (pl. ajraasun)": "jarasun (pl. ajraasun)", "qaa'imatun (pl. qawaa'imu)": "qaa'imatun (pl. qawaa'imu)", "ma'nan": "ma'nan", "'alaaqatun": "'alaaqatun", "laḥẓatun": "laḥẓatun", "al-jaddu": "al-jaddu", "several": "da dama", "well done": "madalla", "The teacher entered the class and found only fifteen students in it.": "Malamin ya shiga ajin kuma bai sami ɗalibai a cikinsa ba sai goma sha biyar kawai.", "Where are the five new students who came yesterday?": "Ina sababbin ɗalibai biyar da suka zo jiya?", "We went to him because we did not find our names in the list.": "Mun je wurinsa saboda ba mu sami sunayenmu a cikin jerin ba.", "Did you understand it? They said: yes, we understood it well. How easy this lesson is!": "Kun fahimce shi? Suka ce: i, mun fahimce shi sosai. Kai, wannan darasi akwai sauƙi!", "From what did Allah create man, Uthman? Allah created man from clay.": "Daga me Allah ya halicci mutum, Usman? Allah ya halicci mutum daga taɓo.", "Well done, Abu Bakr. How many heavens did Allah create, Abdullah? Allah created seven heavens.": "Madalla, Abubakar. Sammai nawa Allah ya halitta, Abdullahi? Allah ya halicci sammai bakwai.", "Both the verb and the noun end in -a.": "Fi'ilin da sunan duka suna ƙarewa da -a.", "Say “how …!”:": "Ka ce “kai, … !”:", "One word: -u. Two words: -a on the first.": "Kalma ɗaya: -u. Kalmomi biyu: -a a kan ta farko.", "Calling with": "Kira da", "Call him or her:": "Kira shi ko ita:", "As an object,": "A matsayin maf'uli,", "The plural object": "Jam'i na maf'uli", "takes a kasra.": "yana ɗaukar kasra.", "خَلَقَ اللهُ …… (the heavens)": "خَلَقَ اللهُ …… Wato sammai", "سَأَلَتْ زَيْنَبُ …… (her classmates)": "سَأَلَتْ زَيْنَبُ …… Wato abokan ajinta mata", "قَرَأْتُ …… (the magazines)": "قَرَأْتُ …… Wato mujallun", "رَأَيْتُ الْأَطِبَّاءَ وَ…… (the doctors, f)": "رَأَيْتُ الْأَطِبَّاءَ وَ…… Wato likitoci mata", "رَأَيْتُ …… (cars)": "رَأَيْتُ …… Wato motoci", "Choose the answer.": "Zaɓi amsar.", "Look at the answer to choose the question word.": "Duba amsar don zaɓar kalmar tambaya.", "Match the joining word to the noun.": "Haɗa kalmar haɗawa da sunan.", "Allah created me.": "Allah ne ya halicce ni.", "Calling with يَا": "Kira da يَا", "The plural object ـَاتٍ": "Jam'i na maf'uli ـَاتٍ", "Who is the girl who came in?": "Wace ce yarinyar da ta shigo?", "Listen, then write the word. (fire)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato wuta.", "✅ Choose the answer.": "✅ Zaɓi amsar.", "✅ How easy this lesson is!": "✅ Kai, wannan darasi akwai sauƙi!", "✅ Who is the girl who came in?": "✅ Wace ce yarinyar da ta shigo?", "✅ Write: fire": "✅ Rubuta: wuta", "In this lesson you will learn the present verb,": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi fi'ili mai zuwa, wato mudari'i,", "he went, becomes": "ya tafi, yana zama", "he goes. The middle letter can take": "yana tafiya. Harafin tsakiya yana iya ɗaukar", "You will say does not with": "Za ka faɗi ba ya yi da", "count from twenty-one to thirty, and use": "ka ƙirga daga ashirin da ɗaya zuwa talatin, ka kuma yi amfani da", "early, and": "da wuri, da", "late.": "a makare.", "The present verb starts with": "Fi'ili mai zuwa yana farawa da", "for he, and ends in": "ga shi, kuma yana ƙarewa da", "he goes.": "yana tafiya.", "The middle letter of the present verb can take": "Harafin tsakiya na fi'ili mai zuwa yana iya ɗaukar", "You learn it with each verb:": "Kana koyon sa tare da kowane fi'ili:", "before the present verb to say does not:": "kafin fi'ili mai zuwa don faɗar ba ya yi:", "Compare": "Kwatanta", "he did not go.": "bai tafi ba.", "From twenty-one to twenty-nine, say the unit first, then": "Daga ashirin da ɗaya zuwa ashirin da tara, ka faɗi raka'a da farko, sannan", "then": "sannan", "Thirty is": "Talatin ita ce", "means early, and": "ma'anarsa da wuri, kuma", "means late. For a woman,": "ma'anarsa a makare. Ga mace,", "يَذْهَبُ (he goes)": "يَذْهَبُ, wato yana tafiya", "Past → present": "Wanda ya wuce → mai zuwa", "In a sentence": "A cikin jumla", "لَا or مَا": "لَا ko مَا", "Early, late": "Da wuri, a makare", "In this lesson you will learn the present verb, الْمُضَارِعُ. ذَهَبَ, he went, becomes يَذْهَبُ, he goes. The middle letter can take ضَمَّةْ, كَسْرَةْ or فَتْحَةْ: يَكْتُبُ, يَجْلِسُ, يَذْهَبُ. You will say does not with لَا, count from twenty-one to thirty, and use مُبَكِّرًا, early, and مُتَأَخِّرًا, late.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi fi'ili mai zuwa, wato mudari'i: الْمُضَارِعُ. ذَهَبَ, ya tafi, yana zama يَذْهَبُ, yana tafiya. Harafin tsakiya yana iya ɗaukar ضَمَّةْ, كَسْرَةْ ko فَتْحَةْ: يَكْتُبُ, يَجْلِسُ, يَذْهَبُ. Za ka faɗi ba ya yi da لَا, ka ƙirga daga ashirin da ɗaya zuwa talatin, ka kuma yi amfani da مُبَكِّرًا, da wuri, da مُتَأَخِّرًا, a makare.", "yadh-habu": "yadh-habu", "he goes": "yana tafiya", "The present verb (": "Fi'ili mai zuwa (", ") starts with": ") yana farawa da", "for “he”, the first letter takes a": "ga “shi”, harafin farko yana ɗaukar", ", and it ends in": ", kuma yana ƙarewa da", "Ali went to school yesterday.": "Ali ya tafi makaranta jiya.", "Ali goes to school every day.": "Ali yana tafiya makaranta kowace rana.", "Ismail reads the Qur'an after the Fajr prayer every day.": "Isma'ila yana karanta Alƙur'ani bayan sallar Asuba kowace rana.", "The man washes his car every week.": "Mutumin yana wanke motarsa kowane mako.", "yaktubu": "yaktubu", "middle damma": "damma a tsakiya", "yajlisu": "yajlisu", "middle kasra": "kasra a tsakiya", "middle fatha": "fatha a tsakiya", "middle letter": "harafin tsakiya", "of the present verb can take a damma, a kasra or a fatha. You learn it with each verb:": "na fi'ili mai zuwa yana iya ɗaukar damma, kasra ko fatha. Kana koyon sa tare da kowane fi'ili:", ". A verb like": ". Fi'ili kamar", "(kasra in the past) usually has a fatha in the present.": "mai kasra a lokacin da ya wuce, yawanci yana da fatha a mai zuwa.", "damma: يَدْخُلُ، يَخْرُجُ، يَسْجُدُ": "damma: يَدْخُلُ، يَخْرُجُ، يَسْجُدُ", "kasra: يَرْجِعُ، يَغْسِلُ، يَنْزِلُ": "kasra: يَرْجِعُ، يَغْسِلُ، يَنْزِلُ", "fatha: يَفْتَحُ، يَفْهَمُ، يَلْعَبُ": "fatha: يَفْتَحُ، يَفْهَمُ، يَلْعَبُ", "he writes": "yana rubutu", "he sits": "yana zama", "he hears": "yana ji", "laa yadh-habu": "laa yadh-habu", "he does not go": "ba ya tafiya", "before the present verb to say": "kafin fi'ili mai zuwa don faɗar", "does not": "ba ya yi", ". Compare:": ". Kwatanta:", "(he did not go) and": "wato bai tafi ba, da", "(he does not go).": "wato ba ya tafiya.", "Does he go to the factory again after Dhuhr? No, he does not.": "Yana sake tafiya masana'anta bayan Azahar? A'a, ba ya tafiya.", "He sits here in his office after the Asr prayer.": "Yana zama a nan ofishinsa bayan sallar La'asar.", "waaḥidun wa 'ishruuna … thalaathuuna": "waaḥidun wa 'ishruuna … thalaathuuna", "From 21 to 29 say the": "Daga 21 zuwa 29 ka faɗi", "unit first": "raka'a da farko", ", then": ", sannan", ". The noun after it is one, ending in": ". Sunan da ke bayanta ɗaya ne, mai ƙarewa da", ". Thirty is": ". Talatin ita ce", "mubakkiran": "mubakkiran", "early": "da wuri", "muta'akhkhiran": "muta'akhkhiran", "late": "a makare", "For a woman:": "Ga mace:", ". Also:": ". Haka kuma:", "(always),": "wato koyaushe,", "(sometimes),": "wato wani lokaci,", "(again).": "wato kuma, sau ɗaya.", "I went to school early today, and came back home late.": "Na tafi makaranta da wuri yau, kuma na dawo gida a makare.", "Layla went to the university late.": "Laila ta tafi jami'a a makare.", "He always goes to the market after the Fajr prayer.": "Koyaushe yana tafiya kasuwa bayan sallar Asuba.", "He comes back at seven o'clock, and sometimes at eight.": "Yana dawowa ƙarfe bakwai, wani lokaci kuma ƙarfe takwas.", "he worked": "ya yi aiki", "he did": "ya aikata", "he rode": "ya hau", "he bowed (in prayer)": "ya yi ruku'u", "he prostrated": "ya yi sujada", "'amila (ya'malu)": "'amila (ya'malu)", "fa'ala (yaf'alu)": "fa'ala (yaf'alu)", "rakiba (yarkabu)": "rakiba (yarkabu)", "raka'a (yarka'u)": "raka'a (yarka'u)", "sajada (yasjudu)": "sajada (yasjudu)", "a factory": "masana'anta", "an office": "ofis", "a worker": "ma'aikaci", "New words: work words": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin aiki", "maṣna'un (pl. maṣaani'u)": "maṣna'un (pl. maṣaani'u)", "'aamilun (pl. 'ummaalun)": "'aamilun (pl. 'ummaalun)", "a distance": "nisa", "length": "tsawo", "width": "faɗi", "a metre": "mita", "a kilometre": "kilomita", "New words: measuring": "Sababbin kalmomi: awo", "masaafatun": "masaafatun", "ṭuulun": "ṭuulun", "'arḍun": "'arḍun", "mitrun (pl. amtaarun)": "mitrun (pl. amtaarun)", "keeluumitrun": "keeluumitrun", "always": "koyaushe", "sometimes": "wani lokaci", "another time, again": "wani lokaci kuma, sake", "New words: how often": "Sababbin kalmomi: sau nawa", "daa'iman": "daa'iman", "aḥyaanan": "aḥyaanan", "marratan ukhraa": "marratan ukhraa", "the present verb": "fi'ili mai zuwa", "Zakariyya went to visit Hamid after Fajr, but he did not find him at home.": "Zakariyya ya tafi ziyarar Hamid bayan Asuba, amma bai same shi a gida ba.", "Where is your father? He went to the market. Does he go to the market every day?": "Ina babanka yake? Ya tafi kasuwa. Yana tafiya kasuwa kowace rana?", "Yes, he always goes to the market after the Fajr prayer.": "I, koyaushe yana tafiya kasuwa bayan sallar Asuba.", "What does he do at home? He reads the newspapers and listens to the news on the radio.": "Me yake yi a gida? Yana karanta jaridu kuma yana sauraron labarai a rediyo.", "When does he go to the factory? He goes at half past nine.": "Yaushe yake tafiya masana'anta? Yana tafiya ƙarfe tara da rabi.", "How many workers work in your factory? A hundred and twenty-five workers work in it.": "Ma'aikata nawa ne ke aiki a masana'antarku? Ma'aikata ɗari da ashirin da biyar ne ke aiki a cikinta.", "It is now a quarter to nine, and your father has not come back. Perhaps he is coming back late today.": "Yanzu ƙarfe tara saura kwata, kuma babanka bai dawo ba. Watakila zai dawo a makare yau.", "Watch the vowel on the middle letter.": "Ka lura da wasalin da ke kan harafin tsakiya.", "Make the present verb": "Yi fi'ili mai zuwa", "Present:": "Mai zuwa:", "Choose the verb that fits.": "Zaɓi fi'ilin da ya dace.", "Use the present verb": "Yi amfani da fi'ili mai zuwa", "before the present,": "kafin mai zuwa,", "before the past.": "kafin wanda ya wuce.", "The unit first, then": "Raka'a da farko, sannan", "Count 21 to 30": "Ƙirga 21 zuwa 30", "Choose the matching sentence.": "Zaɓi jumlar da ta yi daidai.", "“I went to school early.”": "“Na tafi makaranta da wuri.”", "“He always goes to the market.”": "“Koyaushe yana tafiya kasuwa.”", "“He sometimes comes back at eight.”": "“Wani lokaci yana dawowa ƙarfe takwas.”", "“Layla went to the university late.”": "“Laila ta tafi jami'a a makare.”", "Perhaps he is coming back late today.": "Watakila zai dawo a makare yau.", "“The doctor (f) went to the hospital early.”": "“Likitar ta tafi asibiti da wuri.”", "He reads the newspapers.": "Yana karanta jaridu.", "✅ Ali goes to school every day.": "✅ Ali yana tafiya makaranta kowace rana.", "✅ “The doctor (f) went to the hospital early.”": "✅ “Likitar ta tafi asibiti da wuri.”", "✅ “Layla went to the university late.”": "✅ “Laila ta tafi jami'a a makare.”", "✅ He reads the newspapers.": "✅ Yana karanta jaridu.", "In this lesson you will tell someone not to do something:": "A wannan darasi za ka hana mutum yin wani abu:", "don't go out, and you will learn the difference between this": "kada ka fita, kuma za ka koyi bambanci tsakanin wannan", "and the": "da", "that means does not. You will also learn": "mai ma'anar ba ya yi. Za ka kuma koyi", "I eat,": "ina ci,", "almost, and": "ya kusa, da", "how tall he is. This is the last lesson of Beginner 2.": "kai, yana da tsawo. Wannan shi ne darasi na ƙarshe na Mafari 2.", "To forbid, put": "Don hani, sanya", "before the you verb and end it in a sukun:": "kafin fi'ilin kai kuma ka ƙare shi da sukun:", "To a woman,": "Ga mace,", "Two kinds of": "Iri biyu na", "One forbids and gives a sukun:": "Ɗaya yana hani kuma yana ba da sukun:", "The other only denies and keeps the": "Ɗayan kuma yana korewa ne kawai kuma yana barin", "Two hamzas together become one long": "Hamza biyu a tare suna zama dogon", "I eat.": "Ina ci.", "I take.": "Ina ɗauka.", "with a present verb means almost.": "tare da fi'ili mai zuwa ma'anarsa ya kusa.", "with a present verb means not now:": "tare da fi'ili mai zuwa ma'anarsa ba yanzu ba:", "you can join a pronoun:": "za ka iya haɗa wakilin suna:", "لَا تَذْهَبْ (don't go)": "لَا تَذْهَبْ, wato kada ka tafi", "كَادَ (almost)": "كَادَ, wato ya kusa", "Don't!": "Kada ka yi!", "Don't! (all)": "Kada ku yi!", "Forbid or deny?": "Hani ko korewa?", "Almost": "Ya kusa", "In this lesson you will tell someone not to do something: لَا تَخْرُجْ, don't go out, and you will learn the difference between this لَا and the لَا that means does not. You will also learn آكُلُ, I eat, كَادَ, almost, and مَا أَطْوَلَهُ, how tall he is. This is the last lesson of Beginner 2.": "A wannan darasi za ka hana mutum yin wani abu: لَا تَخْرُجْ, kada ka fita, kuma za ka koyi bambanci tsakanin wannan لَا da لَا mai ma'anar ba ya yi. Za ka kuma koyi آكُلُ, ina ci, كَادَ, ya kusa, da مَا أَطْوَلَهُ, kai, yana da tsawo. Wannan shi ne darasi na ƙarshe na Mafari 2.", "takhruju": "takhruju", "you go out": "kana fita", "laa takhruj": "laa takhruj", "don't go out!": "kada ka fita!", "before the “you” verb and end it in a": "kafin fi'ilin “kai” kuma ka ƙare shi da", ". To a woman": ". Ga mace", ", to men": ", ga maza", ", to women": ", ga mata", "Don't go out of the class now.": "Kada ka fita daga ajin yanzu.", "No, don't sit here. Sit there behind Hamid.": "A'a, kada ka zauna a nan. Zauna can bayan Hamid.", "Maryam, don't go.": "Maryam, kada ki tafi.", "Brothers, don't go.": "'Yan'uwa maza, kada ku tafi.", "Sisters, don't go.": "'Yan'uwa mata, kada ku tafi.", "laa ta'kul": "laa ta'kul", "don't eat!": "kada ka ci!", "laa ta'kulu": "laa ta'kulu", "you don't eat": "ba ka ci", "forbids and gives a": "yana hani kuma yana ba da", "only denies and keeps the": "yana korewa ne kawai kuma yana barin", "Don't eat this!": "Kada ka ci wannan!", "Why don't you eat?": "Me ya sa ba ka ci?", "Don't eat this, brother.": "Kada ka ci wannan, ɗan'uwa.", "Why don't you eat, brother?": "Me ya sa ba ka ci, ɗan'uwa?", "Don't go to the playground.": "Kada ka tafi filin wasa.", "Aren't you going to the playground?": "Ba ka tafiya filin wasa?", "aakulu": "aakulu", "I eat": "ina ci", "aakhudhu": "aakhudhu", "I take": "ina ɗauka", "He eats, you eat, I eat.": "Yana ci, kana ci, ina ci.", "He takes, you take, I take.": "Yana ɗauka, kana ɗauka, ina ɗauka.", "Shall I take these notebooks, teacher? No, don't take them.": "In ɗauki waɗannan littattafan rubutu, malam? A'a, kada ka ɗauke su.", "kaada yakhruju": "kaada yakhruju", "he almost went out": "ya kusa fita", "(past) or": "wato wanda ya wuce, ko", "(present) + a present verb means": "wato mai zuwa, tare da fi'ili mai zuwa ma'anarsa", "almost": "ya kusa", "(the bell is about to ring). For a woman": "wato ƙararrawa ta kusa yin ƙara. Ga mace", "Shall I open the door, teacher? The bell is about to ring.": "In buɗe ƙofar, malam? Ƙararrawa ta kusa yin ƙara.", "Hamid's car turned over and he almost died.": "Motar Hamid ta yi juyi kuma ya kusa mutuwa.", "The headmistress hit Suad and she almost cried.": "Shugabar makarantar ta daki Su'ad kuma ta kusa yin kuka.", "It is one o'clock: the principal is about to leave.": "Ƙarfe ɗaya ne: shugaban makaranta ya kusa tafiya.", "maa ashrabu": "maa ashrabu", "I am not drinking coffee now": "ba na shan kofi yanzu", "maa aṭwalahu": "maa aṭwalahu", "How tall he is!": "Kai, yana da tsawo!", "+ a present verb means not": "tare da fi'ili mai zuwa ma'anarsa ba", "(ever) /": "wato har abada, ko", "(now). With": "wato yanzu. Da", "! you can join a pronoun:": "! za ka iya haɗa wakilin suna:", "I am not reading this magazine now. I am only looking at the pictures in it.": "Ba na karanta wannan mujalla yanzu. Ina kallon hotunan da ke cikinta ne kawai.", "Look at this magazine, teacher. How beautiful it is!": "Duba wannan mujalla, malam. Kai, tana da kyau!", "Hamid is tall. How tall he is!": "Hamid dogo ne. Kai, yana da tsawo!", "a seat": "wurin zama", "he lied": "ya yi ƙarya", "he cried": "ya yi kuka", "it turned over": "ya juya, ya kife", "O my father": "Ya babana", "during": "a lokacin", "maq'adun (pl. maqaa'idu)": "maq'adun (pl. maqaa'idu)", "kadhaba (yakdhibu)": "kadhaba (yakdhibu)", "bakaa (yabkee)": "bakaa (yabkee)", "inqalaba (yanqalibu)": "inqalaba (yanqalibu)", "yaa abati": "yaa abati", "fee athnaa'i": "fee athnaa'i", "he almost": "ya kusa", "Where are you going, Abu Bakr? I am going to the principal.": "Ina za ka, Abubakar? Zan tafi wurin shugaban makaranta.", "Don't go out of the class now. Go to him after the lesson.": "Kada ka fita daga ajin yanzu. Je wurinsa bayan darasin.", "Teacher, I am a new student. Where do I sit? No, don't sit here. This is Hisham's seat and he is absent today.": "Malam, ni sabon ɗalibi ne. Ina zan zauna? A'a, kada ka zauna a nan. Wannan wurin zaman Hisham ne kuma ba ya nan yau.", "Don't write the answers with the red pen. The teacher is the one who writes with the red pen.": "Kada ka rubuta amsoshin da jan alƙalami. Malamin ne yake rubutu da jan alƙalami.", "Look at this magazine, teacher. How beautiful it is! Don't read magazines in class, Faisal.": "Duba wannan mujalla, malam. Kai, tana da kyau! Kada ka karanta mujallu a aji, Faisal.", "Shall I open the door, teacher? The bell is about to ring. No, don't open the door now.": "In buɗe ƙofar, malam? Ƙararrawa ta kusa yin ƙara. A'a, kada ka buɗe ƙofar yanzu.", "that forbids": "mai hani", "+ the verb with a sukun.": "tare da fi'ili mai sukun.", "Say “don't”:": "Ka ce “kada”:", "plus the verb with a": "tare da fi'ili mai", "Look at who you are talking to.": "Duba wanda kake magana da shi.", "يَا بِنْتِي، لَا …… مَاءً بَارِدًا. (drink)": "يَا بِنْتِي، لَا …… مَاءً بَارِدًا. (sha)", "يَا أَخِي، لَا …… مِنَ الْحَافِلَةِ فِي هٰذِهِ الْمَحَطَّةِ. (get off)": "يَا أَخِي، لَا …… مِنَ الْحَافِلَةِ فِي هٰذِهِ الْمَحَطَّةِ. (sauka)", "يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، لَا …… الشَّيْطَانَ. (worship)": "يَا أَيُّهَا النَّاسُ، لَا …… الشَّيْطَانَ. (bauta)", "يَا أَبْنَائِي، لَا …… مِنَ الْفَصْلِ فِي أَثْنَاءِ الدَّرْسِ. (go out)": "يَا أَبْنَائِي، لَا …… مِنَ الْفَصْلِ فِي أَثْنَاءِ الدَّرْسِ. (fita)", "يَا أَخَوَاتِي، لَا …… غُرْفَتِي بِالْمِكْنَسَةِ الْقَدِيمَةِ. (sweep)": "يَا أَخَوَاتِي، لَا …… غُرْفَتِي بِالْمِكْنَسَةِ الْقَدِيمَةِ. (share)", "يَا وَلَدُ، لَا …… فِي الْفَصْلِ. (laugh)": "يَا وَلَدُ، لَا …… فِي الْفَصْلِ. (yi dariya)", "Forbid:": "Hani:", "Forbid: sukun. Deny: -u.": "Hani: sukun. Korewa: -u.", "“Why don't you eat, brother?”": "“Me ya sa ba ka ci, ɗan'uwa?”", "Deny: -u.": "Korewa: -u.", "“Don't go to the playground.”": "“Kada ka tafi filin wasa.”", "“Aren't you going to the playground?”": "“Ba ka tafiya filin wasa?”", "“He does not lie.”": "“Ba ya ƙarya.”", "“Don't eat this, brother.”": "“Kada ka ci wannan, ɗan'uwa.”", "Two hamzas become": "Hamza biyu suna zama", "أَ…… هٰذِهِ الدَّفَاتِرَ يَا أُسْتَاذُ؟ (take)": "أَ…… هٰذِهِ الدَّفَاتِرَ يَا أُسْتَاذُ؟ (ɗauka)", "أَنَا …… الْخُبْزَ. (eat)": "أَنَا …… الْخُبْزَ. (ci)", "اِنْقَلَبَتْ سَيَّارَةُ حَامِدٍ وَكَادَ …… (die)": "اِنْقَلَبَتْ سَيَّارَةُ حَامِدٍ وَكَادَ …… (mutu)", "…… الْإِمَامُ يَرْكَعُ. (is about to)": "…… الْإِمَامُ يَرْكَعُ. (ya kusa)", "ضَرَبَتِ الْمُدِيرَةُ سُعَادَ فَ…… تَبْكِي. (almost)": "ضَرَبَتِ الْمُدِيرَةُ سُعَادَ فَ…… تَبْكِي. (ta kusa)", "+ a joined pronoun.": "tare da wakilin suna da aka haɗa.", "plus a joined pronoun.": "tare da wakilin suna da aka haɗa.", "Listen, then write the word. (he lied)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato ya yi ƙarya.", "Add لَا that forbids": "Ƙara لَا mai hani", "يَا بِنْتِي، لَا …… اللَّحْمَ بِهٰذَا السِّكِّينِ. (cut)": "يَا بِنْتِي، لَا …… اللَّحْمَ بِهٰذَا السِّكِّينِ. (yanka)", "لَا تَأْكُلْ or لَا تَأْكُلُ?": "لَا تَأْكُلْ ko لَا تَأْكُلُ?", "“Don't lie.”": "“Kada ka yi ƙarya.”", "أَنَا …… هٰذَا الْكِتَابَ. (take)": "أَنَا …… هٰذَا الْكِتَابَ. (ɗauka)", "✅ Don't go out of the class now.": "✅ Kada ka fita daga ajin yanzu.", "✅ Write: he lied": "✅ Rubuta: ya yi ƙarya", "✅ Brothers, don't go.": "✅ 'Yan'uwa maza, kada ku tafi.", "✅ “Don't lie.”": "✅ “Kada ka yi ƙarya.”", "✅ “Don't eat this, brother.”": "✅ “Kada ka ci wannan, ɗan'uwa.”", "This is the final exam of Beginner 2. It has forty questions from all fifteen lessons, and you have thirty minutes. You need eighty five percent to pass and open Beginner 3.": "Wannan ita ce jarrabawar ƙarshe ta Mafari 2. Tana da tambayoyi arba'in daga dukan darussa goma sha biyar, kuma kana da minti talatin. Kana buƙatar kashi tamanin da biyar cikin ɗari don ka ci ka buɗe Mafari 3.", "Numbers 11–30, first, half": "Lambobi 11 zuwa 30, na farko, rabi", "Objects and endings": "Maf'uli da ƙarshe", "the girls …… came in": "'yan matan …… suka shigo", "The past verb": "Fi'ilin da ya wuce", "Ask a woman: Where did you go?": "Tambayi mace: Ina kika tafi?", "Commands, don't": "Umarni, kada", "Tell a woman: Go!": "Gaya wa mace: Tafi!", "How do you say “Allah created me”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Allah ne ya halicce ni”?", "إِنَّ and its sisters": "إِنَّ da 'yan'uwanta", "How do you say “Indeed, I have three sisters”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Lalle, ina da 'yan'uwa mata uku”?", "Who opened the door? I opened it.": "Wane ne ya buɗe ƙofar? Ni na buɗe ta.", "Taller, how …!, calling": "Ya fi tsawo, kai … !, kira", "Agree: أَنْتَ مِنَ الْهِنْدِ، أَلَيْسَ كَذٰلِكَ؟": "Yarda: أَنْتَ مِنَ الْهِنْدِ، أَلَيْسَ كَذٰلِكَ؟", "The present verb and the future": "Fi'ili mai zuwa da na gaba", "How do you say “he does not go”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ba ya tafiya”?", "perhaps": "watakila", "as for": "amma game da", "لَيْسَ, ذُو, 100 and 1000": "لَيْسَ, ذُو, 100 da 1000", "The command of تَأْكُلُ": "Umarnin تَأْكُلُ", "How do you say “The student read the Qur'an”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ɗalibin ya karanta Alƙur'ani”?", "How do you say “How beautiful it is!” (f)": "Yaya ake cewa “Kai, tana da kyau!”, mace", "a student (f) with good character": "ɗaliba mai kyawawan halaye", "How do you say “Did you all read the Qur'an?”": "Yaya ake cewa “Kun karanta Alƙur'ani?”", "Call Abdullah.": "Kira Abdullahi.", "Ask some women: Where are you going?": "Tambayi wasu mata: Ina za ku?", "Ask a woman: What are you doing?": "Tambayi mace: Me kike yi?", "How do you say “I eat”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ina ci”?", "How do you say “This door is for entering”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Wannan ƙofa ta shiga ce”?", "How do you say “It seems he is your brother”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Kamar dai ɗan'uwanka ne”?", "The present of كَتَبَ": "Mai zuwa na كَتَبَ", "The command of تَذْهَبُ": "Umarnin تَذْهَبُ", "How do you say “I came back because I am sick”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na dawo saboda ba ni da lafiya”?", "an address": "adireshi", "How do you say “Hamid is taller than him”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Hamid ya fi shi tsawo”?", "How do you say “I am from India” with إِنَّ?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ni daga Indiya nake” da إِنَّ?", "Add إِنَّ: حَامِدٌ مُتَزَوِّجٌ.": "Ƙara إِنَّ: حَامِدٌ مُتَزَوِّجٌ.", "Tell some men: Sit down!": "Gaya wa wasu maza: Ku zauna!", "✅ the girls …… came in": "✅ 'yan matan …… suka shigo", "✅ Ask a woman: Where did you go?": "✅ Tambayi mace: Ina kika tafi?", "✅ Tell a woman: Go!": "✅ Gaya wa mace: Tafi!", "✅ How do you say “Allah created me”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Allah ne ya halicce ni”?", "✅ How do you say “Indeed, I have three sisters”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Lalle, ina da 'yan'uwa mata uku”?", "✅ Who opened the door? I opened it.": "✅ Wane ne ya buɗe ƙofar? Ni na buɗe ta.", "✅ How do you say “the third lesson”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “darasi na uku”?", "✅ Agree: أَنْتَ مِنَ الْهِنْدِ، أَلَيْسَ كَذٰلِكَ؟": "✅ Yarda: أَنْتَ مِنَ الْهِنْدِ، أَلَيْسَ كَذٰلِكَ؟", "✅ How do you say “he does not go”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ba ya tafiya”?", "✅ How do you say “100 riyals”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “riyal 100”?", "✅ The command of تَأْكُلُ": "✅ Umarnin تَأْكُلُ", "✅ How do you say “The student read the Qur'an”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ɗalibin ya karanta Alƙur'ani”?", "✅ How do you say “the first student (f)”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗaliba ta farko”?", "✅ How do you say “How beautiful it is!” (f)": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Kai, tana da kyau!”, mace", "✅ a student (f) with good character": "✅ ɗaliba mai kyawawan halaye", "✅ How do you say “Did you all read the Qur'an?”": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Kun karanta Alƙur'ani?”", "✅ Call Abdullah.": "✅ Kira Abdullahi.", "✅ the book with the red cover": "✅ littafin mai jan bango", "✅ Ask some women: Where are you going?": "✅ Tambayi wasu mata: Ina za ku?", "✅ Ask a woman: What are you doing?": "✅ Tambayi mace: Me kike yi?", "✅ How do you say “I eat”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ina ci”?", "✅ How do you say “This door is for entering”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Wannan ƙofa ta shiga ce”?", "✅ How do you say “It seems he is your brother”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Kamar dai ɗan'uwanka ne”?", "✅ How do you say “you all (men) went”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “kun tafi”, maza?", "✅ The present of كَتَبَ": "✅ Mai zuwa na كَتَبَ", "✅ The command of تَذْهَبُ": "✅ Umarnin تَذْهَبُ", "✅ How do you say “I came back because I am sick”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na dawo saboda ba ni da lafiya”?", "✅ How do you say “Hamid is taller than him”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Hamid ya fi shi tsawo”?", "✅ How do you say “I am from India” with إِنَّ?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ni daga Indiya nake” da إِنَّ?", "✅ Add إِنَّ: حَامِدٌ مُتَزَوِّجٌ.": "✅ Ƙara إِنَّ: حَامِدٌ مُتَزَوِّجٌ.", "✅ Tell some men: Sit down!": "✅ Gaya wa wasu maza: Ku zauna!", "Welcome to Beginner 3. In this level you will study the second half of Book 2, lessons 16 to 31. It ends with a final exam and a certificate.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 3. A wannan mataki za ka karanta rabi na biyu na Littafi na 2, darussa 16 zuwa 31. Yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida.", "In this lesson you will use": "A wannan darasi za ka yi amfani da", "he wants, with every person, like": "yana so, da kowane mutum, kamar", "I want, and": "ina so, da", "you want, to a woman. You will learn colours for a man and a woman, like": "kina so, ga mace. Za ka koyi launuka na namiji da na mace, kamar", "the words": "kalmomin", "another,": "wani, ɗayan,", "meaning what or that which, and": "mai ma'anar me ko abin da, da", "not.": "ba.", "starts with": "yana farawa da", "Colours on the pattern": "Launuka a kan tsarin", "have the feminine": "na macensu shi ne", "means another, and has no tanween. The feminine is": "ma'anarsa wani, ko ɗayan, kuma ba shi da tanwini. Na macensa shi ne", "And": "Da", "as an object:": "a matsayin maf'uli:", "Some names never take tanween:": "Wasu sunaye ba sa taɓa ɗaukar tanwini:", "The name": "Sunan", "is written with a": "ana rubuta shi da", "that is not read, to tell it apart from": "wanda ba a karanta shi, don a bambanta shi da", "can mean not, what, or that which.": "yana iya nufin ba, me, ko abin da.", "means I eat what you eat.": "ma'anarsa ina cin abin da kake ci.", "means not:": "ma'anarsa ba:", "يُرِيدُ (he wants)": "يُرِيدُ, wato yana so", "آخَرُ or أُخْرَى": "آخَرُ ko أُخْرَى", "ذُو or ذَا": "ذُو ko ذَا", "Kinds of مَا": "Nau'o'in مَا", "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Welcome to Beginner 3. In this level you will study the second half of Book 2, lessons 16 to 31. It ends with a final exam and a certificate. مَا شَاءَ اللهُ, you have come far. Keep going.": "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Barka da zuwa Mafari 3. A wannan mataki za ka karanta rabi na biyu na Littafi na 2, darussa 16 zuwa 31. Yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida. مَا شَاءَ اللهُ, ka yi nisa. Ka ci gaba.", "yureedu": "yureedu", "tureedu": "tureedu", "you, she": "kai, ita", "ureedu": "ureedu", "nureedu": "nureedu", "we want": "muna so", "(he wants) starts with a": "wato yana so, yana farawa da", "damma": "damma", ". The rest is like any present verb:": ". Sauran kamar kowane fi'ili mai zuwa ne:", ". But for women:": ". Amma ga mata:", "(the": "wato harafin", "drops).": "yana faɗuwa.", "Do you want anything from the market, my sons? Yes, we want many things.": "Kuna son wani abu daga kasuwa, 'ya'yana? I, muna son abubuwa da yawa.", "What do you want, Umar? I want a pen.": "Me kake so, Umar? Ina son alƙalami.", "What do you want, Hafsah? I want a bag.": "Me kike so, Hafsa? Ina son jaka.", "What do you want, girls?": "Me kuke so, 'yan mata?", "ḥaqeebatun ḥamraa'u": "ḥaqeebatun ḥamraa'u", "a red bag": "jar jaka", ", and neither takes -un:": ", kuma babu ɗayansu da ke ɗaukar -un:", "red 🔴": "ja 🔴", "black ⚫": "baƙi ⚫", "white ⚪": "fari ⚪", "blue 🔵": "shuɗi 🔵", "yellow 🟡": "rawaya 🟡", "green 🟢": "kore 🟢", "brown 🟤": "ruwan ƙasa 🟤", "aakharu": "aakharu", "another (m)": "wani, namiji", "ukhraa": "ukhraa", "another (f)": "wata, mace", "(another) has no -un; the feminine is": "wato wani, ba shi da -un; na macensa shi ne", "I have a red bag. I want another, black bag.": "Ina da jar jaka. Ina son wata, baƙa.", "Hamzah and another student went out of the class.": "Hamza da wani ɗalibi sun fita daga ajin.", "I want a notebook with lined paper.": "Ina son littafin rubutu mai takarda mai layi.", "I want a Qur'an with large letters.": "Ina son Alƙur'ani mai manyan haruffa.", "'umaru": "'umaru", "Umar": "Umar", "'amrun": "'amrun", "Amr": "Amr", "Some names never take -un:": "Wasu sunaye ba sa taɓa ɗaukar -un:", "that is": "wanda", "not read": "ba a karanta shi ba", ", to tell it apart from": ", don a bambanta shi da", "Umar: no -un": "Umar: babu -un", "Amr: silent و": "Amr: و mara furuci", "Amr hit Umar.": "Amr ya daki Umar.", "Umar hit Amr.": "Umar ya daki Amr.", "This is Amr's book.": "Wannan littafin Amr ne.", "maa = alladhee": "maa yana nufin alladhee", "what, that which": "me, abin da", "has several uses:": "yana da amfani iri-iri:", "what?": "me?", "), and": "), da", "that which": "abin da", "(I eat what you eat).": "wato ina cin abin da kake ci.", "(unlined paper).": "wato takarda mara layi.", "What are you eating, Ali? I am eating what you are eating.": "Me kake ci, Ali? Ina cin abin da kake ci.", "I will buy you what you want, in sha Allah.": "Zan saya maka abin da kake so, in sha Allah.", "That notebook's paper is not lined.": "Takardar wancan littafin rubutu ba mai layi ba ce.", "This news is not true.": "Wannan labarin ba gaskiya ba ne.", "a copy of the Qur'an": "Alƙur'ani, wato mus'hafi", "sweets": "alewa, kayan zaƙi", "cloth": "yadi", "a sample": "samfuri", "a thing": "abu", "muṣḥafun (pl. maṣaaḥifu)": "muṣḥafun (pl. maṣaaḥifu)", "ḥalwaa (pl. ḥalaawaa)": "ḥalwaa (pl. ḥalaawaa)", "qumaashun (pl. aqmishatun)": "qumaashun (pl. aqmishatun)", "namuudhajun (pl. namaadhiju)": "namuudhajun (pl. namaadhiju)", "shay'un (pl. ashyaa'u)": "shay'un (pl. ashyaa'u)", "narrow": "matsatsi, ƙunƙuntacce", "lined (paper)": "mai layi, takarda", "brown, dark-skinned": "ruwan ƙasa, wanda fatarsa ta yi duhu", "another, other": "wani, ɗayan", "New words: describing": "Sababbin kalmomi: siffantawa", "ḍayyiqun": "ḍayyiqun", "musaṭṭarun": "musaṭṭarun", "asmaru (f. samraa'u)": "asmaru (f. samraa'u)", "aakharu (f. ukhraa)": "aakharu (f. ukhraa)", "he was absent": "bai halarta ba", "he bought": "ya saya", "he wants": "yana so", "ghaaba (yagheebu)": "ghaaba (yagheebu)", "ishtaraa (yashtaree)": "ishtaraa (yashtaree)", "not, other than": "ba, ba … ba", "Do you want anything from the market, my sons? I am going to the mosque now and will go to the market after the prayer.": "Kuna son wani abu daga kasuwa, 'ya'yana? Zan tafi masallaci yanzu kuma zan tafi kasuwa bayan sallah.", "What do you want, Umar? A pen. Don't you have a pen? Yes, a blue pen. I want a red pen.": "Me kake so, Umar? Alƙalami. Ba ka da alƙalami? I, shuɗin alƙalami. Ina son jan alƙalami.", "Didn't I buy you a notebook last week? Yes, but that notebook's paper is not lined.": "Ban saya maka littafin rubutu makon da ya wuce ba? I, amma takardar wancan littafin rubutu ba mai layi ba ce.", "What do you want, Hafsah? A bag. I have a red bag. I want another, black bag.": "Me kike so, Hafsa? Jaka. Ina da jar jaka. Ina son wata, baƙa.", "And what do you want, Layla? I want a Qur'an with large letters.": "Ke kuma me kike so, Laila? Ina son Alƙur'ani mai manyan haruffa.", "Don't you want anything, Salma? Yes, I want an English dictionary and another, French one.": "Ba ki son komai, Salma? I, ina son ƙamus na Turanci da wani na Faransanci.", "Take this sample, father. I will buy you what you want, in sha Allah.": "Karɓi wannan samfuri, baba. Zan saya maka abin da kake so, in sha Allah.", "Match the pronoun to the verb.": "Haɗa wakilin suna da fi'ilin.", "The feminine colour is": "Launin mace shi ne", "for a feminine noun.": "ga sunan mace.", "after a noun ending in -an.": "bayan suna mai ƙarewa da -an.", "after a noun ending in": "bayan suna mai ƙarewa da", "not, what?, that which": "ba, me?, abin da", "What does": "Me", "mean here?": "yake nufi a nan?", "never takes -un;": "ba ya taɓa ɗaukar -un;", "has a silent": "yana da", "“Did you see Amr?”": "“Ka ga Amr?”", "never takes": "ba ya taɓa ɗaukar", "“I played with Umar.”": "“Na yi wasa da Umar.”", "“Amr hit Umar.”": "“Amr ya daki Umar.”", "“Umar is a new student.”": "“Umar sabon ɗalibi ne.”", "I want another, black bag.": "Ina son wata jaka, baƙa.", "آخَرُ or أُخْرَى?": "آخَرُ ko أُخْرَى?", "يُرِيدُ with each person": "يُرِيدُ da kowane mutum", "عُمَرُ and عَمْرٌو": "عُمَرُ da عَمْرٌو", "Listen, then write the word. (a copy of the Qur'an)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato Alƙur'ani, mus'hafi.", "ذُو or ذَا?": "ذُو ko ذَا?", "What does مَا mean here?": "Me مَا yake nufi a nan?", "I want a red pen.": "Ina son jan alƙalami.", "✅ “I played with Umar.”": "✅ “Na yi wasa da Umar.”", "✅ Write: a copy of the Qur'an": "✅ Rubuta: Alƙur'ani, mus'hafi", "✅ I want a notebook with lined paper.": "✅ Ina son littafin rubutu mai takarda mai layi.", "✅ I want a red pen.": "✅ Ina son jan alƙalami.", "with a present verb, which then ends in": "tare da fi'ili mai zuwa, wanda sai ya ƙare da", "I want to go. You will learn": "ina son in tafi. Za ka koyi", "in order to, as in": "don, kamar a cikin", "you can,": "za ka iya,", "since,": "tun, tun daga,", "he sees, and the four seasons.": "yana gani, da yanayi huɗu na shekara.", "the present verb ends in": "fi'ili mai zuwa yana ƙarewa da", "means in order to, and also gives the present verb": "ma'anarsa don, kuma shi ma yana ba fi'ili mai zuwa", "means it is possible.": "ma'anarsa yana yiwuwa.", "you can sit here.": "za ka iya zama a nan.", "I cannot.": "ba zan iya ba.", "means since, or for a time.": "ma'anarsa tun, ko na wani lokaci.", "The present of": "Mai zuwa na", "The seasons:": "Yanayin shekara:", "أَنْ أَذْهَبَ (to go)": "أَنْ أَذْهَبَ, wato in tafi", "لِـ (in order to)": "لِـ, wato don", "أَنْ + verb": "أَنْ tare da fi'ili", "In order to": "Don", "Can": "Iya yi", "Since": "Tun", "Seasons": "Yanayin shekara", "In this lesson you will learn أَنْ with a present verb, which then ends in فَتْحَةْ: أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَذْهَبَ, I want to go. You will learn لِـ, in order to, as in خَرَجْتُ لِأَشْرَبَ الْمَاءَ. You will also learn يُمْكِنُكَ, you can, مُنْذُ, since, يَرَى, he sees, and the four seasons.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi أَنْ tare da fi'ili mai zuwa, wanda sai ya ƙare da فَتْحَةْ: أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَذْهَبَ, ina son in tafi. Za ka koyi لِـ, don, kamar a cikin خَرَجْتُ لِأَشْرَبَ الْمَاءَ. Za ka kuma koyi يُمْكِنُكَ, za ka iya, مُنْذُ, tun, يَرَى, yana gani, da yanayi huɗu na shekara.", "adh-habu": "adh-habu", "I go": "ina tafiya", "ureedu an adh-haba": "ureedu an adh-haba", "I want to go": "ina son in tafi", "(to, that) the present verb ends in a": "wato cewa, fi'ili mai zuwa yana ƙarewa da", "Where do you want to go, Hashim? I want to go to Egypt.": "Ina kake son ka tafi, Hashim? Ina son in tafi Masar.", "I want to sit here in front of you.": "Ina son in zauna a nan gabanka.", "Don't you want to go to your country?": "Ba ka son ka tafi ƙasarku?", "I forgot to write the lesson.": "Na manta in rubuta darasin.", "kharajtu li-ashraba l-maa'a": "kharajtu li-ashraba l-maa'a", "I went out to drink water.": "Na fita don in sha ruwa.", "(in order to,": "wato don,", ") also gives the present verb a": ") shi ma yana ba fi'ili mai zuwa", "Why did you go out of the class, Ammar? I went out to drink water.": "Me ya sa ka fita daga ajin, Ammar? Na fita don in sha ruwa.", "He went out to wash his face.": "Ya fita don ya wanke fuskarsa.", "We study Arabic to understand the Noble Qur'an.": "Muna karatun Larabci don mu fahimci Alƙur'ani Mai Girma.", "Allah created us to worship Him.": "Allah ya halicce mu don mu bauta masa.", "yumkinuka an tajlisa": "yumkinuka an tajlisa", "you can sit": "za ka iya zama", "= you can sit.": "yana nufin za ka iya zama.", "= I cannot. Also with a verbal noun:": "yana nufin ba zan iya ba. Haka kuma da masdari:", "You can sit here now.": "Za ka iya zama a nan yanzu.", "I cannot study at the university next year.": "Ba zan iya karatu a jami'a shekara mai zuwa ba.", "Three minutes are left. You can go out now. Go out quietly.": "Minti uku ne suka rage. Za ku iya fita yanzu. Ku fita a natse.", "My father is very sick. He cannot go to the factory.": "Babana ba shi da lafiya sosai. Ba zai iya tafiya masana'anta ba.", "mundhu": "mundhu", "since, for": "tun, na tsawon", "means since or for (a time):": "ma'anarsa tun, ko na tsawon wani lokaci:", "(he has been absent for a week).": "wato bai halarta ba tsawon mako guda.", "He has been absent for a week.": "Bai halarta ba tsawon mako guda.", "I have not seen Muhammad since Friday.": "Ban ga Muhammadu ba tun ranar Juma'a.", "We have lived in this house for a year.": "Mun zauna a wannan gida tsawon shekara guda.", "I have known this shaikh for five years.": "Na san wannan shehin tsawon shekaru biyar.", "yaraa": "yaraa", "he sees": "yana gani", "taraa": "taraa", "you see": "kana gani", "araa": "araa", "I see": "ina gani", "naraa": "naraa", "we see": "muna gani", ". The seasons:": ". Yanayin shekara:", "(winter),": "wato lokacin sanyi,", "(spring),": "wato bazara,", "(summer),": "wato rani,", "(autumn).": "wato kaka.", "What do you see on the desk? I see a pen, a book and a watch.": "Me kake gani a kan teburin? Ina ganin alƙalami, littafi da agogo.", "From there I cannot see what you write on the board.": "Daga can ba zan iya ganin abin da kake rubutawa a allo ba.", "The summer holiday begins in a month.": "Hutun rani zai fara bayan wata guda.", "winter, spring, summer, autumn": "lokacin sanyi, bazara, rani, kaka", "a holiday": "hutu", "next year": "shekara mai zuwa", "flies": "ƙudaje", "family, people": "iyali, mutane", "dinner": "abincin dare", "treatment": "magani, jinya", "an envelope": "ambulan", "an announcement": "sanarwa", "noise": "hayaniya", "calm, quietly": "natsuwa, a natse", "'uṭlatun": "'uṭlatun", "al-'aamul-muqbilu": "al-'aamul-muqbilu", "adh-dhubaabu": "adh-dhubaabu", "ahlun": "ahlun", "'ashaa'un": "'ashaa'un", "'ilaajun": "'ilaajun", "ẓarfun (pl. ẓuruufun)": "ẓarfun (pl. ẓuruufun)", "i'laanun": "i'laanun", "ḍawḍaa'u": "ḍawḍaa'u", "huduu'un": "huduu'un", "he visited": "ya ziyarta", "it began": "ya fara", "he allowed": "ya ba da izini", "it remained": "ya rage, ya saura", "he spat": "ya tofa", "zaara (yazuuru)": "zaara (yazuuru)", "bada'a (yabda'u)": "bada'a (yabda'u)", "samaḥa (yasmaḥu)": "samaḥa (yasmaḥu)", "baqiya (yabqaa)": "baqiya (yabqaa)", "baṣaqa (yabṣuqu)": "baṣaqa (yabṣuqu)", "to (before a verb)": "don, kafin fi'ili", "it is possible": "yana yiwuwa", "Why did you go out, Ammar? To drink water. And why did Yasir go out with you? He went out to wash his face.": "Me ya sa ka fita, Ammar? Don in sha ruwa. Kuma me ya sa Yasir ya fita tare da kai? Ya fita don ya wanke fuskarsa.", "Teacher, I want to sit here in front of you. My seat is far from you, and from there I cannot see what you write on the board.": "Malam, ina son in zauna a nan gabanka. Wurin zamana yana nesa da kai, kuma daga can ba zan iya ganin abin da kake rubutawa a allo ba.", "You can sit here now. This is Hamzah's seat, and he has been absent for a week.": "Za ka iya zama a nan yanzu. Wannan wurin zaman Hamza ne, kuma bai halarta ba tsawon mako guda.", "Listen, my sons. The summer holiday begins in a month. Where are you going in this holiday?": "Ku saurara, 'ya'yana. Hutun rani zai fara bayan wata guda. Ina za ku tafi a wannan hutu?", "I want to go to Egypt to visit my brother who studies at Al-Azhar University.": "Ina son in tafi Masar don in ziyarci ɗan'uwana wanda ke karatu a Jami'ar Azhar.", "I cannot study at the university next year, because I am sick and want to go to the United States for treatment. May Allah cure you.": "Ba zan iya karatu a jami'a shekara mai zuwa ba, saboda ba ni da lafiya kuma ina son in tafi Amurka don jinya. Allah ya ba ka lafiya.", "Teacher, the bell is about to ring. Please allow us to leave now. Three minutes are left. You can go out now. Go out quietly.": "Malam, ƙararrawa ta kusa yin ƙara. Don Allah ka ba mu izinin tafiya yanzu. Minti uku ne suka rage. Za ku iya fita yanzu. Ku fita a natse.", "+ the present verb": "tare da fi'ili mai zuwa", "the verb ends in a fatha.": "fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da fatha.", "the verb ends in a": "fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da", "(in order to)": "wato don", "; the verb ends in a fatha.": "; fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da fatha.", "لِمَ قَامَ الْمُدَرِّسُ؟ (write)": "لِمَ قَامَ الْمُدَرِّسُ؟ (rubuta)", "لِمَ ذَهَبَ أَبُوكَ إِلَى جُدَّةَ؟ (buy)": "لِمَ ذَهَبَ أَبُوكَ إِلَى جُدَّةَ؟ (saya)", "لِمَ خَرَجْتَ مِنَ الْفَصْلِ؟ (drink water)": "لِمَ خَرَجْتَ مِنَ الْفَصْلِ؟ (sha ruwa)", "لِمَ تَدْرُسُونَ الْعَرَبِيَّةَ؟ (understand)": "لِمَ تَدْرُسُونَ الْعَرَبِيَّةَ؟ (fahimta)", "لِمَ دَخَلْتَ الْحَمَّامَ؟ (wash)": "لِمَ دَخَلْتَ الْحَمَّامَ؟ (wanke)", "“You (all) can go out now.”": "“Za ku iya fita yanzu.”", "“You can sit here.”": "“Za ka iya zama a nan.”", "“I cannot go.”": "“Ba zan iya tafiya ba.”", "“He cannot go to the factory.”": "“Ba zai iya tafiya masana'anta ba.”", "Choose the Arabic.": "Zaɓi Larabcin.", "“He has been sick since his return.”": "“Ba shi da lafiya tun dawowarsa.”", "“I have not seen Muhammad since Friday.”": "“Ban ga Muhammadu ba tun ranar Juma'a.”", "“I have known this shaikh for five years.”": "“Na san wannan shehin tsawon shekaru biyar.”", "“He has been absent for a week.”": "“Bai halarta ba tsawon mako guda.”", "Choose the season.": "Zaɓi yanayin shekara.", "The seasons": "Yanayin shekara", "“winter”": "“lokacin sanyi”", "“autumn”": "“kaka”", "“spring”": "“bazara”", "“summer”": "“rani”", "Listen, then write the word. (dinner)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato abincin dare.", "“Can I take this magazine home?”": "“Zan iya ɗaukar wannan mujalla zuwa gida?”", "أَنْ + the present verb": "أَنْ tare da fi'ili mai zuwa", "✅ I went out to drink water.": "✅ Na fita don in sha ruwa.", "✅ “summer”": "✅ “rani”", "✅ “He has been absent for a week.”": "✅ “Bai halarta ba tsawon mako guda.”", "✅ Write: dinner": "✅ Rubuta: abincin dare", "✅ He has been absent for a week.": "✅ Bai halarta ba tsawon mako guda.", "✅ “Can I take this magazine home?”": "✅ “Zan iya ɗaukar wannan mujalla zuwa gida?”", "✅ “He cannot go to the factory.”": "✅ “Ba zai iya tafiya masana'anta ba.”", "In this lesson you will see what": "A wannan darasi za ka ga abin da", "does to the long present forms.": "yake yi wa dogayen siffofin fi'ili mai zuwa.", "because the": "saboda harafin", "drops. The forms for women, like": "yana faɗuwa. Siffofin mata, kamar", "do not change. You will also learn": "ba sa canzawa. Za ka kuma koyi", "that not, and": "cewa kada, da", "like.": "kamar.", "the long forms drop the": "dogayen siffofi suna rasa", "The women's forms ending in -": "Siffofin mata masu ƙarewa da -", "do not change after": "ba sa canzawa bayan", "are written together as": "ana rubuta su a haɗe kamar", "and the verb still ends in": "kuma fi'ilin har yanzu yana ƙarewa da", "means like. It is joined to the next word, which ends in": "ma'anarsa kamar. Ana haɗa shi da kalmar da ke biye, wadda take ƙarewa da", "أَنْ يَذْهَبُوا (that they go)": "أَنْ يَذْهَبُوا, wato cewa su tafi", "The ن drops": "Harafin ن yana faɗuwa", "In this lesson you will see what أَنْ does to the long present forms. يَذْهَبُونَ becomes أَنْ يَذْهَبُوا, and تَذْهَبِينَ becomes أَنْ تَذْهَبِي, because the نُونْ drops. The forms for women, like يَذْهَبْنَ, do not change. You will also learn أَلَّا, that not, and كَـ, like.": "A wannan darasi za ka ga abin da أَنْ yake yi wa dogayen siffofin fi'ili mai zuwa. يَذْهَبُونَ yana zama أَنْ يَذْهَبُوا, kuma تَذْهَبِينَ yana zama أَنْ تَذْهَبِي, saboda harafin نُونْ yana faɗuwa. Siffofin mata, kamar يَذْهَبْنَ, ba sa canzawa. Za ka kuma koyi أَلَّا, cewa kada, da كَـ, kamar.", "yadh-habuuna": "yadh-habuuna", "they go": "suna tafiya", "an yadh-habuu": "an yadh-habuu", "that they go": "cewa su tafi", "the long forms": "dogayen siffofi", "drop the": "suna rasa", ". (A silent alif is written after the": ". Ana rubuta alif mara furuci bayan", "Where do you want to go now, my sons?": "Ina kuke son ku tafi yanzu, 'ya'yana?", "Where do you want to go after the Asr prayer?": "Ina kuke son ku tafi bayan sallar La'asar?", "They wanted to go to the museum today.": "Sun so su tafi gidan kayan tarihi yau.", "After the prayer we want to go to the market to buy pens and notebooks.": "Bayan sallah muna son mu tafi kasuwa don mu saya alƙaluma da littattafan rubutu.", "yadh-habna": "yadh-habna", "they (f) go": "suna tafiya, mata", "an yadh-habna": "an yadh-habna", "that they (f) go": "cewa su tafi, mata", "The women's forms ending in": "Siffofin mata masu ƙarewa da", "do": "ba sa", "not change": "canzawa", "My daughters, do you want to go with me? Yes.": "'Ya'yana mata, kuna son ku tafi tare da ni? I.", "What do you want to take for her?": "Me kuke son ku kai mata?", "Where are Khadijah and Aishah? Do they want to go with us?": "Ina Khadija da A'isha suke? Suna son su tafi tare da mu?", "an laa": "an laa", "allaa": "allaa", "that not": "cewa kada", "is written": "ana rubuta shi", ", and the verb still ends in a fatha:": ", kuma fi'ilin har yanzu yana ƙarewa da fatha:", "(I hope you do not come in).": "wato ina fata ba za ka shigo ba.", "Please sit here.": "Don Allah ka zauna a nan.", "Please do not sit here.": "Don Allah kada ka zauna a nan.", "I hope you will not take all these things.": "Ina fata ba za ku ɗauki dukan waɗannan kayan ba.", "kal-masjidi": "kal-masjidi", "like the mosque": "kamar masallacin", "(like) is a preposition joined to the next word, which ends in": "wato kamar, harafi ne na jarr da ake haɗawa da kalmar da ke biye, wadda take ƙarewa da", "This school is like the mosque.": "Wannan makarantar kamar masallaci take.", "This coffee is like water.": "Wannan gahawar kamar ruwa take.", "Hamid is lazy like his classmate.": "Hamid malalaci ne kamar abokin ajinsa.", "My watch is like your watch.": "Agogona kamar agogonka yake.", "a habit, custom": "al'ada, ɗabi'a", "a museum": "gidan kayan tarihi", "a box, a tin": "akwati, gwangwani", "clothes": "tufafi", "the zoo": "gidan namun daji", "a neighbour (f)": "maƙwabciya", "visiting a sick person": "duba mara lafiya", "'aadatun (pl. 'aadaatun)": "'aadatun (pl. 'aadaatun)", "matḥafun (pl. mataaḥifu)": "matḥafun (pl. mataaḥifu)", "'ulbatun (pl. 'ulabun)": "'ulbatun (pl. 'ulabun)", "malaabisu": "malaabisu", "ḥadeeqatul-ḥayawaanaati": "ḥadeeqatul-ḥayawaanaati", "jaaratun": "jaaratun", "'iyaadatun": "'iyaadatun", "let's go": "mu tafi", "Where do you want to go after Asr? I want to visit our neighbour who visited me yesterday.": "Ina kike son ki tafi bayan La'asar? Ina son in ziyarci maƙwabciyarmu wadda ta ziyarce ni jiya.", "Can you come back before Maghrib? Possibly, in sha Allah.": "Za ki iya dawowa kafin Magariba? Mai yiwuwa, in sha Allah.", "Please wash my white shirt after you come back from the neighbour. I will wash it and iron it, in sha Allah.": "Don Allah ki wanke farar rigata bayan kin dawo daga wurin maƙwabciyar. Zan wanke ta in yi mata guga, in sha Allah.", "Where do you want to go now, my sons? We are going to the mosque, and after the prayer we want to go to the market.": "Ina kuke son ku tafi yanzu, 'ya'yana? Za mu tafi masallaci, kuma bayan sallah muna son mu tafi kasuwa.", "Where are your friends? They did not come to visit you today as usual. They wanted to go to the museum today.": "Ina abokanku suke? Ba su zo ziyararku yau ba kamar yadda suka saba. Sun so su tafi gidan kayan tarihi yau.", "My daughters, I am going to the hospital to visit Salma. Do you want to go with me? Yes.": "'Ya'yana mata, zan tafi asibiti don in duba Salma. Kuna son ku tafi tare da ni? I.", "I hope you will not take all these things; the hospital does not allow many things in. Let's go, girls.": "Ina fata ba za ku ɗauki dukan waɗannan kayan ba; asibitin ba ya barin a shigar da kaya da yawa. Mu tafi, 'yan mata.", ": drop the": ": ka cire", "stays.": "yana nan daram.", "Add يُرِيدُ أَنْ:": "Ƙara يُرِيدُ أَنْ:", "use -": "yi amfani da -", "Look at who wants to go.": "Duba wanda yake son ya tafi.", "“Please do not go out.”": "“Don Allah kada ka fita.”", "“I hope you will not take all these things.”": "“Ina fata ba za ku ɗauki dukan waɗannan kayan ba.”", "“Please do not come in.”": "“Don Allah kada ka shigo.”", "(like)": "wato kamar", "“Hamid is lazy like his classmate.”": "“Hamid malalaci ne kamar abokin ajinsa.”", "“My watch is like your watch.”": "“Agogona kamar agogonka yake.”", "“This school is like the mosque.”": "“Wannan makarantar kamar masallaci take.”", "Where do you (all) want to go?": "Ina kuke son ku tafi?", "أَنْ or أَلَّا?": "أَنْ ko أَلَّا?", "“Please sit here.”": "“Don Allah ka zauna a nan.”", "كَـ (like)": "كَـ, wato kamar", "“This coffee is like water.”": "“Wannan gahawar kamar ruwa take.”", "After أَنْ: drop the ن": "Bayan أَنْ: cire ن", "Where do you (f) want to go?": "Ina kike son ki tafi?", "Listen, then write the word. (a museum)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato gidan kayan tarihi.", "Fill in يَذْهَبُ after أَنْ": "Cika يَذْهَبُ bayan أَنْ", "✅ “Please sit here.”": "✅ “Don Allah ka zauna a nan.”", "✅ “This coffee is like water.”": "✅ “Wannan gahawar kamar ruwa take.”", "✅ Where do you (f) want to go?": "✅ Ina kike son ki tafi?", "✅ Write: a museum": "✅ Rubuta: gidan kayan tarihi", "✅ “I hope you will not take all these things.”": "✅ “Ina fata ba za ku ɗauki dukan waɗannan kayan ba.”", "✅ “Please do not go out.”": "✅ “Don Allah kada ka fita.”", "✅ “This school is like the mosque.”": "✅ “Wannan makarantar kamar masallaci take.”", "✅ Where do you (all) want to go?": "✅ Ina kuke son ku tafi?", "will not. Like": "ba zai … ba. Kamar", "it gives the present verb": "yana ba fi'ili mai zuwa", "and drops the": "kuma yana cire", "I will not go, and": "ba zan tafi ba, da", "they will not go. You will then compare the three ways to say no:": "ba za su tafi ba. Sannan za ka kwatanta hanyoyi uku na faɗar a'a:", "for the past,": "don lokacin da ya wuce,", "for the present and": "don lokacin yanzu, da", "for the future.": "don lokaci mai zuwa.", "means will not. It gives the present verb": "ma'anarsa ba zai … ba. Yana ba fi'ili mai zuwa", "The women's forms do not change:": "Siffofin mata ba sa canzawa:", "Three ways to say no.": "Hanyoyi uku na faɗar a'a.", "with the past:": "da wanda ya wuce:", "with the present:": "da na yanzu:", "for the future:": "don na gaba:", "لَنْ أَذْهَبَ (I will not go)": "لَنْ أَذْهَبَ, wato ba zan tafi ba", "Add لَنْ": "Ƙara لَنْ", "Answer with لَنْ": "Amsa da لَنْ", "In this lesson you will learn لَنْ, will not. Like أَنْ, it gives the present verb فَتْحَةْ and drops the نُونْ: لَنْ أَذْهَبَ, I will not go, and لَنْ يَذْهَبُوا, they will not go. You will then compare the three ways to say no: مَا for the past, لَا for the present and لَنْ for the future.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi لَنْ, ba zai … ba. Kamar أَنْ, yana ba fi'ili mai zuwa فَتْحَةْ kuma yana cire نُونْ: لَنْ أَذْهَبَ, ba zan tafi ba, da لَنْ يَذْهَبُوا, ba za su tafi ba. Sannan za ka kwatanta hanyoyi uku na faɗar a'a: مَا don lokacin da ya wuce, لَا don lokacin yanzu da لَنْ don lokaci mai zuwa.", "sa-adh-habu": "sa-adh-habu", "I will go": "zan tafi", "lan adh-haba": "lan adh-haba", "I will not go": "ba zan tafi ba", "makes the future negative, and gives the present verb a": "yana korewa lokaci mai zuwa, kuma yana ba fi'ili mai zuwa", ", like": ", kamar", "I am sorry. I will not go to India in the summer holiday.": "Yi haƙuri. Ba zan tafi Indiya a hutun rani ba.", "He will go next week, but he will not come back.": "Zai tafi mako mai zuwa, amma ba zai dawo ba.", "I will never leave the prayer.": "Ba zan taɓa barin sallah ba har abada.", "My father will not come back from Makkah before Ramadan.": "Babana ba zai dawo daga Makka ba kafin Ramadan.", "lan yadh-habuu": "lan yadh-habuu", "they will not go": "ba za su tafi ba", ", just like after": ", kamar bayan", ". The women's forms": ". Siffofin mata", "do not change": "ba sa canzawa", "And your brothers, aren't they going to India? They too will not go this year.": "Kuma 'yan'uwanka, ba za su tafi Indiya ba? Su ma ba za su tafi ba a wannan shekara.", "They want to stay in Madinah to memorise the Noble Qur'an.": "Suna son su zauna a Madina don su haddace Alƙur'ani Mai Girma.", "They (f) too will not go to India in this holiday.": "Su ma, mata, ba za su tafi Indiya ba a wannan hutu.", "We will never drink wine.": "Ba za mu taɓa shan giya ba har abada.", "maa dhahabtu": "maa dhahabtu", "I did not go": "ban tafi ba", "laa adh-habu": "laa adh-habu", "I do not go": "ba na tafiya", "Three ways to say no:": "Hanyoyi uku na faɗar a'a:", "+ past (did not),": "tare da wanda ya wuce, wato bai yi ba,", "+ present (does not, the verb keeps -u),": "tare da na yanzu, wato ba ya yi, fi'ilin yana riƙe -u,", "+ present (will not, the verb takes -a).": "tare da na yanzu, wato ba zai yi ba, fi'ilin yana ɗaukar -a.", "past": "wanda ya wuce", "present": "na yanzu", "future": "na gaba", "I went to the market yesterday.": "Na tafi kasuwa jiya.", "I did not go.": "Ban tafi ba.", "I go every day.": "Ina tafiya kowace rana.", "I do not go every day.": "Ba na tafiya kowace rana.", "I will go tomorrow.": "Zan tafi gobe.", "I will not go tomorrow.": "Ba zan tafi gobe ba.", "sorry": "mai neman gafara, yi haƙuri", "tired": "gajiyayye", "available, present": "akwai shi, yana nan", "Indian": "Ba'indiye", "aasifun": "aasifun", "mut'abun": "mut'abun", "mawjuudun": "mawjuudun", "hindiyyun (pl. hunuudun)": "hindiyyun (pl. hunuudun)", "an embassy": "ofishin jakadanci", "a year": "shekara", "silk": "siliki", "this world": "duniya", "the Hereafter": "lahira", "the future": "gaba, lokaci mai zuwa", "Umrah": "Umura", "sifaaratun": "sifaaratun", "'aamun (pl. a'waamun)": "'aamun (pl. a'waamun)", "ḥareerun": "ḥareerun", "ad-dunyaa": "ad-dunyaa", "al-aakhiratu": "al-aakhiratu", "al-mustaqbalu": "al-mustaqbalu", "'umratun": "'umratun", "he wore": "ya sanya, ya saka", "he was patient": "ya yi haƙuri", "he left, abandoned": "ya bari, ya watsar", "he performed Umrah": "ya yi Umura", "labisa (yalbasu)": "labisa (yalbasu)", "ṣabara (yaṣbiru)": "ṣabara (yaṣbiru)", "taraka (yatruku)": "taraka (yatruku)", "i'tamara (ya'tamiru)": "i'tamara (ya'tamiru)", "never, ever": "har abada, taɓa", "anyone": "kowa", "will not": "ba zai … ba", "Please buy me this book from India when you go there in the summer holiday.": "Don Allah ka saya mini wannan littafi daga Indiya idan ka tafi can a hutun rani.", "I am sorry. I will not go to India in the summer holiday. I want to go to Baghdad to visit my uncle who works at the Indian embassy there.": "Yi haƙuri. Ba zan tafi Indiya a hutun rani ba. Ina son in tafi Bagadaza don in ziyarci baffana wanda ke aiki a ofishin jakadancin Indiya a can.", "And your brothers, aren't they going to India? Right. They too will not go this year.": "Kuma 'yan'uwanka, ba za su tafi Indiya ba? Haka ne. Su ma ba za su tafi ba a wannan shekara.", "They (f) too will not go to India. They want to go to Makkah first to perform Umrah.": "Su ma, mata, ba za su tafi Indiya ba. Suna son su tafi Makka da farko don su yi Umura.", "I heard that an Indian student called Khalid will go to India. Yes, I know him. He will go next week, but he will not come back.": "Na ji cewa wani ɗalibi Ba'indiye mai suna Khalid zai tafi Indiya. I, na san shi. Zai tafi mako mai zuwa, amma ba zai dawo ba.", "Why? Because he is sick and will stay in India for treatment.": "Me ya sa? Saboda ba shi da lafiya kuma zai zauna a Indiya don jinya.", "Thank you, Ayyub. May Allah reward you. And peace be upon you. Go in Allah's care.": "Na gode, Ayyub. Allah ya saka maka da alheri. Assalamu alaikum. Ka je lafiya, Allah ya kiyaye.", "-u: use -a; -": "-u: yi amfani da -a; -", "Add لَنْ:": "Ƙara لَنْ:", "Say no about the future.": "Ka ce a'a game da lokaci mai zuwa.", "Past, present or future?": "Wanda ya wuce, na yanzu ko na gaba?", "“He did not come back.”": "“Bai dawo ba.”", "“I will not go to the market tomorrow.”": "“Ba zan tafi kasuwa gobe ba.”", "“He will not come back.”": "“Ba zai dawo ba.”", "“I did not go to the market yesterday.”": "“Ban tafi kasuwa jiya ba.”", "“He does not come back late.”": "“Ba ya dawowa a makare.”", "They (f) will not go to India.": "Su, mata, ba za su tafi Indiya ba.", "Listen, then write the word. (Umrah)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato Umura.", "I will not go to India.": "Ba zan tafi Indiya ba.", "“I do not go to the market every day.”": "“Ba na tafiya kasuwa kowace rana.”", "✅ Write: Umrah": "✅ Rubuta: Umura", "✅ I will not go to India.": "✅ Ba zan tafi Indiya ba.", "✅ I will never leave the prayer.": "✅ Ba zan taɓa barin sallah ba har abada.", "✅ “I do not go to the market every day.”": "✅ “Ba na tafiya kasuwa kowace rana.”", "✅ “He will not come back.”": "✅ “Ba zai dawo ba.”", "In this lesson you will learn how the dual changes. As the doer it ends in -": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi yadda tasniya, wato siffar biyu, take canzawa. A matsayin fa'ili tana ƙarewa da -", "As the object or after a preposition it ends in -": "A matsayin maf'uli ko bayan harafin jarr tana ƙarewa da -", "You will answer": "Za ka amsa tambayoyin", "questions, and learn": "ka kuma koyi", "one of them and the other, and": "ɗaya daga cikinsu da ɗayan, da", "The dual ends in -": "Tasniya tana ƙarewa da -", "as the doer:": "a matsayin fa'ili:", "It ends in -": "Tana ƙarewa da -", "as the object or after a preposition:": "a matsayin maf'uli ko bayan harafin jarr:", "comes one noun ending in -an:": "suna ɗaya mai ƙarewa da -an yana zuwa:", "The answer can use the dual:": "Amsar tana iya amfani da tasniya:", "For two masculine things:": "Ga abubuwa biyu na namiji:", "For two feminine things:": "Ga abubuwa biyu na mace:", "two: -َانِ and -َيْنِ": "biyu: -َانِ da -َيْنِ", "-َانِ or -َيْنِ": "-َانِ ko -َيْنِ", "One and the other": "Ɗaya da ɗayan", "In this lesson you will learn how the dual changes. As the doer it ends in -َانِ, like جَاءَ الْمُدَرِّسَانِ. As the object or after a preposition it ends in -َيْنِ, like رَأَيْتُ الْمُدَرِّسَيْنِ. You will answer كَمْ questions, and learn أَحَدُهُمَا وَالْآخَرُ, one of them and the other, and إِحْدَاهُمَا وَالْأُخْرَى for feminine.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi yadda tasniya, wato siffar biyu, take canzawa. A matsayin fa'ili tana ƙarewa da -َانِ, kamar جَاءَ الْمُدَرِّسَانِ. A matsayin maf'uli ko bayan harafin jarr tana ƙarewa da -َيْنِ, kamar رَأَيْتُ الْمُدَرِّسَيْنِ. Za ka amsa tambayoyin كَمْ, ka kuma koyi أَحَدُهُمَا وَالْآخَرُ, ɗaya daga cikinsu da ɗayan, da إِحْدَاهُمَا وَالْأُخْرَى ga mace.", "jaa'a l-mudarrisaani": "jaa'a l-mudarrisaani", "The two teachers came.": "Malamai biyun sun zo.", "ra'aytu l-mudarrisayni": "ra'aytu l-mudarrisayni", "I saw the two teachers.": "Na ga malamai biyun.", "The dual ends in": "Tasniya tana ƙarewa da", "as the doer or subject (": "a matsayin fa'ili ko mubtada'i (", "), and in": "), kuma da", "as the object (": "a matsayin maf'uli (", ") or after a preposition (": ") ko bayan harafin jarr (", "doer: -aani": "fa'ili: -aani", "object: -ayni": "maf'uli: -ayni", "after a preposition: -ayni": "bayan harafin jarr: -ayni", "Two new teachers came today.": "Sababbin malamai biyu sun zo yau.", "Today I read two new words in this book.": "Yau na karanta sababbin kalmomi biyu a wannan littafi.", "I have two notebooks, and I want two more.": "Ina da littattafan rubutu biyu, kuma ina son ƙarin biyu.", "I bought it for two riyals.": "Na saye shi riyal biyu.", "kam suuratan ḥafiẓta": "kam suuratan ḥafiẓta", "How many surahs have you memorised?": "Surori nawa ka haddace?", "(how many) comes": "wato nawa, yana zuwa", "both are right:": "dukansu daidai ne:", "How many surahs have you memorised, Bashir? One surah.": "Surori nawa ka haddace, Bashir? Sura ɗaya.", "And how many have you memorised, Umar? I have memorised two.": "Kai kuma nawa ka haddace, Umar? Na haddace biyu.", "For how much did you buy it? For two riyals.": "Nawa ka saye shi? Riyal biyu.", "aḥaduhumaa wal-aakharu": "aḥaduhumaa wal-aakharu", "one of them and the other (m)": "ɗaya daga cikinsu da ɗayan, namiji", "iḥdaahumaa wal-ukhraa": "iḥdaahumaa wal-ukhraa", ". For two feminine things:": ". Ga abubuwa biyu na mace:", ". After": ". Bayan", "a dual is possible too:": "tasniya ma tana yiwuwa:", "(the two-coloured pen).": "wato alƙalami mai launi biyu.", "Two new teachers came today, one for fiqh and the other for hadith.": "Sababbin malamai biyu sun zo yau, ɗaya na fiƙihu ɗayan kuma na hadisi.", "I have two pens, one blue and the other red.": "Ina da alƙaluma biyu, ɗaya shuɗi ne ɗayan kuma ja.", "I have two sisters, one a teacher and the other a nurse.": "Ina da 'yan'uwa mata biyu, ɗaya malama ce ɗayan kuma ma'aikaciyar jinya.", "Where did you get this beautiful two-coloured pen?": "Daga ina ka samo wannan kyakkyawan alƙalami mai launi biyu?", "a comb": "matsefi, kitso", "a pillow": "filo, matashin kai", "a button": "maɓalli", "a mirror": "madubi", "a pound (money)": "fam, kuɗi", "mushṭun (pl. amshaaṭun)": "mushṭun (pl. amshaaṭun)", "mikhaddatun (pl. makhaaddu)": "mikhaddatun (pl. makhaaddu)", "zirrun (pl. azraarun)": "zirrun (pl. azraarun)", "mir'aatun (pl. maraayaa)": "mir'aatun (pl. maraayaa)", "junayhun (pl. junayhaatun)": "junayhun (pl. junayhaatun)", "a thief": "ɓarawo", "useful": "mai amfani", "the Prophet's biography": "tarihin Annabi, wato sira", "Qur'an explanation": "tafsirin Alƙur'ani", "New words: people and words": "Sababbin kalmomi: mutane da kalmomi", "liṣṣun (pl. luṣuuṣun)": "liṣṣun (pl. luṣuuṣun)", "mufeedun": "mufeedun", "as-seeratu": "as-seeratu", "at-tafseeru": "at-tafseeru", "he slaughtered": "ya yanka", "he explained": "ya yi bayani", "dhabaḥa (yadhbaḥu)": "dhabaḥa (yadhbaḥu)", "sharaḥa (yashraḥu)": "sharaḥa (yashraḥu)", "one of them (f)": "ɗaya daga cikinsu, mace", "one of them (m)": "ɗaya daga cikinsu, namiji", "How many surahs have you memorised, Bashir? One. And you, Umar? I have memorised two.": "Surori nawa ka haddace, Bashir? Ɗaya. Kai kuma, Umar? Na haddace biyu.", "Father, two new teachers came today, one for fiqh and the other for hadith.": "Baba, sababbin malamai biyu sun zo yau, ɗaya na fiƙihu ɗayan kuma na hadisi.", "Father, I read two new words in this book today. What are they? They are the comb and the pillow.": "Baba, yau na karanta sababbin kalmomi biyu a wannan littafi. Mene ne su? Su ne matsefi da filo.", "Did you know their meaning? Yes, I asked the teacher, and he explained their meaning to me.": "Ka san ma'anarsu? I, na tambayi malamin, kuma ya yi mini bayanin ma'anarsu.", "I have two notebooks and want two more. I have two small files and want two big files.": "Ina da littattafan rubutu biyu kuma ina son ƙarin biyu. Ina da ƙananan fayiloli biyu kuma ina son manyan fayiloli biyu.", "Where did you get this beautiful two-coloured pen, Bashir? I bought it. For how much? For two riyals.": "Daga ina ka samo wannan kyakkyawan alƙalami mai launi biyu, Bashir? Na saye shi. Nawa? Riyal biyu.", "Doer: -": "Fa'ili: -", "or -": "ko -", ". Object or after a preposition: -": ". Maf'uli ko bayan harafin jarr: -", "جَاءَ …… (two teachers)": "جَاءَ …… (malamai biyu)", "Object or after a preposition: -": "Maf'uli ko bayan harafin jarr: -", "قَرَأْتُ …… جَدِيدَتَيْنِ. (two words)": "قَرَأْتُ …… جَدِيدَتَيْنِ. (kalmomi biyu)", "خَرَجَ مِنَ الْفَصْلِ …… (two students)": "خَرَجَ مِنَ الْفَصْلِ …… (ɗalibai biyu)", "أُرِيدُ …… (two notebooks)": "أُرِيدُ …… (littattafan rubutu biyu)", "هٰذِهِ الْحَافِلَةُ لَهَا …… (two doors)": "هٰذِهِ الْحَافِلَةُ لَهَا …… (ƙofofi biyu)", "كَتَبْتُ الْيَوْمَ …… (two letters)": "كَتَبْتُ الْيَوْمَ …… (wasiƙu biyu)", "عِنْدِي …… (two notebooks)": "عِنْدِي …… (littattafan rubutu biyu)", "اِشْتَرَيْتُهُ بِـ…… (two riyals)": "اِشْتَرَيْتُهُ بِـ…… (riyal biyu)", "Use the dual.": "Yi amfani da tasniya.", "with two": "da biyu", "Answer: two.": "Amsa: biyu.", "Feminine things:": "Abubuwa na mace:", "Listen, then write the word. (a comb)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. Wato matsefi.", "-َانِ or -َيْنِ?": "-َانِ ko -َيْنِ?", "I have two pens; one of them is blue.": "Ina da alƙaluma biyu; ɗaya daga cikinsu shuɗi ne.", "Answer كَمْ with two": "Amsa كَمْ da biyu", "✅ Write: a comb": "✅ Rubuta: matsefi", "✅ I have two pens; one of them is blue.": "✅ Ina da alƙaluma biyu; ɗaya daga cikinsu shuɗi ne.", "✅ Answer: two.": "✅ Amsa: biyu.", "✅ Two new teachers came today.": "✅ Sababbin malamai biyu sun zo yau.", "did not. It ends the present verb in a sukun and drops the": "bai … ba. Yana ƙare fi'ili mai zuwa da sukun kuma yana cire", "he did not go, and": "bai tafi ba, da", "they did not go. You will learn": "ba su tafi ba. Za ka koyi", "not yet, the two kinds of sentence, nominal and verbal, and the three kinds of word: noun, verb and particle.": "tukuna, nau'o'in jumla biyu, jumlar suna da jumlar fi'ili, da nau'o'in kalma uku: suna, fi'ili da harafi.", "with the present verb means did not. The verb ends in a sukun:": "tare da fi'ili mai zuwa ma'anarsa bai … ba. Fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da sukun:", "means the same as": "ma'anarsa iri ɗaya da", "means not yet, and also gives a sukun:": "ma'anarsa bai … ba tukuna, kuma shi ma yana ba da sukun:", "It can stand alone:": "Yana iya tsayawa shi kaɗai:", "A nominal sentence starts with a noun:": "Jumlar suna tana farawa da suna:", "both ending in": "dukansu suna ƙarewa da", "A verbal sentence starts with a verb:": "Jumlar fi'ili tana farawa da fi'ili:", "Words are of three kinds:": "Kalmomi iri uku ne:", "the noun.": "suna, wato ism.", "the verb.": "fi'ili.", "the particle, like": "harafi, kamar", "لَمْ يَذْهَبْ (he did not go)": "لَمْ يَذْهَبْ, wato bai tafi ba", "Add لَمْ": "Ƙara لَمْ", "Answer with لَمْ": "Amsa da لَمْ", "Not yet": "Tukuna", "Sentence kind": "Nau'in jumla", "Word kind": "Nau'in kalma", "In this lesson you will learn لَمْ, did not. It ends the present verb in a sukun and drops the نُونْ: لَمْ يَذْهَبْ, he did not go, and لَمْ يَذْهَبُوا, they did not go. You will learn لَمَّا, not yet, the two kinds of sentence, nominal and verbal, and the three kinds of word: noun, verb and particle.": "A wannan darasi za ka koyi لَمْ, bai … ba. Yana ƙare fi'ili mai zuwa da sukun kuma yana cire نُونْ: لَمْ يَذْهَبْ, bai tafi ba, da لَمْ يَذْهَبُوا, ba su tafi ba. Za ka koyi لَمَّا, tukuna, nau'o'in jumla biyu, jumlar suna da jumlar fi'ili, da nau'o'in kalma uku: suna, fi'ili da harafi.", "lam yadh-hab": "lam yadh-hab", "+ the present verb means": "tare da fi'ili mai zuwa ma'anarsa", "+ past). The verb ends in a": "tare da wanda ya wuce). Fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da", ". A sukun before": ". Sukun kafin", "becomes a kasra:": "yana zama kasra:", "I don't see Harun. Didn't he come? Right, he did not come today.": "Ban ga Harun ba. Bai zo ba? Haka ne, bai zo yau ba.", "Did you write the homework? Yes, we did. I did not write it.": "Kun rubuta aikin gida? I, mun rubuta. Ni ban rubuta ba.", "Why didn't you write, son? Because I did not understand the lesson.": "Me ya sa ba ka rubuta ba, ɗana? Saboda ban fahimci darasin ba.", "I have not eaten anything for two days.": "Ban ci komai ba tsawon kwana biyu.", "lam yadh-habuu": "lam yadh-habuu", "they did not go": "ba su tafi ba", "And where are his three friends? They also did not come.": "Kuma ina abokansa uku suke? Su ma ba su zo ba.", "Many students did not understand this.": "Ɗalibai da yawa ba su fahimci wannan ba.", "I asked my sisters who study at the secondary school about this, and they did not know.": "Na tambayi 'yan'uwana mata waɗanda ke karatu a makarantar sakandare game da wannan, kuma ba su sani ba.", "Didn't you hear the adhan, Harun? Yes, I did.": "Ba ka ji kiran sallah ba, Harun? I, na ji.", "lammaa aktub": "lammaa aktub", "I have not written yet": "ban rubuta ba tukuna", "not yet": "tukuna", ". It also gives a sukun:": ". Shi ma yana ba da sukun:", ". It can stand alone as an answer:": ". Yana iya tsayawa shi kaɗai a matsayin amsa:", ". (Say": ". Ka ce", ", not the slang": ", ba na zance na yau da kullum ba", "Has the principal come back from Makkah, teacher? Not yet. He will come back in two days, in sha Allah.": "Shugaban makaranta ya dawo daga Makka, malam? Tukuna. Zai dawo bayan kwana biyu, in sha Allah.", "Shall we start the new lesson? Wait, teacher, we have not yet written what you wrote on the board.": "Mu fara sabon darasin? Dakata, malam, ba mu rubuta abin da ka rubuta a allo ba tukuna.", "The bell has rung, and the teachers have not yet come out of the classes.": "Ƙararrawa ta yi ƙara, kuma malamai ba su fito daga ajujuwa ba tukuna.", "nominal sentence": "jumlar suna, wato jumla ismiyya", "verbal sentence": "jumlar fi'ili, wato jumla fi'iliyya", "The teacher came in.": "Malamin ya shigo.", ") starts with a noun: the": ") tana farawa da suna:", ", both ending in": ", dukansu suna ƙarewa da", ") starts with a verb, then the doer (": ") tana farawa da fi'ili, sannan fa'ili (", "), which also ends in -u.": "), wanda shi ma yana ƙarewa da -u.", "nominal: starts with a noun": "ta suna: tana farawa da suna", "verbal: starts with a verb": "ta fi'ili: tana farawa da fi'ili", "Hamid is sick.": "Hamid ba shi da lafiya.", "The principal said.": "Shugaban makaranta ya ce.", "noun": "suna", "al-fi'lu": "al-fi'lu", "al-ḥarfu": "al-ḥarfu", "particle": "harafi", "Words are of three kinds (": "Kalmomi iri uku ne (", "(noun:": "wato suna:", "(verb:": "wato fi'ili:", "(particle:": "wato harafi:", "). Also:": "). Haka kuma:", "nouns": "sunaye", "verbs": "fi'iloli", "particles": "haruffa", "a head, a president": "kai, shugaba", "welcoming, receiving": "tarba, karɓar baƙo", "a difference": "bambanci", "an example": "misali", "a part, a kind": "sashe, nau'i", "the damma (-u)": "ɗamma (-u)", "the fatha (-a)": "fataha (-a)", "the kasra (-i)": "kasra (-i)", "ra'eesun (pl. ru'asaa'u)": "ra'eesun (jam'i: ru'asaa'u)", "istiqbaalun": "istiqbaalun", "farqun (pl. furuuqun)": "farqun (jam'i: furuuqun)", "mithaalun (pl. amthilatun)": "mithaalun (jam'i: amthilatun)", "qismun (pl. aqsaamun)": "qismun (jam'i: aqsaamun)", "aḍ-ḍammatu": "aḍ-ḍammatu", "al-fatḥatu": "al-fatḥatu", "al-kasratu": "al-kasratu", "he attended": "ya halarta", "rest!": "ka huta!", "ḥaḍara (yaḥḍuru)": "ḥaḍara (yaḥḍuru)", "ataa (ya'tee)": "ataa (ya'tee)", "istariḥ (pl. istareeḥuu)": "istariḥ (jam'i: istareeḥuu)", "wait, slowly": "dakata, a hankali", "How are you, our teacher? Well, I praise Allah and thank Him. I don't see Harun. Didn't he come?": "Yaya kake, malaminmu? Lafiya, ina gode wa Allah ina yabonSa. Ban ga Harun ba. Bai zo ba?", "Right, he did not come today. And where are his three friends? They also did not come.": "Haka ne, bai zo yau ba. Ina abokansa su uku? Su ma ba su zo ba.", "I think they went to the airport to receive their president, who comes to Madinah today.": "Ina tsammani sun tafi filin jirgin sama don su tarbi shugabansu, wanda zai zo Madina yau.", "Did you write the homework, my sons? Yes. I did not. Why not, son? Because I did not understand the lesson.": "Kun rubuta aikin gida, 'ya'yana? Ee. Ni ban rubuta ba. Me ya sa, ɗana? Saboda ban fahimci darasin ba.", "What did you not understand in the lesson? I did not understand the difference between the nominal and the verbal sentence.": "Me ba ka fahimta ba a darasin? Ban fahimci bambanci tsakanin jumla ismiyya da jumla fi'iliyya ba.", "The nominal sentence is the sentence that begins with a noun. The subject and predicate both end in -u.": "Jumla ismiyya ita ce jumlar da take farawa da suna. Mubtada'i da khabari dukansu suna ƙarewa da -u.", "-u: use": "-u: yi amfani da", "-u → sukun; -": "-u → sukun; -", "Add لَمْ:": "Ƙara لَمْ:", "Say no about the past with": "Ka faɗi \"a'a\" game da abin da ya wuce da", "(not yet)": "(har yanzu ba)", "also gives a sukun.": "shi ma yana kawo sukun.", "Answer: not yet.": "Ka amsa: har yanzu ba.", "also gives a": "shi ma yana kawo", "Does it start with a noun or a verb?": "Tana farawa da suna ko da fi'ili?", "verbal": "fi'iliyya", "nominal": "ismiyya", "Nominal or verbal?": "Ismiyya ko fi'iliyya?", "Noun, verb or particle?": "Suna, fi'ili ko harafi?", "The subject and the predicate end in -u.": "Mubtada'i da khabari suna ƙarewa da -u.", "He did not come today.": "Bai zo yau ba.", "Listen, then write the word. (a part, a kind)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (sashe, nau'i)", "Because I did not understand the lesson.": "Saboda ban fahimci darasin ba.", "لَمَّا (not yet)": "لَمَّا (har yanzu ba)", "✅ He did not come today.": "✅ Bai zo yau ba.", "✅ Write: a part, a kind": "✅ Rubuta: sashe, nau'i", "✅ Because I did not understand the lesson.": "✅ Saboda ban fahimci darasin ba.", "✅ Answer: not yet.": "✅ Ka amsa: har yanzu ba.", "This is a review lesson. You will put together the three states of the present verb:": "Wannan darasin bita ne. Za ka haɗa halaye uku na fi'ili mai nuna yanzu (mudari'i):", "ending in a sukun after": "mai ƙarewa da sukun bayan", "that forbids.": "ta hani.", "The present verb has three states. Normal, ending in": "Fi'ili mai nuna yanzu yana da halaye uku. Na yau da kullum, mai ƙarewa da", "that forbids, ending in a sukun:": "ta hani, mai ƙarewa da sukun:", "The long forms keep the": "Dogayen siffofi suna riƙe", "when normal:": "idan suna na yau da kullum:", "They drop it after": "Suna sauke shi bayan", "and after": "da kuma bayan", "never change:": "ba sa canjawa har abada:", "the three states of the present (review)": "halaye uku na fi'ili mai nuna yanzu (bita)", "Lesson 22, p. 153": "Darasi na 22, shafi na 153", "Which state?": "Wane hali?", "This is a review lesson. You will put together the three states of the present verb: يَذْهَبُ, ending in ضَمَّةْ, لَنْ يَذْهَبَ, ending in فَتْحَةْ after أَنْ, لَنْ and لِـ, and لَمْ يَذْهَبْ, ending in a sukun after لَمْ, لَمَّا and لَا that forbids.": "Wannan darasin bita ne. Za ka haɗa halaye uku na fi'ili mai nuna yanzu: يَذْهَبُ, mai ƙarewa da ضَمَّةْ, لَنْ يَذْهَبَ, mai ƙarewa da فَتْحَةْ bayan أَنْ, لَنْ da لِـ, da kuma لَمْ يَذْهَبْ, mai ƙarewa da sukun bayan لَمْ, لَمَّا da لَا ta hani.", "marfuu'": "marfuu'", "manṣuub": "manṣuub", "majzuum": "majzuum", "The present verb has three states.": "Fi'ili mai nuna yanzu yana da halaye uku.", "(normal).": "(na yau da kullum).", "normal: -u": "na yau da kullum: -u", "Hamid goes.": "Hamid yana tafiya.", "Hamid will not go.": "Hamid ba zai tafi ba.", "Hamid did not go.": "Hamid bai tafi ba.", "Aminah goes": "Aminah tana tafiya", "will not go": "ba za ta tafi ba", "did not go": "ba ta tafi ba", "The long forms (-": "Dogayen siffofi (-", ") keep the": ") suna riƙe", "when normal, and": "idan na yau da kullum ne, kuma", "drop it": "suna sauke shi", "after both kinds:": "bayan nau'ukan biyu:", ". So": ". Don haka", "look the same here.": "sun yi kama da juna a nan.", "The students go.": "Ɗalibai suna tafiya.", "The students will not go.": "Ɗalibai ba za su tafi ba.", "The students did not go.": "Ɗalibai ba su tafi ba.", "you go": "kina tafiya", "did not go (f)": "ba ki tafi ba (mace)", "lan yadh-habna": "lan yadh-habna", "lam yadh-habna": "lam yadh-habna", "never change": "ba sa canjawa har abada", "The students (f) go.": "Ɗalibai (mata) suna tafiya.", "The students (f) will not go.": "Ɗalibai (mata) ba za su tafi ba.", "The students (f) did not go.": "Ɗalibai (mata) ba su tafi ba.", "he will not go": "ba zai tafi ba", "don't go!": "kada ka tafi!", "New words: the three states": "Sababbin kalmomi: halaye uku", "lan yadh-haba": "lan yadh-haba", "laa tadh-hab": "laa tadh-hab", "ending in a sukun": "mai ƙarewa da sukun", "ending in -u": "mai ƙarewa da -u", "ending in -a": "mai ƙarewa da -a", "Hamid goes, will not go, did not go.": "Hamid yana tafiya, ba zai tafi ba, bai tafi ba.", "The students go, will not go, did not go.": "Ɗalibai suna tafiya, ba za su tafi ba, ba su tafi ba.", "Aminah goes, will not go, did not go.": "Aminah tana tafiya, ba za ta tafi ba, ba ta tafi ba.", "The students (f) go, will not go, did not go.": "Ɗalibai (mata) suna tafiya, ba za su tafi ba, ba su tafi ba.", "You (f) go, will not go, did not go.": "Ke (mace) kina tafiya, ba za ki tafi ba, ba ki tafi ba.", "I go, will not go, did not go.": "Ina tafiya, ba zan tafi ba, ban tafi ba.", ": sukun. Long forms drop": ": sukun. Dogayen siffofi suna sauke", "Long forms drop": "Dogayen siffofi suna sauke", "-u, -a or": "-u, -a ko", "sukun (majzuum)": "sukun (majzuum)", "-a (manṣuub)": "-a (manṣuub)", "Which ending, and why?": "Wane ƙarshe, kuma me ya sa?", "-u, -a or sukun?": "-u, -a ko sukun?", "-u (marfuu')": "-u (marfuu')", "Will not, or did not?": "Ba zai yi ba, ko bai yi ba?", "Choose the Arabic": "Zaɓi Larabcin", "“You (f) will not go.”": "“Ke (mace) ba za ki tafi ba.”", "“The students (f) did not go.”": "“Ɗalibai (mata) ba su tafi ba.”", "“The students will not go.”": "“Ɗalibai ba za su tafi ba.”", "“Hamid did not go.”": "“Hamid bai tafi ba.”", "“Hamid will not go.”": "“Hamid ba zai tafi ba.”", "لَنْ or لَمْ with each person": "لَنْ ko لَمْ tare da kowane mutum", "✅ “The students (f) did not go.”": "✅ “Ɗalibai (mata) ba su tafi ba.”", "✅ The students did not go.": "✅ Ɗalibai ba su tafi ba.", "✅ The students (f) will not go.": "✅ Ɗalibai (mata) ba za su tafi ba.", "✅ “The students will not go.”": "✅ “Ɗalibai ba za su tafi ba.”", "✅ “Hamid will not go.”": "✅ “Hamid ba zai tafi ba.”", "✅ “You (f) will not go.”": "✅ “Ke (mace) ba za ki tafi ba.”", "In this lesson you will learn how the plural ending -": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi yadda ƙarshen jam'i -", "changes. As the doer it is": "yake canjawa. A matsayin mai aikatawa (fa'ili) shi ne", "and as the object or after a preposition it becomes": "kuma a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki (maf'uli) ko bayan harafin jarri yana komawa", "The tens, from": "Goma-goma, daga", "twenty, to": "ashirin, zuwa", "ninety, change in the same way. You will also learn": "casa'in, suna canjawa haka nan. Za ka kuma koyi", "with a past verb.": "tare da fi'ili na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci.", "The plural -": "Jam'i -", "is for the doer:": "na mai aikatawa ne:", "As the object or after a preposition it becomes -": "A matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki ko bayan harafin jarri yana komawa -", "The tens end like this plural:": "Goma-goma suna ƙarewa kamar wannan jam'in:", "As object they end in -": "A matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki suna ƙarewa da -", "In a compound number both parts change:": "A lamba mai haɗi sassan biyu duka suna canjawa:", "can come before a past verb only when it is repeated:": "yana iya zuwa kafin fi'ili na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci ne kawai idan an maimaita shi:", "-ُونَ and -ِينَ": "-ُونَ da -ِينَ", "-ُونَ or -ِينَ": "-ُونَ ko -ِينَ", "The tens": "Goma-goma", "Tens in a sentence": "Goma-goma a cikin jumla", "In this lesson you will learn how the plural ending -ُونَ changes. As the doer it is الْمُدَرِّسُونَ, and as the object or after a preposition it becomes الْمُدَرِّسِينَ. The tens, from عِشْرُونَ, twenty, to تِسْعُونَ, ninety, change in the same way. You will also learn لَا … وَلَا with a past verb.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi yadda ƙarshen jam'i -ُونَ yake canjawa. A matsayin mai aikatawa shi ne الْمُدَرِّسُونَ, kuma a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki ko bayan harafin jarri yana komawa الْمُدَرِّسِينَ. Goma-goma, daga عِشْرُونَ, ashirin, zuwa تِسْعُونَ, casa'in, suna canjawa haka nan. Za ka kuma koyi لَا … وَلَا tare da fi'ili na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci.", "jaa'a l-mudarrisuuna": "jaa'a l-mudarrisuuna", "The teachers came.": "Malaman sun zo.", "ra'aytu l-mudarriseena": "ra'aytu l-mudarriseena", "I saw the teachers.": "Na ga malaman.", "The sound masculine plural ends in": "Jam'in namiji salimi yana ƙarewa da", "as the doer or subject, and in": "a matsayin mai aikatawa ko mubtada'i, kuma da", "doer: -uuna": "mai aikatawa: -uuna", "object: -eena": "wanda aka yi wa aiki: -eena", "after a preposition: -eena": "bayan harafin jarri: -eena", "Where are the teachers? They neither entered the classes nor are they in the teachers' room.": "Ina malaman? Ba su shiga azuzuwa ba, kuma ba sa ɗakin malamai.", "Did you see the new teachers?": "Ka ga sababbin malaman?", "Allah loves the Muslims.": "Allah yana son Musulmi.", "These are hardworking students.": "Waɗannan ɗalibai ne masu ƙoƙari.", "'ishruuna": "'ishruuna", "twenty (doer)": "ashirin (mai aikatawa)", "'ishreena": "'ishreena", "twenty (object)": "ashirin (wanda aka yi wa aiki)", "The tens (": "Goma-goma (", ") end like this plural:": ") suna ƙarewa kamar wannan jam'in:", ". As object or after a preposition:": ". A matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki ko bayan harafin jarri:", ". The noun after them is one, ending in": ". Sunan da yake bayansu ɗaya ne, mai ƙarewa da", "qara'naa thalaathan wa khamseena ṣafḥatan": "qara'naa thalaathan wa khamseena ṣafḥatan", "We read fifty-three pages.": "Mun karanta shafuka hamsin da uku.", ". Also": ". Haka kuma", "(like):": "(kamar):", "How many pages have you read in it? We have read fifty-three pages.": "Shafuka nawa kuka karanta a cikinsa? Mun karanta shafuka hamsin da uku.", "The book has ninety pages, so thirty-seven pages are left.": "Littafin yana da shafuka casa'in, don haka shafuka talatin da bakwai suka rage.", "I bought it for eighty riyals.": "Na saye shi riyal tamanin.", "I bought one like it for seventy riyals.": "Na sayi irinsa riyal saba'in.", "laa akaltu wa laa sharibtu": "laa akaltu wa laa sharibtu", "I neither ate nor drank.": "Ban ci ba, ban sha ba.", "can come before a past verb only when it is": "yana iya zuwa kafin fi'ili na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci ne kawai idan", "repeated": "an maimaita shi", "That student neither memorised the lesson nor wrote the homework.": "Wannan ɗalibin bai haddace darasin ba, kuma bai rubuta aikin gida ba.", "He did not hit me and I did not hit him.": "Bai buge ni ba, ni ma ban buge shi ba.", "He did not see me and I did not see him.": "Bai gan ni ba, ni ma ban gan shi ba.", "a story": "labari, ƙissa", "a prophet": "annabi", "a family": "iyali", "a prize": "kyauta", "a second (time)": "daƙiƙa", "a hall": "zaure, babban ɗaki", "ijtimaa'un": "ijtimaa'un", "qiṣṣatun (pl. qiṣaṣun)": "qiṣṣatun (jam'i: qiṣaṣun)", "nabiyyun (pl. anbiyaa'u)": "nabiyyun (jam'i: anbiyaa'u)", "usratun (pl. usarun)": "usratun (jam'i: usarun)", "jaa'izatun (pl. jawaa'izu)": "jaa'izatun (jam'i: jawaa'izu)", "thaaniyatun (pl. thawaanin)": "thaaniyatun (jam'i: thawaanin)", "qaa'atun (pl. qaa'aatun)": "qaa'atun (jam'i: qaa'aatun)", "he passed, succeeded": "ya ci jarrabawa, ya yi nasara", "he failed": "ya faɗi jarrabawa", "najaḥa (yanjaḥu)": "najaḥa (yanjaḥu)", "rasaba (yarsubu)": "rasaba (yarsubu)", "twenty": "ashirin", "like, the same as": "kamar, irin", "Where are the teachers? They neither entered the classes nor are they in the teachers' room. I think they are in a meeting.": "Ina malaman? Ba su shiga azuzuwa ba, kuma ba sa ɗakin malamai. Ina tsammani suna taro.", "Did you see the new teachers? Did new teachers come? Yes. Five new teachers came.": "Ka ga sababbin malaman? Sababbin malamai sun zo? Ee. Sababbin malamai biyar sun zo.", "Thank you, brothers. How many students are in this class? Thirty. But I see only twenty-five.": "Na gode, 'yan'uwa. Ɗalibai nawa ne a wannan ajin? Talatin. Amma ashirin da biyar kawai nake gani.", "Which book are you reading? We are reading this book. Its name is Stories of the Prophets.": "Wane littafi kuke karantawa? Muna karanta wannan littafin. Sunansa Labaran Annabawa.", "How many pages have you read? Fifty-three. The book has ninety pages, so thirty-seven are left.": "Shafuka nawa kuka karanta? Hamsin da uku. Littafin yana da shafuka casa'in, don haka talatin da bakwai suka rage.", "How beautiful your bag is, teacher! For how much did you buy it? For eighty riyals.": "Jakarka tana da kyau, malam! Nawa ka saye ta? Riyal tamanin.", "I bought one like it for seventy riyals. I bought a smaller bag for sixty riyals.": "Na sayi irinta riyal saba'in. Na sayi ƙaramar jaka riyal sittin.", "Doer or subject: -": "Mai aikatawa ko mubtada'i: -", "سَمِعْتُ هٰذَا الْخَبَرَ مِنَ …… (the teachers)": "سَمِعْتُ هٰذَا الْخَبَرَ مِنَ …… (malaman)", "أَيْنَ ……؟ (the engineers)": "أَيْنَ ……؟ (injiniyoyin)", "يَعْبُدُ …… اللهَ. (the Muslims)": "يَعْبُدُ …… اللهَ. (Musulmi)", "يُحِبُّ اللهُ …… (the Muslims)": "يُحِبُّ اللهُ …… (Musulmi)", "هٰذِهِ الْجَائِزَةُ لِلطُّلَّابِ …… (hardworking)": "هٰذِهِ الْجَائِزَةُ لِلطُّلَّابِ …… (masu ƙoƙari)", "يُحِبُّ الْمُدَرِّسُ الطُّلَّابَ …… (hardworking)": "يُحِبُّ الْمُدَرِّسُ الطُّلَّابَ …… (masu ƙoƙari)", "قُلْتُ لِـ…… (the teachers)": "قُلْتُ لِـ…… (malaman)", "دَخَلَ …… (the teachers)": "دَخَلَ …… (malaman)", "Choose the number.": "Zaɓi lambar.", "The tens change like the plural.": "Goma-goma suna canjawa kamar jam'i.", "on the tens": "a kan goma-goma", "Before a past verb,": "Kafin fi'ili na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci,", "with the past": "tare da shuɗaɗɗen lokaci", "must be repeated.": "dole a maimaita shi.", "“He neither memorised nor wrote.”": "“Bai haddace ba, bai rubuta ba.”", "“He did not hit me and I did not hit him.”": "“Bai buge ni ba, ni ma ban buge shi ba.”", "“I neither ate nor drank.”": "“Ban ci ba, ban sha ba.”", "-ُونَ or -ِينَ on the tens": "-ُونَ ko -ِينَ a kan goma-goma", "-ُونَ or -ِينَ?": "-ُونَ ko -ِينَ?", "سَأَلْتُ …… (the teachers)": "سَأَلْتُ …… (malaman)", "هٰؤُلَاءِ طُلَّابٌ …… (hardworking)": "هٰؤُلَاءِ طُلَّابٌ …… (masu ƙoƙari)", "لَا … وَلَا with the past": "لَا … وَلَا tare da shuɗaɗɗen lokaci", "Listen, then write the word. (a hall)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (zaure)", "✅ “He neither memorised nor wrote.”": "✅ “Bai haddace ba, bai rubuta ba.”", "✅ I neither ate nor drank.": "✅ Ban ci ba, ban sha ba.", "✅ “He did not hit me and I did not hit him.”": "✅ “Bai buge ni ba, ni ma ban buge shi ba.”", "✅ Write: a hall": "✅ Rubuta: zaure", "✅ Allah loves the Muslims.": "✅ Allah yana son Musulmi.", "This is a review of numbers, from one to a million. You will learn when the number agrees with the noun and when it is opposite, and what the counted noun looks like after each number. You will also learn the hundreds, like": "Wannan bita ce ta lambobi, daga ɗaya zuwa miliyan. Za ka koyi yaushe lambar take dacewa da suna, da yaushe take saɓa masa, da yadda sunan da ake ƙirgawa yake kasancewa bayan kowace lamba. Za ka kuma koyi ɗari-ɗari, kamar", "and the thousands, like": "da dubu-dubu, kamar", "One and two agree with the noun and come after it:": "Ɗaya da biyu suna dacewa da suna kuma suna zuwa bayansa:", "Three to ten are opposite. With a masculine noun the number has": "Uku zuwa goma suna saɓawa. Tare da suna na namiji lambar tana da", "With a feminine noun it has none:": "Tare da suna na mace ba ta da shi:", "The noun is plural, ending in": "Sunan jam'i ne, mai ƙarewa da", "From eleven to ninety-nine the noun is one, ending in -an:": "Daga goma sha ɗaya zuwa casa'in da tara sunan ɗaya ne, mai ƙarewa da -an:", "After a hundred and a thousand the noun is one, ending in": "Bayan ɗari da dubu sunan ɗaya ne, mai ƙarewa da", "Two hundred:": "Ɗari biyu:", "Three hundred:": "Ɗari uku:", "Two thousand:": "Dubu biyu:", "Three thousand:": "Dubu uku:", "numbers (review)": "lambobi (bita)", "Hundreds, thousands": "Ɗari-ɗari, dubu-dubu", "The counted noun": "Sunan da ake ƙirgawa", "This is a review of numbers, from one to a million. You will learn when the number agrees with the noun and when it is opposite, and what the counted noun looks like after each number. You will also learn the hundreds, like مِائَتَانِ and ثَلَاثُمِائَةٍ, and the thousands, like أَلْفَانِ and ثَلَاثَةُ آلَافٍ.": "Wannan bita ce ta lambobi, daga ɗaya zuwa miliyan. Za ka koyi yaushe lambar take dacewa da suna, da yaushe take saɓa masa, da yadda sunan da ake ƙirgawa yake kasancewa bayan kowace lamba. Za ka kuma koyi ɗari-ɗari, kamar مِائَتَانِ da ثَلَاثُمِائَةٍ, da dubu-dubu, kamar أَلْفَانِ da ثَلَاثَةُ آلَافٍ.", "ṭaalibun waaḥidun": "ṭaalibun waaḥidun", "one student": "ɗalibi ɗaya", "ṭaalibaani thnaani": "ṭaalibaani thnaani", "two students": "ɗalibai biyu", "1 and 2 agree": "1 da 2 suna dacewa", "with the noun and come": "da suna kuma suna zuwa", "it:": "bayansa:", "one student (m": "ɗalibi ɗaya (namiji", "two students (m": "ɗalibai biyu (maza", "3 students (m)": "ɗalibai 3 (maza)", "3 to 10 are opposite": "3 zuwa 10 suna saɓawa", ": with a masculine noun the number has": ": tare da suna na namiji lambar tana da", ", with a feminine noun it has none. The noun is": ", tare da suna na mace ba ta da shi. Sunan", "masculine noun → ة on the number": "suna na namiji → ة a kan lambar", "feminine noun → no ة": "suna na mace → babu ة", "aḥada 'ashara ṭaaliban": "aḥada 'ashara ṭaaliban", "{0} students": "ɗalibai {0}", "thalaathata 'ashara ṭaaliban": "thalaathata 'ashara ṭaaliban", "11 and 12": "11 da 12", ": both parts agree.": ": sassan biyu duka suna dacewa.", ": the first part is opposite, the second (": ": sashe na farko yana saɓawa, na biyu (", ") agrees.": ") yana dacewa.", ": the unit follows the 3–10 rule, the tens stay the same. From 11 to 99 the noun is": ": lambar ɗaya-ɗaya tana bin ƙa'idar 3 zuwa 10, goma-goma ba sa canjawa. Daga 11 zuwa 99 sunan", "mi'atu ṭaalibin": "mi'atu ṭaalibin", "alfu ṭaalibin": "alfu ṭaalibin", "100 and 1000": "100 da 1000", "the noun is": "sunan", "never changes for masculine or feminine.": "ba ya canjawa don namiji ko mace.", "two hundred": "ɗari biyu", "three hundred": "ɗari uku", "two thousand": "dubu biyu", "thousands": "dubbai", "New words: numbers": "Sababbin kalmomi: lambobi", "waaḥidun (f. waaḥidatun)": "waaḥidun (mace: waaḥidatun)", "ithnaani (f. ithnataani)": "ithnaani (mace: ithnataani)", "mi'ataani": "mi'ataani", "thalaathumi'atin": "thalaathumi'atin", "alfaani": "alfaani", "aalaafun": "aalaafun", "the counted noun": "sunan da ake ƙirgawa", "the number": "lambar", "One student, one student (f), two students, two students (f).": "Ɗalibi ɗaya, ɗaliba ɗaya, ɗalibai biyu, ɗalibai mata biyu.", "Three students, three students (f), ten students, ten students (f).": "Ɗalibai uku, ɗalibai mata uku, ɗalibai goma, ɗalibai mata goma.", "Eleven students, eleven (f), thirteen students, thirteen (f).": "Ɗalibai goma sha ɗaya, mata goma sha ɗaya, ɗalibai goma sha uku, mata goma sha uku.", "Twenty-five students, twenty-five students (f).": "Ɗalibai ashirin da biyar, ɗalibai mata ashirin da biyar.", "100, 200, 300, 1000, 2000, 3000 students.": "Ɗalibai 100, 200, 300, 1000, 2000, 3000.", "Masculine noun: use": "Suna na namiji: yi amfani da", "3 to 10: opposite": "3 zuwa 10: suna saɓawa", "Masculine noun →": "Suna na namiji →", "on the number.": "a kan lambar.", "How do you say “{0} students (f)”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai mata {0}”?", "How do you say “10 pages”?": "Yaya ake cewa “shafuka 10”?", "How do you say “99 pages”?": "Yaya ake cewa “shafuka 99”?", "How do you say “15 students (m)”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai maza 15”?", "100 to 100,000": "100 zuwa 100,000", "3 10: plural -in. 11 99: one": "3 10: jam'i -in. 11 99: ɗaya", "Which noun comes next?": "Wane suna ne yake biyowa?", "3–10: plural -in. 11–99: one -an. 100, 1000: one -in.": "3 zuwa 10: jam'i mai -in. 11 zuwa 99: ɗaya mai -an. 100, 1000: ɗaya mai -in.", "100, 1000: one -in.": "100, 1000: ɗaya mai -in.", "fifteen students": "ɗalibai goma sha biyar", "Listen, then write the word. (two thousand)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (dubu biyu)", "three thousand riyals": "riyal dubu uku", "three students (f)": "ɗalibai mata uku", "✅ Write: two thousand": "✅ Rubuta: dubu biyu", "✅ How do you say “10 pages”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “shafuka 10”?", "✅ How do you say “{0} students (f)”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai mata {0}”?", "✅ three thousand riyals": "✅ riyal dubu uku", "✅ three students (f)": "✅ ɗalibai mata uku", "✅ How do you say “15 students (m)”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai maza 15”?", "✅ How do you say “5 cars”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “motoci 5”?", "In this lesson you will learn what": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi abin da", "does to a sentence: the second word ends in": "yake yi wa jumla: kalma ta biyu tana ƙarewa da", "as in": "kamar a", "Hamid was sick.": "Hamid ya kasance mara lafiya.", "still, works the same way. You will also see how": "har yanzu, yana aiki haka nan. Za ka kuma ga yadda", "change before an ending:": "suke canjawa kafin ƙari:", "enters a nominal sentence. The first word keeps": "yana shiga jumla ismiyya. Kalma ta farko tana riƙe", "and the second takes": "kuma ta biyu tana ɗaukar", "means still. It is a sister of": "yana nufin har yanzu. 'Yar'uwar", "so the second word takes": "ce, don haka kalma ta biyu tana ɗaukar", "change before an ending. As the doer,": "suna canjawa kafin ƙari. A matsayin mai aikatawa,", "As the object,": "A matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki,", "After a preposition,": "Bayan harafin jarri,", "كَانَ مَرِيضًا (he was sick)": "كَانَ مَرِيضًا (ya kasance mara lafiya)", "Still": "Har yanzu", "In this lesson you will learn what كَانَ does to a sentence: the second word ends in فَتْحَةْ, as in كَانَ حَامِدٌ مَرِيضًا, Hamid was sick. لَا يَزَالُ, still, works the same way. You will also see how أَبٌ and أَخٌ change before an ending: أَبُوكَ, أَبَاكَ, أَبِيكَ.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi abin da كَانَ yake yi wa jumla: kalma ta biyu tana ƙarewa da فَتْحَةْ, kamar a كَانَ حَامِدٌ مَرِيضًا, Hamid ya kasance mara lafiya. لَا يَزَالُ, har yanzu, yana aiki haka nan. Za ka kuma ga yadda أَبٌ da أَخٌ suke canjawa kafin ƙari: أَبُوكَ, أَبَاكَ, أَبِيكَ.", "ḥaamidun mareeḍun": "ḥaamidun mareeḍun", "kaana ḥaamidun mareeḍan": "kaana ḥaamidun mareeḍan", "enters a nominal sentence. The first word (": "yana shiga jumla ismiyya. Kalma ta farko (", ") keeps": ") tana riƙe", ", and the second (": ", kuma ta biyu (", ") takes": ") tana ɗaukar", "الْخَبَرُ: -u -un": "الْخَبَرُ: -u -un", "خَبَرُ كَانَ -an": "خَبَرُ كَانَ -an", "He was standing outside the class.": "Ya kasance a tsaye a wajen aji.", "He was sick a week ago.": "Ya yi rashin lafiya mako ɗaya da ya wuce.", "He was a minister two years ago. He is now an ambassador.": "Ya kasance minista shekaru biyu da suka wuce. Yanzu jakada ne.", "The library is closed now. They say it was open until the Dhuhr adhan.": "Ɗakin karatu a rufe yake yanzu. Sun ce a buɗe yake har zuwa kiran sallar Azahar.", "laa yazaalu mareeḍan": "laa yazaalu mareeḍan", "he is still sick": "har yanzu bai da lafiya", "(still) is a sister of": "(har yanzu) 'yar'uwar", ": the second word takes": "ce: kalma ta biyu tana ɗaukar", "How is Ammar now, Sa'd? He was sick a week ago. He is still sick.": "Yaya Ammar yake yanzu, Sa'd? Ya yi rashin lafiya mako ɗaya da ya wuce. Har yanzu bai da lafiya.", "Is he retired now? No, he is still a dean.": "Ya yi ritaya yanzu? A'a, har yanzu shi shugaban tsangaya ne.", "Ibrahim is still asleep.": "Ibrahim har yanzu yana barci.", "Aminah is still asleep.": "Aminah har yanzu tana barci.", "your father came": "babanka ya zo", "abaaka": "abaaka", "I saw": "na ga", "abeeka": "abeeka", "I said to": "na ce wa", "(two of": "(biyu daga cikin", ") change before an ending or another noun:": ") suna canjawa kafin ƙari ko wani suna:", "as the doer,": "a matsayin mai aikatawa,", "as the object,": "a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki,", "after a preposition:": "bayan harafin jarri:", ". Same with": ". Haka ma", "doer: -uu": "mai aikatawa: -uu", "object: -aa": "wanda aka yi wa aiki: -aa", "after a preposition: -ee": "bayan harafin jarri: -ee", "What does your father do, Ibrahim?": "Me babanka yake yi, Ibrahim?", "Akhtar, I heard that your brother is a famous doctor.": "Akhtar, na ji cewa ɗan'uwanka shahararren likita ne.", "You told me that your father is the dean of the College of Engineering.": "Ka gaya mini cewa babanka shi ne shugaban Tsangayar Injiniyanci.", "Abbas, tell your brother who studies in the second year to come tomorrow.": "Abbas, ka gaya wa ɗan'uwanka da yake karatu a shekara ta biyu ya zo gobe.", "an ambassador": "jakada", "a policeman": "ɗan sanda", "a dean": "shugaban tsangaya", "retired": "mai ritaya", "a supervisor": "mai kulawa, sufabaiza", "New words: jobs and people": "Sababbin kalmomi: ayyuka da mutane", "safeerun (pl. sufaraa'u)": "safeerun (jam'i: sufaraa'u)", "shurṭiyyun (pl. shurṭatun)": "shurṭiyyun (jam'i: shurṭatun)", "'ameedun (pl. 'umadaa'u)": "'ameedun (jam'i: 'umadaa'u)", "mutaqaa'idun": "mutaqaa'idun", "sick, a patient": "mara lafiya", "he wrote (a book)": "ya wallafa (littafi)", "mareeḍun (pl. marḍaa)": "mareeḍun (jam'i: marḍaa)", "allafa (yu'allifu)": "allafa (yu'allifu)", "before, previously": "a da, kafin haka", "still": "har yanzu", "Where is Anwar, Umar? I don't know. I saw him a little while ago. He was standing outside the class.": "Ina Anwar, Umar? Ban sani ba. Na gan shi ɗan lokaci kaɗan da ya wuce. Yana tsaye a wajen aji.", "How is Ammar now, Sa'd? He was sick a week ago. He is still sick, honourable shaikh.": "Yaya Ammar yake yanzu, Sa'd? Ya yi rashin lafiya mako ɗaya da ya wuce. Har yanzu bai da lafiya, mai girma shehi.", "What does your father do, Ibrahim? I heard he is a minister. He was a minister two years ago. He is now an ambassador.": "Me babanka yake yi, Ibrahim? Na ji cewa minista ne. Ya kasance minista shekaru biyu da suka wuce. Yanzu jakada ne.", "And what does your father do, Amr? He was a teacher before, and he is now a supervisor in the secondary schools.": "Kai kuma me babanka yake yi, Amr? A da malami ne, yanzu kuma mai kula da makarantun sakandare ne.", "And what does your father do, Ya'qub? He was a policeman, and he is now retired.": "Kai kuma me babanka yake yi, Ya'qub? Ya kasance ɗan sanda, yanzu kuma ya yi ritaya.", "Abu Bakr, you told me your father is the dean of Engineering. Is he retired now? No, he is still a dean.": "Abubakar, ka gaya mini babanka shi ne shugaban tsangayar Injiniyanci. Ya yi ritaya yanzu? A'a, har yanzu shi shugaban tsangaya ne.", "The library is closed now, shaikh. They say it was open until the Dhuhr adhan.": "Ɗakin karatu a rufe yake yanzu, shehi. Sun ce a buɗe yake har zuwa kiran sallar Azahar.", "The second word takes -a.": "Kalma ta biyu tana ɗaukar -a.", "Add كَانَ:": "Ƙara كَانَ:", "for a feminine word.": "don kalma ta mace.", "Say “still”:": "Ka ce “har yanzu”:", "Doer -": "Mai aikatawa -", ", object -": ", wanda aka yi wa aiki -", ", after a preposition -": ", bayan harafin jarri -", "أَيْنَ ذَهَبَ …… يَا فَاطِمَةُ؟ (your father)": "أَيْنَ ذَهَبَ …… يَا فَاطِمَةُ؟ (babanki)", "object -": "wanda aka yi wa aiki -", "after a preposition -": "bayan harafin jarri -", "أَخَذْتُ أَلْفَ رِيَالٍ مِنْ …… (your brother)": "أَخَذْتُ أَلْفَ رِيَالٍ مِنْ …… (ɗan'uwanka)", "أَيْنَ …… يَا سَلْمَى؟ (your brother)": "أَيْنَ …… يَا سَلْمَى؟ (ɗan'uwanki)", "هٰذِهِ السَّيَّارَةُ لِـ…… (our father)": "هٰذِهِ السَّيَّارَةُ لِـ…… (babanmu)", "أَبْحَثُ عَنْ …… (your brother)": "أَبْحَثُ عَنْ …… (ɗan'uwanka)", "كَتَبْتُ رِسَالَةً إِلَى …… (your father)": "كَتَبْتُ رِسَالَةً إِلَى …… (babanka)", "أَنَا أَعْرِفُ …… يَا عُثْمَانُ. (your father)": "أَنَا أَعْرِفُ …… يَا عُثْمَانُ. (babanka)", "Hamid was sick yesterday.": "Hamid ya yi rashin lafiya jiya.", "Add لَا يَزَالُ": "Ƙara لَا يَزَالُ", "Listen, then write the word. (standing)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (a tsaye)", "✅ Hamid was sick yesterday.": "✅ Hamid ya yi rashin lafiya jiya.", "✅ Write: standing": "✅ Rubuta: a tsaye", "✅ He was standing outside the class.": "✅ Ya kasance a tsaye a wajen aji.", "In this lesson you will learn verbs that start with": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli da suke farawa da", "drops in the present,": "yana faɗuwa a mudari'i,", "he finds, and in the command,": "yana samu, da kuma a umarni,", "stop. You will also learn the small form of a noun,": "tsaya. Za ka kuma koyi ƙaramar siffar suna (tasgiri),", "little boy, comparing words like": "ƙaramin yaro, kalmomin kwatanci kamar", "less, and": "mafi ƙaranci, da", "dearer,": "mafi soyuwa,", "here it is, and": "ga shi nan, da", "it is a duty on.": "wajibi ne a kan.", "Verbs whose first letter is": "Fi'iloli da harafinsu na farko shi ne", "in the present:": "a mudari'i:", "Their command needs no alif, because it begins with a vowel:": "Umarninsu ba ya buƙatar alif, saboda yana farawa da wasali:", "stop.": "tsaya.", "weigh.": "auna.", "put. To a woman:": "ajiye. Ga mace:", "The small form of a noun is on the pattern": "Ƙaramar siffar suna tana kan wazanin", "a little boy.": "ƙaramin yaro.", "a little mountain.": "ƙaramin dutse.", "When the last two root letters are the same, the comparing word has a shadda:": "Idan haruffan asali biyu na ƙarshe iri ɗaya ne, kalmar kwatanci tana da shadda:", "To answer where is it:": "Don amsa ina yake:", "here it is.": "ga shi nan.", "here I am.": "ga ni nan.", "we must understand the Qur'an.": "wajibi ne mu fahimci Alƙur'ani.", "وَجَدَ ← يَجِدُ (he finds)": "وَجَدَ ← يَجِدُ (yana samu)", "قِفْ (stop!)": "قِفْ (tsaya!)", "Present": "Mudari'i", "Command": "Umarni", "Small form": "Ƙaramar siffa", "Here it is": "Ga shi nan", "In this lesson you will learn verbs that start with وَاوْ, like وَجَدَ. The وَاوْ drops in the present, يَجِدُ, he finds, and in the command, قِفْ, stop. You will also learn the small form of a noun, وُلَيْدٌ, little boy, comparing words like أَقَلُّ, less, and أَحَبُّ, dearer, هَا هُوَ ذَا, here it is, and يَجِبُ عَلَى, it is a duty on.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli da suke farawa da وَاوْ, kamar وَجَدَ. Harafin وَاوْ ɗin yana faɗuwa a mudari'i, يَجِدُ, yana samu, da kuma a umarni, قِفْ, tsaya. Za ka kuma koyi ƙaramar siffar suna, وُلَيْدٌ, ƙaramin yaro, kalmomin kwatanci kamar أَقَلُّ, mafi ƙaranci, da أَحَبُّ, mafi soyuwa, هَا هُوَ ذَا, ga shi nan, da يَجِبُ عَلَى, wajibi ne a kan.", "yajidu": "yajidu", "he finds": "yana samu", ". Most have a kasra in the middle;": ". Yawancinsu suna da kasra a tsakiya;", "have a fatha.": "suna da fataha.", "We want to buy this dictionary but we don't find it in the bookshops.": "Muna so mu sayi wannan ƙamus ɗin amma ba ma samunsa a shagunan littattafai.", "You will find it in the big bookshop in front of the mosque.": "Za ka same shi a babban shagon littattafai da yake gaban masallaci.", "When does he arrive here? The plane from Jeddah arrives at one o'clock.": "Yaushe zai iso nan? Jirgin sama daga Jidda yana isowa ƙarfe ɗaya.", "Why did you put it on the desk? You must put it in your pocket.": "Me ya sa ka ajiye shi a kan tebur? Wajibi ne ka sa shi a aljihunka.", "taqifu": "taqifu", "qif": "qif", "taḍa'u": "taḍa'u", "stop!": "tsaya!", "put!": "ajiye!", "Their command needs": "Umarninsu ba ya buƙatar", "no alif": "alif", "at the start, because it begins with a vowel:": "a farko, saboda yana farawa da wasali:", ". To a woman:": ". Ga mace:", "Stop, little boy. Where do you want to go?": "Tsaya, ƙaramin yaro. Ina kake so ka je?", "Take it and put it in your pocket.": "Karɓe shi ka sa shi a aljihunka.", "Stop here, driver. I want to get off.": "Tsaya nan, direba. Ina so in sauka.", "Weigh me a kilogram of sugar, grocer.": "Auna mini kilo ɗaya na sukari, mai shago.", "Salma, put this book on my desk.": "Salma, ajiye wannan littafin a kan teburina.", "wulaydun": "wulaydun", "a little boy": "ƙaramin yaro", "small form": "ƙaramar siffa", ") is on the pattern": ") yana kan wazanin", "a little mountain": "ƙaramin dutse", "a little river": "ƙaramin kogi", "a little dog": "ƙaramin kare", "qaleelun": "qaleelun", "few": "kaɗan", "aqallu": "aqallu", "fewer": "mafi ƙaranci", "ḥabeebun": "ḥabeebun", "dear": "masoyi", "aḥabbu": "aḥabbu", "dearer": "mafi soyuwa", "When the last two root letters are the": "Idan haruffan asali biyu na ƙarshe", "same": "iri ɗaya ne", ", the comparing word has a": ", kalmar kwatanci tana da", "shadda": "shadda", "Half an hour or less is left.": "Rabin awa ko ƙasa da haka ya rage.", "Oranges are tasty and apples are tastier.": "Lemu yana da daɗi, tuffa kuma ta fi daɗi.", "My father is dear to me, and my mother is dearer to me than him.": "Babana masoyina ne, kuma mahaifiyata ta fi shi soyuwa a gare ni.", "Who is the dearest person to you? The dearest to me is the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him.": "Wane ne mafi soyuwa a gare ka a cikin mutane? Mafi soyuwa a gare ni shi ne Manzon Allah, tsira da amincin Allah su tabbata a gare shi.", "haa huwa dhaa": "haa huwa dhaa", "here it is (m)": "ga shi nan (namiji)", "haa hiya dhee": "haa hiya dhee", "ha'anadhaa": "ha'anadhaa", "here I am": "ga ni nan", "To answer “where is it?”:": "Don amsa “ina yake?”:", "(here it is, m),": "(ga shi nan, namiji),", "(here I am).": "(ga ni nan).", "= it is a duty on:": "yana nufin wajibi ne a kan:", "is the verbal noun of": "masdarin", "Where is the book? Here it is.": "Ina littafin? Ga shi nan.", "Where is the watch? Here it is.": "Ina agogon? Ga shi nan.", "Where is Ibrahim? Here I am.": "Ina Ibrahim? Ga ni nan.", "We must understand the Noble Qur'an and act on it.": "Wajibi ne mu fahimci Alƙur'ani Mai girma mu yi aiki da shi.", "Please allow me to go to the hospital.": "Don Allah ka ba ni izini in tafi asibiti.", "a wallet": "walat, jakar kuɗi", "money": "kuɗi", "a ticket": "tikiti", "a tablet, a pill": "ƙwaya, kwayar magani", "a kilogram": "kilogram", "a mistake": "kuskure", "miḥfaẓatun": "miḥfaẓatun", "nuquudun (sg. naqdun)": "nuquudun (ɗaya: naqdun)", "tadhkiratun (pl. tadhaakiru)": "tadhkiratun (jam'i: tadhaakiru)", "qurṣun (pl. aqraaṣun)": "qurṣun (jam'i: aqraaṣun)", "keeluu ghiraamun": "keeluu ghiraamun", "khaṭa'un (pl. akhṭaa'un)": "khaṭa'un (jam'i: akhṭaa'un)", "foreign": "baƙo, na ƙasar waje", "a male": "namiji", "a female": "mace", "regularly": "a kai a kai", "ajnabiyyun": "ajnabiyyun", "dhakarun (pl. dhukuurun)": "dhakarun (jam'i: dhukuurun)", "unthaa (pl. inaathun)": "unthaa (jam'i: inaathun)", "bintiẓaamin": "bintiẓaamin", "he arrived": "ya iso", "he stood, stopped": "ya tsaya", "he weighed": "ya auna", "he promised": "ya yi alƙawari", "he swallowed": "ya haɗiye", "waṣala (yaṣilu)": "waṣala (yaṣilu)", "waqafa (yaqifu)": "waqafa (yaqifu)", "wazana (yazinu)": "wazana (yazinu)", "wa'ada (ya'idu)": "wa'ada (ya'idu)", "bala'a (yabla'u)": "bala'a (yabla'u)", "going": "tafiya", "returning": "dawowa", "it is a duty, must": "wajibi ne, dole ne", "Honourable shaikh, we want to buy this dictionary you have, but we don't find it in the bookshops.": "Mai girma shehi, muna so mu sayi wannan ƙamus ɗin da kake da shi, amma ba ma samunsa a shagunan littattafai.", "You will find it in the big bookshop in front of the mosque. You will find Arabic and foreign dictionaries there.": "Za ka same shi a babban shagon littattafai da yake gaban masallaci. Za ka sami ƙamusai na Larabci da na harsunan waje a can.", "Honourable shaikh, I can't find my wallet. Is there much money in it? Yes, three hundred riyals.": "Mai girma shehi, ban sami walat ɗina ba. Akwai kuɗi da yawa a cikinsa? Ee, riyal ɗari uku.", "Why did you put it on the desk? This is a big mistake. You must put it in your pocket.": "Me ya sa ka ajiye shi a kan tebur? Wannan babban kuskure ne. Wajibi ne ka sa shi a aljihunka.", "Here it is, teacher. It is under his chair. Take it and put it in your pocket.": "Ga shi nan, malam. Yana ƙarƙashin kujerarsa. Karɓe shi ka sa shi a aljihunka.", "Stop, little boy. Where do you want to go? Please let me go, because my father comes to Madinah today.": "Tsaya, ƙaramin yaro. Ina kake so ka je? Don Allah ka bar ni in tafi, saboda babana zai zo Madina yau.", "When does he arrive? The plane from Jeddah arrives at one. Go quickly. Half an hour or less is left.": "Yaushe zai iso? Jirgin sama daga Jidda yana isowa ƙarfe ɗaya. Tafi da sauri. Rabin awa ko ƙasa da haka ya rage.", "- verbs": "- fi'iloli", "drops.": "yana faɗuwa.", "No alif at the start.": "Babu alif a farko.", "Command:": "Umarni:", "Small form:": "Ƙaramar siffa:", "Same two last letters: use": "Haruffa biyu na ƙarshe iri ɗaya: yi amfani da", "Same two last letters → shadda.": "Haruffa biyu na ƙarshe iri ɗaya → shadda.", "Answer where is it?": "Amsa ina yake?", "Answer “where is it?”": "Amsa “ina yake?”", "Answer: here it is.": "Amsa: ga shi nan.", "You are Ibrahim. Answer:": "Kai ne Ibrahim. Ka amsa:", "I can't find my wallet.": "Ban sami walat ɗina ba.", "The present of وَ- verbs": "Mudari'in fi'iloli masu farawa da وَ-", "Stop here, driver.": "Tsaya nan, direba.", "The plane arrives at one o'clock.": "Jirgin sama yana isowa ƙarfe ɗaya.", "Listen, then write the word. (money)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (kuɗi)", "✅ Answer: here it is.": "✅ Amsa: ga shi nan.", "✅ Stop here, driver.": "✅ Tsaya nan, direba.", "✅ The plane arrives at one o'clock.": "✅ Jirgin sama yana isowa ƙarfe ɗaya.", "✅ Write: money": "✅ Rubuta: kuɗi", "In this lesson you will learn hollow verbs, whose middle letter is long, like": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli masu harafin tsakiya mai rauni (ajwaf), waɗanda harafinsu na tsakiya dogo ne, kamar", "he said,": "ya ce,", "he sold, and": "ya sayar, da", "he slept. With an ending the long letter becomes short:": "ya yi barci. Idan aka ƙara ƙarshe, dogon harafin yana zama gajere:", "It also becomes short after": "Yana kuma zama gajere bayan", "in the command, and after": "a umarni, da bayan", "that forbids:": "ta hani:", "Hollow verbs have a long vowel in the middle. In the present it can be": "Fi'iloli ajwaf suna da dogon wasali a tsakiya. A mudari'i yana iya zama", "Or": "Ko", "In the past, with an ending like -": "A shuɗaɗɗen lokaci, tare da ƙarshe kamar -", "the long vowel becomes short.": "dogon wasalin yana zama gajere.", "But": "Amma", "stay long.": "suna zama dogaye.", "When the last letter gets a sukun, the long vowel becomes short.": "Idan harafin ƙarshe ya sami sukun, dogon wasalin yana zama gajere.", "he did not say.": "bai ce ba.", "say.": "ka ce.", "don't say.": "kada ka ce.", "Past": "Shuɗaɗɗen lokaci", "Shortened": "Gajartacce", "In this lesson you will learn hollow verbs, whose middle letter is long, like قَالَ, he said, بَاعَ, he sold, and نَامَ, he slept. With an ending the long letter becomes short: قُلْتُ, بِعْتُ, نِمْتُ. It also becomes short after لَمْ, in the command, and after لَا that forbids: لَمْ يَقُلْ, قُلْ, لَا تَقُلْ.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli ajwaf, waɗanda harafinsu na tsakiya dogo ne, kamar قَالَ, ya ce, بَاعَ, ya sayar, da نَامَ, ya yi barci. Idan aka ƙara ƙarshe, dogon harafin yana zama gajere: قُلْتُ, بِعْتُ, نِمْتُ. Yana kuma zama gajere bayan لَمْ, a umarni, da bayan لَا ta hani: لَمْ يَقُلْ, قُلْ, لَا تَقُلْ.", "qaala yaquulu": "qaala yaquulu", "baa'a yabee'u": "baa'a yabee'u", "sell": "sayar", "naama yanaamu": "naama yanaamu", "sleep": "yi barci", "Hollow verbs": "Fi'iloli ajwaf", ") have a long vowel in the middle. In the present it is": ") suna da dogon wasali a tsakiya. A mudari'i yana zama", "Hamid says, the students say, Aminah says.": "Hamid yana cewa, ɗalibai suna cewa, Aminah tana cewa.", "I visit you and you don't visit me.": "Ina ziyartar ka, kai kuma ba ka ziyarta ta.", "The pilgrims go around the Ka'bah.": "Mahajjata suna ɗawafi a kewayen Ka'aba.", "I want to be a teacher.": "Ina so in zama malami.", "qultu": "qultu", "bi'tu": "bi'tu", "nimtu": "nimtu", "I said": "na ce", "I sold": "na sayar", "I slept": "na yi barci", "In the past, when a": "A shuɗaɗɗen lokaci, idan aka ƙara ƙarshen", "ending is added, the long vowel becomes": ", dogon wasalin yana zama", "-verbs take": "-fi'iloli suna ɗaukar", "-verbs and": "-fi'iloli da", "be": "su zama", "lam yaqul": "lam yaqul", "qul": "qul", "laa taqul": "laa taqul", "he did not say": "bai ce ba", "say!": "ka ce!", "don't say!": "kada ka ce!", "When the last letter gets a": "Idan harafin ƙarshe ya sami", "(after": "(bayan", ", in the command, after": ", a umarni, bayan", "that forbids), the long vowel becomes": "ta hani), dogon wasalin yana zama", ", because two sukuns cannot meet:": ", saboda sukun biyu ba sa haɗuwa:", "No one told me that you were sick.": "Babu wanda ya gaya mini cewa ba ka da lafiya.", "Why didn't you sleep? I had a bad headache, so I could not sleep because of it.": "Me ya sa ba ka yi barci ba? Na yi ciwon kai mai tsanani, don haka ban iya barci ba saboda shi.", "Get up, Adam. Are you sleeping in class?": "Tashi, Adam. Kana barci a aji?", "Visit me tomorrow, for I am busy today.": "Ka ziyarce ni gobe, saboda yau ina da aiki.", "Don't say that. Don't be lazy, boy.": "Kada ka faɗi haka. Kada ka zama malalaci, yaro.", "a headache": "ciwon kai", "ṣudaa'un": "ṣudaa'un", "salt": "gishiri", "oil": "mai", "cheese": "cuku", "eggs": "ƙwai", "flour": "fulawa", "lentils": "wake (adas)", "lunch": "abincin rana", "New words: food": "Sababbin kalmomi: abinci", "al-milḥu": "al-milḥu", "az-zaytu": "az-zaytu", "al-jubnu": "al-jubnu", "bayḍun (sg. bayḍatun)": "bayḍun (ɗaya: bayḍatun)", "ad-daqeequ": "ad-daqeequ", "al-'adasu": "al-'adasu", "al-ghadaa'u": "al-ghadaa'u", "the train": "jirgin ƙasa", "the forest": "daji", "busy": "mai aiki, ba shi da hutu", "complete, full": "cikakke", "al-qiṭaaru": "al-qiṭaaru", "al-ghaabatu": "al-ghaabatu", "mashghuulun": "mashghuulun", "kaamilun": "kaamilun", "he stood up": "ya tashi tsaye", "he sold": "ya sayar", "he slept": "ya yi barci", "he fasted": "ya yi azumi", "he feared": "ya ji tsoro", "qaama (yaquumu)": "qaama (yaquumu)", "baa'a (yabee'u)": "baa'a (yabee'u)", "naama (yanaamu)": "naama (yanaamu)", "ṣaama (yaṣuumu)": "ṣaama (yaṣuumu)", "khaafa (yakhaafu)": "khaafa (yakhaafu)", "one should": "ya kamata", "where (that)": "inda", "When did you come from Jeddah, Khalid? Yesterday. Did Ibrahim come with you? Not yet. He will come today or tomorrow, in sha Allah.": "Yaushe ka zo daga Jidda, Khalid? Jiya. Ibrahim ya zo tare da kai? Tukuna. Zai zo yau ko gobe, in sha Allah.", "Did you visit the ambassador? I went to his office and did not find him. I heard he was not in Jeddah that day.": "Ka ziyarci jakadan? Na je ofishinsa ban same shi ba. Na ji cewa ba ya Jidda a ranar.", "Adnan, you were absent two weeks. Where were you? In hospital. I was very sick. By Allah, I almost died.": "Adnan, ka yi makonni biyu ba ka zo ba. Ina ka kasance? A asibiti. Na yi rashin lafiya sosai. Wallahi, na kusa mutuwa.", "By Allah, I did not know. No one told me you were sick. Praise Allah. I am better now, but I am still weak.": "Wallahi, ban sani ba. Babu wanda ya gaya mini cewa ba ka da lafiya. Alhamdu lillah. Na ji sauƙi yanzu, amma har yanzu ina da rauni.", "A student should not be absent a lot. I wasn't absent three days, only one day. Don't lie, brother.": "Bai kamata ɗalibi ya riƙa fashi da yawa ba. Ban yi fashin kwana uku ba, kwana ɗaya kawai. Kada ka yi ƙarya, ɗan'uwa.", "Get up, Adam. Are you sleeping in class? Sorry, teacher. Sleep overcame me because I did not sleep last night.": "Tashi, Adam. Kana barci a aji? Ka yi haƙuri, malam. Barci ya rinjaye ni saboda ban yi barci a daren jiya ba.", "Why didn't you sleep? I had a bad headache. Teacher, I want to visit you today. Visit me tomorrow, I'm busy today.": "Me ya sa ba ka yi barci ba? Na yi ciwon kai mai tsanani. Malam, ina so in ziyarce ka yau. Ka ziyarce ni gobe, yau ina da aiki.", "The present of hollow verbs": "Mudari'in fi'iloli ajwaf", "in the middle.": "a tsakiya.", "With -": "Tare da -", "With a sukun at the end, the long vowel drops.": "Idan akwai sukun a ƙarshe, dogon wasalin yana faɗuwa.", "at the end, the long vowel drops.": "a ƙarshe, dogon wasalin yana faɗuwa.", "command: تَزُورُ": "umarni: تَزُورُ", "command: تَقُولُ": "umarni: تَقُولُ", "command: تَنَامُ": "umarni: تَنَامُ", "Commands and don'ts.": "Umarni da hani.", "“Don't be afraid.”": "“Kada ka ji tsoro.”", "“Visit me tomorrow.”": "“Ka ziyarce ni gobe.”", "“Fast tomorrow.”": "“Ka yi azumi gobe.”", "“Get up from here.”": "“Ka tashi daga nan.”", "Because I did not sleep last night.": "Saboda ban yi barci a daren jiya ba.", "Listen, then write the word. (he slept)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (ya yi barci)", "“Don't sleep in class.”": "“Kada ka yi barci a aji.”", "“Say to him.”": "“Ka ce masa.”", "Don't be afraid.": "Kada ka ji tsoro.", "✅ “Visit me tomorrow.”": "✅ “Ka ziyarce ni gobe.”", "✅ “Fast tomorrow.”": "✅ “Ka yi azumi gobe.”", "✅ Write: he slept": "✅ Rubuta: ya yi barci", "✅ “Don't sleep in class.”": "✅ “Kada ka yi barci a aji.”", "✅ “Say to him.”": "✅ “Ka ce masa.”", "✅ Because I did not sleep last night.": "✅ Saboda ban yi barci a daren jiya ba.", "✅ Don't be afraid.": "✅ Kada ka ji tsoro.", "In this lesson you will learn verbs whose last letter is a vowel, like": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli da harafinsu na ƙarshe wasali ne (naqis), kamar", "he walked,": "ya yi tafiya,", "he called, and": "ya kira, da", "he forgot. Their present is": "ya manta. Mudari'insu shi ne", "in the command and after": "a umarni da bayan", "that forbids, the last vowel drops:": "ta hani, wasalin ƙarshe yana faɗuwa:", "Verbs whose last letter is weak end in a long vowel in the present.": "Fi'iloli masu harafin ƙarshe mai rauni suna ƙarewa da dogon wasali a mudari'i.", "In the past with -": "A shuɗaɗɗen lokaci tare da -", "the last letter becomes": "harafin ƙarshe yana zama", "For she:": "Ga “ita”:", "For they:": "Ga “su”:", "that forbids, the last long vowel drops.": "ta hani, dogon wasalin ƙarshe yana faɗuwa.", "The vowel drops": "Wasalin yana faɗuwa", "In this lesson you will learn verbs whose last letter is a vowel, like مَشَى, he walked, دَعَا, he called, and نَسِيَ, he forgot. Their present is يَمْشِي, يَدْعُو and يَنْسَى. After لَمْ, in the command and after لَا that forbids, the last vowel drops: لَمْ يَمْشِ, اُدْعُ, لَا تَنْسَ.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli da harafinsu na ƙarshe wasali ne, kamar مَشَى, ya yi tafiya, دَعَا, ya kira, da نَسِيَ, ya manta. Mudari'insu shi ne يَمْشِي, يَدْعُو da يَنْسَى. Bayan لَمْ, a umarni da bayan لَا ta hani, wasalin ƙarshe yana faɗuwa: لَمْ يَمْشِ, اُدْعُ, لَا تَنْسَ.", "mashaa yamshee": "mashaa yamshee", "walk": "yi tafiya", "da'aa yad'uu": "da'aa yad'uu", "call": "kira", "nasiya yansaa": "nasiya yansaa", "forget": "manta", "Verbs whose": "Fi'iloli da", "last letter is weak": "harafinsu na ƙarshe mai rauni ne", ") end in a long vowel in the present:": ") suna ƙarewa da dogon wasali a mudari'i:", "), or": "), ko", "-ee: يَجْرِي، يَرْمِي، يَبْكِي": "-ee: يَجْرِي، يَرْمِي، يَبْكِي", "-uu: يَشْكُو، يَتْلُو": "-uu: يَشْكُو، يَتْلُو", "-aa: يَخْشَى، يَبْقَى": "-aa: يَخْشَى، يَبْقَى", "Muhammad is running on the stairs. I fear he will fall.": "Muhammad yana gudu a kan matakala. Ina tsoron kada ya faɗi.", "Why is the baby crying, Aminah?": "Me ya sa jaririn yake kuka, Aminah?", "We pray to Allah to cure you.": "Muna roƙon Allah Ya ba ka lafiya.", "I forget a lot.": "Ina yawan mantuwa.", "kawaytu": "kawaytu", "da'awtu": "da'awtu", "naseetu": "naseetu", "I ironed": "na yi guga", "I invited": "na gayyata", "I forgot": "na manta", "In the past with": "A shuɗaɗɗen lokaci tare da", ", the": ",", ". For “she”:": ". Ga “ita”:", "(the alif drops). For “they”:": "(alif ɗin yana faɗuwa). Ga “su”:", "invite": "gayyata", "lam yamshi": "lam yamshi", "imshi": "imshi", "laa tamshi": "laa tamshi", "he did not walk": "bai yi tafiya ba", "walk!": "yi tafiya!", "don't walk!": "kada ka yi tafiya!", ", in the": ", a", "command": "umarni", ", and after": ", da bayan", "that forbids, the": "ta hani,", "last long vowel drops": "dogon wasalin ƙarshe yana faɗuwa", ". With -": ". Tare da -", "and -": "da -", "I have not ironed it yet. I will iron it now, in sha Allah.": "Har yanzu ban yi masa guga ba. Zan yi masa guga yanzu, in sha Allah.", "Don't run, Muhammad. Come here.": "Kada ka yi gudu, Muhammad. Zo nan.", "Invite them to have dinner the day after tomorrow.": "Ka gayyace su su ci abincin dare jibi.", "Don't forget what I told you.": "Kada ka manta da abin da na gaya maka.", "Don't walk in the sun.": "Kada ka yi tafiya a rana.", "the right hand": "hannun dama", "the left hand": "hannun hagu", "rubbish": "shara", "dust, earth": "ƙura, ƙasa", "a companion": "abokin tafiya, aboki", "the night": "dare", "the daytime": "rana (lokacin hasken rana)", "a gift": "kyauta", "torn": "yayyage", "al-yameenu": "al-yameenu", "al-yasaaru": "al-yasaaru", "qumaamatun": "qumaamatun", "turaabun": "turaabun", "ṣaaḥibun (pl. aṣḥaabun)": "ṣaaḥibun (jam'i: aṣḥaabun)", "al-laylu": "al-laylu", "an-nahaaru": "an-nahaaru", "hadiyyatun": "hadiyyatun", "mumazzaqun": "mumazzaqun", "he ran": "ya yi gudu", "he threw": "ya jefa", "he built": "ya gina", "he called, invited": "ya kira, ya gayyata", "he complained": "ya yi ƙorafi", "he recited": "ya karanta", "he forgot": "ya manta", "mashaa (yamshee)": "mashaa (yamshee)", "jaraa (yajree)": "jaraa (yajree)", "ramaa (yarmee)": "ramaa (yarmee)", "banaa (yabnee)": "banaa (yabnee)", "da'aa (yad'uu)": "da'aa (yad'uu)", "shakaa (yashkuu)": "shakaa (yashkuu)", "talaa (yatluu)": "talaa (yatluu)", "nasiya (yansaa)": "nasiya (yansaa)", "khashiya (yakhshaa)": "khashiya (yakhshaa)", "show me": "nuna mini", "come here!": "zo nan!", "What are you doing, my daughter? I am ironing the clothes we washed yesterday.": "Me kike yi, 'yata? Ina guga tufafin da muka wanke jiya.", "Did you iron the white shirt? Yes. And the green shirt? Not yet. I will iron it now, in sha Allah.": "Kin yi wa farar rigar guga? Ee. Koriyar riga fa? Tukuna. Zan yi mata guga yanzu, in sha Allah.", "Yes, my classmate Salwa invited me to her house this evening. Go, and come back after Maghrib.": "Ee, abokiyar ajina Salwa ta gayyace ni gidansu a yammacin yau. Ki tafi, ki dawo bayan Magriba.", "Abu Muhammad, come here and look. Muhammad is running on the stairs. I fear he will fall.": "Baban Muhammad, zo nan ka gani. Muhammad yana gudu a kan matakala. Ina tsoron kada ya faɗi.", "Don't run, Muhammad. Come here. What is this in your right hand? Show me. Throw it away. This is dirt.": "Kada ka yi gudu, Muhammad. Zo nan. Mene ne wannan a hannunka na dama? Nuna mini. Jefar da shi. Wannan datti ne.", "Today I complained about a classmate to the principal. Why? Because he always takes my books and notebooks and folds their pages.": "Yau na kai ƙarar wani abokin ajina wurin shugaban makaranta. Me ya sa? Saboda kullum yana ɗaukar littattafaina da littattafan rubutuna yana ninke shafukansu.", "I bought them because I want to invite three classmates home tomorrow. Invite them to dinner the day after tomorrow.": "Na saye su ne saboda ina so in gayyaci abokan ajina uku gida gobe. Ka gayyace su cin abincin dare jibi.", "The present of these verbs": "Mudari'in waɗannan fi'iloli", "at the end.": "a ƙarshe.", "Choose the right past form.": "Zaɓi siffar shuɗaɗɗen lokaci daidai.", "The last long vowel drops.": "Dogon wasalin ƙarshe yana faɗuwa.", "command: تَمْشِي": "umarni: تَمْشِي", "command: تَدْعُو": "umarni: تَدْعُو", "“Invite them to dinner.”": "“Ka gayyace su cin abincin dare.”", "“Don't forget what I told you.”": "“Kada ka manta da abin da na gaya maka.”", "“Recite Surat ar-Rahman.”": "“Karanta Suratul Rahman.”", "“Don't run, Muhammad.”": "“Kada ka yi gudu, Muhammad.”", "“Give me cold water to drink.”": "“Ba ni ruwa mai sanyi in sha.”", "Don't run, Muhammad.": "Kada ka yi gudu, Muhammad.", "“Don't throw the rubbish in the street.”": "“Kada ka jefa shara a titi.”", "Why is the baby crying?": "Me ya sa jaririn yake kuka?", "Listen, then write the word. (the night)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (dare)", "✅ “Give me cold water to drink.”": "✅ “Ba ni ruwa mai sanyi in sha.”", "✅ “Don't forget what I told you.”": "✅ “Kada ka manta da abin da na gaya maka.”", "✅ Don't run, Muhammad.": "✅ Kada ka yi gudu, Muhammad.", "✅ “Don't throw the rubbish in the street.”": "✅ “Kada ka jefa shara a titi.”", "✅ Why is the baby crying?": "✅ Me ya sa jaririn yake kuka?", "✅ Write: the night": "✅ Rubuta: dare", "In this lesson you will learn doubled verbs, whose last two letters are the same, like": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli masu harafi biyu iri ɗaya a ƙarshe (mudha'af), kamar", "he made Hajj. With an ending the two letters separate:": "ya yi Hajji. Idan aka ƙara ƙarshe haruffan biyu suna rabuwa:", "I made Hajj. After": "na yi Hajji. Bayan", "and in the command they stay together with": "da kuma a umarni suna zama a haɗe tare da", "never in the past, and": "taɓa a shuɗaɗɗen lokaci, da", "never in the future.": "har abada a nan gaba.", "Doubled verbs have the same last two letters, joined with a shadda:": "Fi'iloli mudha'af suna da haruffa biyu iri ɗaya a ƙarshe, a haɗe da shadda:", "With an ending like -": "Tare da ƙarshe kamar -", "the two letters separate:": "haruffan biyu suna rabuwa:", "I made Hajj.": "Na yi Hajji.", "I counted.": "Na ƙirga.", "that forbids, the doubled letter stays joined and takes": "ta hani, harafin da aka ninka yana zama a haɗe kuma yana ɗaukar", "pull.": "ja.", "give back.": "mayar.", "don't think.": "kada ka zaci.", "is for the past:": "na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci ne:", "is for the future:": "na nan gaba ne:", "حَجَّ يَحُجُّ (doubled verbs)": "حَجَّ يَحُجُّ (fi'iloli mudha'af)", "Joined, with -a": "A haɗe, tare da -a", "قَطُّ or أَبَدًا": "قَطُّ ko أَبَدًا", "In this lesson you will learn doubled verbs, whose last two letters are the same, like حَجَّ, he made Hajj. With an ending the two letters separate: حَجَجْتُ, I made Hajj. After لَمْ and in the command they stay together with فَتْحَةْ: لَمْ يَحُجَّ, جُرَّ. You will also learn قَطُّ, never in the past, and أَبَدًا, never in the future.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'iloli mudha'af, waɗanda haruffansu biyu na ƙarshe iri ɗaya ne, kamar حَجَّ, ya yi Hajji. Idan aka ƙara ƙarshe haruffan biyu suna rabuwa: حَجَجْتُ, na yi Hajji. Bayan لَمْ da kuma a umarni suna zama a haɗe tare da فَتْحَةْ: لَمْ يَحُجَّ, جُرَّ. Za ka kuma koyi قَطُّ, ban taɓa ba a shuɗaɗɗen lokaci, da أَبَدًا, har abada a nan gaba.", "ḥajja yaḥujju": "ḥajja yaḥujju", "ḥajajtu": "ḥajajtu", "he made Hajj": "ya yi Hajji", "he makes Hajj": "yana yin Hajji", "I made Hajj": "na yi Hajji", "Doubled verbs": "Fi'iloli mudha'af", ") have the same last two letters, joined with a shadda:": ") suna da haruffa biyu iri ɗaya a ƙarshe, a haɗe da shadda:", "). With an ending like": "). Tare da ƙarshe kamar", "the two letters": "haruffan biyu", "separate": "suna rabuwa", "stay joined.": "suna zama a haɗe.", "joined": "a haɗe", "separated before -تُ, -نَا, -نَ": "a rabe kafin -تُ, -نَا, -نَ", "Did you make Hajj, Mas'ud? No, teacher. All my classmates made Hajj but I did not.": "Ka yi Hajji, Mas'ud? A'a, malam. Duk abokan ajina sun yi Hajji amma ni ban yi ba.", "My brother made Hajj three years ago, and I made Hajj this year.": "Ɗan'uwana ya yi Hajji shekaru uku da suka wuce, ni kuma na yi Hajji a bana.", "Take these copies and count them. Did you count them? Yes. They are twenty-five copies.": "Karɓi waɗannan kwafe-kwafen ka ƙirga su. Ka ƙirga su? Ee. Kwafi ashirin da biyar ne.", "Don't you smell a bad smell, brothers? Yes, we smell it.": "Ba ku jin wani mugun wari, 'yan'uwa? Ee, muna jin sa.", "lam yaḥujja": "lam yaḥujja", "jurra": "jurra", "laa tajurra": "laa tajurra", "he did not make Hajj": "bai yi Hajji ba", "pull!": "ja!", "don't pull!": "kada ka ja!", "that forbids, the doubled letter stays": "ta hani, harafin da aka ninka yana zama", "and takes a": "kuma yana ɗaukar", "(two sukuns cannot meet):": "(sukun biyu ba sa haɗuwa):", "Did you make Hajj, teacher? Not this year. But I made Hajj five times before.": "Ka yi Hajji, malam? Ba a bana ba. Amma na yi Hajji sau biyar a da.", "Come, Sa'id, and pull it forward.": "Zo, Sa'id, ka jawo shi gaba.", "Don't think I am unaware of what you are doing. Put it back in the bag.": "Kada ka zaci ban san abin da kake yi ba. Mayar da shi cikin jakar.", "Pour the coffee for the guests.": "Zuba wa baƙi kofi.", "Don't be sad. You will make Hajj next year, in sha Allah.": "Kada ka yi baƙin ciki. Za ka yi Hajji a baɗi, in sha Allah.", "qaṭṭu": "qaṭṭu", "never (past)": "ban taɓa ba (shuɗaɗɗen lokaci)", "abadan": "abadan", "never (future)": "har abada (nan gaba)", "is for the": "na", "(softer) and": "(mafi taushi) da", "(better-smelling).": "(mafi ƙamshi).", "I have never eaten food as tasty as this.": "Ban taɓa cin abinci mai daɗi kamar wannan ba.", "I have never left the prayer and I never will.": "Ban taɓa barin sallah ba, kuma ba zan bar ta ba har abada.", "I am sorry, teacher. I will never do it again, in sha Allah.": "Ka yi haƙuri, malam. Ba zan sake yin haka ba har abada, in sha Allah.", "I never touched brocade or silk softer than the palm of the Messenger of Allah, peace be upon him.": "Ban taɓa shafar alharini ko siliki da ya fi tafin hannun Manzon Allah taushi ba, tsira da amincin Allah su tabbata a gare shi.", "a smell": "wari, ƙamshi", "bad, nasty": "mummuna, mai ƙyama", "good, pleasant": "mai kyau, mai daɗi", "soft": "mai taushi", "a palm (of the hand)": "tafin hannu", "brocade (a kind of silk)": "alharini (irin siliki)", "a copy": "kwafi", "more": "ƙari", "a drain": "magudanar ruwa", "unaware, careless": "mai rafkanwa, gafali", "raa'iḥatun": "raa'iḥatun", "kareehun": "kareehun", "ṭayyibun": "ṭayyibun", "layyinun": "layyinun", "kaffun (pl. akuffun)": "kaffun (jam'i: akuffun)", "ad-deebaaju": "ad-deebaaju", "nuskhatun (pl. nusakhun)": "nuskhatun (jam'i: nusakhun)", "mazeedun": "mazeedun", "baaluu'atun": "baaluu'atun", "ghaafilun": "ghaafilun", "he counted": "ya ƙirga", "he pulled": "ya ja", "he smelled": "ya ji ƙamshi", "he returned (something)": "ya mayar (da wani abu)", "he poured": "ya zuba", "he passed by": "ya wuce ta", "he pushed": "ya tura", "he was sad": "ya yi baƙin ciki", "ḥajja (yaḥujju)": "ḥajja (yaḥujju)", "'adda (ya'uddu)": "'adda (ya'uddu)", "jarra (yajurru)": "jarra (yajurru)", "shamma (yashammu)": "shamma (yashammu)", "radda (yaruddu)": "radda (yaruddu)", "ṣabba (yaṣubbu)": "ṣabba (yaṣubbu)", "marra (yamurru)": "marra (yamurru)", "dafa'a (yadfa'u)": "dafa'a (yadfa'u)", "ḥazina (yaḥzanu)": "ḥazina (yaḥzanu)", "a time, once": "sau ɗaya, lokaci", "never (in the past)": "ban taɓa ba (a shuɗaɗɗen lokaci)", "Did you make Hajj, Mas'ud? No, teacher. All my classmates did, but I did not. I was sick during the days of Hajj.": "Ka yi Hajji, Mas'ud? A'a, malam. Duk abokan ajina sun yi, amma ni ban yi ba. Ina rashin lafiya a lokacin kwanakin Hajji.", "Don't be sad. You will make Hajj next year, in sha Allah. The year passes quickly.": "Kada ka yi baƙin ciki. Za ka yi Hajji a baɗi, in sha Allah. Shekara tana wucewa da sauri.", "I smell a bad smell. Don't you smell it, brothers? Yes. I think it is from the bathroom.": "Ina jin mugun wari. Ba ku jin sa, 'yan'uwa? Ee. Ina tsammani daga banɗaki yake.", "Yes, it is from the bathroom. The rubbish someone threw blocked the drain.": "Ee, daga banɗaki yake. Sharar da wani ya jefa ta toshe magudanar ruwa.", "Who pushed the board back? Come, Sa'id, and pull it forward. Enough. Leave it now.": "Wa ya tura allon baya? Zo, Sa'id, ka jawo shi gaba. Ya isa. Bar shi yanzu.", "Ali, don't think I don't see what you're doing. You're writing a letter. Put it back in the bag. Sorry. I will never do it again, in sha Allah.": "Ali, kada ka zaci ban ga abin da kake yi ba. Kana rubuta wasiƙa. Mayar da ita cikin jakar. Ka yi haƙuri. Ba zan sake yin haka ba har abada, in sha Allah.", "Before -": "Kafin -", "the two letters separate.": "haruffan biyu suna rabuwa.", "Choose the present.": "Zaɓi mudari'i.", "The present of doubled verbs": "Mudari'in fi'iloli mudha'af", "The doubled letter stays joined, with a": "Harafin da aka ninka yana zama a haɗe, tare da", "The doubled letter stays joined, with a fatha.": "Harafin da aka ninka yana zama a haɗe, tare da fataha.", "command: تَجُرُّ": "umarni: تَجُرُّ", "command: تَعُدُّ": "umarni: تَعُدُّ", "command: تَصُبُّ": "umarni: تَصُبُّ", ": past.": ": shuɗaɗɗen lokaci.", ": future.": ": nan gaba.", "“I have never gone to India.”": "“Ban taɓa zuwa Indiya ba.”", "past.": "shuɗaɗɗen lokaci.", "future.": "nan gaba.", "“I have never done this.”": "“Ban taɓa yin wannan ba.”", "“I have never heard such words.”": "“Ban taɓa jin irin waɗannan maganganu ba.”", "“I will never leave the prayer.”": "“Ba zan bar sallah ba har abada.”", "Don't think that I am unaware.": "Kada ka zaci ni gafali ne.", "command: تَرُدُّ": "umarni: تَرُدُّ", "قَطُّ or أَبَدًا?": "قَطُّ ko أَبَدًا?", "I will never do it again.": "Ba zan sake yin haka ba har abada.", "Listen, then write the word. (a time, once)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (sau ɗaya)", "✅ Don't think that I am unaware.": "✅ Kada ka zaci ni gafali ne.", "✅ “I have never gone to India.”": "✅ “Ban taɓa zuwa Indiya ba.”", "✅ I will never do it again.": "✅ Ba zan sake yin haka ba har abada.", "✅ Write: a time, once": "✅ Rubuta: sau ɗaya", "✅ “I will never leave the prayer.”": "✅ “Ba zan bar sallah ba har abada.”", "In this lesson you will talk to and about two people. The pronouns are": "A wannan darasin za ka yi magana da mutum biyu da kuma game da mutum biyu (tasniya). Wakilan sunan su ne", "you two, and": "ku biyu, da", "they two. The past verb is": "su biyu. Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci shi ne", "for two men,": "ga maza biyu,", "for two women and": "ga mata biyu da", "for you two. The present is": "ga ku biyu. Mudari'i shi ne", "and the command is": "kuma umarni shi ne", "For two people, men or women:": "Ga mutum biyu, maza ko mata:", "you two.": "ku biyu.", "they two. The endings are": "su biyu. Ƙarshen su ne", "The past verb for two:": "Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci ga mutum biyu:", "for two men.": "ga maza biyu.", "for two women.": "ga mata biyu.", "for you two.": "ga ku biyu.", "The present for two:": "Mudari'i ga mutum biyu:", "drops:": "yana faɗuwa:", "The command:": "Umarni:", "two people: ذَهَبَا": "mutum biyu: ذَهَبَا", "Past for two": "Shuɗaɗɗen lokaci ga mutum biyu", "Present for two": "Mudari'i ga mutum biyu", "Command for two": "Umarni ga mutum biyu", "You two": "Ku biyu", "In this lesson you will talk to and about two people. The pronouns are أَنْتُمَا, you two, and هُمَا, they two. The past verb is ذَهَبَا for two men, ذَهَبَتَا for two women and ذَهَبْتُمَا for you two. The present is يَذْهَبَانِ and تَذْهَبَانِ, and the command is اِذْهَبَا.": "A wannan darasin za ka yi magana da mutum biyu da kuma game da mutum biyu. Wakilan sunan su ne أَنْتُمَا, ku biyu, da هُمَا, su biyu. Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci shi ne ذَهَبَا ga maza biyu, ذَهَبَتَا ga mata biyu da ذَهَبْتُمَا ga ku biyu. Mudari'i shi ne يَذْهَبَانِ da تَذْهَبَانِ, kuma umarni shi ne اِذْهَبَا.", "antumaa": "antumaa", "you two": "ku biyu", "humaa": "humaa", "people, men or women:": "mutum biyu, maza ko mata:", "(you two),": "(ku biyu),", "(they two). The ending is": "(su biyu). Ƙarshen shi ne", "(your, of two) and": "(naku, na mutum biyu) da", "(their, of two):": "(nasu, na mutum biyu):", "Come in, you two. Who are you? We are two new students.": "Ku shigo, ku biyu. Su wane ne ku? Mu sababbin ɗalibai ne biyu.", "Welcome to you both. Where are you two from? We are from China.": "Barka da zuwanku duka. Daga ina ku biyu kuka fito? Mun fito daga Sin.", "What are your names? My name is al-Hasan, and my brother's name is al-Husayn.": "Mene ne sunayenku? Sunana al-Hasan, sunan ɗan'uwana kuma al-Husayn.", "Are you two twins? Yes. I knew from the likeness between you.": "Ku 'yan biyu ne? Ee. Na gane daga kamannin da ke tsakaninku.", "dhahabaa": "dhahabaa", "they two went (m)": "su biyu sun tafi (maza)", "dhahabataa": "dhahabataa", "dhahabtumaa": "dhahabtumaa", "you two went": "ku biyu kun tafi", "(two men),": "(maza biyu),", "(two women),": "(mata biyu),", "(you two). The answer is": "(ku biyu). Amsar ita ce", "When did you two arrive in Madinah? We arrived yesterday.": "Yaushe ku biyu kuka iso Madina? Mun iso jiya.", "As for the two brothers, they work at the airline office. They studied at this language institute.": "Amma 'yan'uwan biyu maza, suna aiki a ofishin kamfanin jiragen sama. Sun yi karatu a wannan cibiyar koyon harsuna.", "We had two other sisters who died when they were small.": "Muna da wasu 'yan'uwa mata biyu da suka rasu tun suna ƙanana.", "They are in the library. They went to get the set books.": "Suna ɗakin karatu. Sun tafi su karɓo littattafan da aka tsara.", "yadh-habaani": "yadh-habaani", "they two go": "su biyu suna tafiya", "tadh-habaani": "tadh-habaani", "you two go, they two (f) go": "ku biyu kuna tafiya, su biyu (mata) suna tafiya", "idh-habaa": "idh-habaa", "go, you two!": "ku tafi, ku biyu!", "(two women, or you two). After": "(mata biyu, ko ku biyu). Bayan", "drops": "yana faɗuwa", ". The command:": ". Umarni:", ". (These are part of": ". (Waɗannan suna cikin", "As for the two sisters, they study at the secondary school.": "Amma 'yan'uwan biyu mata, suna karatu a makarantar sakandare.", "In which college do you two want to study after studying Arabic?": "A wace tsangaya ku biyu kuke so ku yi karatu bayan kun karanci Larabci?", "Don't go to him now, he is busy. You can go to him after the period ends.": "Kada ku je wurinsa yanzu, yana da aiki. Kuna iya zuwa wurinsa bayan lokacin darasin ya ƙare.", "Go now to the library, you two, and take the set books.": "Ku tafi ɗakin karatu yanzu, ku biyu, ku karɓi littattafan da aka tsara.", "a twin": "'yan biyu", "resemblance": "kamanni", "childhood, small age": "yarinta, ƙuruciya", "the airline": "kamfanin jiragen sama", "an institute": "cibiyar ilimi", "the supervisor": "mai kulawa", "the set books": "littattafan da aka tsara", "may Allah grant you two success": "Allah Ya ba ku biyu nasara", "fatan (pl. fityaanun)": "fatan (jam'i: fityaanun)", "taw'amun (pl. tawaa'imu)": "taw'amun (jam'i: tawaa'imu)", "ash-shabahu": "ash-shabahu", "aṣ-ṣigharu": "aṣ-ṣigharu", "al-khuṭuuṭul-jawwiyyatu": "al-khuṭuuṭul-jawwiyyatu", "ma'hadun (pl. ma'aahidu)": "ma'hadun (jam'i: ma'aahidu)", "al-muraaqibu": "al-muraaqibu", "al-kutubul-muqarraratu": "al-kutubul-muqarraratu", "waffaqakumu llaahu": "waffaqakumu llaahu", "Come in, you two. Who are you? Two new students. Welcome. Where are you from? From China.": "Ku shigo, ku biyu. Su wane ne ku? Sababbin ɗalibai biyu. Barka da zuwa. Daga ina kuka fito? Daga Sin.", "When did you arrive in Madinah? Yesterday. Are you twins? Yes, how did you know, teacher?": "Yaushe kuka iso Madina? Jiya. Ku 'yan biyu ne? Ee, yaya ka gane, malam?", "I knew from the likeness between you. What are your names? Mine is al-Hasan, and my brother's is al-Husayn.": "Na gane daga kamannin da ke tsakaninku. Mene ne sunayenku? Nawa al-Hasan, na ɗan'uwana kuma al-Husayn.", "Do you have brothers and sisters? Yes, two brothers and two sisters. The two brothers work at an airline office.": "Kuna da 'yan'uwa maza da mata? Ee, 'yan'uwa maza biyu da mata biyu. 'Yan'uwan biyu maza suna aiki a ofishin kamfanin jiragen sama.", "And the two sisters study at the secondary school. We had two other sisters who died when small.": "'Yan'uwan biyu mata kuma suna karatu a makarantar sakandare. Muna da wasu 'yan'uwa mata biyu da suka rasu tun suna ƙanana.", "In which college do you two want to study after Arabic? I want to study at the College of Shari'ah. May Allah grant you success.": "A wace tsangaya ku biyu kuke so ku yi karatu bayan Larabci? Ina so in yi karatu a Tsangayar Shari'a. Allah Ya ba ku nasara.", "Don't go to him now, he is busy. Go now to the library and take the set books.": "Kada ku je wurinsa yanzu, yana da aiki. Ku tafi ɗakin karatu yanzu ku karɓi littattafan da aka tsara.", "Two men, two women, or you two?": "Maza biyu, mata biyu, ko ku biyu?", "Talk to two people.": "Yi magana da mutum biyu.", "“May Allah grant you two success.”": "“Allah Ya ba ku biyu nasara.”", "“They two are in the library.”": "“Su biyu suna ɗakin karatu.”", "“Who are you two?”": "“Su wane ne ku biyu?”", "“Welcome to you two.”": "“Barka da zuwanku, ku biyu.”", "We are two new students.": "Mu sababbin ɗalibai ne biyu.", "When did you two arrive in Madinah?": "Yaushe ku biyu kuka iso Madina?", "Go to the library, you two.": "Ku tafi ɗakin karatu, ku biyu.", "Listen, then write the word. (an institute)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (cibiyar ilimi)", "✅ When did you two arrive in Madinah?": "✅ Yaushe ku biyu kuka iso Madina?", "✅ Go to the library, you two.": "✅ Ku tafi ɗakin karatu, ku biyu.", "✅ Write: an institute": "✅ Rubuta: cibiyar ilimi", "✅ “Who are you two?”": "✅ “Su wane ne ku biyu?”", "✅ “May Allah grant you two success.”": "✅ “Allah Ya ba ku biyu nasara.”", "This is the last lesson of Book 2. You will put together the five verbs,": "Wannan shi ne darasi na ƙarshe na Littafi na 2. Za ka haɗa fi'iloli biyar (al-af'aal al-khamsa),", "which keep the": "waɗanda suke riƙe", "normally and drop it after": "a yanayin al'ada kuma suke sauke shi bayan", "You will also learn that a describing word,": "Za ka kuma koyi cewa kalmar siffantawa (na'ati),", "follows its noun in four ways: its ending, masculine or feminine, singular, dual or plural, and": "tana bin sunanta ta hanyoyi huɗu: ƙarshenta, namiji ko mace, ɗaya, biyu ko jam'i, da kuma", "The five verbs end in -": "Fi'iloli biyar suna ƙarewa da -", "Normally they keep the": "A yanayin al'ada suna riƙe", "they drop it.": "suna sauke shi.", "is the describing word. It follows its noun in four things: the ending, masculine or feminine, one, two or many, and": "ita ce kalmar siffantawa. Tana bin sunanta a abubuwa huɗu: ƙarshe, namiji ko mace, ɗaya, biyu ko jam'i, da kuma", "the five verbs": "fi'iloli biyar", "the describing word": "kalmar siffantawa (na'ati)", "The five verbs": "Fi'iloli biyar", "Describing word": "Kalmar siffantawa", "Find it": "Nemo ta", "This is the last lesson of Book 2. You will put together the five verbs, الْأَفْعَالُ الْخَمْسَةُ, like يَذْهَبَانِ, يَذْهَبُونَ and تَذْهَبِينَ, which keep the نُونْ normally and drop it after أَنْ, لَنْ and لَمْ. You will also learn that a describing word, النَّعْتُ, follows its noun in four ways: its ending, masculine or feminine, singular, dual or plural, and الْ.": "Wannan shi ne darasi na ƙarshe na Littafi na 2. Za ka haɗa fi'iloli biyar, الْأَفْعَالُ الْخَمْسَةُ, kamar يَذْهَبَانِ, يَذْهَبُونَ da تَذْهَبِينَ, waɗanda suke riƙe نُونْ a yanayin al'ada kuma suke sauke shi bayan أَنْ, لَنْ da لَمْ. Za ka kuma koyi cewa kalmar siffantawa, النَّعْتُ, tana bin sunanta ta hanyoyi huɗu: ƙarshenta, namiji ko mace, ɗaya, biyu ko jam'i, da kuma الْ.", "they": "su", "tadh-habuuna": "tadh-habuuna", "you all": "ku duka", "tadh-habeena": "tadh-habeena", "you (f) go": "ke (mace) kina tafiya", "are the present forms ending in": "su ne siffofin mudari'i masu ƙarewa da", ". Normal: they": ". A yanayin al'ada: suna", "keep the": "riƙe", "(-a state) and": "(yanayin -a) da", "that forbids (sukun state): they": "ta hani (yanayin sukun): suna", "they two (m)": "su biyu (maza)", "you two, they two (f)": "ku biyu, su biyu (mata)", "'indee mu'jamun jayyidun": "'indee mu'jamun jayyidun", "I have a good dictionary.": "Ina da ƙamus mai kyau.", "(the describing word) and": "(kalmar siffantawa) da", ". The describing word follows its noun in": ". Kalmar siffantawa tana bin sunanta a", "four": "abubuwa huɗu", "things: (1) the ending, (2) masculine or feminine, (3) one, two or many, (4) with or without": ": (1) ƙarshe, (2) namiji ko mace, (3) ɗaya, biyu ko jam'i, (4) da ko ba tare da", "the ending: -un": "ƙarshe: -un", "masculine or feminine": "namiji ko mace", "one, two or many": "ɗaya, biyu ko jam'i", "with or without الْ": "da ko ba tare da الْ", "Al-Mu'jam al-Waseet (a dictionary)": "Al-Mu'jam al-Waseet (wani ƙamus)", "he guided, showed": "ya nuna, ya shiryar", "it ended": "ya ƙare", "the part, volume": "sashe, juzu'i", "al-mu'jamul-waseeṭu": "al-mu'jamul-waseeṭu", "dalla (yadullu)": "dalla (yadullu)", "intahaa (yantahee)": "intahaa (yantahee)", "al-juz'u (pl. ajzaa'un)": "al-juz'u (jam'i: ajzaa'un)", "the noun described": "sunan da aka siffanta (man'uti)", "Where are the two new students? In the library. They went to get the set books.": "Ina sababbin ɗaliban nan biyu? A ɗakin karatu. Sun tafi su karɓo littattafan da aka tsara.", "When did they go? They went in the second period.": "Yaushe suka tafi? Sun tafi a lokacin darasi na biyu.", "Teacher, I want to buy an Arabic dictionary. I want you to point me to a good dictionary.": "Malam, ina so in sayi ƙamus na Larabci. Ina so ka nuna mini ƙamus mai kyau.", "Buy al-Mu'jam al-Waseet, for it is a good dictionary.": "Ka sayi al-Mu'jam al-Waseet, domin ƙamus ne mai kyau.", "Today the second book ends. When do we start the third book?": "Yau littafi na biyu ya ƙare. Yaushe za mu fara littafi na uku?", "Next week, in sha Allah. Today we read the last two pages of the second book.": "Mako mai zuwa, in sha Allah. Yau za mu karanta shafuka biyu na ƙarshe na littafi na biyu.", "Normal: keep. After": "Yanayin al'ada: riƙe. Bayan", "Keep or drop the": "Riƙe ko sauke", "that forbids: drop.": "ta hani: sauke.", "Ending, gender, number and": "Ƙarshe, jinsi, adadi da", "Make the describing word follow": "Sa kalmar siffantawa ta bi", "أَيْنَ مُحَمَّدٌ ……؟ (Japanese)": "أَيْنَ مُحَمَّدٌ ……؟ (Bajafane)", "Which word describes the other?": "Wace kalma ce take siffanta ɗayar?", "Find the describing word": "Nemo kalmar siffantawa", "Which is النَّعْتُ?": "Wace ce النَّعْتُ?", "The new car is expensive.": "Sabuwar motar tana da tsada.", "I want you to point me to a good dictionary.": "Ina so ka nuna mini ƙamus mai kyau.", "Keep or drop the ن?": "Riƙe ko sauke ن?", "Listen, then write the word. (the part, volume)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (juzu'i)", "✅ I want you to point me to a good dictionary.": "✅ Ina so ka nuna mini ƙamus mai kyau.", "✅ Write: the part, volume": "✅ Rubuta: juzu'i", "✅ The new car is expensive.": "✅ Sabuwar motar tana da tsada.", "This is the final exam of Beginner 3. It has forty questions from Lessons sixteen to thirty one of Book 2, and you have thirty minutes. You need eighty five percent to pass and open Beginner 4.": "Wannan ita ce jarrabawar ƙarshe ta Mafari 3. Tana da tambayoyi arba'in daga Darasi na goma sha shida zuwa talatin da ɗaya na Littafi na 2, kuma kana da minti talatin. Kana buƙatar kashi tamanin da biyar cikin ɗari don ka ci, ka buɗe Mafari 4.", "Other rules": "Wasu ƙa'idoji", "How do you say “We must understand the Qur'an”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Wajibi ne mu fahimci Alƙur'ani”?", "How do you say “You can sit here”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Kana iya zama nan”?", "كَانَ, still, أَبُو": "كَانَ, har yanzu, أَبُو", "How do you say “Your father came”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Babanka ya zo”?", "How do you say “I saw your father”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na ga babanka”?", "Weak and doubled verbs": "Fi'iloli masu rauni da mudha'af", "The present of وَجَدَ": "Mudari'in وَجَدَ", "How do you say “I will not go”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ba zan tafi ba”?", "يُرِيدُ, colours, آخَرُ": "يُرِيدُ, launuka, آخَرُ", "How do you say “I want”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ina so”?", "How do you say “They want to go”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Suna so su tafi”?", "Two and plurals": "Mutum biyu da jam'i", "How do you say “The two sisters study”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'Yan'uwan biyu mata suna karatu”?", "How do you say “I asked the teachers”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na tambayi malaman”?", "Where is the watch? (Here it is.)": "Ina agogon? (Ga shi nan.)", "لَمْ, لَمَّا, sentence kinds": "لَمْ, لَمَّا, nau'ukan jumla", "Which word is a particle?": "Wace kalma ce harafi?", "How do you say “He did not come”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Bai zo ba”?", "How do you say “I want a notebook with lined paper”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ina son littafin rubutu mai layi”?", "How do you say “I saw the two teachers”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na ga malaman biyu”?", "How do you say “I have not written yet”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Har yanzu ban rubuta ba”?", "it is a duty": "wajibi ne", "How do you say “The two teachers came”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Malaman biyu sun zo”?", "How do you say “I said to your brother”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na ce wa ɗan'uwanka”?", "How do you say “I bought it for two riyals”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na saye shi riyal biyu”?", "How do you say “I bought it for 80 riyals”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na saye shi riyal 80”?", "How do you say “He did not make Hajj”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Bai yi Hajji ba”?", "How do you say “a white sheet of paper”?": "Yaya ake cewa “farar takarda”?", "How do you say “He is still a dean”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Har yanzu shi shugaban tsangaya ne”?", "How do you say “They did not understand”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ba su fahimta ba”?", "How do you say “a red bag”?": "Yaya ake cewa “jar jaka”?", "How do you say “Please do not come in”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Don Allah kada ka shigo”?", "How do you say “I have never done this”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ban taɓa yin wannan ba”?", "Tell a man: Don't run.": "Ka gaya wa namiji: Kada ka yi gudu.", "How do you say “The new car is expensive”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Sabuwar motar tana da tsada”?", "Which sentence is verbal?": "Wace jumla ce fi'iliyya?", "How do you say “I want to go”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ina so in tafi”?", "How do you say “Don't forget”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Kada ka manta”?", "How do you say “I said”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na ce”?", "How do you say “I slept”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na yi barci”?", "✅ How do you say “We must understand the Qur'an”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Wajibi ne mu fahimci Alƙur'ani”?", "✅ How do you say “You can sit here”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Kana iya zama nan”?", "✅ How do you say “Your father came”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Babanka ya zo”?", "✅ How do you say “I saw your father”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na ga babanka”?", "✅ The present of وَجَدَ": "✅ Mudari'in وَجَدَ", "✅ How do you say “I will not go”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ba zan tafi ba”?", "✅ How do you say “I want”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ina so”?", "✅ How do you say “They want to go”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Suna so su tafi”?", "✅ How do you say “The two sisters study”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “'Yan'uwan biyu mata suna karatu”?", "✅ How do you say “I asked the teachers”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na tambayi malaman”?", "✅ Where is the watch? (Here it is.)": "✅ Ina agogon? (Ga shi nan.)", "✅ Which word is a particle?": "✅ Wace kalma ce harafi?", "✅ How do you say “He did not come”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Bai zo ba”?", "✅ How do you say “I want a notebook with lined paper”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ina son littafin rubutu mai layi”?", "✅ How do you say “I saw the two teachers”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na ga malaman biyu”?", "✅ How do you say “I have not written yet”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Har yanzu ban rubuta ba”?", "✅ How do you say “The two teachers came”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Malaman biyu sun zo”?", "✅ How do you say “I said to your brother”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na ce wa ɗan'uwanka”?", "✅ How do you say “I bought it for two riyals”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na saye shi riyal biyu”?", "✅ How do you say “I bought it for 80 riyals”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na saye shi riyal 80”?", "✅ How do you say “He did not make Hajj”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Bai yi Hajji ba”?", "✅ How do you say “a white sheet of paper”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “farar takarda”?", "✅ How do you say “He is still a dean”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Har yanzu shi shugaban tsangaya ne”?", "✅ How do you say “They did not understand”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ba su fahimta ba”?", "✅ How do you say “a red bag”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “jar jaka”?", "✅ How do you say “Please do not come in”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Don Allah kada ka shigo”?", "✅ How do you say “I have never done this”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ban taɓa yin wannan ba”?", "✅ Tell a man: Don't run.": "✅ Ka gaya wa namiji: Kada ka yi gudu.", "✅ How do you say “The new car is expensive”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Sabuwar motar tana da tsada”?", "✅ Which sentence is verbal?": "✅ Wace jumla ce fi'iliyya?", "✅ How do you say “I want to go”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Ina so in tafi”?", "✅ How do you say “Don't forget”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Kada ka manta”?", "✅ How do you say “I said”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na ce”?", "✅ How do you say “I slept”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Na yi barci”?", "Welcome to Beginner 4. In this level you will study Book 3. It ends with a final exam and a certificate.": "Barka da zuwa Mafari 4. A wannan matakin za ka karanci Littafi na 3. Yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida.", "Welcome to Book 3. This book teaches the grammar behind everything you have learned. In this lesson you will learn": "Barka da zuwa Littafi na 3. Wannan littafin yana koyar da nahawun da ke bayan duk abin da ka koya. A wannan darasin za ka koyi", "a word whose ending changes, and": "kalmar da ƙarshenta yake canjawa (mu'rab), da", "a word that never changes. You will review the main signs,": "kalmar da ba ta canjawa har abada (mabni). Za ka yi bitar manyan alamomi,", "the other signs, and the hidden signs in words like": "sauran alamomi, da alamomin da suke ɓoye a kalmomi kamar", "word changes its ending:": "kalma tana canja ƙarshenta:", "word never changes:": "kalma ba ta canjawa har abada:", "Pronouns, pointing words, joining words and question words are fixed.": "Wakilan suna, kalmomin nuni, kalmomin haɗi da kalmomin tambaya ba sa canjawa.", "The original signs for nouns are": "Alamomin asali na sunaye su ne", "For the present verb:": "Ga fi'ili mai nuna yanzu:", "and sukun:": "da sukun:", "The past verb and the command never change.": "Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci da umarni ba sa canjawa har abada.", "Some words use other signs: the plural -": "Wasu kalmomi suna amfani da wasu alamomi: jam'i -", "for -a. Words without tanween take": "a madadin -a. Kalmomin da ba sa karɓar tanwini suna ɗaukar", "for -i:": "a madadin -i:", "And the dual -": "Da kuma tasniya -", "In three kinds of noun the signs are hidden. Words ending in": "A nau'ukan suna guda uku alamomin suna ɓoye. Kalmomin da suke ƙarewa da", "all signs hidden. Words ending in": "dukan alamomi a ɓoye. Kalmomin da suke ƙarewa da", "are hidden, but": "a ɓoye suke, amma", "shows. And a noun with my, like": "tana bayyana. Da kuma suna mai “nawa”, kamar", "all hidden.": "duka a ɓoye.", "Followers copy the ending of the word before them. There are four:": "Mabiya (tawabi'u) suna kwaikwayon ƙarshen kalmar da ke gabansu. Su huɗu ne:", "the describing word.": "kalmar siffantawa.", "the emphasis, like": "ƙarfafawa (tawkidi), kamar", "joining with": "haɗawa da", "a word in place of another.": "kalmar da take a madadin wata (badali).", "الْإِعْرَابُ وَالْبِنَاءُ (changing and fixed words)": "الْإِعْرَابُ وَالْبِنَاءُ (kalmomi masu canjawa da marasa canjawa)", "Noun: changing or fixed?": "Suna: mai canjawa ko mara canjawa?", "Verb: changing or fixed?": "Fi'ili: mai canjawa ko mara canjawa?", "Other signs": "Sauran alamomi", "Hidden signs": "Alamomi a ɓoye", "Followers": "Mabiya", "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Welcome to Beginner 4. In this level you will study Book 3. It ends with a final exam and a certificate. مَا شَاءَ اللهُ, you have come far. Keep going.": "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Barka da zuwa Mafari 4. A wannan matakin za ka karanci Littafi na 3. Yana ƙarewa da jarrabawar ƙarshe da takardar shaida. مَا شَاءَ اللهُ, ka yi nisa. Ka ci gaba.", "jaa'a l-mudarrisu": "jaa'a l-mudarrisu", "The teacher came.": "Malamin ya zo.", "jaa'a haa'ulaa'i": "jaa'a haa'ulaa'i", "These came.": "Waɗannan sun zo.", ". Fixed nouns: pronouns (": ". Sunaye marasa canjawa: wakilan suna (", "), pointing words (": "), kalmomin nuni (", "), joining words (": "), kalmomin haɗi (", "), question words (": "), kalmomin tambaya (", "), some time words (": "), wasu kalmomin lokaci (", "), and 11–19 (except 12).": "), da 11 zuwa 19 (ban da 12).", "مُعْرَبٌ: the ending changes": "مُعْرَبٌ: ƙarshe yana canjawa", "مَبْنِيٌّ: never changes": "مَبْنِيٌّ: ba ya canjawa har abada", "changing: -u": "mai canjawa: -u", "fixed: always the same": "mara canjawa: kullum iri ɗaya", "12: the first part changes": "12: sashe na farko yana canjawa", "original signs": "alamomin asali", ") for nouns are the": ") na sunaye su ne", ") and": ") da", "). For the present verb: damma (": "). Ga fi'ili mai nuna yanzu: ɗamma (", "), fatha (": "), fataha (", ". The past verb and the command are always fixed.": ". Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci da umarni kullum ba sa canjawa.", "-u: normal (marfuu')": "-u: yanayin al'ada (marfuu')", "-a: after أَنْ (manṣuub)": "-a: bayan أَنْ (manṣuub)", "sukun: after لَمْ (majzuum)": "sukun: bayan لَمْ (majzuum)", "khalaqa llaahu s-samaawaati": "khalaqa llaahu s-samaawaati", "Allah created the heavens": "Allah Ya halicci sammai", "idh-hab ilaa fir'awna": "idh-hab ilaa fir'awna", "Go to Pharaoh": "Ka tafi wurin Fir'auna", "Some words use": "Wasu kalmomi suna amfani da", "other signs": "wasu alamomi", "): (1) the plural": "): (1) jam'in", "takes a kasra for -a; (2) words without -un (": "yana ɗaukar kasra a madadin -a; (2) kalmomin da ba sa karɓar -un (", ") take a fatha for -i:": ") suna ɗaukar fataha a madadin -i:", "; (5) the dual": "; (5) tasniya", ". For verbs: the five verbs keep or drop the": ". Ga fi'iloli: fi'iloli biyar suna riƙe ko sauke", ", and verbs ending in a vowel drop it after": ", kuma fi'iloli masu ƙarewa da wasali suna sauke shi bayan", "-َاتِ for -a": "-َاتِ a madadin -a", "fatha for -i": "fataha a madadin -i", "the ن drops": "ن yana faɗuwa", "the vowel drops": "wasalin yana faɗuwa", "al-fataa": "al-fataa", "the young man": "saurayin", "al-qaaḍee": "al-qaaḍee", "the judge": "alƙalin", "ṣadeeqee": "ṣadeeqee", "my friend": "abokina", "In three kinds of noun the signs are": "A nau'ukan suna guda uku alamomin suna", "): (1) words ending in": "): (1) kalmomin da suke ƙarewa da", "— all three signs hidden; (2) words ending in": "— dukan alamomi uku a ɓoye; (2) kalmomin da suke ƙarewa da", "— -u and -i hidden, but -a shows:": "— -u da -i a ɓoye, amma -a tana bayyana:", "; (3) a noun with": "; (3) suna mai", "— all hidden.": "— duka a ɓoye.", "The young man killed the snake with the stick.": "Saurayin ya kashe macijin da sandar.", "The judge asked the lawyer about the criminal.": "Alƙalin ya tambayi lauyan game da mai laifin.", "My grandfather invited my teacher with my classmates.": "Kakana ya gayyaci malamina tare da abokan ajina.", "A judge went to a lawyer.": "Wani alƙali ya je wurin wani lauya.", "al-marfuu'aatu": "al-marfuu'aatu", "-u words": "kalmomin -u", "al-manṣuubaatu": "al-manṣuubaatu", "-a words": "kalmomin -a", "al-majruuraatu": "al-majruuraatu", "-i words": "kalmomin -i", "at-tawaabi'u": "at-tawaabi'u", "followers": "mabiya", "the objects (": "wanda aka yi wa aiki (", "and after a preposition.": "da bayan harafin jarri.", ") copy the word before:": ") suna kwaikwayon kalmar da ke gabansu:", "a word whose ending changes": "kalmar da ƙarshenta yake canjawa", "a fixed word": "kalma mara canjawa", "in the -u state": "a yanayin -u", "in the -a state": "a yanayin -a", "in the -i state": "a yanayin -i", "in the sukun state (verbs)": "a yanayin sukun (fi'iloli)", "New words: grammar words": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin nahawu", "mu'rabun": "mu'rabun", "mabniyyun": "mabniyyun", "marfuu'un": "marfuu'un", "manṣuubun": "manṣuubun", "majruurun": "majruurun", "majzuumun": "majzuumun", "the lawyer": "lauya", "New words: example words": "Sababbin kalmomi: kalmomin misali", "al-muḥaamee": "al-muḥaamee", "the change of endings": "canjin ƙarshen kalmomi (i'irabi)", "hidden, understood": "a ɓoye, wanda ake fahimta", "The teacher came. I asked the teacher. I greeted the teacher.": "Malamin ya zo. Na tambayi malamin. Na gaishe da malamin.", "These came. I asked these. I greeted these.": "Waɗannan sun zo. Na tambayi waɗannan. Na gaishe da waɗannan.", "The students all came. This principal himself told me.": "Ɗaliban duka sun zo. Wannan shugaban makarantar da kansa ya gaya mini.", "Pronouns, pointing, joining and question words are fixed.": "Wakilan suna, kalmomin nuni, kalmomin haɗi da na tambaya ba sa canjawa.", "? (nouns)": "? (sunaye)", "Past and command are fixed; the present changes, except with -": "Shuɗaɗɗen lokaci da umarni ba sa canjawa; mudari'i yana canjawa, sai dai tare da -", "? (verbs)": "? (fi'iloli)", "The secondary signs.": "Alamomin reshe.", "dropping the ن": "sauke ن", "the fatha": "fataha", "Which sign is used?": "Wace alama ce aka yi amfani da ita?", "أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَذْهَبُوا (the -a sign)": "أَتُرِيدُونَ أَنْ تَذْهَبُوا (alamar -a)", "the ا": "ا", "the و": "و", "أَعْرِفُ أَبَاكَ (the -a sign)": "أَعْرِفُ أَبَاكَ (alamar -a)", "the ي": "ي", "غَابَ طَالِبَانِ (the -u sign)": "غَابَ طَالِبَانِ (alamar -u)", "the kasra": "kasra", "خَلَقَ اللهُ السَّمَاوَاتِ (the -a sign)": "خَلَقَ اللهُ السَّمَاوَاتِ (alamar -a)", "سَأَلْتُ الْمُدَرِّسِينَ (the -a sign)": "سَأَلْتُ الْمُدَرِّسِينَ (alamar -a)", "the sukun": "sukun", "dropping the last letter": "sauke harafin ƙarshe", "لَمْ يَمْشِ (the sukun sign)": "لَمْ يَمْشِ (alamar sukun)", "all three signs hidden": "dukan alamomi uku a ɓoye", "-a shows, -u and -i hidden": "-a tana bayyana, -u da -i a ɓoye", "Which signs are hidden?": "Waɗanne alamomi ne a ɓoye?", "· with": "· tare da", "only -a shows": "-a kaɗai ce take bayyana", "Only the": "Sai", "Only the fatha shows on": "Fataha kaɗai ce take bayyana a kan", "shows on": "tana bayyana a kan", "The followers copy the ending": "Mabiya suna kwaikwayon ƙarshe", "I did not understand this lesson.": "Ban fahimci wannan darasin ba.", "مُعْرَبٌ or مَبْنِيٌّ? (nouns)": "مُعْرَبٌ ko مَبْنِيٌّ? (sunaye)", "Listen, then write the word. (the judge)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (alƙalin)", "الْقَاضِي or الْقَاضِيَ?": "الْقَاضِي ko الْقَاضِيَ?", "مُعْرَبٌ or مَبْنِيٌّ? (verbs)": "مُعْرَبٌ ko مَبْنِيٌّ? (fi'iloli)", "The students all came.": "Ɗaliban duka sun zo.", "The judge asked the lawyer.": "Alƙalin ya tambayi lauyan.", "✅ Write: the judge": "✅ Rubuta: alƙalin", "✅ The students all came.": "✅ Ɗaliban duka sun zo.", "✅ The judge asked the lawyer.": "✅ Alƙalin ya tambayi lauyan.", "In this lesson you will learn the": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi", "that means while,": "mai ma'anar yayin da,", "I saw him while he was entering the bathroom. You will compare it with the": "na gan shi yayin da yake shiga banɗaki. Za ka kwatanta shi da", "that means and, and the": "mai ma'anar da (haɗawa), da", "of oath,": "na rantsuwa,", "for hope and fear,": "don fata da tsoro,", "here you are,": "ga shi, karɓa,", "is there any question, and": "akwai tambaya, da", "with.": "a wurin.", "means while. It tells the state someone was in.": "yana nufin yayin da. Yana nuna halin da wani yake ciki.", "has many uses. And:": "yana da amfani da yawa. Da (haɗawa):", "By, for an oath:": "Rantsuwa:", "While:": "Yayin da:", "shows hope for something good:": "yana nuna fatan abu mai kyau:", "And fear for something bad:": "Da kuma tsoron abu mara kyau:", "A past verb can be a prayer:": "Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci yana iya zama addu'a:", "means take, here you are:": "yana nufin karɓa, ga shi:", "is extra, for emphasis.": "ƙari ne, don ƙarfafawa.", "means with or at:": "yana nufin a wurin ko tare da:", "I have a question.": "Ina da tambaya.", "وَاوُ الْحَالِ (و meaning “while”)": "وَاوُ الْحَالِ (و mai ma'anar “yayin da”)", "Which و?": "Wane و?", "Use “while”": "Yi amfani da “yayin da”", "Hope or fear?": "Fata ko tsoro?", "Expressions": "Maganganu", "In this lesson you will learn the وَاوْ that means while, وَاوُ الْحَالِ, as in رَأَيْتُهُ وَهُوَ يَدْخُلُ الْحَمَّامَ, I saw him while he was entering the bathroom. You will compare it with the وَاوْ that means and, and the وَاوْ of oath, وَاللهِ. You will also learn لَعَلَّ for hope and fear, إِلَيْكَ, here you are, هَلْ مِنْ سُؤَالٍ, is there any question, and لَدَى, with.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi وَاوْ mai ma'anar yayin da, وَاوُ الْحَالِ, kamar a رَأَيْتُهُ وَهُوَ يَدْخُلُ الْحَمَّامَ, na gan shi yayin da yake shiga banɗaki. Za ka kwatanta shi da وَاوْ mai ma'anar da (haɗawa), da kuma وَاوْ na rantsuwa, وَاللهِ. Za ka kuma koyi لَعَلَّ don fata da tsoro, إِلَيْكَ, ga shi, karɓa, هَلْ مِنْ سُؤَالٍ, akwai tambaya, da لَدَى, a wurin.", "ra'aytuhu wa huwa yadkhulu l-ḥammaama": "ra'aytuhu wa huwa yadkhulu l-ḥammaama", "I saw him while he was entering the bathroom.": "Na gan shi yayin da yake shiga banɗaki.", "while": "yayin da", ": it tells the state someone was in. After it comes a nominal sentence:": ": yana nuna halin da wani yake ciki. Bayansa jumla ismiyya take zuwa:", "= while he was in the mosque.": "yana nufin yayin da yake cikin masallaci.", "I saw him going into the clinic. Perhaps he is sick.": "Na gan shi yana shiga asibitin shan magani. Watakila ba shi da lafiya.", "My father died when I was small.": "Babana ya rasu lokacin ina ƙarami.", "I sought knowledge when I was old.": "Na nemi ilimi lokacin na tsufa.", "Read sitting down. I want to read standing.": "Karanta kana zaune. Ina so in karanta a tsaye.", "waawul-'aṭfi": "waawul-'aṭfi", "waawul-qasami": "waawul-qasami", "by (oath)": "na rantsuwa", "waawul-ḥaali": "waawul-ḥaali", "has many uses:": "yana da amfani da yawa:", "by": "na rantsuwa", ", an oath, a preposition giving -i):": ", rantsuwa ce, harafin jarri ne mai kawo -i):", "I went to the market and bought things.": "Na je kasuwa na sayi kayayyaki.", "By Allah, I have never been absent.": "Wallahi, ban taɓa yin fashi ba.", "I entered the mosque while the imam was giving the sermon.": "Na shiga masallaci yayin da liman yake huɗuba.", "We came back yesterday evening. We left Makkah as the sun was rising.": "Mun dawo jiya da yamma. Mun bar Makka yayin da rana take fitowa.", "la'allahu bikhayrin": "la'allahu bikhayrin", "I hope he is well": "ina fatan yana lafiya", "la'allahu mareeḍun": "la'allahu mareeḍun", "I fear he is sick": "ina tsoron ba shi da lafiya", "shows": "yana nuna", "hope": "fata", ") for something good:": ") ga abu mai kyau:", ". And": ". Da kuma", "fear": "tsoro", ") for something bad:": ") ga abu mara kyau:", ". The past verb can be a": ". Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci yana iya zama", "prayer": "addu'a", "(may Allah cure him),": "(Allah Ya ba shi lafiya),", "I hope you have passed.": "Ina fatan ka ci jarrabawa.", "I fear you have failed.": "Ina tsoron kada ka faɗi jarrabawa.", "May Allah accept your Umrah. Amen.": "Allah Ya karɓi Umrarka. Amin.", "ilayka": "ilayka", "here you are": "ga shi, karɓa", "hal min su'aalin": "hal min su'aalin", "is there any question?": "akwai wata tambaya?", "ladayya": "ladayya", "take, here you are": "karɓa, ga shi", ", a word that acts like a verb, like": ", kalma ce da take aiki kamar fi'ili, kamar", ". In": ". A cikin", "is extra (": "ƙari ne (", "), for emphasis.": "), don ƙarfafawa.", "(with, at); with a pronoun:": "(a wurin, tare da); tare da wakilin suna:", "Here is this book, take it.": "Ga wannan littafin, karɓe shi.", "Sister, here are the spoons.": "'Yar'uwa, ga cokulan.", "Three minutes are left. Is there any question? Yes, I have a question.": "Minti uku suka rage. Akwai wata tambaya? Ee, ina da tambaya.", "I found him at the door.": "Na same shi a bakin ƙofa.", "the clinic": "asibitin shan magani", "Taybah (Madinah)": "Ɗaiba (Madina)", "the canteen": "kantin abinci na makaranta", "in the state of ihram": "a cikin harami (ihrami)", "drunk (pl.)": "masu maye (jam'i)", "disbelievers": "kafirai", "he gave a sermon": "ya yi huɗuba", "it rose (the sun)": "ta fito (rana)", "he carried": "ya ɗauka", "he lived": "ya rayu", "al-mustawṣafu": "al-mustawṣafu", "ṭaybatu": "ṭaybatu", "al-miqṣafu": "al-miqṣafu", "ḥurumun (sg. ḥaraamun)": "ḥurumun (ɗaya: ḥaraamun)", "al-'umratu": "al-'umratu", "sukaaraa": "sukaaraa", "kuffaarun (sg. kaafirun)": "kuffaarun (ɗaya: kaafirun)", "khaṭaba (yakhṭubu)": "khaṭaba (yakhṭubu)", "ṭala'a (yaṭlu'u)": "ṭala'a (yaṭlu'u)", "ḥamala (yaḥmilu)": "ḥamala (yaḥmilu)", "'aasha (ya'eeshu)": "'aasha (ya'eeshu)", "amen": "amin", "with, at": "a wurin, tare da", "here you are, take": "ga shi, karɓa", "Where is Hamid? He will come shortly, in sha Allah. I saw him going into the bathroom.": "Ina Hamid? Zai zo nan ba da daɗewa ba, in sha Allah. Na gan shi yana shiga banɗaki.", "And where is Hamzah? He left the class carrying his books. I saw him going into the clinic. Perhaps he is sick.": "Hamza fa? Ya fita daga aji yana ɗauke da littattafansa. Na gan shi yana shiga asibitin shan magani. Watakila ba shi da lafiya.", "May Allah cure him. When did you return from Makkah, brothers? Yesterday evening. We left Makkah as the sun was rising.": "Allah Ya ba shi lafiya. Yaushe kuka dawo daga Makka, 'yan'uwa? Jiya da yamma. Mun bar Makka yayin da rana take fitowa.", "We reached Madinah as people were leaving the Prophet's Mosque after Dhuhr. May Allah accept your Umrah. Amen.": "Mun isa Madina yayin da mutane suke fitowa daga Masallacin Annabi bayan Azahar. Allah Ya karɓi Umrarku. Amin.", "Read the hadith written on the board, Mu'awiyah. Read sitting. I want to read standing. As you wish.": "Karanta hadisin da aka rubuta a kan allo, Mu'awiya. Karanta kana zaune. Ina so in karanta a tsaye. Yadda ka so.", "Give an example of the oath و, Mu'awiyah. By Allah, I have never been absent. Well done. An example of the while و. I entered the mosque while the imam was preaching.": "Ba da misalin و na rantsuwa, Mu'awiya. Wallahi, ban taɓa yin fashi ba. Madalla. Misalin و na yayin da. Na shiga masallaci yayin da liman yake huɗuba.", "Well done. Three minutes are left. Is there any question? Yes, I have a question. May Allah reward you.": "Madalla. Minti uku suka rage. Akwai wata tambaya? Ee, ina da tambaya. Allah Ya saka maka da alheri.", "and, by (oath), while": "da, na rantsuwa, yayin da", "Which kind of": "Wane irin", "Which و means “while”?": "Wane و ne yake nufin “yayin da”?", "Which و means “and”?": "Wane و ne yake nufin “da”?", "+ a nominal sentence.": "+ jumla ismiyya.", "“Don't read the newspaper while you walk in the street.”": "“Kada ka karanta jarida yayin da kake tafiya a titi.”", "plus a nominal sentence.": "tare da jumla ismiyya.", "“I saw him while he was writing.”": "“Na gan shi yayin da yake rubutu.”", "“I entered while the imam was reciting al-Fatihah.”": "“Na shiga yayin da liman yake karanta Fatiha.”", "“I made Hajj when I was small.”": "“Na yi Hajji lokacin ina ƙarami.”", "Something good hope. Something bad fear.": "Abu mai kyau fata. Abu mara kyau tsoro.", ": hope or fear?": ": fata ko tsoro?", "Something good = hope. Something bad = fear.": "Abu mai kyau, fata ne. Abu mara kyau, tsoro ne.", "“I have a question.”": "“Ina da tambaya.”", "“Is there any question?”": "“Akwai wata tambaya?”", "“Here is this book (take it).”": "“Ga wannan littafin (karɓe shi).”", "“May Allah cure him.”": "“Allah Ya ba shi lafiya.”", "“By Allah, I have never been absent.”": "“Wallahi, ban taɓa yin fashi ba.”", "Read while you are sitting.": "Karanta kana zaune.", "“May Allah accept your Umrah.”": "“Allah Ya karɓi Umrarka.”", "لَعَلَّ: hope or fear?": "لَعَلَّ: fata ko tsoro?", "Which kind of وَ?": "Wane irin وَ?", "Use وَاوُ الْحَالِ": "Yi amfani da وَاوُ الْحَالِ", "Listen, then write the word. (with, at)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (a wurin, tare da)", "Which و is an oath?": "Wane و ne na rantsuwa?", "Is there any question?": "Akwai wata tambaya?", "✅ “May Allah accept your Umrah.”": "✅ “Allah Ya karɓi Umrarka.”", "✅ “Here is this book (take it).”": "✅ “Ga wannan littafin (karɓe shi).”", "✅ Which و means “while”?": "✅ Wane و ne yake nufin “yayin da”?", "✅ “Don't read the newspaper while you walk in the street.”": "✅ “Kada ka karanta jarida yayin da kake tafiya a titi.”", "✅ “I entered while the imam was reciting al-Fatihah.”": "✅ “Na shiga yayin da liman yake karanta Fatiha.”", "✅ Which و means “and”?": "✅ Wane و ne yake nufin “da”?", "✅ Write: with, at": "✅ Rubuta: a wurin, tare da", "✅ Which و is an oath?": "✅ Wane و ne na rantsuwa?", "✅ Is there any question?": "✅ Akwai wata tambaya?", "✅ My father died when I was small.": "✅ Babana ya rasu lokacin ina ƙarami.", "In this lesson you will learn the passive verb, when we do not say who did the action. In the past the first letter takes": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'ili majhuli (wanda ba a ambaci mai aikatawa ba), idan ba mu faɗi wanda ya yi aikin ba. A shuɗaɗɗen lokaci harafin farko yana ɗaukar", "and the one before the last takes": "kuma harafin da ke gaban na ƙarshe yana ɗaukar", "it was written. In the present the first letter takes": "an rubuta shi. A mudari'i harafin farko yana ɗaukar", "The object then takes the doer's place and ends in": "Sai wanda aka yi wa aiki ya ɗauki matsayin mai aikatawa, ya ƙare da", "You will also learn the ending": "Za ka kuma koyi ƙarshen", "the Islamic months, and": "watannin Musulunci, da", "either … or.": "ko dai … ko kuma.", "In the passive the doer is dropped and the object takes its place, ending in": "A majhuli ana cire mai aikatawa, wanda aka yi wa aiki ya ɗauki matsayinsa, ya ƙare da", "It is called": "Ana kiransa", "Past passive:": "Majhuli na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci:", "on the first letter and": "a kan harafin farko da", "before the last:": "a gaban na ƙarshe:", "Present passive:": "Majhuli na mudari'i:", "In use:": "A amfani:", "If the object was a pronoun, it joins the verb:": "Idan wanda aka yi wa aiki wakilin suna ne, yana haɗuwa da fi'ilin:", "I was asked.": "An tambaye ni.", "To say from, add": "Don faɗin daga wurin, ƙara", "means either or:": "yana nufin ko dai ko kuma:", "The twelve Islamic months:": "Watanni goma sha biyu na Musulunci:", "the passive: قُتِلَ (he was killed)": "majhuli: قُتِلَ (an kashe shi)", "Past passive": "Majhuli na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci", "Present passive": "Majhuli na mudari'i", "Make it passive": "Mayar da shi majhuli", "Find نَائِبُ الْفَاعِلِ": "Nemo نَائِبُ الْفَاعِلِ", "Months": "Watanni", "In this lesson you will learn the passive verb, when we do not say who did the action. In the past the first letter takes ضَمَّةْ and the one before the last takes كَسْرَةْ: كُتِبَ, it was written. In the present the first letter takes ضَمَّةْ and the one before the last takes فَتْحَةْ: يُكْتَبُ. The object then takes the doer's place and ends in ضَمَّةْ. You will also learn the ending ـِيٌّ, as in هِنْدِيٌّ, the Islamic months, and إِمَّا … وَإِمَّا, either … or.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi fi'ili majhuli, idan ba mu faɗi wanda ya yi aikin ba. A shuɗaɗɗen lokaci harafin farko yana ɗaukar ضَمَّةْ kuma harafin da ke gaban na ƙarshe yana ɗaukar كَسْرَةْ: كُتِبَ, an rubuta shi. A mudari'i harafin farko yana ɗaukar ضَمَّةْ kuma harafin da ke gaban na ƙarshe yana ɗaukar فَتْحَةْ: يُكْتَبُ. Sai wanda aka yi wa aiki ya ɗauki matsayin mai aikatawa, ya ƙare da ضَمَّةْ. Za ka kuma koyi ƙarshen ـِيٌّ, kamar a هِنْدِيٌّ, watannin Musulunci, da إِمَّا … وَإِمَّا, ko dai … ko kuma.", "qatala l-jundiyyu l-jaasuusa": "qatala l-jundiyyu l-jaasuusa", "The soldier killed the spy.": "Sojan ya kashe ɗan leƙen asirin.", "qutila l-jaasuusu": "qutila l-jaasuusu", "The spy was killed.": "An kashe ɗan leƙen asirin.", "In the": "A", "passive": "majhuli", ") the doer is": ") ana", "dropped": "cire", "and the object takes its place, ending in": "mai aikatawa, wanda aka yi wa aiki ya ɗauki matsayinsa, ya ƙare da", ". It is called": ". Ana kiransa", "active: الْفَاعِلُ + الْمَفْعُولُ": "ma'lumi: الْفَاعِلُ + الْمَفْعُولُ", "passive: نَائِبُ الْفَاعِلِ": "majhuli: نَائِبُ الْفَاعِلِ", "Man was created from clay.": "An halicci mutum daga yumɓu.", "Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was killed while leading the people in prayer in the Prophet's Mosque.": "An kashe Umar, Allah Ya yarda da shi, yayin da yake yi wa mutane limanci a Masallacin Annabi.", "My book was stolen, teacher. It was stolen from my room last night.": "An sace littafina, malam. An sace shi daga ɗakina a daren jiya.", "He, peace be upon him, was born in the month of Rabi' al-Awwal.": "An haife shi, tsira da amincin Allah su tabbata a gare shi, a watan Rabi'ul Awwal.", "kutiba": "kutiba", "it was written": "an rubuta shi", "yuktabu": "yuktabu", "it is written": "ana rubuta shi", ": the first letter takes a": ": harafin farko yana ɗaukar", "and the letter before the last a": "kuma harafin da ke gaban na ƙarshe yana ɗaukar", "write": "rubuta", "hear": "ji", "read": "karanta", "take": "ɗauka", "mataa yuftaḥu l-maṭ'amu": "mataa yuftaḥu l-maṭ'amu", "When does the restaurant open?": "Yaushe ake buɗe gidan abincin?", "su'iltu": "su'iltu", "I was asked": "an tambaye ni", ". If the object was a": ". Idan wanda aka yi wa aiki", "pronoun": "wakilin suna ne", ", it becomes the subject pronoun:": ", yana zama wakilin sunan mai aikatawa:", "(I was asked),": "(an tambaye ni),", "Why were you late? Because the restaurant opened late today.": "Me ya sa kuka makara? Saboda an buɗe gidan abincin a makare yau.", "And when does it open every day? At a quarter to six.": "To yaushe ake buɗe shi kowace rana? Ƙarfe shida saura kwata.", "Surat al-Fatihah is read in every rak'ah.": "Ana karanta Suratul Fatiha a kowace raka'a.", "The sound of the bell is not heard in this class of ours.": "Ba a jin ƙarar ƙararrawa a wannan ajin namu.", "Did the principal ask you about the absence? Were you asked about the absence?": "Shugaban makaranta ya tambaye ku game da fashin? An tambaye ku game da fashin?", "hindiyyun": "hindiyyun", "'iraaqiyyun": "'iraaqiyyun", "Iraqi": "Ba'iraƙe", "To say": "Don faɗin", "“from, of”": "“daga, na”", ") add": ") ƙara", ". Also: a name with": ". Haka kuma: suna mai", "drops it when called:": "yana sauke shi idan ana kiran mutum:", "= either … or.": "yana nufin ko dai … ko kuma.", "So you are Pakistani.": "To kai ɗan Pakistan ne.", "the Prophet's Mosque": "Masallacin Annabi", "Hasan, can you mention a verse?": "Hasan, za ka iya ambaton wata aya?", "A noun in Arabic is either masculine or feminine.": "Suna a Larabci ko dai namiji ne ko kuma mace.", "Ibrahim is either sick or travelling.": "Ibrahim ko dai ba shi da lafiya ko kuma yana tafiya.", "al-muḥarramu": "al-muḥarramu", "Muharram": "Muharram", "ṣafarun": "ṣafarun", "Safar": "Safar", "rabee'un l-awwalu … dhul-ḥijjati": "rabee'un l-awwalu … dhul-ḥijjati", "Rabi' al-Awwal … Dhul-Hijjah": "Rabi'ul Awwal … Zul Hijja", "The 12 Islamic months:": "Watanni 12 na Musulunci:", "the restaurant": "gidan abinci", "it was stolen": "an sace shi", "he was born": "an haife shi", "he compensated": "ya biya diyya, ya maye gurbi", "a soldier": "soja", "a spy": "ɗan leƙen asiri", "a war (f)": "yaƙi (mace)", "clearly": "a fili, sarari", "the Hijrah": "Hijira", "the birth (of Christ), AD": "haihuwar Annabi Isa, miladiyya", "Ramadan": "Ramadan", "al-maṭ'amu": "al-maṭ'amu", "suriqa (yusraqu)": "suriqa (yusraqu)", "wulida (yuwladu)": "wulida (yuwladu)", "'awwaḍa": "'awwaḍa", "jundiyyun (pl. junuudun)": "jundiyyun (jam'i: junuudun)", "jaasuusun (pl. jawaaseesu)": "jaasuusun (jam'i: jawaaseesu)", "ḥarbun (pl. ḥuruubun)": "ḥarbun (jam'i: ḥuruubun)", "biwuḍuuḥin": "biwuḍuuḥin", "al-hijratu": "al-hijratu", "al-meelaadu": "al-meelaadu", "ramaḍaanu": "ramaḍaanu", "either … or": "ko dai … ko kuma", "the deputy of the doer": "madadin mai aikatawa (na'ibul fa'il)", "Why were you late, brothers? Because the restaurant opened late today. When did it open? At six.": "Me ya sa kuka makara, 'yan'uwa? Saboda an buɗe gidan abincin a makare yau. Yaushe aka buɗe shi? Ƙarfe shida.", "Sit down and open the book. Where is your book, Idris? My book was stolen, teacher.": "Ku zauna ku buɗe littafi. Ina littafinka, Idris? An sace littafina, malam.", "It was stolen from my room last night while I was away. Other things were stolen with it: my watch, my shoes and most of my clothes. May Allah compensate you.": "An sace shi daga ɗakina a daren jiya lokacin ba na nan. An sace wasu abubuwa tare da shi: agogona, takalmana da yawancin tufafina. Allah Ya maye maka.", "In which month was the Messenger of Allah born? In Rabi' al-Awwal. He was born in the year 570 AD.": "A wane wata aka haifi Manzon Allah? A Rabi'ul Awwal. An haife shi a shekara ta 570 miladiyya.", "Where were you born, Ahmad? In Pakistan. So you are Pakistani.": "A ina aka haife ka, Ahmad? A Pakistan. To kai ɗan Pakistan ne.", "The soldier killed the spy; the spy was killed. People hear the adhan clearly; the adhan is heard clearly.": "Sojan ya kashe ɗan leƙen asirin; an kashe ɗan leƙen asirin. Mutane suna jin kiran sallah a fili; ana jin kiran sallah a fili.", "Surat al-Fatihah is read in every rak'ah. The bell is not heard in this class. Since when? For two weeks or more.": "Ana karanta Suratul Fatiha a kowace raka'a. Ba a jin ƙararrawa a wannan ajin. Tun yaushe? Tun makonni biyu ko fiye.", "Damma on the first letter,": "Ɗamma a kan harafin farko,", "Damma on the first letter, kasra before the last.": "Ɗamma a kan harafin farko, kasra a gaban na ƙarshe.", "Passive:": "Majhuli:", "before the last.": "a gaban na ƙarshe.", "Damma on the first letter, fatha before the last.": "Ɗamma a kan harafin farko, fataha a gaban na ƙarshe.", "Drop the doer; the object takes -u.": "Cire mai aikatawa; wanda aka yi wa aiki ya ɗauki -u.", "Make the sentence passive": "Mayar da jumlar majhuli", "Make it passive:": "Mayar da ita majhuli:", "The word that takes the doer's place.": "Kalmar da take ɗaukar matsayin mai aikatawa.", "Find": "Nemo", "Choose the month.": "Zaɓi watan.", "The Islamic months": "Watannin Musulunci", "the 12th month (the Hajj month)": "wata na 12 (watan Hajji)", "the 9th month (the fasting month)": "wata na 9 (watan azumi)", "the 3rd month (the Prophet was born)": "wata na 3 (an haifi Annabi)", "the 1st month": "wata na 1", "My book was stolen, teacher.": "An sace littafina, malam.", "Listen, then write the word. (the Hijrah)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (Hijira)", "The restaurant opens at six o'clock.": "Ana buɗe gidan abincin ƙarfe shida.", "the 10th month (Eid al-Fitr)": "wata na 10 (Ƙaramar Sallah)", "✅ Write: the Hijrah": "✅ Rubuta: Hijira", "✅ The restaurant opens at six o'clock.": "✅ Ana buɗe gidan abincin ƙarfe shida.", "✅ the 10th month (Eid al-Fitr)": "✅ wata na 10 (Ƙaramar Sallah)", "✅ My book was stolen, teacher.": "✅ An sace littafina, malam.", "In this lesson you will make two kinds of noun from a verb. The doer noun,": "A wannan darasin za ka yi nau'ukan suna guda biyu daga fi'ili. Sunan mai aikatawa (ismul fa'il),", "is on the pattern": "yana kan wazanin", "gives": "yana bayar da", "a thief. The done-to noun,": "ɓarawo. Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki (ismul maf'ul),", "stolen. You will also learn": "abin da aka sata. Za ka kuma koyi", "that works like": "da take aiki kamar", "I am not unaware.": "ni ba gafali ba ne.", "names the one who does the action. It is on the pattern": "yana sunanta wanda yake yin aikin. Yana kan wazanin", "a thief.": "ɓarawo.", "a scholar.": "malami, masani.", "a writer.": "marubuci.", "names the thing the action is done to. It is on the pattern": "yana sunanta abin da aka yi wa aikin. Yana kan wazanin", "stolen.": "abin da aka sata.", "written.": "abin da aka rubuta.", "broken.": "abin da ya karye.", "can work like": "tana iya aiki kamar", "The second word takes": "Kalma ta biyu tana ɗaukar", "Or it takes": "Ko kuma ta ɗauki", "ends in a vowel, so the vowel drops in the command:": "yana ƙarewa da wasali, don haka wasalin yana faɗuwa a umarni:", "And after": "Da kuma bayan", "سَارِقٌ (a thief)": "سَارِقٌ (ɓarawo)", "مَسْرُوقٌ (stolen)": "مَسْرُوقٌ (abin da aka sata)", "Doer noun": "Sunan mai aikatawa", "Done-to noun": "Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki", "Which noun?": "Wane suna?", "مَا like لَيْسَ": "مَا kamar لَيْسَ", "In this lesson you will make two kinds of noun from a verb. The doer noun, اسْمُ الْفَاعِلِ, is on the pattern فَاعِلٌ: سَرَقَ gives سَارِقٌ, a thief. The done-to noun, اسْمُ الْمَفْعُولِ, is on the pattern مَفْعُولٌ: مَسْرُوقٌ, stolen. You will also learn مَا that works like لَيْسَ, as in مَا أَنَا بِغَافِلٍ, I am not unaware.": "A wannan darasin za ka yi nau'ukan suna guda biyu daga fi'ili. Sunan mai aikatawa, اسْمُ الْفَاعِلِ, yana kan wazanin فَاعِلٌ: سَرَقَ yana bayar da سَارِقٌ, ɓarawo. Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki, اسْمُ الْمَفْعُولِ, yana kan wazanin مَفْعُولٌ: مَسْرُوقٌ, abin da aka sata. Za ka kuma koyi مَا da take aiki kamar لَيْسَ, kamar a مَا أَنَا بِغَافِلٍ, ni ba gafali ba ne.", "saraqa yasriqu": "saraqa yasriqu", "saariqun": "saariqun", "he stole": "ya yi sata", "he steals": "yana sata", "names the one who": "yana sunanta wanda yake", "does": "yin", "the action. From a three-letter verb it is on the pattern": "aikin. Daga fi'ili mai harafi uku yana kan wazanin", "You have all passed, praise be to Allah.": "Dukanku kun ci jarrabawa, alhamdu lillah.", "Who is the writer of this on the board?": "Wane ne ya rubuta wannan a kan allo?", "Is anyone going to the market today? I am going, in sha Allah.": "Akwai wanda zai je kasuwa yau? Ni zan je, in sha Allah.", "You are a good reciter. Are you a hafiz? Yes.": "Kai mai karatu ne nagari. Kai mahaddaci ne? Ee.", "As for the male thief and the female thief, cut off their hands.": "Ɓarawo namiji da ɓarauniya mace, ku yanke hannayensu.", "suriqa yusraqu": "suriqa yusraqu", "masruuqun": "masruuqun", "it is stolen": "ana sace shi", "stolen": "abin da aka sata", "names the thing the action is": "yana sunanta abin da aka", "done to": "yi wa aikin", ". It comes from the passive verb, on the pattern": ". Yana fitowa daga fi'ili majhuli, a kan wazanin", "the one who stole": "wanda ya yi sata", "the stolen money": "kuɗin da aka sata", "We found it written when we entered the class.": "Mun same shi a rubuce lokacin da muka shiga aji.", "The class is left open, so students come in from different sides.": "Ana barin ajin a buɗe, don haka ɗalibai suna shigowa ta ɓangarori daban-daban.", "The lock is broken.": "Makullin ya karye.", "Don't you know that going out during the lesson is not allowed?": "Ba ka san cewa ba a yarda a fita lokacin darasi ba?", "The principal said to the two students: which of you is the hitter and which the one hit?": "Shugaban makaranta ya ce wa ɗaliban biyu: wane ne a cikinku ya yi dukan, wane ne kuma aka daka?", "maa ana bighaafilin": "maa ana bighaafilin", "I am not unaware": "ni ba gafali ba ne", "maa haadhaa basharan": "maa haadhaa basharan", "This is not a human": "Wannan ba mutum ba ne", "): the first word keeps -u and the second takes": "): kalma ta farko tana riƙe -u kuma ta biyu tana ɗaukar", ". Often the second word has": ". Sau da yawa kalma ta biyu tana da", "I am not unaware of what you are doing, Mansur.": "Ni ba gafali ba ne game da abin da kake yi, Mansur.", "And Allah is not unaware of what you do.": "Kuma Allah ba Ya gafala ga abin da kuke aikatawa.", "This is not a human being.": "Wannan ba mutum ba ne.", "You are hardworking": "Kai mai ƙoƙari ne", "You are not hardworking.": "Kai ba mai ƙoƙari ba ne.", "ishtaraa yashtaree": "ishtaraa yashtaree", "ishtari": "ishtari", "he buys": "yana saye", "buy!": "saya!", "(he bought) ends in a vowel, so the vowel drops in the command and after": "(ya saya) yana ƙarewa da wasali, don haka wasalin yana faɗuwa a umarni da bayan", "For how much did you buy this watch?": "Nawa ka sayi wannan agogon?", "Please buy a good lock.": "Don Allah ka sayi makulli mai kyau.", "Don't buy this dictionary. Buy that one, it is better.": "Kada ka sayi wannan ƙamus ɗin. Sayi wancan, shi ya fi kyau.", "a result": "sakamako", "the monthly test": "jarrabawar wata-wata", "failing (a student)": "mai faɗuwa (ɗalibi)", "a lock": "makulli, kwaɗo", "a reciter": "mai karatu", "one who has memorised (the Qur'an)": "mahaddaci (na Alƙur'ani)", "the photocopier": "injin kwafi", "the orphan": "maraya", "one who takes care of": "mai ɗaukar nauyi", "he took the chance": "ya yi amfani da dama", "nateejatun": "nateejatun", "al-ikhtibaarush-shahriyyu": "al-ikhtibaarush-shahriyyu", "raasibun": "raasibun", "qufulun (pl. aqfaalun)": "qufulun (jam'i: aqfaalun)", "qaari'un": "qaari'un", "ḥaafiẓun": "ḥaafiẓun", "an-naasikhu": "an-naasikhu", "al-yateemu (pl. aytaamun)": "al-yateemu (jam'i: aytaamun)", "kaafilun": "kaafilun", "ightanama": "ightanama", "the doer noun": "sunan mai aikatawa", "the done-to noun": "sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki", "We want to know the monthly test result, teacher. How many failed in our class? You all passed, praise Allah.": "Muna so mu san sakamakon jarrabawar wata-wata, malam. Mutum nawa suka faɗi a ajinmu? Dukanku kun ci, alhamdu lillah.", "We are glad. Did anyone fail in the other classes? Yes, but those who failed are few.": "Mun yi farin ciki. Akwai wanda ya faɗi a sauran azuzuwa? Ee, amma waɗanda suka faɗi kaɗan ne.", "Who wrote this on the board? We don't know. We found it written when we came in. The class is left open.": "Wane ne ya rubuta wannan a kan allo? Ba mu sani ba. Mun same shi a rubuce lokacin da muka shigo. Ana barin ajin a buɗe.", "What shall we do? The lock is broken. Is anyone going to the market today? I am, in sha Allah. Please buy a good lock.": "Me za mu yi? Makullin ya karye. Akwai wanda zai je kasuwa yau? Ni zan je, in sha Allah. Don Allah ka sayi makulli mai kyau.", "Ma sha Allah! You are a good reciter. I haven't heard you recite before. Are you a hafiz? Yes.": "Ma sha Allah! Kai mai karatu ne nagari. Ban taɓa jin ka karanta ba a da. Kai mahaddaci ne? Ee.", "I am not unaware of what you're doing, Mansur. Please let me go out; I want to go to the photocopier.": "Ni ba gafali ba ne game da abin da kake yi, Mansur. Don Allah ka bar ni in fita; ina so in je wurin injin kwafi.", "I won't allow that. Don't you know going out during the lesson is not allowed? I'm sorry, teacher.": "Ba zan yarda da haka ba. Ba ka san cewa ba a yarda a fita lokacin darasi ba? Ka yi haƙuri, malam.", "Make the doer noun.": "Yi sunan mai aikatawa.", "Doer noun:": "Sunan mai aikatawa:", "Make the done-to noun.": "Yi sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki.", "Done-to noun:": "Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "Doer or done-to?": "Mai aikatawa ko wanda aka yi wa aiki?", "Look at the underlined idea: the -ـِلٌ / مَفْـ word.": "Duba ma'anar da aka ja wa layi: kalmar -ـِلٌ / مَفْـ.", "The second word takes -a, or comes with": "Kalma ta biyu tana ɗaukar -a, ko tana zuwa da", "أَنْتَ مُجْتَهِدٌ. (not)": "أَنْتَ مُجْتَهِدٌ. (ba)", "هُوَ قَرِيبٌ. (not)": "هُوَ قَرِيبٌ. (ba)", "نَحْنُ تُجَّارٌ. (not)": "نَحْنُ تُجَّارٌ. (ba)", "أَنَا قَارِئٌ. (not)": "أَنَا قَارِئٌ. (ba)", "“Don't buy this car.”": "“Kada ka sayi wannan motar.”", "“What do you want to buy?”": "“Me kake so ka saya?”", "“Buy that one.”": "“Sayi wancan.”", "I am not unaware of what you are doing.": "Ni ba gafali ba ne game da abin da kake yi.", "أَنَا غَافِلٌ. (not)": "أَنَا غَافِلٌ. (ba)", "Going out during the lesson is not allowed.": "Ba a yarda a fita lokacin darasi ba.", "✅ “Don't buy this car.”": "✅ “Kada ka sayi wannan motar.”", "✅ Going out during the lesson is not allowed.": "✅ Ba a yarda a fita lokacin darasi ba.", "✅ The lock is broken.": "✅ Makullin ya karye.", "✅ “Buy that one.”": "✅ “Sayi wancan.”", "In this lesson you will make doer and done-to nouns from weak and doubled verbs. From": "A wannan darasin za ka yi sunan mai aikatawa da na wanda aka yi wa aiki daga fi'iloli masu rauni da mudha'af. Daga", "From": "Daga", "the done-to noun is": "sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki shi ne", "and the done-to noun is": "kuma sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki shi ne", "You will also learn the passive of hollow verbs:": "Za ka kuma koyi majhulin fi'iloli ajwaf:", "it was said, and": "an ce, da", "it is sold.": "ana sayar da shi.", "From a hollow verb the doer noun has a hamza in the middle:": "Daga fi'ili ajwaf sunan mai aikatawa yana da hamza a tsakiya:", "a visitor.": "baƙo mai ziyara.", "fasting.": "mai azumi.", "The passive of hollow verbs: past": "Majhulin fi'iloli ajwaf: shuɗaɗɗen lokaci", "The done-to noun:": "Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "From a verb ending in a vowel, the doer noun ends in -in:": "Daga fi'ili mai ƙarewa da wasali, sunan mai aikatawa yana ƙarewa da -in:", "invited.": "wanda aka gayyata.", "built.": "wanda aka gina.", "From a doubled verb the doer noun has a shadda:": "Daga fi'ili mudha'af sunan mai aikatawa yana da shadda:", "a pilgrim.": "alhaji, mahajjaci.", "The done-to noun is regular:": "Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki yana bin ƙa'ida:", "counted.": "wanda aka ƙirga.", "قِيلَ (it was said)": "قِيلَ (an ce)", "Hollow passive": "Majhulin ajwaf", "دَاعٍ or الدَّاعِي": "دَاعٍ ko الدَّاعِي", "In this lesson you will make doer and done-to nouns from weak and doubled verbs. From قَالَ, the doer is قَائِلٌ. From بَاعَ, the done-to noun is مَبِيعٌ. From دَعَا, the doer is دَاعٍ and the done-to noun is مَدْعُوٌّ. From حَجَّ, the doer is حَاجٌّ. You will also learn the passive of hollow verbs: قِيلَ, it was said, and يُبَاعُ, it is sold.": "A wannan darasin za ka yi sunan mai aikatawa da na wanda aka yi wa aiki daga fi'iloli masu rauni da mudha'af. Daga قَالَ, mai aikatawa shi ne قَائِلٌ. Daga بَاعَ, sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki shi ne مَبِيعٌ. Daga دَعَا, mai aikatawa shi ne دَاعٍ kuma sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki shi ne مَدْعُوٌّ. Daga حَجَّ, mai aikatawa shi ne حَاجٌّ. Za ka kuma koyi majhulin fi'iloli ajwaf: قِيلَ, an ce, da يُبَاعُ, ana sayar da shi.", "qaa'ilun": "qaa'ilun", "baa'i'un": "baa'i'un", "zaa'irun": "zaa'irun", "one who says": "mai faɗa", "a seller": "mai sayarwa", "a visitor": "baƙo mai ziyara", "From a": "Daga fi'ili", "hollow": "ajwaf", "verb (long middle vowel) the doer noun has": "(mai dogon wasali a tsakiya) sunan mai aikatawa yana da", "in the middle:": "a tsakiya:", "Are you a new student? No, I am a visitor.": "Kai sabon ɗalibi ne? A'a, ni baƙo ne mai ziyara.", "Are you fasting?": "Kana azumi?", "Are you still asleep? Get up, the Asr adhan has been called.": "Har yanzu kana barci? Tashi, an kira sallar La'asar.", "qeela": "qeela", "it was said": "an ce", "bee'a": "bee'a", "it was sold": "an sayar da shi", "yuqaalu": "yuqaalu", "it is said": "ana cewa", "yubaa'u": "yubaa'u", "it is sold": "ana sayar da shi", "of hollow verbs: past": "na fi'iloli ajwaf: shuɗaɗɗen lokaci", "(long": "(dogon", "); present": "); mudari'i", "). The done-to noun:": "). Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "I was told that it is the best institute for teaching Arabic.": "An gaya mini cewa ita ce mafi kyawun cibiyar koyar da Larabci.", "These books are not sold. You can get them free of charge.": "Ba a sayar da waɗannan littattafan. Kana iya samunsu kyauta.", "Goods sold are not returned unless they are faulty.": "Ba a mayar da kayan da aka sayar sai dai idan suna da lahani.", "daa'in": "daa'in", "mad'uwwun": "mad'uwwun", "saaqin": "saaqin", "one who calls": "mai kira", "invited": "wanda aka gayyata", "one who serves drinks": "mai shayarwa, mai zuba abin sha", "From a verb": "Daga fi'ili", "ending in a vowel": "mai ƙarewa da wasali", ": the doer noun ends in": ": sunan mai aikatawa yana ƙarewa da", ". The done-to noun:": ". Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "A server comes in and pours them coffee.": "Wani mai shayarwa ya shigo ya zuba musu kofi.", "I am invited to attend a conference in Pakistan in a few months.": "An gayyace ni in halarci wani taro a Pakistan nan da 'yan watanni.", "And for every people there is a guide.": "Kuma kowace al'umma tana da mai shiryarwa.", "How beautiful this house built of stone is!": "Wannan gidan da aka gina da dutse yana da kyau sosai!", "ḥaajjun": "ḥaajjun", "ma'duudun": "ma'duudun", "a pilgrim": "alhaji, mahajjaci", "counted": "wanda aka ƙirga", "doubled": "mudha'af", "verb the doer noun has a": "fi'ili sunan mai aikatawa yana da", "(from": "(daga", ". The done-to noun is regular:": ". Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki yana bin ƙa'ida:", "I came as a pilgrim, so I took this chance to visit your famous institute.": "Na zo a matsayin mahajjaci, don haka na yi amfani da wannan damar in ziyarci shahararriyar cibiyarku.", "The one who guides to good is like the one who does it.": "Wanda ya nuna hanyar alheri kamar wanda ya aikata shi ne.", "The one passing greets the one sitting.": "Mai wucewa yana yi wa wanda yake zaune sallama.", "a lecturer": "malamin jami'a, mai lacca", "a chance": "dama", "a syllabus, method": "manhaja, tsarin karatu", "a period of time": "wani lokaci", "free of charge": "kyauta, ba tare da biya ba", "a conference": "taro", "have a safe journey": "Allah Ya kiyaye hanya", "zaa'irun (pl. zuwwaarun)": "zaa'irun (jam'i: zuwwaarun)", "muḥaaḍirun": "muḥaaḍirun", "furṣatun (pl. furaṣun)": "furṣatun (jam'i: furaṣun)", "manhajun (pl. manaahiju)": "manhajun (jam'i: manaahiju)", "muddatun": "muddatun", "majjaanan": "majjaanan", "mu'tamarun": "mu'tamarun", "saaqin (as-saaqee)": "saaqin (as-saaqee)", "ṣaḥibatkas-salaamatu": "ṣaḥibatkas-salaamatu", "Come in. And peace be upon you. Are you a new student? No, I am a visitor.": "Shigo. Wa alaikumus salam. Kai sabon ɗalibi ne? A'a, ni baƙo ne mai ziyara.", "I am from Pakistan, a lecturer at the Arabic institute in Lahore. I came as a pilgrim, so I took this chance to visit your famous institute.": "Ni daga Pakistan nake, malami a cibiyar Larabci da ke Lahore. Na zo a matsayin mahajjaci, don haka na yi amfani da wannan damar in ziyarci shahararriyar cibiyarku.", "I was told it is the best institute for teaching Arabic to non-native speakers.": "An gaya mini cewa ita ce mafi kyawun cibiyar koyar da Larabci ga waɗanda ba Larabawa ba.", "The period of study is two years. This is a copy of the syllabus, a gift for you.": "Tsawon lokacin karatu shekara biyu ne. Ga kwafin manhajar, kyauta ce gare ka.", "Where can I buy these books? These books are not sold. You can get them free.": "A ina zan iya sayen waɗannan littattafan? Ba a sayar da waɗannan littattafan. Kana iya samunsu kyauta.", "I am invited to a conference in Pakistan in a few months. I will take the chance to visit your institute, in sha Allah.": "An gayyace ni wani taro a Pakistan nan da 'yan watanni. Zan yi amfani da damar in ziyarci cibiyarku, in sha Allah.", "Shall I pour you more coffee, shaikh? No, thank you. Goodbye. Have a safe journey.": "In ƙara maka kofi, shehi? A'a, na gode. Sai an jima. Allah Ya kiyaye hanya.", "Past: long": "Shuɗaɗɗen lokaci: dogon", ". Present: long": ". Mudari'i: dogon", "Present: long": "Mudari'i: dogon", ": -in. With": ": -in. Tare da", ": -ee.": ": -ee.", "وَلِكُلِّ قَوْمٍ …… (a guide)": "وَلِكُلِّ قَوْمٍ …… (mai shiryarwa)", "جَاءَ …… (a server)": "جَاءَ …… (mai shayarwa)", "أَنَا …… لِحُضُورِ مُؤْتَمَرٍ (invited)": "أَنَا …… لِحُضُورِ مُؤْتَمَرٍ (wanda aka gayyata)", "هٰذَا …… (the caller)": "هٰذَا …… (mai kiran)", "These books are not sold.": "Ba a sayar da waɗannan littattafan.", "I am a visitor.": "Ni baƙo ne mai ziyara.", "سَاقٍ or السَّاقِي?": "سَاقٍ ko السَّاقِي?", "Listen, then write the word. (a visitor)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (baƙo mai ziyara)", "✅ I am a visitor.": "✅ Ni baƙo ne mai ziyara.", "✅ These books are not sold.": "✅ Ba a sayar da waɗannan littattafan.", "✅ Write: a visitor": "✅ Rubuta: baƙo mai ziyara", "In this lesson you will learn nouns that name the place or the time of an action. They are on two patterns.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi sunayen da suke sunanta wurin ko lokacin aiki (ismuz zaman wal makan). Suna kan wazanai biyu.", "a place to play, and": "wurin wasa, da", "a place to write. And": "wurin rubutu (ofis). Da kuma", "a place to sit,": "wurin zama,", "a place to stop, and": "wurin tsayawa, da", "an appointed time.": "lokacin da aka ƙayyade.", "names the time or place of an action. It is on the pattern": "yana sunanta lokaci ko wurin aiki. Yana kan wazanin", "the car park.": "wurin ajiye motoci.", "is used when the present verb has": "ana amfani da shi idan fi'ilin mudari'i yana da", "And when the verb ends in a vowel:": "Da kuma idan fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da wasali:", "And for verbs starting with": "Da kuma ga fi'iloli masu farawa da", "مَلْعَبٌ (a playground)": "مَلْعَبٌ (filin wasa)", "مَوْعِدٌ (an appointment)": "مَوْعِدٌ (lokacin alƙawari)", "Make the place noun": "Yi sunan wuri", "In this lesson you will learn nouns that name the place or the time of an action. They are on two patterns. مَفْعَلٌ, as in مَلْعَبٌ, a place to play, and مَكْتَبٌ, a place to write. And مَفْعِلٌ, as in مَجْلِسٌ, a place to sit, مَوْقِفٌ, a place to stop, and مَوْعِدٌ, an appointed time.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi sunayen da suke sunanta wurin ko lokacin aiki. Suna kan wazanai biyu. مَفْعَلٌ, kamar a مَلْعَبٌ, wurin wasa, da مَكْتَبٌ, wurin rubutu. Da kuma مَفْعِلٌ, kamar a مَجْلِسٌ, wurin zama, مَوْقِفٌ, wurin tsayawa, da مَوْعِدٌ, lokacin da aka ƙayyade.", "wa'ada ya'idu": "wa'ada ya'idu", "maw'idun": "maw'idun", "an appointed time or place": "lokaci ko wurin alƙawari", "names the": "yana sunanta", "time": "lokaci", "place": "wuri", "of an action. From a three-letter verb it is on the pattern": "na aiki. Daga fi'ili mai harafi uku yana kan wazanin", "(the time of travel),": "(lokacin tafiya),", "(the car park).": "(wurin ajiye motoci).", "You must be there half an hour before the time of departure.": "Wajibi ne ka kasance a can rabin awa kafin lokacin tashi.", "We meet in the car park at the university.": "Za mu haɗu a wurin ajiye motoci na jami'a.", "Indeed, their appointed time is the morning. Is not the morning near?": "Lalle lokacin alƙawarinsu safiya ce. Shin safiya ba ta kusa ba?", "mal'abun": "mal'abun", "a playground": "filin wasa", "(fatha) is used when the present verb has a": "(fataha) ana amfani da shi idan fi'ilin mudari'i yana da", "fatha or damma": "fataha ko ɗamma", ". Also when the verb": ". Haka kuma idan fi'ilin", "ends in a vowel": "yana ƙarewa da wasali", ". Hollow:": ". Ajwaf:", "a place to play ⚽": "wurin wasa ⚽", "an office 🗄️": "ofis 🗄️", "an entrance 🚪": "ƙofar shiga 🚪", "a kitchen 🍳": "kicin, madafa 🍳", "a course, channel": "hanya, mashiga", "the place of Tawaf 🕋": "wurin ɗawafi 🕋", "majlisun": "majlisun", "mawqifun": "mawqifun", "a sitting place": "wurin zama", "a stopping place": "wurin tsayawa", "(kasra) is used when the present verb has a": "(kasra) ana amfani da shi idan fi'ilin mudari'i yana da", ". And for verbs": ". Da kuma ga fi'iloli", "starting with": "masu farawa da", ". Some take": ". Wasu suna ɗaukar", "مَفْعَلٌ: middle -a / -u in the present": "مَفْعَلٌ: tsakiya -a / -u a mudari'i", "مَفْعِلٌ: middle -i, or a وَ- verb": "مَفْعِلٌ: tsakiya -i, ko fi'ili mai farawa da وَ-", "a sitting place 🪑": "wurin zama 🪑", "a house, a stop 🏠": "gida, wurin sauka 🏠", "a stopping place 🅿️": "wurin tsayawa 🅿️", "an appointment ⏰": "lokacin alƙawari ⏰", "a place 📍": "wuri 📍", "with ة 🏫": "tare da ة 🏫", "a trip": "tafiya, ziyara", "a participant": "mai shiga, ɗan takara", "ready": "a shirye", "a bag": "jaka", "the crowd": "cunkoso", "the place of Sa'y": "wurin sa'ayi", "the place of Tawaf": "wurin ɗawafi", "he met": "ya haɗu da", "he caught up with": "ya riski", "al-mushrifu": "al-mushrifu", "riḥlatun": "riḥlatun", "mushtarikun": "mushtarikun", "musta'iddun": "musta'iddun", "ḥaqeebatun (pl. ḥaqaa'ibu)": "ḥaqeebatun (jam'i: ḥaqaa'ibu)", "az-ziḥaamu": "az-ziḥaamu", "al-mas'aa": "al-mas'aa", "al-maṭaafu": "al-maṭaafu", "iltaqaa (yaltaqee)": "iltaqaa (yaltaqee)", "laḥiqa (yalḥaqu)": "laḥiqa (yalḥaqu)", "noun of time": "sunan lokaci", "noun of place": "sunan wuri", "Are you the participants in the Hajj trip? Yes. You are now eighteen. Where are Hamid and Abdul-Hadi?": "Ku ne masu shiga tafiyar Hajji? Ee. Yanzu ku goma sha takwas ne. Ina Hamid da Abdulhadi?", "Hamid is in the restaurant; Abdul-Hadi went to the bank. They will come in ten minutes, in sha Allah.": "Hamid yana gidan abinci; Abdulhadi ya tafi banki. Za su zo nan da minti goma, in sha Allah.", "Are you ready? In sha Allah. When is the trip? At three o'clock, by Allah's leave.": "Kun shirya? In sha Allah. Yaushe tafiyar take? Ƙarfe uku, da izinin Allah.", "Where do we meet? In the university car park. You must be there half an hour before departure.": "A ina za mu haɗu? A wurin ajiye motoci na jami'a. Wajibi ne ku kasance a can rabin awa kafin tashi.", "Bring your bags, and put them in the car parked in front of the dormitory entrance.": "Ku kawo jakunkunanku, ku sa su a motar da take tsaye a gaban ƙofar shiga ɗakin kwana.", "We are going on the seventh day. I fear the crowd will be very heavy at the Tawaf and Sa'y places.": "Za mu tafi a rana ta bakwai. Ina tsoron cunkoso zai yi yawa sosai a wurin ɗawafi da na sa'ayi.", "Don't be afraid. Allah makes it easy. I am going to my office. Don't forget our appointment is half past two in the car park.": "Kada ka ji tsoro. Allah Yana sauƙaƙawa. Zan tafi ofishina. Kada ka manta alƙawarinmu ƙarfe biyu da rabi a wurin ajiye motoci.", "Middle -a -u in the present: use": "Tsakiya -a -u a mudari'i: yi amfani da", "Middle -a/-u in the present →": "Tsakiya -a/-u a mudari'i →", ". Middle -i or": ". Tsakiya -i ko", "- verb →": "- fi'ili →", "Place / time noun:": "Sunan wuri / lokaci:", "Middle": "Tsakiya", "- verb: use": "- fi'ili: yi amfani da", "Places and times.": "Wurare da lokuta.", "“the place of Tawaf”": "“wurin ɗawafi”", "“the car park”": "“wurin ajiye motoci”", "“the time of departure”": "“lokacin tashi”", "“the kitchen”": "“kicin”", "“the playground”": "“filin wasa”", "Which word is": "Wace kalma ce", "Find the place or time noun": "Nemo sunan wuri ko lokaci", "half an hour before departure time": "rabin awa kafin lokacin tashi", "مَفْعَلٌ or مَفْعِلٌ?": "مَفْعَلٌ ko مَفْعِلٌ?", "We meet in the car park.": "Za mu haɗu a wurin ajiye motoci.", "“the entrance of the dormitory”": "“ƙofar shiga ɗakin kwana”", "✅ We meet in the car park.": "✅ Za mu haɗu a wurin ajiye motoci.", "✅ “the entrance of the dormitory”": "✅ “ƙofar shiga ɗakin kwana”", "✅ “the place of Tawaf”": "✅ “wurin ɗawafi”", "✅ “the car park”": "✅ “wurin ajiye motoci”", "✅ “the playground”": "✅ “filin wasa”", "✅ “the kitchen”": "✅ “kicin”", "✅ half an hour before departure time": "✅ rabin awa kafin lokacin tashi", "In this lesson you will learn nouns that name a tool,": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi sunayen da suke sunanta kayan aiki (ismul ala),", "They have three patterns.": "Suna da wazanai uku.", "a key, from": "mabuɗi, daga", "to open.": "buɗewa.", "a file, and": "kartaki, da", "scissors. And": "almakashi. Da kuma", "a broom, and": "tsintsiya, da", "a spoon.": "cokali.", "names the tool used for an action. It has three patterns. The first is": "yana sunanta kayan aikin da ake yin aiki da shi. Yana da wazanai uku. Na farko shi ne", "a key.": "mabuɗi.", "scales.": "ma'auni.", "The second pattern is": "Wazani na biyu shi ne", "a file.": "kartaki.", "scissors.": "almakashi.", "a lift. The third is": "lif. Na uku shi ne", "a broom.": "tsintsiya.", "a hammer. From verbs ending in a vowel:": "guduma. Daga fi'iloli masu ƙarewa da wasali:", "means woe to:": "yana nufin bone ya tabbata ga:", "woe to those who give short measure.": "bone ya tabbata ga masu tauye mudu.", "مِفْتَاحٌ (a key)": "مِفْتَاحٌ (mabuɗi)", "tool nouns": "sunayen kayan aiki", "Make the tool noun": "Yi sunan kayan aiki", "Which pattern?": "Wane wazani?", "Kind of noun": "Irin suna", "In this lesson you will learn nouns that name a tool, اسْمُ الْآلَةِ. They have three patterns. مِفْعَالٌ, as in مِفْتَاحٌ, a key, from فَتَحَ, to open. مِفْعَلٌ, as in مِبْرَدٌ, a file, and مِقَصٌّ, scissors. And مِفْعَلَةٌ, as in مِكْنَسَةٌ, a broom, and مِلْعَقَةٌ, a spoon.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi sunayen da suke sunanta kayan aiki, اسْمُ الْآلَةِ. Suna da wazanai uku. مِفْعَالٌ, kamar a مِفْتَاحٌ, mabuɗi, daga فَتَحَ, buɗewa. مِفْعَلٌ, kamar a مِبْرَدٌ, kartaki, da مِقَصٌّ, almakashi. Da kuma مِفْعَلَةٌ, kamar a مِكْنَسَةٌ, tsintsiya, da مِلْعَقَةٌ, cokali.", "tool": "kayan aikin", "used to do an action. It has three patterns:": "da ake yin aiki da shi. Yana da wazanai uku:", ". Pattern 1,": ". Wazani na 1,", "(a saw)": "(zarto)", "(a plough)": "(garma)", "Bring the car key from my room.": "Kawo mabuɗin mota daga ɗakina.", "The cheese I bought from him a few days ago, I weighed it on our scales and found it short.": "Cukun da na saya a wurinsa 'yan kwanaki da suka wuce, na auna shi a ma'auninmu na same shi ya yi ƙasa.", "And do not give short measure and weight.": "Kuma kada ku tauye mudu da ma'auni.", "mibradun": "mibradun", "a file": "kartaki", "miqaṣṣun": "miqaṣṣun", "scissors": "almakashi", "miknasatun": "miknasatun", "Pattern 2,": "Wazani na 2,", "(a lift)": "(lif)", ". Pattern 3,": ". Wazani na 3,", "(a hammer)": "(guduma)", ". From verbs ending in a vowel:": ". Daga fi'iloli masu ƙarewa da wasali:", "I want a ladle, a frying pan, an iron and scissors.": "Ina son ludayi, kasko na soya, ƙarfen guga da almakashi.", "I want a ruler, an eraser and a sharpener.": "Ina son rula, gogi da mai fensir.", "I am at the door of the lift.": "Ina bakin ƙofar lif.", "waylun lil-muṭaffifeena": "waylun lil-muṭaffifeena", "Woe to those who give short measure.": "Bone ya tabbata ga masu tauye mudu.", "woe to": "bone ya tabbata ga", ". In the dialogue: the grocer gives short measure, so the son says:": ". A cikin tattaunawar: mai shagon yana tauye mudu, don haka ɗan ya ce:", "(I am at the lift door).": "(ina bakin ƙofar lif).", "This new grocer gives short measure, so don't buy anything from him.": "Wannan sabon mai shagon yana tauye mudu, don haka kada ka sayi komai a wurinsa.", "I will advise him and recite to him the words of Allah. Perhaps Allah will guide him.": "Zan yi masa nasiha in karanta masa maganar Allah. Watakila Allah Ya shiryar da shi.", "scales": "ma'auni", "a file (tool)": "kartaki (kayan aiki)", "a ladle": "ludayi", "a frying pan": "kasko na soya", "a ruler": "rula", "an eraser": "gogi", "a pencil sharpener": "mai fensir", "New words: tools": "Sababbin kalmomi: kayan aiki", "miftaaḥun (pl. mafaateeḥu)": "miftaaḥun (jam'i: mafaateeḥu)", "meezaanun (pl. mawaazeenu)": "meezaanun (jam'i: mawaazeenu)", "mighrafatun": "mighrafatun", "miqlaatun": "miqlaatun", "mil'aqatun (pl. malaa'iqu)": "mil'aqatun (jam'i: malaa'iqu)", "misṭaratun": "misṭaratun", "mimḥaatun": "mimḥaatun", "mibraatun": "mibraatun", "the style, model": "salo, irin ƙira", "wheat": "alkama", "one who gives short measure": "mai tauye mudu", "aṭ-ṭiraazu": "aṭ-ṭiraazu", "al-qamḥu": "al-qamḥu", "muṭaffifun": "muṭaffifun", "the noun of instrument": "sunan kayan aiki", "Do you want anything from the market, Umm Ahmad? Yes. A ladle, a frying pan, an iron and scissors.": "Kina son wani abu daga kasuwa, Ummu Ahmad? Ee. Ludayi, kasko na soya, ƙarfen guga da almakashi.", "How many requests you have, Umm Ahmad! Didn't I buy you these things last year?": "Buƙatunki sun yi yawa, Ummu Ahmad! Ban saya miki waɗannan abubuwan a bara ba?", "Yes, but they are the old style. Modern styles have now come to the market.": "Ee, amma tsohon salo ne. Sababbin salo sun shigo kasuwa yanzu.", "Listen, this new grocer gives short measure, so don't buy from him. Woe to those who give short measure. But how did you know?": "Saurara, wannan sabon mai shagon yana tauye mudu, don haka kada ka saya a wurinsa. Bone ya tabbata ga masu tauye mudu. Amma yaya kika gane?", "Do you want anything, Ahmad? Yes. I want a ruler, an eraser and a sharpener.": "Kana son wani abu, Ahmad? Ee. Ina son rula, gogi da mai fensir.", "Bring the car key from my room. I am at the lift door.": "Kawo mabuɗin mota daga ɗakina. Ina bakin ƙofar lif.", "Tool noun:": "Sunan kayan aiki:", "Review of the derived nouns.": "Bitar sunayen da aka samo daga fi'ili.", "place noun": "sunan wuri", "tool noun": "sunan kayan aiki", "Tool, place, doer or done-to?": "Kayan aiki, wuri, mai aikatawa ko wanda aka yi wa aiki?", "doer noun": "sunan mai aikatawa", "done-to noun": "sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki", "Bring the car key.": "Kawo mabuɗin mota.", "Listen, then write the word. (scissors)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (almakashi)", "✅ Write: scissors": "✅ Rubuta: almakashi", "✅ Woe to those who give short measure.": "✅ Bone ya tabbata ga masu tauye mudu.", "✅ Bring the car key.": "✅ Kawo mabuɗin mota.", "In this lesson you will learn the difference between an indefinite noun,": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi bambanci tsakanin suna nakira (wanda ba a sani ba),", "a man, and a definite noun,": "wani mutum, da suna ma'arifa (sananne),", "There are seven kinds of definite noun: pronouns, names, pointing words, joining words, nouns with": "Akwai nau'ukan suna ma'arifa guda bakwai: wakilan suna, sunayen yanka, kalmomin nuni, kalmomin haɗi, sunaye masu", "a noun joined to a definite noun, and a person called with": "sunan da aka rataya ga suna ma'arifa, da mutumin da aka kira da", "A noun is either": "Suna ko dai", "definite, pointing to something known, or": "ma'arifa ne, yana nuna abin da aka sani, ko kuma", "indefinite, anyone or anything.": "nakira, kowane mutum ko kowane abu.", "are indefinite.": "nakira ne.", "are definite.": "ma'arifa ne.", "There are seven kinds of definite noun. First, pronouns:": "Akwai nau'ukan suna ma'arifa guda bakwai. Na farko, wakilan suna:", "Second, names:": "Na biyu, sunayen yanka:", "Third, pointing words:": "Na uku, kalmomin nuni:", "Fourth, joining words:": "Na huɗu, kalmomin haɗi:", "Fifth, a noun with": "Na biyar, suna mai", "Sixth, a noun joined to a definite noun:": "Na shida, sunan da aka rataya ga suna ma'arifa:", "stays indefinite. Seventh, a particular person called with": "yana zama nakira. Na bakwai, takamaiman mutumin da aka kira da", "means give me.": "yana nufin ba ni.", "means it ran out:": "yana nufin ya ƙare:", "الْمَعْرِفَةُ وَالنَّكِرَةُ (definite and indefinite)": "الْمَعْرِفَةُ وَالنَّكِرَةُ (ma'arifa da nakira)", "Definite or not?": "Ma'arifa ko a'a?", "Which kind?": "Wane nau'i?", "Make it definite": "Mayar da shi ma'arifa", "In this lesson you will learn the difference between an indefinite noun, نَكِرَةٌ, like رَجُلٌ, a man, and a definite noun, مَعْرِفَةٌ, like مُحَمَّدٌ. There are seven kinds of definite noun: pronouns, names, pointing words, joining words, nouns with الْ, a noun joined to a definite noun, and a person called with يَا. You will also learn أَعْطِنِي, give me.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi bambanci tsakanin suna nakira, نَكِرَةٌ, kamar رَجُلٌ, wani mutum, da suna ma'arifa, مَعْرِفَةٌ, kamar مُحَمَّدٌ. Akwai nau'ukan suna ma'arifa guda bakwai: wakilan suna, sunayen yanka, kalmomin nuni, kalmomin haɗi, sunaye masu الْ, sunan da aka rataya ga suna ma'arifa, da mutumin da aka kira da يَا. Za ka kuma koyi أَعْطِنِي, ba ni.", "a man (indefinite)": "wani mutum (nakira)", "muḥammadun": "muḥammadun", "Muhammad (definite)": "Muhammad (ma'arifa)", "(definite: it points to someone or something known) or": "(ma'arifa: yana nuna wani ko wani abu sananne) ko", "(indefinite: anyone or anything):": "(nakira: kowane mutum ko kowane abu):", "نَكِرَةٌ: any one": "نَكِرَةٌ: kowane ɗaya", "مَعْرِفَةٌ: a known one": "مَعْرِفَةٌ: sananne", "Do you have pens?": "Kana da alƙaluma?", "Give me a pencil.": "Ba ni fensir.", "Give me that one.": "Ba ni wancan.", "This is a pencil.": "Wannan fensir ne.", "ana": "ana", "aḥmadu": "aḥmadu", "Ahmad": "Ahmad", "The definite nouns are": "Sunaye ma'arifa", "seven": "nau'i bakwai", "kinds: (1)": "ne: (1)", "pronouns:": "wakilan suna:", "names:": "sunayen yanka:", "pronouns": "wakilan suna", "pointing words": "kalmomin nuni", "joining words": "kalmomin haɗi", "al-kitaabu": "al-kitaabu", "the book": "littafin", "kitaabul-mudarrisi": "kitaabul-mudarrisi", "yaa waladu": "yaa waladu", "O boy": "Ya kai yaro", "a noun with": "suna mai", "a noun joined to a definite noun": "sunan da aka rataya ga suna ma'arifa", ". But joined to an indefinite noun it stays indefinite:": ". Amma idan aka rataya shi ga suna nakira yana zama nakira:", "a person called with": "mutumin da aka kira da", "when you mean a particular one:": "idan kana nufin takamaiman mutum:", "(a blind man calling anyone) stays indefinite.": "(makaho yana kiran kowa) yana zama nakira.", "with الْ": "tare da الْ", "joined to a definite noun": "an rataya shi ga suna ma'arifa", "still indefinite": "har yanzu nakira ne", "a particular person called": "takamaiman mutumin da aka kira", "a'ṭaa yu'ṭee": "a'ṭaa yu'ṭee", "a'ṭinee": "a'ṭinee", "he gave": "ya bayar", "he gives": "yana bayarwa", "= give me (command of": "yana nufin ba ni (umarnin", "). The last vowel drops in the command. Also new:": "). Wasalin ƙarshe yana faɗuwa a umarni. Sabo kuma:", "(it ran out):": "(ya ƙare):", "(he handed over):": "(ya miƙa):", "Give me a notebook.": "Ba ni littafin rubutu.", "Give each student his pen.": "Ba kowane ɗalibi alƙalaminsa.", "The copies of this book have run out at the bookshop.": "Kwafin wannan littafin sun ƙare a shagon littattafai.", "I handed the notebook to the teacher.": "Na miƙa wa malamin littafin rubutun.", "the buyer": "mai saye", "the shopkeeper": "mai shago", "a fountain pen": "alƙalamin tawada", "a ballpoint pen": "biro", "a pencil": "fensir", "a map": "taswira", "a bag (plastic)": "leda", "a price, value": "farashi, daraja", "a board, a plaque": "allo, allon rubutu", "it ran out": "ya ƙare", "al-mushtaree": "al-mushtaree", "ṣaaḥibul-maḥalli": "ṣaaḥibul-maḥalli", "qalamu ḥibrin": "qalamu ḥibrin", "qalamun jaaffun": "qalamun jaaffun", "qalamu raṣaaṣin": "qalamu raṣaaṣin", "khareeṭatun (pl. kharaa'iṭu)": "khareeṭatun (jam'i: kharaa'iṭu)", "keesun (pl. akyaasun)": "keesun (jam'i: akyaasun)", "qeematun": "qeematun", "lawḥatun": "lawḥatun", "nafida (yanfadu)": "nafida (yanfadu)", "definite": "ma'arifa", "indefinite": "nakira", "Do you have pens? Yes, fountain pens and ballpoints. Give me that one. This? No, the one above it.": "Kana da alƙaluma? Ee, alƙaluman tawada da biro. Ba ni wancan. Wannan? A'a, wanda yake samansa.", "Give me a pencil. This is a pencil. Give me a notebook. Notebooks come in different kinds. Which kind do you want?": "Ba ni fensir. Wannan fensir ne. Ba ni littafin rubutu. Littattafan rubutu iri-iri ne. Wane iri kake so?", "I want a notebook with lined paper and a map of the Islamic world on its cover.": "Ina son littafin rubutu mai layi da taswirar duniyar Musulunci a bangonsa.", "Do you want anything else? No. Boy, put these things in a bag. Are you a pupil? Yes.": "Kana son wani abu kuma? A'a. Yaro, sa waɗannan abubuwan a leda. Kai ɗalibi ne? Ee.", "What is your name? Malik. Which school do you study at? At Umar ibn al-Khattab Secondary School.": "Mene ne sunanka? Malik. A wace makaranta kake karatu? A Makarantar Sakandare ta Umar ɗan Khaddabi.", "Malik, come. This is a beautiful plaque containing verses and hadiths. It is a gift for you. Thank you.": "Malik, zo. Wannan allo ne mai kyau da yake ɗauke da ayoyi da hadisai. Kyauta ce gare ka. Na gode.", "What you have runs out, and what Allah has remains.": "Abin da yake wurinku yana ƙarewa, abin da yake wurin Allah kuma yana dawwama.", "Is it a known one, or any one?": "Sananne ne, ko kowane ɗaya?", "The seven kinds.": "Nau'uka bakwai.", "joined noun": "sunan da aka rataya", "Which kind of definite noun?": "Wane nau'in suna ma'arifa?", "joining word": "kalmar haɗi", "pointing word": "kalmar nuni", "name": "sunan yanka", "called with يَا": "an kira shi da يَا", "By joining, with": "Ta hanyar ratayawa, da", ", or by calling.": ", ko ta hanyar kira.", "سَيَّارَةٌ (make it definite by joining)": "سَيَّارَةٌ (mayar da shi ma'arifa ta hanyar ratayawa)", "or by calling.": "ko ta hanyar kira.", "أُسْتَاذٌ (make it definite by calling)": "أُسْتَاذٌ (mayar da shi ma'arifa ta hanyar kira)", "رَسُولٌ (make it definite with الْ)": "رَسُولٌ (mayar da shi ma'arifa da الْ)", "قَلَمٌ (make it definite by joining)": "قَلَمٌ (mayar da shi ma'arifa ta hanyar ratayawa)", "This is a gift for you.": "Wannan kyauta ce gare ka.", "Listen, then write the word. (a bag (plastic))": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (leda)", "مَسْجِدٌ (make it definite with الْ)": "مَسْجِدٌ (mayar da shi ma'arifa da الْ)", "مَعْرِفَةٌ or نَكِرَةٌ?": "مَعْرِفَةٌ ko نَكِرَةٌ?", "Boy, put these things in a bag.": "Yaro, sa waɗannan abubuwan a leda.", "✅ Write: a bag (plastic)": "✅ Rubuta: leda", "✅ Boy, put these things in a bag.": "✅ Yaro, sa waɗannan abubuwan a leda.", "✅ Give me a pencil.": "✅ Ba ni fensir.", "In this lesson you will see that the": "A wannan darasin za ka ga cewa", "of the dual and of the plural -": "na tasniya da na jam'i -", "drops when the word is joined to another noun:": "yana faɗuwa idan aka rataya kalmar ga wani suna:", "both, the pointing words for two far things,": "duka biyun, kalmomin nuni ga abubuwa biyu na nesa,", "and the command": "da kuma umarnin", "bring or come.": "kawo ko zo.", "When a dual or a plural in -": "Idan aka rataya tasniya ko jam'i mai -", "is joined to another noun, its": "ga wani suna, sai", "With my, the dual becomes -": "Tare da “nawa”, tasniya tana zama -", "And -": "Da kuma -", "as the object:": "a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "means both for masculine, and": "yana nufin duka biyun ga namiji, da", "for feminine. Joined to a pronoun they change like the dual:": "ga mace. Idan aka rataya su ga wakilin suna suna canjawa kamar tasniya:", "Joined to a noun they do not change:": "Idan aka rataya su ga suna ba sa canjawa:", "Pointing to two far things:": "Nuni ga abubuwa biyu na nesa:", "for feminine. Near:": "ga mace. Na kusa:", "means come or bring:": "yana nufin zo ko kawo:", "قَلَمَايَ (my two pens)": "قَلَمَايَ (alƙalumana biyu)", "كِلَاهُمَا (both of them)": "كِلَاهُمَا (su duka biyun)", "My two": "Nawa biyu", "Both": "Duka biyun", "Those two": "Waɗancan biyun", "In this lesson you will see that the نُونْ of the dual and of the plural -ُونَ drops when the word is joined to another noun: قَلَمَانِ becomes قَلَمَا حَامِدٍ, and مُسْلِمُونَ becomes مُسْلِمُو الْيَابَانِ. You will learn كِلَا and كِلْتَا, both, the pointing words for two far things, ذَانِكَ and تَانِكَ, and the command اِئْتِ, bring or come.": "A wannan darasin za ka ga cewa نُونْ na tasniya da na jam'i -ُونَ yana faɗuwa idan aka rataya kalmar ga wani suna: قَلَمَانِ yana zama قَلَمَا حَامِدٍ, kuma مُسْلِمُونَ yana zama مُسْلِمُو الْيَابَانِ. Za ka koyi كِلَا da كِلْتَا, duka biyun, kalmomin nuni ga abubuwa biyu na nesa, ذَانِكَ da تَانِكَ, da kuma umarnin اِئْتِ, kawo ko zo.", "qalamaa ḥaamidin": "qalamaa ḥaamidin", "mudarrisul-fiqhi": "mudarrisul-fiqhi", "Hamid's two pens": "alƙaluman Hamid biyu", "the fiqh teachers": "malaman fiƙihu", "When a": "Idan", "dual": "tasniya", "or a plural in": "ko jam'i mai", "is joined to another noun (": "aka rataya shi ga wani suna (", "), its": "), sai", ". It also drops before an ending:": ". Yana kuma faɗuwa kafin ƙari:", "dual: the ن drops": "tasniya: ن yana faɗuwa", "plural -ُونَ: the ن drops": "jam'i -ُونَ: ن yana faɗuwa", "The two rak'ahs of Fajr are better than the world and what is in it.": "Raka'o'i biyu na Asuba sun fi duniya da abin da ke cikinta.", "Aishah, my eyes sleep but my heart does not sleep.": "Aisha, idanuna biyu suna barci amma zuciyata ba ta barci.", "Indeed I am your Lord, so remove your sandals.": "Lalle Ni ne Ubangijinka, don haka ka cire takalmanka biyu.", "The Qur'an teachers are in a meeting with the principal.": "Malaman Alƙur'ani suna taro tare da shugaban makaranta.", "qalamaaya": "qalamaaya", "daftarayya": "daftarayya", "my two pens": "alƙalumana biyu", "my two notebooks": "littattafan rubutuna biyu", "(my), the dual becomes": "(nawa), tasniya tana zama", "as the doer and": "a matsayin mai aikatawa da", "takes a fatha.": "yana ɗaukar fataha.", "Where are my two pens? Did you see my two pens, brothers?": "Ina alƙalumana biyu? Kun ga alƙalumana biyu, 'yan'uwa?", "Here they are, teacher. They are under your bag.": "Ga su nan, malam. Suna ƙarƙashin jakarka.", "These are my two notebooks, and these are Hamid's two notebooks.": "Waɗannan littattafan rubutuna ne biyu, waɗannan kuma littattafan rubutun Hamid ne biyu.", "kilaahumaa mareeḍun": "kilaahumaa mareeḍun", "both of them are sick": "su duka biyun ba su da lafiya", "kiltaahumaa lil-qur'aani": "kiltaahumaa lil-qur'aani", "both are for the Qur'an": "duka biyun na Alƙur'ani ne", "(both, m) and": "(duka biyun, namiji) da", "(both, f) are always joined to another word. Joined to a": "(duka biyun, mace) kullum ana rataya su ga wata kalma. Idan aka rataya su ga", "they change like the dual:": "suna canjawa kamar tasniya:", ". Joined to a": ". Idan aka rataya su ga", "they do not change:": "ba sa canjawa:", "Mas'ud, where are your two brothers? They have not come for two days. Both of them are sick.": "Mas'ud, ina 'yan'uwanka biyu? Ba su zo ba tsawon kwana biyu. Su duka biyun ba su da lafiya.", "Both of them have bad diarrhoea. May Allah cure them both.": "Su duka biyun suna fama da gudawa mai tsanani. Allah Ya ba su lafiya su duka biyun.", "Which lesson do you have in the last two periods? Both are for the Noble Qur'an.": "Wane darasi kuke da shi a lokutan ƙarshe biyu? Duka biyun na Alƙur'ani Mai girma ne.", "Both gardens produced their fruit.": "Gonakin biyu duka sun ba da 'ya'yansu.", "dhaanika": "dhaanika", "those two (m)": "waɗancan biyun (maza)", "taanika": "taanika", "those two (f)": "waɗancan biyun (mata)", "Pointing to": "Nuni ga", "two far": "abubuwa biyu", "things:": "na nesa:", "(m) and": "(namiji) da", "(f). As the object:": "(mace). A matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki:", ". Near:": ". Na kusa:", "(come, bring), from": "(zo, kawo), daga", "(go to the dormitory and bring them).": "(ka je ɗakin kwana ka kawo su).", "These are my two books, and those are my classmate's two books.": "Waɗannan littattafaina biyu ne, waɗancan kuma littattafan abokin ajina ne biyu.", "Come, Hisham. Take your two notebooks. Those are your classmate's two notebooks.": "Zo, Hisham. Karɓi littattafan rubutunka biyu. Waɗancan littattafan rubutun abokin ajinka ne biyu.", "These two buses go to the university, and those two to the airport.": "Waɗannan bas biyu suna zuwa jami'a, waɗancan biyun kuma zuwa filin jirgin sama.", "Go to the dormitory at break and bring them.": "Ka je ɗakin kwana lokacin hutu ka kawo su.", "suffering from, struck by": "wanda yake fama da, wanda abu ya same shi", "diarrhoea": "gudawa", "the break (at school)": "lokacin hutu (a makaranta)", "a unit of prayer": "raka'a", "a heart": "zuciya", "a sandal": "takalmi (silifas)", "the teachers of fiqh": "malaman fiƙihu", "muṣaabun": "muṣaabun", "ishaalun": "ishaalun", "al-fus-ḥatu": "al-fus-ḥatu", "rak'atun (dual rak'ataani)": "rak'atun (tasniya: rak'ataani)", "'aynun (dual 'aynaani)": "'aynun (tasniya: 'aynaani)", "qalbun (pl. quluubun)": "qalbun (jam'i: quluubun)", "na'lun (dual na'laani)": "na'lun (tasniya: na'laani)", "both (m)": "duka biyun (maza)", "come, bring": "zo, kawo", "both (f)": "duka biyun (mata)", "Where are my two pens? Did you see my two pens, brothers? Here they are, teacher, under your bag.": "Ina alƙalumana biyu? Kun ga alƙalumana biyu, 'yan'uwa? Ga su nan, malam, ƙarƙashin jakarka.", "Bring your notebooks, brothers. Each of you hand me two notebooks: the grammar notebook and the morphology notebook.": "Ku kawo littattafan rubutunku, 'yan'uwa. Kowannenku ya miƙa mini littattafan rubutu biyu: na nahawu da na sarfu.", "Did you hand me your two notebooks, Majid? I forgot to bring them. Go to the dormitory at break and bring them.": "Ka miƙa mini littattafan rubutunka biyu, Majid? Na manta ban kawo su ba. Ka je ɗakin kwana lokacin hutu ka kawo su.", "Whose notebooks are these, Harith? These two are mine, and these are Hamid's. Come, Hisham. Take your two notebooks. Those are your classmate's.": "Littattafan rubutun wane ne waɗannan, Harith? Waɗannan biyun nawa ne, waɗannan kuma na Hamid ne. Zo, Hisham. Karɓi littattafan rubutunka biyu. Waɗancan na abokin ajinka ne.", "Mas'ud, where are your two brothers? They have not come for two or three days. Both are sick, with bad diarrhoea. May Allah cure them.": "Mas'ud, ina 'yan'uwanka biyu? Ba su zo ba tsawon kwana biyu ko uku. Su duka biyun ba su da lafiya, suna fama da gudawa mai tsanani. Allah Ya ba su lafiya.", "From Aishah, from the Prophet, peace be upon him: the two rak'ahs of Fajr are better than the world and what is in it.": "Daga Aisha, daga Annabi, tsira da amincin Allah su tabbata a gare shi: raka'o'i biyu na Asuba sun fi duniya da abin da ke cikinta.", "Which lesson do you have in the last two periods? Both are for the Qur'an. The Qur'an teachers are in a meeting with the principal.": "Wane darasi kuke da shi a lokutan ƙarshe biyu? Duka biyun na Alƙur'ani ne. Malaman Alƙur'ani suna taro tare da shugaban makaranta.", "Dual -": "Tasniya -", "Join it: the": "Rataya shi:", "هٰذَانِ دَفْتَرَانِ. (Hamid's)": "هٰذَانِ دَفْتَرَانِ. (na Hamid)", "رَكْعَتَانِ (of Fajr)": "رَكْعَتَانِ (na Asuba)", "رَأَيْتُ بِنْتَيْنِ. (Hamid's)": "رَأَيْتُ بِنْتَيْنِ. (na Hamid)", "أَبْحَثُ عَنِ الْمُدَرِّسِينَ. (of fiqh)": "أَبْحَثُ عَنِ الْمُدَرِّسِينَ. (na fiƙihu)", "بَابَانِ (of the school)": "بَابَانِ (na makarantar)", "مُسْلِمُونَ (of Japan)": "مُسْلِمُونَ (na Japan)", "أَرَأَيْتُمْ ……؟ (my two pens)": "أَرَأَيْتُمْ ……؟ (alƙalumana biyu)", "إِنَّ …… تَنَامَانِ (my two eyes)": "إِنَّ …… تَنَامَانِ (idanuna biyu)", "غَسَلْتُ …… (my two hands)": "غَسَلْتُ …… (hannayena biyu)", "أَيْنَ ……؟ (my two pens)": "أَيْنَ ……؟ (alƙalumana biyu)", "With a pronoun they change; with a noun they don't.": "Tare da wakilin suna suna canjawa; tare da suna ba sa canjawa.", "إِنَّ …… مُصَابٌ بِإِسْهَالٍ. (both m)": "إِنَّ …… مُصَابٌ بِإِسْهَالٍ. (duka biyun, maza)", "Pointing to two far things.": "Nuni ga abubuwa biyu na nesa.", "هٰذَا أَخِي، وَ…… صَدِيقِي. (that, far)": "هٰذَا أَخِي، وَ…… صَدِيقِي. (wancan, na nesa)", "هَاتَانِ الْحَافِلَتَانِ إِلَى الْجَامِعَةِ، وَ…… إِلَى الْمَطَارِ. (those two f, far)": "هَاتَانِ الْحَافِلَتَانِ إِلَى الْجَامِعَةِ، وَ…… إِلَى الْمَطَارِ. (waɗancan biyun, mata, na nesa)", "هٰذَانِ أَخَوَايَ، وَ…… زَمِيلَايَ. (those two, far)": "هٰذَانِ أَخَوَايَ، وَ…… زَمِيلَايَ. (waɗancan biyun, na nesa)", "These are Hamid's two notebooks.": "Waɗannan littattafan rubutun Hamid ne biyu.", "قَلَمَايَ or قَلَمَيَّ?": "قَلَمَايَ ko قَلَمَيَّ?", "Both of them are sick.": "Su duka biyun ba su da lafiya.", "Listen, then write the word. (a sandal)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (takalmi)", "Join it: the ن drops": "Rataya shi: ن yana faɗuwa", "جَاءَ الْمُدَرِّسُونَ. (of fiqh)": "جَاءَ الْمُدَرِّسُونَ. (na fiƙihu)", "✅ Both of them are sick.": "✅ Su duka biyun ba su da lafiya.", "✅ These are Hamid's two notebooks.": "✅ Waɗannan littattafan rubutun Hamid ne biyu.", "✅ Write: a sandal": "✅ Rubuta: takalmi", "In this lesson you will look closely at the two kinds of sentence. A nominal sentence can start with a noun, with": "A wannan darasin za ka duba nau'ukan jumla guda biyu sosai. Jumla ismiyya tana iya farawa da suna, da", "and a verb, or with": "da fi'ili, ko kuma da", "and its sisters. A verbal sentence can start with a complete verb, like": "da 'yan'uwanta. Jumla fi'iliyya tana iya farawa da cikakken fi'ili, kamar", "or with": "ko kuma da", "and its sisters. You will also learn that": "da 'yan'uwanta. Za ka kuma koyi cewa", "with a verb can stand for a verbal noun:": "tare da fi'ili yana iya tsayawa a madadin masdari:", "equals": "daidai yake da", "And you will learn": "Kuma za ka koyi", "meaning began to.": "masu ma'anar ya fara.", "Or with": "Ko kuma da", "and a verb:": "da fi'ili:", "and its sisters:": "da 'yan'uwanta:", "A verbal sentence starts with a complete verb, which needs only a doer:": "Jumla fi'iliyya tana farawa da cikakken fi'ili, wanda yake buƙatar mai aikatawa kaɗai:", "Or with an incomplete verb,": "Ko kuma da fi'ili naqis (mara cika),", "and its sisters, which needs a second word:": "da 'yan'uwanta, wanda yake buƙatar kalma ta biyu:", "with a verb can be replaced by a verbal noun.": "tare da fi'ili ana iya maye gurbinsa da masdari.", "can mean began to. The second part must have a present verb:": "yana iya nufin ya fara. Sashe na biyu dole ya kasance da fi'ili mudari'i:", "the students began to move.": "ɗaliban suka fara motsi.", "the two sentences": "jumloli biyu", "Which sentence?": "Wace jumla?", "How does it start?": "Da me take farawa?", "Verbal noun": "Masdari", "Began to": "Ya fara", "In this lesson you will look closely at the two kinds of sentence. A nominal sentence can start with a noun, with أَنْ and a verb, or with إِنَّ and its sisters. A verbal sentence can start with a complete verb, like طَلَعَتِ الشَّمْسُ, or with كَانَ and its sisters. You will also learn that أَنْ with a verb can stand for a verbal noun: أَنْ تَذْهَبُوا equals ذَهَابُكُمْ. And you will learn طَفِقَ, جَعَلَ and أَخَذَ, meaning began to.": "A wannan darasin za ka duba nau'ukan jumla guda biyu sosai. Jumla ismiyya tana iya farawa da suna, da أَنْ da fi'ili, ko kuma da إِنَّ da 'yan'uwanta. Jumla fi'iliyya tana iya farawa da cikakken fi'ili, kamar طَلَعَتِ الشَّمْسُ, ko kuma da كَانَ da 'yan'uwanta. Za ka kuma koyi cewa أَنْ tare da fi'ili yana iya tsayawa a madadin masdari: أَنْ تَذْهَبُوا daidai yake da ذَهَابُكُمْ. Kuma za ka koyi طَفِقَ, جَعَلَ da أَخَذَ, masu ma'anar ya fara.", "allaahu ghafuurun": "allaahu ghafuurun", "Allah is Forgiving": "Allah Mai gafara ne", "an taṣuumuu khayrun lakum": "an taṣuumuu khayrun lakum", "Fasting is better for you": "Yin azumi shi ya fi alheri gare ku", "inna llaaha ghafuurun": "inna llaaha ghafuurun", "Indeed Allah is Forgiving": "Lalle Allah Mai gafara ne", ") starts with: (a) a plain noun:": ") tana farawa da: (a) suna kawai:", ". (b) an": ". (b) wani", "interpreted verbal noun": "masdari mu'awwali (wanda aka fassara)", "+ verb):": "+ fi'ili):", "or one of its sisters:": "ko ɗaya daga cikin 'yan'uwanta:", "Allah is Forgiving.": "Allah Mai gafara ne.", "And that you fast is better for you.": "Kuma ku yi azumi shi ya fi alheri gare ku.", "Indeed Allah is Forgiving, Merciful.": "Lalle Allah Mai gafara ne, Mai jinƙai.", "This is a school.": "Wannan makaranta ce.", "ṭala'atish-shamsu": "ṭala'atish-shamsu", "The sun rose.": "Rana ta fito.", "kaanal-jawwu baaridan": "kaanal-jawwu baaridan", "The weather was cold.": "Yanayin ya kasance da sanyi.", ") starts with: (a) a": ") tana farawa da: (a)", "complete verb": "cikakken fi'ili", "), which needs only a doer:": "), wanda yake buƙatar mai aikatawa kaɗai:", "incomplete verb": "fi'ili naqis", "), which needs a second word ending in -a:": "), wanda yake buƙatar kalma ta biyu mai ƙarewa da -a:", ". The incomplete verbs are": ". Fi'iloli naqis su ne", "and its sisters.": "da 'yan'uwanta.", "فِعْلٌ تَامٌّ: complete": "فِعْلٌ تَامٌّ: cikakke", "فِعْلٌ نَاقِصٌ: needs more": "فِعْلٌ نَاقِصٌ: yana buƙatar ƙari", "And Allah is ever Forgiving, Merciful.": "Kuma Allah Ya kasance Mai gafara, Mai jinƙai.", "The bell rang and the fifth period began.": "Ƙararrawa ta buga kuma lokacin darasi na biyar ya fara.", "an tadh-habuu ilal-maktabati khayrun lakum": "an tadh-habuu ilal-maktabati khayrun lakum", "Going to the library is better for you.": "Zuwanku ɗakin karatu shi ya fi alheri gare ku.", "+ a verb can be replaced by a": "+ fi'ili ana iya maye gurbinsa da", "verbal noun": "masdari", "Your going to the library is better for you.": "Zuwanku ɗakin karatu shi ya fi alheri gare ku.", "Attending the lesson is better for you.": "Halartar darasi shi ya fi alheri gare ka.", "And that you forgive is nearer to piety.": "Kuma ku yafe shi ya fi kusa da taƙawa.", "ṭafiquu yataḥarrakuuna": "ṭafiquu yataḥarrakuuna", "they began to move": "suka fara motsi", "ja'ala yaktubu": "ja'ala yaktubu", "he began to write": "ya fara rubutu", "akhadha yaqra'u": "akhadha yaqra'u", "he began to read": "ya fara karatu", "can mean": "yana iya nufin", "began to": "ya fara", ". They work like": ". Suna aiki kamar", ", but the second part must be a sentence with a": ", amma sashe na biyu dole ya zama jumla mai", "present verb": "fi'ili mudari'i", "The students got tired of waiting and began moving from their places and messing about.": "Ɗaliban sun gaji da jira suka fara tashi daga wurarensu suna wasa.", "Some stood up making speeches, and some began writing on the board.": "Wasu suka tashi suna jawabi, wasu kuma suka fara rubutu a kan allo.", "The imam began to recite Surat al-Kahf.": "Liman ya fara karanta Suratul Kahfi.", "waiting": "jira", "chaos, disorder": "hargitsi, rashin tsari", "leaving, going away": "tafiya, tashi", "the opinion": "ra'ayi", "suitable": "wanda ya dace", "he moved": "ya motsa", "he messed about": "ya yi wasa, ya yi shirme", "he got bored": "ya gaji, ya ƙosa", "al-intiẓaaru": "al-intiẓaaru", "fawḍaa": "fawḍaa", "al-inṣiraafu": "al-inṣiraafu", "mabnan": "mabnan", "ar-ra'yu": "ar-ra'yu", "munaasibun": "munaasibun", "taḥarraka": "taḥarraka", "'abitha (ya'bathu)": "'abitha (ya'bathu)", "sa'ima (yas'amu)": "sa'ima (yas'amu)", "he began to": "ya fara", "the interpreted verbal noun": "masdari mu'awwali", "The bell rang and the fifth period began. Ten minutes or more passed and the teacher did not come.": "Ƙararrawa ta buga kuma lokacin darasi na biyar ya fara. Minti goma ko fiye suka wuce malamin bai zo ba.", "The students got bored of waiting and began moving from their places and messing about.": "Ɗaliban sun gaji da jira suka fara tashi daga wurarensu suna wasa.", "The supervisor suddenly came in and said: what is this? Your state is chaos. It is as if the class were a market!": "Sai mai kulawa ya shigo ba zato ya ce: mene ne wannan? Halinku hargitsi ne. Kamar ajin kasuwa ne!", "Listen. Your teacher is sick and did not come today. You can go to the library or leave for the dormitories. Going to the library is better for you.": "Ku saurara. Malaminku ba shi da lafiya bai zo yau ba. Kuna iya zuwa ɗakin karatu ko ku tafi ɗakunan kwana. Zuwanku ɗakin karatu shi ya fi alheri gare ku.", "We left the institute building. It was half past twelve. Some classmates thought we should visit our sick teacher.": "Muka bar ginin cibiyar. Ƙarfe goma sha biyu da rabi ne. Wasu abokan aji suka ga ya kamata mu ziyarci malaminmu mara lafiya.", "I told them: it is not a good time to visit. We will visit him after Asr, in sha Allah. They said: as you see fit.": "Na ce musu: wannan ba lokaci ne mai kyau na ziyara ba. Za mu ziyarce shi bayan La'asar, in sha Allah. Suka ce: yadda ka ga dama.", "start nominal sentences;": "suna fara jumla ismiyya;", "starts a verbal one.": "yana fara jumla fi'iliyya.", "The five kinds of start.": "Nau'ukan farawa guda biyar.", "إِنَّ or a sister": "إِنَّ ko ɗaya daga 'yan'uwanta", "an incomplete verb": "fi'ili naqis", "What does it start with?": "Da me take farawa?", "a plain noun": "suna kawai", "أَنْ + a verb": "أَنْ + fi'ili", "a complete verb": "cikakken fi'ili", "Choose the verbal noun that replaces it.": "Zaɓi masdarin da yake maye gurbinsa.", "+ verb = verbal noun": "+ fi'ili = masdari", "The second part has a present verb.": "Sashe na biyu yana da fi'ili mudari'i.", "The students began to move.": "Ɗaliban suka fara motsi.", "Listen, then write the word. (chaos, disorder)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (hargitsi)", "أَنْ + verb = verbal noun": "أَنْ + fi'ili = masdari", "✅ Going to the library is better for you.": "✅ Zuwanku ɗakin karatu shi ya fi alheri gare ku.", "✅ Write: chaos, disorder": "✅ Rubuta: hargitsi", "✅ The weather was cold.": "✅ Yanayin ya kasance da sanyi.", "In this lesson you will study the nominal sentence closely.": "A wannan darasin za ka yi nazarin jumla ismiyya sosai.", "is the noun we talk about, and": "shi ne sunan da muke magana a kansa, kuma", "is what we say about it, like": "shi ne abin da muke faɗa game da shi, kamar", "You will learn when the subject can be indefinite, as in": "Za ka koyi yaushe mubtada'i yake iya zama nakira, kamar a", "when the order changes, when a word can be dropped, the three kinds of predicate, and how the predicate agrees with the subject.": "yaushe tsari yake canjawa, yaushe ake iya cire kalma, nau'ukan khabari guda uku, da yadda khabari yake dacewa da mubtada'i.", "completes the meaning. Both end in": "yana cika ma'anar. Dukansu suna ƙarewa da", "The subject is normally definite:": "Mubtada'i a al'ada ma'arifa ne:", "The subject can be indefinite when the predicate is a place word or preposition that comes first:": "Mubtada'i yana iya zama nakira idan khabari kalmar wuri ne ko harafin jarri kuma ya zo a gaba:", "Or when the subject is a question word:": "Ko kuma idan mubtada'i kalmar tambaya ce:", "A question word always comes first.": "Kalmar tambaya kullum tana zuwa a farko.", "A word can be dropped when it is known. The subject:": "Ana iya cire kalma idan an san ta. Mubtada'i:", "The predicate:": "Khabari:", "Or both:": "Ko duka biyun:", "The predicate can be a single word:": "Khabari yana iya zama kalma ɗaya:", "Or a phrase, a place word or preposition:": "Ko kuma jumla, ko kalmar wuri ko harafin jarri:", "A one-word predicate agrees with its subject in number and gender.": "Khabari mai kalma ɗaya yana dacewa da mubtada'insa a adadi da jinsi.", "الْمُبْتَدَأُ وَالْخَبَرُ (subject and predicate)": "الْمُبْتَدَأُ وَالْخَبَرُ (mubtada'i da khabari)", "Word order": "Tsarin kalmomi", "Kind of predicate": "Irin khabari", "Agreement": "Dacewa", "What was dropped?": "Me aka cire?", "In this lesson you will study the nominal sentence closely. الْمُبْتَدَأُ is the noun we talk about, and الْخَبَرُ is what we say about it, like الْقَمَرُ جَمِيلٌ. You will learn when the subject can be indefinite, as in عِنْدَنَا سَيَّارَةٌ, when the order changes, when a word can be dropped, the three kinds of predicate, and how the predicate agrees with the subject.": "A wannan darasin za ka yi nazarin jumla ismiyya sosai. الْمُبْتَدَأُ shi ne sunan da muke magana a kansa, kuma الْخَبَرُ shi ne abin da muke faɗa game da shi, kamar الْقَمَرُ جَمِيلٌ. Za ka koyi yaushe mubtada'i yake iya zama nakira, kamar a عِنْدَنَا سَيَّارَةٌ, yaushe tsari yake canjawa, yaushe ake iya cire kalma, nau'ukan khabari guda uku, da yadda khabari yake dacewa da mubtada'i.", "al-qamaru jameelun": "al-qamaru jameelun", "The moon is beautiful.": "Wata yana da kyau.", ". The subject can be a plain noun (": ". Mubtada'i yana iya zama suna kawai (", ") or": ") ko", "+ verb (": "+ fi'ili (", "). It is normally": "). A al'ada yana zama", "Sitting here is not allowed.": "Ba a yarda a zauna nan ba.", "The key to Paradise is the prayer.": "Mabuɗin Aljanna shi ne sallah.", "'indanaa sayyaaratun": "'indanaa sayyaaratun", "We have a car.": "Muna da mota.", "lee akhun": "lee akhun", "I have a brother.": "Ina da ɗan'uwa.", "man mareeḍun": "man mareeḍun", "Who is sick?": "Wa ba shi da lafiya?", "The subject can be": "Mubtada'i yana iya zama", "when: (a) the predicate is a": "idan: (a) khabari", "place word or preposition": "kalmar wuri ne ko harafin jarri", "and comes": "kuma ya zo", ". (b) the subject is a": ". (b) mubtada'i", "question word": "kalmar tambaya ce", "A question word always comes": "Kalmar tambaya kullum tana zuwa", ", subject or predicate:": ", mubtada'i ce ko khabari:", "What is wrong with you? He has a stomach ache.": "Me ke damun ka? Yana ciwon ciki.", "How many students are in the class?": "Ɗalibai nawa ne a ajin?", "Are you a teacher?": "Kai malami ne?", "ḥaamidun": "ḥaamidun", "Hamid (my name is Hamid)": "Hamid (sunana Hamid)", "Yes (I am a student)": "Ee (ni ɗalibi ne)", "A word can be": "Ana iya", "when it is known: the": "kalma idan an san ta:", "subject": "mubtada'i", "). The": "). Da", "predicate": "khabari", "). Or": "). Ko", "both": "duka biyun", "What is your name? Munir.": "Mene ne sunanka? Munir.", "Are you German? No, British.": "Kai Bajamushe ne? A'a, Baturen Ingila.", "Who understands? Me.": "Wa ya fahimta? Ni.", "Are you a student? Yes.": "Kai ɗalibi ne? Ee.", "al-mu'minu mir'aatul-mu'mini": "al-mu'minu mir'aatul-mu'mini", "single word": "kalma ɗaya", "al-mudeeru mas-muhu": "al-mudeeru mas-muhu", "sentence": "jumla", "al-ḥamdu lillaahi": "al-ḥamdu lillaahi", "phrase": "shibhul jumla (kalmar wuri ko harafin jarri)", "The predicate is: (a) a": "Khabari yana zama: (a)", "), nominal or verbal:": "), ismiyya ko fi'iliyya:", "): a place word or a preposition:": "): kalmar wuri ko harafin jarri:", "مُفْرَدٌ: one word": "مُفْرَدٌ: kalma ɗaya", "جُمْلَةٌ: a sentence": "جُمْلَةٌ: jumla", "شِبْهُ جُمْلَةٍ: a phrase": "شِبْهُ جُمْلَةٍ: kalmar wuri ko harafin jarri", "The religion is ease.": "Addini sauƙi ne.", "The teacher is with the principal.": "Malamin yana tare da shugaban makaranta.", "The students are on the playground.": "Ɗaliban suna filin wasa.", "The intention: its place is the heart.": "Niyya: wurinta zuciya ce.", "Islam wipes out what came before it.": "Musulunci yana shafe abin da ya gabace shi.", "al-mudarrisu waaqifun": "al-mudarrisu waaqifun", "baabal-faṣli mughlaqaani": "baabal-faṣli mughlaqaani", "The teacher is standing.": "Malamin yana tsaye.", "The two doors are closed.": "Ƙofofin biyu a rufe suke.", "A one-word predicate": "Khabari mai kalma ɗaya", "agrees": "yana dacewa", "with its subject in": "da mubtada'insa a", "number": "adadi", ". And in": ". Da kuma a", "gender": "jinsi", "The teacher is standing, and the students are sitting.": "Malamin yana tsaye, ɗaliban kuma suna zaune.", "The two doors of the class are closed, and its two windows are open.": "Ƙofofin ajin biyu a rufe suke, tagoginsa biyu kuma a buɗe suke.", "Hamid is an engineer, his wife is a doctor, their two sons are merchants, and their two daughters are teachers.": "Hamid injiniya ne, matarsa likita ce, 'ya'yansu maza biyu 'yan kasuwa ne, 'ya'yansu mata biyu kuma malamai ne.", "stomach ache": "ciwon ciki", "the sports club": "ƙungiyar wasanni", "wanted, called for": "wanda ake nema, wanda aka kira", "chalk": "alli", "exactly": "daidai, tabbatacce", "British": "Baturen Ingila", "German": "Bajamushe", "maghaṣun": "maghaṣun", "an-naadir-riyaaḍiyyu": "an-naadir-riyaaḍiyyu", "maṭluubun": "maṭluubun", "ṭabaasheeru": "ṭabaasheeru", "biḍ-ḍabṭi": "biḍ-ḍabṭi", "bireeṭaaniyyun": "bireeṭaaniyyun", "almaaniyyun": "almaaniyyun", "the predicate": "khabari", "a phrase (place word or preposition)": "shibhul jumla (kalmar wuri ko harafin jarri)", "the subject": "mubtada'i", "The students are few. Where are the others? Umar is absent, Hamid is with the principal, Ishaq is in the toilet, and al-Hasan went to the supervisor's room.": "Ɗaliban kaɗan ne. Ina sauran? Umar ba ya nan, Hamid yana tare da shugaban makaranta, Ishaq yana banɗaki, al-Hasan kuma ya tafi ɗakin mai kulawa.", "And al-Zubayr's brother is sick; he asked the principal's permission to go to hospital. What is wrong with him? He has a stomach ache.": "Ɗan'uwan al-Zubayr kuma ba shi da lafiya; ya nemi izinin shugaban makaranta ya tafi asibiti. Me ke damun sa? Yana ciwon ciki.", "Hamid, it seems you want to say something. Do you have a question? Yes. I am wanted now at the sports club. Shall I go or attend the lesson?": "Hamid, kamar kana so ka faɗi wani abu. Kana da tambaya? Ee. Ana nema na yanzu a ƙungiyar wasanni. In tafi ko in halarci darasi?", "Attending the lesson is better for you. You can go to the club at break. What is in the box, Hasan? There is chalk in it.": "Halartar darasi shi ya fi alheri gare ka. Kana iya zuwa ƙungiyar lokacin hutu. Me ke cikin akwatin, Hasan? Akwai alli a cikinsa.", "This is a new student. Welcome. How are you? Well, praise Allah. What is your name? Munir.": "Wannan sabon ɗalibi ne. Barka da zuwa. Yaya kake? Lafiya, alhamdu lillah. Mene ne sunanka? Munir.", "Are you German? No. British. Where did you study Arabic, Munir? At an Islamic school.": "Kai Bajamushe ne? A'a. Baturen Ingila. A ina ka koyi Larabci, Munir? A wata makarantar Islamiyya.", "Are there Islamic schools in Britain? Yes. How many are there? I don't know exactly. The schools are many.": "Akwai makarantun Islamiyya a Birtaniya? Ee. Nawa ne su? Ban sani ba daidai. Makarantun suna da yawa.", "Indefinite subject: use phrase first. Question word: use always first.": "Mubtada'i nakira: yi amfani da shibhul jumla a gaba. Kalmar tambaya: kullum a gaba.", "Which order is right?": "Wane tsari ne daidai?", "Indefinite subject → phrase first. Question word → always first.": "Mubtada'i nakira → shibhul jumla a gaba. Kalmar tambaya → kullum a gaba.", "Make a sentence:": "Yi jumla:", "Single word, sentence, or phrase?": "Kalma ɗaya, jumla, ko shibhul jumla?", "What kind of predicate?": "Wane irin khabari?", "Number and gender.": "Adadi da jinsi.", "Make the predicate agree": "Sa khabari ya dace", "The subject, the predicate, or both?": "Mubtada'i, khabari, ko duka biyun?", "What is wrong with you?": "Me ke damun ka?", "Listen, then write the word. (chalk)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (alli)", "✅ What is wrong with you?": "✅ Me ke damun ka?", "✅ Attending the lesson is better for you.": "✅ Halartar darasi shi ya fi alheri gare ka.", "✅ Write: chalk": "✅ Rubuta: alli", "a noun ending in": "suna mai ƙarewa da", "that tells when or where something happened, like": "wanda yake nuna yaushe ko a ina wani abu ya faru (zarfi), kamar", "on Tuesday, and": "ranar Talata, da", "with the principal. Some of these words never change, like": "a wurin shugaban makaranta. Wasu daga cikin waɗannan kalmomi ba sa canjawa har abada, kamar", "if, as in": "da a ce, kamar a", "before.": "a da, kafin haka.", "is a noun ending in": "suna ne mai ƙarewa da", "that tells when or where. When:": "wanda yake nuna yaushe ko a ina. Yaushe:", "Where:": "A ina:", "Some time and place words are fixed and never change:": "Wasu kalmomin lokaci da wuri ba sa canjawa (mabni) har abada:", "Some words stand in for a time or place word:": "Wasu kalmomi suna tsayawa a madadin kalmar lokaci ko wuri:", "means if, for something that did not happen:": "yana nufin da a ce, ga abin da bai faru ba:", "A positive answer takes": "Amsa ta tabbatarwa tana ɗaukar", "A negative answer does not:": "Amsa ta korewa ba ta ɗauka:", "الْمَفْعُولُ فِيهِ (when and where)": "الْمَفْعُولُ فِيهِ (yaushe da a ina)", "لَوْ (if)": "لَوْ (da a ce)", "Time or place?": "Lokaci ko wuri?", "Fixed?": "Ba ya canjawa?", "In this lesson you will learn الْمَفْعُولُ فِيهِ, a noun ending in فَتْحَةْ that tells when or where something happened, like يَوْمَ الثُّلَاثَاءِ, on Tuesday, and عِنْدَ الْمُدِيرِ, with the principal. Some of these words never change, like مَتَى, أَيْنَ, أَمْسِ, قَطُّ, الْآنَ and حَيْثُ. You will also learn لَوْ, if, as in لَوِ اجْتَهَدْتَ لَنَجَحْتَ, and مِنْ قَبْلُ, before.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi الْمَفْعُولُ فِيهِ, suna mai ƙarewa da فَتْحَةْ wanda yake nuna yaushe ko a ina wani abu ya faru, kamar يَوْمَ الثُّلَاثَاءِ, ranar Talata, da عِنْدَ الْمُدِيرِ, a wurin shugaban makaranta. Wasu daga cikin waɗannan kalmomi ba sa canjawa har abada, kamar مَتَى, أَيْنَ, أَمْسِ, قَطُّ, الْآنَ da حَيْثُ. Za ka kuma koyi لَوْ, da a ce, kamar a لَوِ اجْتَهَدْتَ لَنَجَحْتَ, da مِنْ قَبْلُ, a da.", "waṣaltu yawma th-thulaathaa'i": "waṣaltu yawma th-thulaathaa'i", "I arrived on Tuesday": "Na iso ranar Talata", "jalastu 'indal-mudeeri": "jalastu 'indal-mudeeri", "I sat with the principal": "Na zauna a wurin shugaban makaranta", "(also called": "(ana kuma kiransa", ") is a noun ending in": ") suna ne mai ƙarewa da", "that tells": "wanda yake nuna", "when": "yaushe", "where": "a ina", "ظَرْفُ زَمَانٍ: when": "ظَرْفُ زَمَانٍ: yaushe", "ظَرْفُ مَكَانٍ: where": "ظَرْفُ مَكَانٍ: a ina", "We arrived a week ago.": "Mun iso mako ɗaya da ya wuce.", "I arrived on Tuesday, and went to Makkah.": "Na iso ranar Talata, sai na tafi Makka.", "Shall I sit behind Jamal?": "In zauna a bayan Jamal?", "I don't want to sit under the fan, it harms me.": "Ba na so in zauna a ƙarƙashin fanka, tana cutar da ni.", "mataa": "mataa", "ayna": "ayna", "amsi": "amsi", "yesterday": "jiya", "never": "ban taɓa ba", "hunaa": "hunaa", "al-aana": "al-aana", "ḥaythu": "ḥaythu", "wherever": "duk inda", "Some time and place words are": "Wasu kalmomin lokaci da wuri", "fixed": "mabni ne", ") and never change:": ") kuma ba sa canjawa har abada:", "Sit wherever you like.": "Zauna duk inda kake so.", "I have never travelled there.": "Ban taɓa tafiya can ba.", "I stayed there a day or part of a day.": "Na zauna can yini ɗaya ko wani ɓangare na yini.", "Where did you travel in the summer holiday? To Indonesia.": "Ina ka yi tafiya a hutun bazara? Zuwa Indonesiya.", "kullan-nahaari": "kullan-nahaari", "we travelled all day": "mun yi tafiya yini guda", "ṭaweelan": "ṭaweelan", "I sat a long time": "na zauna na dogon lokaci", "haadhal-usbuu'a": "haadhal-usbuu'a", "I came this week": "na zo a wannan makon", "Some words": "Wasu kalmomi", "stand in": "suna tsayawa a madadin", "for a time or place word and also end in -a: (1)": "kalmar lokaci ko wuri kuma suna ƙarewa da -a: (1)", "joined to a time or place:": "an rataya shi ga lokaci ko wuri:", "describing word": "kalmar siffantawa", "We travelled all day.": "Mun yi tafiya yini guda.", "I waited for you a quarter of an hour.": "Na jira ka kwata na awa.", "I stayed there three days.": "Na zauna can kwana uku.", "I did not stay there long.": "Ban daɗe a can ba.", "lawij-tahadta lanajaḥta": "lawij-tahadta lanajaḥta", "If you had worked hard, you would have passed.": "Da a ce ka yi ƙoƙari, da ka ci jarrabawa.", "(if, in the past) shows something that": "(da a ce, a abin da ya wuce) yana nuna abin da", "did not happen": "bai faru ba", "because something else did not happen:": "saboda wani abu bai faru ba:", "= you did not work hard, so you did not pass. A positive answer usually takes": "yana nufin ba ka yi ƙoƙari ba, don haka ba ka ci ba. Amsa ta tabbatarwa yawanci tana ɗaukar", "; a negative answer does not:": "; amsa ta korewa ba ta ɗauka:", "(before / after) end in -u when nothing follows:": "(kafin / bayan) suna ƙarewa da -u idan babu abin da ya biyo baya:", "If I had known you were coming to my country, I would have met you at the airport.": "Da a ce na san za ka zo ƙasata, da na tarbe ka a filin jirgin sama.", "If you had heard his story, you would have cried.": "Da a ce ka ji labarinsa, da ka yi kuka.", "If you had come yesterday, I would not have reported you to the principal.": "Da a ce ka zo jiya, da ban kai ƙararka wurin shugaban makaranta ba.", "To Allah belongs the command before and after.": "Al'amari na Allah ne a gabani da bayan haka.", "the fan": "fanka", "registration, record": "rajista, rubutu", "empty": "fanko, babu kowa", "a mile": "mil", "it harmed": "ya cutar", "he stayed": "ya zauna, ya daɗe", "he welcomed": "ya tarba", "he travelled": "ya yi tafiya", "al-mirwaḥatu": "al-mirwaḥatu", "qaydun": "qaydun", "khaalin (al-khaalee)": "khaalin (al-khaalee)", "meelun": "meelun", "ḍarra (yaḍurru)": "ḍarra (yaḍurru)", "labitha (yalbathu)": "labitha (yalbathu)", "makatha (yamkuthu)": "makatha (yamkuthu)", "istaqbala": "istaqbala", "saafara (yusaafiru)": "saafara (yusaafiru)", "if (it had been)": "da a ce (ya kasance)", "the time or place word": "kalmar lokaci ko wuri", "I welcome you on the first day of the new year. When did you arrive from your countries? A week ago. As for me, I arrived yesterday.": "Ina yi muku maraba a rana ta farko ta sabuwar shekara. Yaushe kuka iso daga ƙasashenku? Mako ɗaya da ya wuce. Ni kuwa na iso jiya.", "I arrived on Tuesday, went to Makkah for Umrah, stayed there three days, and came back last night.": "Na iso ranar Talata, na tafi Makka don Umra, na zauna can kwana uku, na dawo jiya da dare.", "Teacher, may I sit in front of you? This seat is empty; its owner's registration was ended last year. Sit wherever you like.": "Malam, zan iya zama a gabanka? Wannan kujerar fanko ce; an soke rajistar mai ita a bara. Zauna duk inda kake so.", "I don't want to sit under the fan, it harms me. Shall I sit behind Jamal? I have no objection.": "Ba na so in zauna a ƙarƙashin fanka, tana cutar da ni. In zauna a bayan Jamal? Ba ni da ƙin yarda.", "Where did you travel this summer, teacher? To Indonesia. Didn't you pass through Kuala Lumpur? Yes, but I did not stay there long.": "Ina ka yi tafiya a wannan bazara, malam? Zuwa Indonesiya. Ba ka wuce ta Kuala Lumpur ba? Ee, amma ban daɗe a can ba.", "How long did you stay there, teacher? A day or part of a day. If I had known you were coming to my country, I would have met you at the airport.": "Har tsawon yaushe ka zauna can, malam? Yini ɗaya ko wani ɓangare na yini. Da a ce na san za ka zo ƙasata, da na tarbe ka a filin jirgin sama.", "Did you travel to Singapore too? No. Have you not been there before? Right, I have never been there.": "Ka yi tafiya zuwa Singapore ma? A'a. Ba ka taɓa zuwa can a da ba? Haka ne, ban taɓa zuwa can ba.", "The word that tells when or where.": "Kalmar da take nuna yaushe ko a ina.", "changing": "mai canjawa", "Fixed or changing?": "Mara canjawa ko mai canjawa?", "; a negative one does not.": "; ta korewa ba ta ɗauka.", "“If I had known, I would not have been late.”": "“Da a ce na sani, da ban makara ba.”", "a negative one does not.": "ta korewa ba ta ɗauka.", "“If you had worked hard, you would have passed.”": "“Da a ce ka yi ƙoƙari, da ka ci jarrabawa.”", "“If you had heard his story, you would have cried.”": "“Da a ce ka ji labarinsa, da ka yi kuka.”", "Find الْمَفْعُولُ فِيهِ": "Nemo الْمَفْعُولُ فِيهِ", "Listen, then write the word. (a mile)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (mil)", "✅ “If you had worked hard, you would have passed.”": "✅ “Da a ce ka yi ƙoƙari, da ka ci jarrabawa.”", "✅ I waited for you a quarter of an hour.": "✅ Na jira ka kwata na awa.", "✅ I have never travelled there.": "✅ Ban taɓa tafiya can ba.", "✅ “If you had heard his story, you would have cried.”": "✅ “Da a ce ka ji labarinsa, da ka yi kuka.”", "✅ Write: a mile": "✅ Rubuta: mil", "that makes a command for someone absent or for us:": "mai yin umarni ga wanda ba ya nan ko gare mu:", "let him come in, and": "bari ya shigo, da", "let us read. You will use": "bari mu karanta. Za ka yi amfani da", "that forbids for the absent:": "ta hani ga wanda ba ya nan:", "You will review the four particles that give one verb a sukun, and see that a verb answering a command also takes a sukun:": "Za ka yi bitar haruffa huɗu da suke ba fi'ili ɗaya sukun, kuma za ka ga cewa fi'ilin da yake amsa umarni shi ma yana ɗaukar sukun:", "read it and you will understand it.": "karanta shi za ka fahimce shi.", "is a": "shi ne", "that comes before the present verb of the absent person or the speaker and gives it a sukun. It makes a command:": "wanda yake zuwa kafin fi'ili mudari'i na wanda ba ya nan ko na mai magana, ya ba shi sukun. Yana yin umarni:", "let him come in.": "bari ya shigo.", "let us read. After": "bari mu karanta. Bayan", "it takes a sukun:": "yana ɗaukar sukun:", "that forbids is used not only for you, but also for someone absent:": "ta hani ba ga “kai” kaɗai ake amfani da ita ba, har ma ga wanda ba ya nan:", "The four particles that give one present verb a sukun are:": "Haruffa huɗu da suke ba fi'ili mudari'i ɗaya sukun su ne:", "that forbids, and": "ta hani, da", "When a present verb answers a command or a don't, it takes a sukun:": "Idan fi'ili mudari'i yana amsa umarni ko hani, yana ɗaukar sukun:", "And for crying out in pain:": "Da kuma don kururuwar zafi:", "لِيَدْخُلْ (let him come in)": "لِيَدْخُلْ (bari ya shigo)", "Let him…": "Bari ya…", "Don't (absent)": "Kada (ga wanda ba ya nan)", "Answer to a command": "Amsar umarni", "Oh my…!": "Wayyo…!", "In this lesson you will learn لَامُ الْأَمْرِ, the لِـ that makes a command for someone absent or for us: لِيَدْخُلْ, let him come in, and لِنَقْرَأْ, let us read. You will use لَا that forbids for the absent: لَا يَخْرُجْ أَحَدٌ. You will review the four particles that give one verb a sukun, and see that a verb answering a command also takes a sukun: اِقْرَأْهُ تَفْهَمْهُ, read it and you will understand it.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi لَامُ الْأَمْرِ, لِـ mai yin umarni ga wanda ba ya nan ko gare mu: لِيَدْخُلْ, bari ya shigo, da لِنَقْرَأْ, bari mu karanta. Za ka yi amfani da لَا ta hani ga wanda ba ya nan: لَا يَخْرُجْ أَحَدٌ. Za ka yi bitar haruffa huɗu da suke ba fi'ili ɗaya sukun, kuma za ka ga cewa fi'ilin da yake amsa umarni shi ma yana ɗaukar sukun: اِقْرَأْهُ تَفْهَمْهُ, karanta shi za ka fahimce shi.", "liyadkhul": "liyadkhul", "linaqra'": "linaqra'", "let him come in": "bari ya shigo", "let us read": "bari mu karanta", "with a kasra that comes before the present verb of the": "mai kasra wanda yake zuwa kafin fi'ili mudari'i na", "absent": "wanda ba ya nan", "person or the": "ko na", "speaker": "mai magana", "and gives it a": "kuma yake ba shi", ": it makes a command.": ": yana yin umarni.", "There is a man at the door who wants to come in. Let him come in.": "Akwai wani mutum a bakin ƙofa da yake so ya shigo. Bari ya shigo.", "Let the new students go to the hospital, and let them come back after the vaccination.": "Bari sababbin ɗalibai su tafi asibiti, kuma su dawo bayan rigakafin.", "And let every student wear a nice thobe.": "Kuma kowane ɗalibi ya sa riga mai kyau.", "Let us read the lesson now.": "Bari mu karanta darasin yanzu.", "Then let man look at his food.": "To mutum ya duba abincinsa.", "laa yakhruj aḥadun fee athnaa'id-darsi": "laa yakhruj aḥadun fee athnaa'id-darsi", "No one is to go out during the lesson.": "Kada wani ya fita lokacin darasi.", "(don't) is used not only for “you” (": "(kada) ba ga “kai” kaɗai ake amfani da ita ba (", ") but also for the": ") har ma ga", "A delegation from a Nigerian university will visit the institute tomorrow. So no one is to be absent or late.": "Wata tawaga daga wata jami'ar Najeriya za ta ziyarci cibiyar gobe. Don haka kada wani ya yi fashi ko ya makara.", "None of you is to enter the class during the lesson.": "Kada wani daga cikinku ya shiga aji lokacin darasi.", "No one is to eat with the left hand.": "Kada wani ya ci abinci da hannun hagu.", "lam": "lam", "lammaa": "lammaa", "don't": "kada", "li": "li", "let": "bari", "four particles": "haruffa huɗu", "that give": "da suke ba", "present verb a": "fi'ili mudari'i", "let him go": "bari ya tafi", "Did We not make for him two eyes?": "Shin ba Mu sanya masa idanu biyu ba?", "And faith has not yet entered your hearts.": "Kuma imani bai riga ya shiga zukatanku ba.", "Do not grieve; indeed Allah is with us.": "Kada ka yi baƙin ciki; lalle Allah Yana tare da mu.", "iqra'hu marratan ukhraa tafhamhu": "iqra'hu marratan ukhraa tafhamhu", "Read it again and you will understand it.": "Ka sake karanta shi za ka fahimce shi.", "When a present verb is the": "Idan fi'ili mudari'i yana", "answer to a command or a “don't”": "amsa umarni ko “kada”", "), it takes a": "), yana ɗaukar", "(crying out in pain):": "(kururuwar zafi):", "Teacher, I did not understand yesterday's lesson well. Read it again and you will understand it, in sha Allah.": "Malam, ban fahimci darasin jiya sosai ba. Ka sake karanta shi za ka fahimce shi, in sha Allah.", "I could not find my notebook, teacher. Look well and you will find it, in sha Allah.": "Ban sami littafin rubutuna ba, malam. Ka duba sosai za ka same shi, in sha Allah.", "Visit me and I will visit you.": "Ka ziyarce ni in ziyarce ka.", "Oh my head! What's wrong, Zubayr? I have a bad headache.": "Wayyo kaina! Me ya faru, Zubayr? Ina ciwon kai mai tsanani.", "a male nurse": "nas namiji, ma'aikacin jinya", "vaccination": "rigakafi", "a delegation": "tawaga", "nice, beautiful": "mai kyau", "housing, residence": "gidan zama, mazauni", "oh my head! (pain)": "wayyo kaina! (zafi)", "ah! (pain)": "wayyo! (zafi)", "mumarriḍun": "mumarriḍun", "at-taṭ'eemu": "at-taṭ'eemu", "wafdun (pl. wufuudun)": "wafdun (jam'i: wufuudun)", "sakanun": "sakanun", "waa ra'saah": "waa ra'saah", "aah": "aah", "the لِـ of command": "لِـ ta umarni", "Teacher, I didn't understand yesterday's lesson well. Read it again and you will understand it, in sha Allah. Take your notebooks.": "Malam, ban fahimci darasin jiya sosai ba. Ka sake karanta shi za ka fahimce shi, in sha Allah. Ku ɗauki littattafan rubutunku.", "I couldn't find my notebook, teacher. Look well and you'll find it, in sha Allah. It has a yellow cover, doesn't it? Yes. Here it is.": "Ban sami littafin rubutuna ba, malam. Ka duba sosai za ka same shi, in sha Allah. Bangonsa rawaya ne, ko ba haka ba? Ee. Ga shi nan.", "There's a man at the door who wants to come in. Let him come in. I am a nurse at the university hospital. I want to take the new students for vaccination.": "Akwai wani mutum a bakin ƙofa da yake so ya shigo. Bari ya shigo. Ni ma'aikacin jinya ne a asibitin jami'a. Ina so in tafi da sababbin ɗalibai don rigakafi.", "Take them. Let the new students go to the hospital and let them come back after the vaccination.": "Ka tafi da su. Bari sababbin ɗalibai su tafi asibiti kuma su dawo bayan rigakafin.", "Listen, brothers: a delegation from a Nigerian university will visit tomorrow. So no one is to be absent or late, and every student should wear a nice thobe.": "Ku saurara, 'yan'uwa: wata tawaga daga wata jami'ar Najeriya za ta zo ziyara gobe. Don haka kada wani ya yi fashi ko ya makara, kuma kowane ɗalibi ya sa riga mai kyau.", "Let us read the lesson now. Teacher, I want to go out. No one is to go out during the lesson.": "Bari mu karanta darasin yanzu. Malam, ina so in fita. Kada wani ya fita lokacin darasi.", "Oh my head! What's wrong, Zubayr? A bad headache. Ah, ah. Go to the hospital, and let one of your housemates go with you.": "Wayyo kaina! Me ya faru, Zubayr? Ciwon kai mai tsanani. Wayyo, wayyo. Ka tafi asibiti, kuma ɗaya daga cikin abokan gidanka ya tafi tare da kai.", "+ the verb with a sukun (the": "+ fi'ili mai sukun (", "drops; a final vowel drops).": "yana faɗuwa; wasalin ƙarshe yana faɗuwa).", "Make it “let …”:": "Mayar da shi “bari …”:", "that forbids for the absent: sukun.": "ta hani ga wanda ba ya nan: sukun.", "The verb that answers a command takes a": "Fi'ilin da yake amsa umarni yana ɗaukar", "The verb that answers a command takes a sukun.": "Fi'ilin da yake amsa umarni yana ɗaukar sukun.", "Cry out in pain:": "Yi kururuwar zafi:", "Let him come in.": "Bari ya shigo.", "Listen, then write the word. (a male nurse)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (ma'aikacin jinya)", "✅ Let us read the lesson now.": "✅ Bari mu karanta darasin yanzu.", "✅ Read it again and you will understand it.": "✅ Ka sake karanta shi za ka fahimce shi.", "✅ Write: a male nurse": "✅ Rubuta: ma'aikacin jinya", "when or if. It usually comes before a past verb but gives a future meaning:": "idan ko lokacin da. Yawanci yana zuwa kafin fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci amma yana ba da ma'anar nan gaba:", "You will learn when the answer must start with": "Za ka koyi yaushe dole amsar ta fara da", "when it is a nominal sentence, or a command, a don't or a question, as in": "idan jumla ismiyya ce, ko umarni, hani ko tambaya, kamar a", "on words with": "a kan kalmomi masu", "and what to say after a sneeze.": "da abin da ake faɗa bayan atishawa.", "means when or if. It usually comes before a past verb but gives a future meaning. The first part is the condition, and the second is the answer:": "yana nufin idan ko lokacin da. Yawanci yana zuwa kafin fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci amma yana ba da ma'anar nan gaba. Sashe na farko shi ne sharaɗi, na biyu kuma amsa:", "The answer must start with": "Dole amsar ta fara da", "when it is a nominal sentence:": "idan jumla ismiyya ce:", "Or a command, a don't or a question:": "Ko umarni, hani ko tambaya:", "When you add": "Idan ka ƙara", "to a word ending in": "ga kalma mai ƙarewa da", "is dropped:": "ana cire", "is a school dictionary.": "ƙamus ne na makaranta.", "After a sneeze: the one who sneezes says": "Bayan atishawa: wanda ya yi atishawa yana cewa", "His brother says": "Ɗan'uwansa yana cewa", "Then he answers": "Sai ya amsa", "إِذَا (when)": "إِذَا (idan)", "the answer with فَـ": "amsa tare da فَـ", "With فَـ or not?": "Tare da فَـ ko babu?", "Why فَـ?": "Me ya sa فَـ?", "In this lesson you will learn إِذَا, when or if. It usually comes before a past verb but gives a future meaning: إِذَا جَاءَ رَمَضَانُ فُتِحَتْ أَبْوَابُ الْجَنَّةِ. You will learn when the answer must start with فَـ: when it is a nominal sentence, or a command, a don't or a question, as in إِذَا جَاءَ فَقُلْ لَهُ. You will also learn the ending ـِيٌّ on words with تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ, like مَدْرَسِيٌّ and مَكِّيٌّ, and what to say after a sneeze.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi إِذَا, idan ko lokacin da. Yawanci yana zuwa kafin fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci amma yana ba da ma'anar nan gaba: إِذَا جَاءَ رَمَضَانُ فُتِحَتْ أَبْوَابُ الْجَنَّةِ. Za ka koyi yaushe dole amsar ta fara da فَـ: idan jumla ismiyya ce, ko umarni, hani ko tambaya, kamar a إِذَا جَاءَ فَقُلْ لَهُ. Za ka kuma koyi ƙarshen ـِيٌّ a kan kalmomi masu تَاءْ مَرْبُوطَةْ, kamar مَدْرَسِيٌّ da مَكِّيٌّ, da abin da ake faɗa bayan atishawa.", "idhaa jaa'a ramaḍaanu futiḥat abwaabul-jannati": "idhaa jaa'a ramaḍaanu futiḥat abwaabul-jannati", "When Ramadan comes, the gates of Paradise are opened.": "Idan Ramadan ya zo, ana buɗe ƙofofin Aljanna.", "(when, if) is a time word with the meaning of a": "(idan, lokacin da) kalmar lokaci ce mai ma'anar", "condition": "sharaɗi", ". It usually comes before a": ". Yawanci yana zuwa kafin fi'ilin", "verb but turns its meaning to the": "amma yana mayar da ma'anarsa zuwa", ". The first part is": ". Sashe na farko shi ne", "the condition": "sharaɗi", ") and the second is": ") na biyu kuma shi ne", "the answer": "amsa", "الشَّرْطُ: the condition": "الشَّرْطُ: sharaɗi", "جَوَابُ الشَّرْطِ: the answer": "جَوَابُ الشَّرْطِ: amsar sharaɗi", "When a servant falls sick or travels, there is written for him the like of what he used to do when at home and healthy.": "Idan bawa ya yi rashin lafiya ko ya yi tafiya, ana rubuta masa kwatankwacin abin da yake yi lokacin yana gida da lafiya.", "When you hear the call, say the same as the muadhdhin says.": "Idan kuka ji kiran sallah, ku faɗi kamar abin da ladani yake faɗa.", "idhaa jaa'a faqul lahu ya'teenee": "idhaa jaa'a faqul lahu ya'teenee", "When he comes, tell him to come to me.": "Idan ya zo, ka gaya masa ya zo wurina.", "fa innee qareebun": "fa innee qareebun", "then I am near.": "to lalle Ni kusa nake.", "The answer": "Amsar", "must start with": "dole ta fara da", "when it is: (1) a": "idan ta kasance: (1)", "command, a don't, or a question": "umarni, hani, ko tambaya", "When he comes, tell him to come to me in my office.": "Idan ya zo, ka gaya masa ya zo wurina a ofishina.", "When he comes, do not let him in, and let him go to the principal.": "Idan ya zo, kada ka bar shi ya shigo, kuma ya tafi wurin shugaban makaranta.", "And when My servants ask you about Me, then I am near.": "Kuma idan bayina suka tambaye ka game da Ni, to lalle Ni kusa nake.", "When you see Hamid, ask him about the time of departure.": "Idan ka ga Hamid, ka tambaye shi lokacin tashi.", "When you find the patient asleep, don't wake him.": "Idan ka sami mara lafiyar yana barci, kada ka tashe shi.", "madrasatun": "madrasatun", "school": "makaranta", "madrasiyyun": "madrasiyyun", "of school": "na makaranta", "makkiyyun": "makkiyyun", "Makkan": "Bamakke", "= a school dictionary)": "yana nufin ƙamus na makaranta)", "This is a school dictionary. If you want to buy a dictionary, buy this one; it is very useful.": "Wannan ƙamus ne na makaranta. Idan kana so ka sayi ƙamus, sayi wannan; yana da amfani sosai.", "Is مَدْرَسِيٌّ related to مَدْرَسَةٌ? Then where is its ة?": "Shin مَدْرَسِيٌّ yana da alaƙa da مَدْرَسَةٌ? To ina ة ɗinsa?", "If you relate to Makkah, you say: مَكِّيٌّ.": "Idan ka danganta ga Makka, sai ka ce: مَكِّيٌّ.", "Praise be to Allah": "Alhamdu lillah, godiya ta tabbata ga Allah", "yarḥamuka llaahu": "yarḥamuka llaahu", "May Allah have mercy on you": "Allah Ya yi maka rahama", "yahdeekumu llaahu": "yahdeekumu llaahu", "May Allah guide you": "Allah Ya shiryar da ku", "The sneeze:": "Atishawa:", ". Note the": ". Ka lura da", "Praise be to Allah. (the one who sneezes)": "Alhamdu lillah. (wanda ya yi atishawa)", "May Allah have mercy on you. (the listener)": "Allah Ya yi maka rahama. (mai sauraro)", "May Allah guide you and set your affairs right. (the answer)": "Allah Ya shiryar da ku Ya gyara al'amuranku. (amsa)", "of school, for school": "na makaranta, don makaranta", "related to": "wanda aka danganta ga", "he sneezed": "ya yi atishawa", "sneezing": "atishawa", "staying at home": "mazaunin gida, wanda ba ya tafiya", "the plague": "annoba", "he woke someone": "ya tayar da wani daga barci", "mansuubun": "mansuubun", "'aṭasa (ya'ṭisu)": "'aṭasa (ya'ṭisu)", "al-'uṭaasu": "al-'uṭaasu", "muqeemun": "muqeemun", "aṭ-ṭaa'uunu": "aṭ-ṭaa'uunu", "ayqaẓa (yuwqiẓu)": "ayqaẓa (yuwqiẓu)", "may Allah have mercy on you": "Allah Ya yi maka rahama", "when, if": "idan, lokacin da", "Is this a dictionary, honourable shaikh? Yes. It's a school dictionary. If you want to buy one, buy this; it's very useful.": "Wannan ƙamus ne, mai girma shehi? Ee. Ƙamus ne na makaranta. Idan kana so ka saya, sayi wannan; yana da amfani sosai.", "You said a school dictionary. Is مَدْرَسِيٌّ related to مَدْرَسَةٌ? Where is its ة? If you relate to a noun ending in ة, you drop the ة. So for Makkah you say مَكِّيٌّ.": "Ka ce ƙamus na makaranta. Shin مَدْرَسِيٌّ yana da alaƙa da مَدْرَسَةٌ? Ina ة ɗinsa? Idan ka danganta ga suna mai ƙarewa da ة, kana cire ة ɗin. Don haka ga Makka kana cewa مَكِّيٌّ.", "Hasn't al-Husayn come? Not yet. When he comes, tell him to come to my office; there is a telegram for him.": "Al-Husayn bai zo ba? Tukuna. Idan ya zo, ka gaya masa ya zo ofishina; akwai saƙon waya (telegram) gare shi.", "Where is Ibrahim? Is he late again today as usual? When he comes, don't let him in; let him go to the principal.": "Ina Ibrahim? Ya sake makara yau kamar yadda ya saba? Idan ya zo, kada ka bar shi ya shigo; ya tafi wurin shugaban makaranta.", "Who sneezed? Me. Abdul-Hadi, when you sneeze, praise Allah. When one of you sneezes, let him say: praise be to Allah, and let his brother say: may Allah have mercy on you.": "Wa ya yi atishawa? Ni. Abdulhadi, idan ka yi atishawa, ka gode wa Allah. Idan ɗayanku ya yi atishawa, ya ce: alhamdu lillah, ɗan'uwansa kuma ya ce: Allah Ya yi maka rahama.", "The answer of": "Amsar", "before a nominal sentence, a command, a don't or a question.": "kafin jumla ismiyya, umarni, hani ko tambaya.", "What kind of answer is it?": "Wane irin amsa ce?", "a command": "umarni", "a don't": "hani", "Why does it need": "Me ya sa take buƙatar", "a nominal sentence": "jumla ismiyya", "Drop the": "Cire", "The answer of إِذَا": "Amsar إِذَا", "Why does it need فَـ?": "Me ya sa take buƙatar فَـ?", "If you find the patient asleep, don't wake him.": "Idan ka sami mara lafiyar yana barci, kada ka tashe shi.", "Listen, then write the word. (of school, for school)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (na makaranta)", "This is a school dictionary.": "Wannan ƙamus ne na makaranta.", "✅ If you find the patient asleep, don't wake him.": "✅ Idan ka sami mara lafiyar yana barci, kada ka tashe shi.", "✅ Write: of school, for school": "✅ Rubuta: na makaranta", "✅ This is a school dictionary.": "✅ Wannan ƙamus ne na makaranta.", "In this lesson you will learn the conditional words that give two verbs a sukun:": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi kalmomin sharaɗi da suke ba fi'iloli biyu sukun:", "You will learn more places where the answer needs": "Za ka koyi ƙarin wuraren da amsa take buƙatar", "for saying how many!,": "don faɗin “da yawa!”,", "until or so that,": "har zuwa ko don,", "here, take, and the small form": "ga shi, karɓa, da ƙaramar siffa", "a booklet.": "ƙaramin littafi.", "means if. It gives two verbs a sukun, the condition and the answer:": "yana nufin idan. Yana ba fi'iloli biyu sukun, sharaɗi da amsa:", "Other conditional words also give two verbs a sukun:": "Sauran kalmomin sharaɗi su ma suna ba fi'iloli biyu sukun:", "whoever.": "duk wanda.", "whatever.": "duk abin da.", "whenever.": "duk lokacin da.", "wherever.": "duk inda.", "whichever.": "duk wanne.", "The answer also takes": "Amsa tana kuma ɗaukar", "when it is": "idan ta kasance", "Or starts with": "Ko ta fara da", "can also mean how many, a lot, and the noun after it ends in": "yana iya nufin da yawa, kuma sunan da yake bayansa yana ƙarewa da", "! The question": "! Tambayar", "takes -an:": "tana ɗaukar -an:", "means until:": "yana nufin har zuwa:", "إِنْ تَجْتَهِدْ تَنْجَحْ (if you work hard you will pass)": "إِنْ تَجْتَهِدْ تَنْجَحْ (idan ka yi ƙoƙari za ka ci)", "Two sukuns": "Sukun biyu", "With فَـ": "Tare da فَـ", "In this lesson you will learn the conditional words that give two verbs a sukun: إِنْ, if, as in إِنْ تَجْتَهِدْ تَنْجَحْ, and مَنْ, مَا, مَتَى, أَيْنَ, أَيُّ and مَهْمَا. You will learn more places where the answer needs فَـ, like فَقَدْ, فَلَنْ and فَسَـ. You will also learn كَمْ for saying how many!, حَتَّى, until or so that, هَاؤُمْ, here, take, and the small form كُتَيِّبٌ, a booklet.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi kalmomin sharaɗi da suke ba fi'iloli biyu sukun: إِنْ, idan, kamar a إِنْ تَجْتَهِدْ تَنْجَحْ, da kuma مَنْ, مَا, مَتَى, أَيْنَ, أَيُّ da مَهْمَا. Za ka koyi ƙarin wuraren da amsa take buƙatar فَـ, kamar فَقَدْ, فَلَنْ da فَسَـ. Za ka kuma koyi كَمْ don faɗin “da yawa!”, حَتَّى, har zuwa ko don, هَاؤُمْ, ga shi, karɓa, da ƙaramar siffa كُتَيِّبٌ, ƙaramin littafi.", "in tajtahid tanjaḥ": "in tajtahid tanjaḥ", "If you work hard, you will pass.": "Idan ka yi ƙoƙari, za ka ci jarrabawa.", "(if) gives": "(idan) yana ba", "verbs a": "fi'iloli biyu", ": the condition (": ": sharaɗi (", ") and the answer (": ") da amsa (", ". Both verbs can also be past:": ". Fi'ilolin biyu suna iya zama na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci:", "فِعْلُ الشَّرْطِ: sukun": "فِعْلُ الشَّرْطِ: sukun", "جَوَابُ الشَّرْطِ: sukun": "جَوَابُ الشَّرْطِ: sukun", "If you are absent after this, you will be expelled.": "Idan ka yi fashi bayan wannan, za a kore ka.", "If you support Allah, He will support you and make your feet firm.": "Idan kuka taimaki Allah, zai taimake ku Ya tabbatar da dugaduganku.", "And unless You forgive me and have mercy on me, I will be among the losers.": "Kuma idan ba Ka gafarta mini ba Ka yi mini rahama, zan kasance cikin masu hasara.", "And if you return, We will return.": "Kuma idan kuka koma, Mu ma za Mu koma.", "whoever": "duk wanda", "whatever": "duk abin da", "whenever": "duk lokacin da", "ayyu": "ayyu", "whichever": "duk wanne", "mahmaa": "mahmaa", "Other conditional words also give": "Sauran kalmomin sharaɗi su ma suna ba", "verbs a sukun:": "fi'iloli biyu sukun:", "So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it.": "To duk wanda ya aikata alheri gwargwadon ƙwayar zarra zai gan shi.", "Whenever you come, we will come.": "Duk lokacin da ka zo, za mu zo.", "Whichever class we find empty, we will sit in it.": "Duk ajin da muka samu fanko, za mu zauna a cikinsa.", "Wherever you are, death will overtake you.": "Duk inda kuke, mutuwa za ta riske ku.", "Whatever you say, we will believe you.": "Duk abin da ka faɗa, za mu gaskata ka.", "faman fahima haadhad-darsa faqad fahima duruusan katheeratan": "faman fahima haadhad-darsa faqad fahima duruusan katheeratan", "Whoever understands this lesson has understood many lessons.": "Duk wanda ya fahimci wannan darasin, ya fahimci darussa da yawa.", "Besides a nominal sentence and a command, the answer takes": "Bayan jumla ismiyya da umarni, amsa tana ɗaukar", "when it: is a fixed verb like": "idan: fi'ili ne mara canjawa kamar", "); starts with": "); ta fara da", "); with": "); da", "; or with": "; ko da", ". Then the answer does not take a sukun.": ". A wannan hali amsar ba ta ɗaukar sukun.", "Whoever wants to benefit, let him come; and whoever does not come is not blamed.": "Duk wanda yake so ya amfana, ya zo; wanda bai zo ba kuma ba za a zarge shi ba.", "Whoever cheats us is not one of us.": "Duk wanda ya yaudare mu ba ya cikinmu.", "Whatever the excuse, it will not be accepted from now on.": "Duk abin da uzurin ya kasance, ba za a karɓe shi ba daga yanzu.", "If you travel, I will travel.": "Idan ka yi tafiya, ni ma zan yi tafiya.", "kam najmin fis-samaa'i": "kam najmin fis-samaa'i", "How many stars are in the sky!": "Taurari nawa ne a sama!", "kam kitaaban 'indaka": "kam kitaaban 'indaka", "how many …!": "… da yawa!", "(a lot), and the noun after it ends in": "(da yawa), kuma sunan da yake bayansa yana ƙarewa da", "! (or with": "! (ko da", "). The question": "). Tambayar", "Also": "Haka kuma", "= until or so that, and the verb after it ends in -a:": "yana nufin har zuwa ko don, kuma fi'ilin da yake bayansa yana ƙarewa da -a:", "= here, take (to many);": "yana nufin ga shi, karɓa (ga mutane da yawa);", "to one. And the small form": "ga mutum ɗaya. Da ƙaramar siffa", "How many times have I told you this!": "Sau nawa na gaya maka wannan!", "How many a small group has overcome a large group by Allah's leave!": "Ƙananan jama'a nawa ne suka rinjayi manyan jama'a da izinin Allah!", "Whoever comes late, let him not enter until he asks permission.": "Duk wanda ya makara, kada ya shiga sai ya nemi izini.", "Here is an important announcement.": "Ga wata muhimmiyar sanarwa.", "These are five useful booklets containing Islamic stories.": "Waɗannan ƙananan littattafai biyar ne masu amfani da suke ɗauke da labaran Musulunci.", "the regulations": "ƙa'idoji, dokoki", "he was expelled": "an kore shi", "an excuse": "uzuri", "extra": "ƙari", "a competition": "gasa", "a booklet": "ƙaramin littafi", "he registered": "ya yi rajista", "he apologised": "ya ba da haƙuri", "al-laa'iḥatu": "al-laa'iḥatu", "fuṣila (yufṣalu)": "fuṣila (yufṣalu)", "'udhrun (pl. a'dhaarun)": "'udhrun (jam'i: a'dhaarun)", "iḍaafiyyun": "iḍaafiyyun", "musaabaqatun": "musaabaqatun", "kutayyibun": "kutayyibun", "jaa'izatun": "jaa'izatun", "sajjala (yusajjilu)": "sajjala (yusajjilu)", "i'tadhara (ya'tadhiru)": "i'tadhara (ya'tadhiru)", "until, so that": "har zuwa, don", "if": "idan", "Yasir, you were absent two whole weeks. If you are absent after this, you will be expelled. The rules say whoever is absent more than two weeks has his registration ended.": "Yasir, ka yi fashin cikakkun makonni biyu. Idan ka yi fashi bayan wannan, za a kore ka. Dokoki sun ce duk wanda ya yi fashi fiye da makonni biyu za a soke rajistarsa.", "I will not be absent after this, in sha Allah. How many times have you told me that! I was only absent with an excuse. Whatever the excuse, it will not be accepted from now on.": "Ba zan yi fashi ba bayan wannan, in sha Allah. Sau nawa ka gaya mini haka! Na yi fashi ne kawai da uzuri. Duk abin da uzurin ya kasance, ba za a karɓe shi ba daga yanzu.", "Whoever comes late, let him not enter until he asks permission. I'm sorry. I saw you were busy, so I came in so as not to disturb you.": "Duk wanda ya makara, kada ya shiga sai ya nemi izini. Ka yi haƙuri. Na ga kana da aiki, don haka na shigo don kada in dame ka.", "Here is an important announcement. These are five useful booklets with Islamic stories. Whoever reads them and answers the questions gets a prize.": "Ga wata muhimmiyar sanarwa. Waɗannan ƙananan littattafai biyar ne masu amfani da labaran Musulunci. Duk wanda ya karanta su ya amsa tambayoyin zai sami kyauta.", "Whoever wants to join this competition, let him register with me. Shaikh, we often don't find you in your office. If you don't find me in my office, you will find me in the principal's office.": "Duk wanda yake so ya shiga wannan gasar, ya yi rajista a wurina. Shehi, sau da yawa ba ma samun ka a ofishinka. Idan ba ku same ni a ofishina ba, za ku same ni a ofishin shugaban makaranta.", "إِنْ is a conditional word that gives two verbs a sukun, as in: if you work hard you will pass. If you go to the market I will go with you.": "إِنْ kalmar sharaɗi ce da take ba fi'iloli biyu sukun, kamar: idan ka yi ƙoƙari za ka ci. Idan ka tafi kasuwa zan tafi tare da kai.", "Understand this lesson well; whoever understands it has understood many lessons. I have an extra lesson this evening. Whoever wants to benefit, let him come.": "Ku fahimci wannan darasin sosai; duk wanda ya fahimce shi ya fahimci darussa da yawa. Ina da ƙarin darasi a yammacin yau. Duk wanda yake so ya amfana, ya zo.", "Condition and answer: sukun": "Sharaɗi da amsa: sukun", "… give two verbs a sukun.": "… suna ba fi'iloli biyu sukun.", "give two verbs a": "suna ba fi'iloli biyu", "Does the answer need": "Amsar tana buƙatar", "Exclamation:": "Mamaki:", "…! or": "…! ko", "Exclamation: -i. Question: -an.": "Mamaki: -i. Tambaya: -an.", "“How many stars are in the sky!”": "“Taurari nawa ne a sama!”", "Question:": "Tambaya:", "“How many students were absent today?”": "“Ɗalibai nawa ne suka yi fashi yau?”", "كَمْ …! or كَمْ …?": "كَمْ …! ko كَمْ …?", "Listen, then write the word. (whatever)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (duk abin da)", "“How many times have I told you!”": "“Sau nawa na gaya maka!”", "Does the answer need فَـ?": "Amsar tana buƙatar فَـ?", "✅ “How many stars are in the sky!”": "✅ “Taurari nawa ne a sama!”", "✅ Write: whatever": "✅ Rubuta: duk abin da", "✅ How many times have I told you this!": "✅ Sau nawa na gaya maka wannan!", "✅ “How many students were absent today?”": "✅ “Ɗalibai nawa ne suka yi fashi yau?”", "✅ “How many times have I told you!”": "✅ “Sau nawa na gaya maka!”", "✅ Whatever you say, we will believe you.": "✅ Duk abin da ka faɗa, za mu gaskata ka.", "In this lesson you will learn that a verb has three or four root letters,": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi cewa fi'ili yana da haruffan asali uku ko huɗu,", "and is bare,": "kuma yana iya zama tsirara (mujarrad),", "or has extra letters,": "ko kuma yana da ƙarin haruffa (mazid),", "You will see the six patterns of the bare three-letter verb, and the pattern": "Za ka ga wazanai shida na fi'ili mai harafi uku tsirara, da wazanin", "which doubles the middle letter:": "wanda yake ninka harafin tsakiya:", "and its doer noun": "da sunan mai aikatawa", "and done-to noun": "da sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki", "You will also learn two plural patterns,": "Za ka kuma koyi wazanan jam'i guda biyu,", "A verb has three root letters,": "Fi'ili yana da haruffan asali uku,", "or four,": "ko huɗu,", "It is": "Yana iya zama", "with only the root letters, or": "da haruffan asali kaɗai, ko", "with extra letters, like": "da ƙarin haruffa, kamar", "The bare three-letter verb has six patterns:": "Fi'ili mai harafi uku tsirara yana da wazanai shida:", "doubles the middle letter:": "yana ninka harafin tsakiya:", "The present starts with": "Mudari'i yana farawa da", "The verbal noun:": "Masdari:", "the verbal noun is": "masdari shi ne", "For these verbs, the doer noun is the present verb with": "A waɗannan fi'iloli, sunan mai aikatawa shi ne fi'ili mudari'i tare da", "before the last letter:": "a gaban harafin ƙarshe:", "The done-to noun has": "Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki yana da", "recorded. And the place noun is the same:": "abin da aka naɗa (rikodi). Sunan wuri kuma iri ɗaya ne:", "a prayer place.": "wurin sallah.", "Two plural patterns.": "Wazanan jam'i guda biyu.", "سَلَّمَ يُسَلِّمُ (the pattern فَعَّلَ)": "سَلَّمَ يُسَلِّمُ (wazanin فَعَّلَ)", "Kind of verb": "Irin fi'ili", "Present of فَعَّلَ": "Mudari'in فَعَّلَ", "In this lesson you will learn that a verb has three or four root letters, ثُلَاثِيٌّ or رُبَاعِيٌّ, and is bare, مُجَرَّدٌ, or has extra letters, مَزِيدٌ. You will see the six patterns of the bare three-letter verb, and the pattern فَعَّلَ, which doubles the middle letter: سَلَّمَ, يُسَلِّمُ, سَلِّمْ, تَسْلِيمٌ, and its doer noun مُسَلِّمٌ and done-to noun مُسَلَّمٌ. You will also learn two plural patterns, طَلَبَةٌ and نُسَخٌ.": "A wannan darasin za ka koyi cewa fi'ili yana da haruffan asali uku ko huɗu, ثُلَاثِيٌّ ko رُبَاعِيٌّ, kuma yana iya zama tsirara, مُجَرَّدٌ, ko kuma yana da ƙarin haruffa, مَزِيدٌ. Za ka ga wazanai shida na fi'ili mai harafi uku tsirara, da wazanin فَعَّلَ, wanda yake ninka harafin tsakiya: سَلَّمَ, يُسَلِّمُ, سَلِّمْ, تَسْلِيمٌ, da sunan mai aikatawa مُسَلِّمٌ da sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki مُسَلَّمٌ. Za ka kuma koyi wazanan jam'i guda biyu, طَلَبَةٌ da نُسَخٌ.", "he wrote (3 letters)": "ya rubuta (harafi 3)", "tarjama": "tarjama", "he translated (4)": "ya fassara (4)", "sallama": "sallama", "he handed over (extended)": "ya miƙa (mai ƙari)", "A verb is": "Fi'ili yana iya zama", "(three root letters:": "(haruffan asali uku:", "(four:": "(huɗu:", "). Each is either": "). Kowannensu ko dai", "(only the root letters) or": "(haruffan asali kaɗai) ko", "(with one or more extra letters:": "(da ƙarin harafi ɗaya ko fiye:", "مَزِيدٌ: extra letters": "مَزِيدٌ: ƙarin haruffa", "three-letter, bare": "mai harafi uku, tsirara", "four-letter": "mai harafi huɗu", "three-letter + a doubled middle letter": "mai harafi uku + harafin tsakiya da aka ninka", "three-letter + extra letters": "mai harafi uku + ƙarin haruffa", "kataba yaktubu": "kataba yaktubu", "jalasa yajlisu": "jalasa yajlisu", "dhahaba yadh-habu …": "dhahaba yadh-habu …", "the six patterns of the bare three-letter verb": "wazanai shida na fi'ili mai harafi uku tsirara", "The bare three-letter verb has": "Fi'ili mai harafi uku tsirara yana da", "six patterns": "wazanai shida", "he handed over": "ya miƙa", "yusallimu": "yusallimu", "he hands over": "yana miƙawa", "sallim": "sallim", "hand over!": "miƙa!", "tasleemun": "tasleemun", "handing over": "miƙawa", "doubles the middle letter (": "yana ninka harafin tsakiya (", "). The present starts with a": "). Mudari'i yana farawa da", "). The command:": "). Umarni:", "). The verbal noun:": "). Masdari:", "when the verb ends in a vowel or a hamza (": "idan fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da wasali ko hamza (", "hand over": "miƙa", "kiss": "sumbata", "glorify": "tasbihi, tsarkake Allah", "hand out": "raba", "congratulate": "taya murna", "yu'allimu": "yu'allimu", "he teaches": "yana koyarwa", "mu'allimun": "mu'allimun", "yusajjalu": "yusajjalu", "it is recorded": "ana naɗa shi (rikodi)", "musajjalun": "musajjalun", "recorded": "wanda aka naɗa", "For verbs": "Ga fi'iloli", "other than the bare three-letter verb": "banda fi'ili mai harafi uku tsirara", ": the": ":", "= the present verb with": "yana nufin fi'ili mudari'i tare da", "instead of the present letter, and a": "a madadin harafin mudari'i, da", "= the same with a": "shi ma haka ne tare da", "place/time noun": "sunan wuri/lokaci", "has the same form as the done-to noun:": "yana da siffa ɗaya da sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "(a prayer place).": "(wurin sallah).", "doer: kasra before the last letter": "mai aikatawa: kasra a gaban harafin ƙarshe", "done-to / place: fatha before the last letter": "wanda aka yi wa aiki / wuri: fataha a gaban harafin ƙarshe", "Let us listen to the noble hadith recorded on the tape.": "Bari mu saurari hadisi mai daraja da aka naɗa a kaset.", "It contains coloured pictures to explain the meanings of some words.": "Yana ɗauke da hotuna masu launi don bayyana ma'anonin wasu kalmomi.", "Let Ali go out to the prayer place and call the adhan.": "Bari Ali ya fita zuwa wurin sallah ya yi kiran sallah.", "You are a skilled teacher.": "Kai malami ne gwani.", "ṭalabatun": "ṭalabatun", "students": "ɗalibai", "nuskhatun": "nuskhatun", "nusakhun": "nusakhun", "copies": "kwafe-kwafe", "Two broken plural patterns:": "Wazanan jam'i masu karyewa guda biyu:", "Marwan, hand out these copies to the students.": "Marwan, raba wa ɗalibai waɗannan kwafe-kwafen.", "It contains coloured pictures.": "Yana ɗauke da hotuna masu launi.", "These rooms are for the new students.": "Waɗannan ɗakunan na sababbin ɗalibai ne.", "he congratulated": "ya taya murna", "winning": "nasara", "he handed out": "ya raba", "huge": "babba sosai, ƙato", "a volume": "juzu'i (bango)", "smoking": "shan taba", "the air conditioner": "na'urar sanyaya ɗaki (AC)", "he kissed": "ya sumbata", "hanna'a (yuhanni'u)": "hanna'a (yuhanni'u)", "fawzun": "fawzun", "wazza'a (yuwazzi'u)": "wazza'a (yuwazzi'u)", "ḍakhmun": "ḍakhmun", "mujalladun": "mujalladun", "at-tadkheenu": "at-tadkheenu", "al-mukayyifu": "al-mukayyifu", "qabbala (yuqabbilu)": "qabbala (yuqabbilu)", "with extra letters": "mai ƙarin haruffa", "three-letter": "mai harafi uku", "Abdus-Salam, I congratulate you on winning the Qur'an memorisation and tajwid competition. Thank you, doctor. May Allah reward you.": "Abdussalam, ina taya ka murnar nasarar da ka samu a gasar haddar Alƙur'ani da tajwidi. Na gode, Dakta. Allah Ya saka maka da alheri.", "Marwan, hand out these copies to the students. What is this huge book you have, doctor?": "Marwan, raba wa ɗalibai waɗannan kwafe-kwafen. Mene ne wannan ƙaton littafin da kake da shi, Dakta?", "This is a university dictionary. It has many benefits, and contains coloured pictures to explain some words. In how many volumes? In two huge volumes.": "Wannan ƙamus ne na jami'a. Yana da amfani da yawa, kuma yana ɗauke da hotuna masu launi don bayyana wasu kalmomi. Juzu'i nawa ne? Juzu'i biyu manya.", "Who wrote it? A group of language scholars. Your absences have increased, Hamid. My father came to Madinah last week, so I was busy receiving him, serving him and seeing him off.": "Wa ya wallafa shi? Wasu gungun masana harshe. Fashinka ya yi yawa, Hamid. Babana ya zo Madina makon da ya wuce, don haka na shagala da tarbarsa, hidimarsa da rakiyarsa.", "Shall I turn on the air conditioner, doctor? It has got very hot. No objection. Let us listen to the noble hadith recorded on the tape.": "In kunna na'urar sanyaya ɗaki, Dakta? Zafi ya yi yawa sosai. Ba laifi. Bari mu saurari hadisi mai daraja da aka naɗa a kaset.", "The Prophet kissed al-Hasan ibn Ali. Al-Aqra' said: I have ten children and have never kissed one of them. He said: whoever does not show mercy is not shown mercy.": "Annabi ya sumbaci al-Hasan ɗan Ali. Al-Aqra' ya ce: ina da 'ya'ya goma ban taɓa sumbatar ko ɗaya daga cikinsu ba. Sai ya ce: duk wanda ba ya jin tausayi, ba za a ji tausayinsa ba.", "The time of Dhuhr has come and the adhan has not yet been called. It seems the muadhdhin is not here. Let Ali go out to the prayer place and call the adhan.": "Lokacin Azahar ya yi kuma har yanzu ba a kira sallah ba. Kamar ladanin ba ya nan. Bari Ali ya fita zuwa wurin sallah ya yi kiran sallah.", "three-letter, extended": "mai harafi uku, mai ƙari", "What kind of verb?": "Wane irin fi'ili?", "Damma on the present letter,": "Ɗamma a kan harafin mudari'i,", "Damma on the present letter, kasra before the last.": "Ɗamma a kan harafin mudari'i, kasra a gaban na ƙarshe.", "Choose the verbal noun.": "Zaɓi masdarin.", "Verbal noun:": "Masdari:", "Kasra for the doer;": "Kasra ga mai aikatawa;", "Doer, done-to, place": "Mai aikatawa, wanda aka yi wa aiki, wuri", "Kasra for the doer; fatha for the done-to and the place.": "Kasra ga mai aikatawa; fataha ga wanda aka yi wa aiki da wuri.", "يُسَجِّلُ → doer": "يُسَجِّلُ → mai aikatawa", "for the done-to and the place.": "ga wanda aka yi wa aiki da wuri.", "يُصَلِّي → place": "يُصَلِّي → wuri", "يُعَلِّمُ → doer": "يُعَلِّمُ → mai aikatawa", "يُؤَذِّنُ → doer": "يُؤَذِّنُ → mai aikatawa", "يُلَوَّنُ → done-to": "يُلَوَّنُ → wanda aka yi wa aiki", "Plural:": "Jam'i:", "Let Ali go out to the prayer place.": "Bari Ali ya fita zuwa wurin sallah.", "Hand out these copies to the students.": "Raba wa ɗalibai waɗannan kwafe-kwafen.", "Listen, then write the word. (huge)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (ƙato)", "I congratulate you on your win.": "Ina taya ka murnar nasararka.", "✅ Hand out these copies to the students.": "✅ Raba wa ɗalibai waɗannan kwafe-kwafen.", "✅ Write: huge": "✅ Rubuta: ƙato", "✅ I congratulate you on your win.": "✅ Ina taya ka murnar nasararka.", "This is the last lesson of Book 3. You will learn the pattern": "Wannan shi ne darasi na ƙarshe na Littafi na 3. Za ka koyi wazanin", "which adds a hamza at the start:": "wanda yake ƙara hamza a farko:", "he sent,": "ya aika,", "for emphasis, as in": "don ƙarfafawa, kamar a", "he became,": "ya zama,", "it was about to,": "ya kusa,", "even if,": "ko da,", "with two objects, and": "mai abubuwa biyu da aka yi wa aiki, da", "meaning some.": "mai ma'anar wani.", "adds a hamza at the start:": "yana ƙara hamza a farko:", "The present:": "Mudari'i:", "Its doer noun is": "Sunan mai aikatawa nasa shi ne", "a sender.": "mai aikawa.", "a Muslim. Its done-to noun is": "Musulmi. Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki nasa shi ne", "sent.": "wanda aka aika.", "closed.": "a rufe.", "strengthens a sentence:": "yana ƙarfafa jumla:", "became, is a sister of": "ya zama, kuma 'yar'uwa ce ta", "was about to, takes": "ya kusa, yana ɗaukar", "takes two objects:": "yana ɗaukar abubuwa biyu da aka yi wa aiki:", "means even if:": "yana nufin ko da:", "after an indefinite noun means some:": "bayan suna nakira yana nufin wani:", "for some reason.": "saboda wani dalili.", "أَرْسَلَ يُرْسِلُ (the pattern أَفْعَلَ)": "أَرْسَلَ يُرْسِلُ (wazanin أَفْعَلَ)", "This is the last lesson of Book 3. You will learn the pattern أَفْعَلَ, which adds a hamza at the start: أَرْسَلَ, he sent, يُرْسِلُ, إِرْسَالٌ, أَرْسِلْ, مُرْسِلٌ and مُرْسَلٌ. You will also learn لَـ for emphasis, as in لَهٰذَا مُسْتَحِيلٌ, أَصْبَحَ, he became, أَوْشَكَ, it was about to, وَلَوْ, even if, أَعْطَى with two objects, and مَا meaning some.": "Wannan shi ne darasi na ƙarshe na Littafi na 3. Za ka koyi wazanin أَفْعَلَ, wanda yake ƙara hamza a farko: أَرْسَلَ, ya aika, يُرْسِلُ, إِرْسَالٌ, أَرْسِلْ, مُرْسِلٌ da مُرْسَلٌ. Za ka kuma koyi لَـ don ƙarfafawa, kamar a لَهٰذَا مُسْتَحِيلٌ, أَصْبَحَ, ya zama, أَوْشَكَ, ya kusa, وَلَوْ, ko da, أَعْطَى mai abubuwa biyu da aka yi wa aiki, da مَا mai ma'anar wani.", "arsala": "arsala", "he sent": "ya aika", "yursilu": "yursilu", "he sends": "yana aikawa", "irsaalun": "irsaalun", "sending": "aikawa", "arsil": "arsil", "send!": "aika!", "adds a": "yana ƙara", "hamza": "hamza", "at the start of a three-letter verb:": "a farkon fi'ili mai harafi uku:", ". Present:": ". Mudari'i:", "). Verbal noun:": "). Masdari:", "). Command:": "). Umarni:", "). Hollow:": "). Ajwaf:", "send": "aika", "become Muslim": "musulunta", "close": "rufe", "put out": "kashe (wuta, fitila)", "mursilun": "mursilun", "a sender": "mai aikawa", "mursalun": "mursalun", "sent": "wanda aka aika", "Its doer noun:": "Sunan mai aikatawa nasa:", "). Its done-to noun:": "). Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki nasa:", "doer: مُفْعِلٌ": "mai aikatawa: مُفْعِلٌ", "done-to: مُفْعَلٌ": "wanda aka yi wa aiki: مُفْعَلٌ", "The name of the addressee is written on the right side of the envelope, and the sender's on the left.": "Ana rubuta sunan wanda aka aika wa a gefen dama na ambulan, na mai aikawa kuma a gefen hagu.", "If his office is closed, you will find him in the supervisor's office.": "Idan ofishinsa a rufe yake, za ka same shi a ofishin mai kulawa.", "Close the door, and don't close the windows.": "Rufe ƙofar, kuma kada ka rufe tagogin.", "Put out the lights before closing the room.": "Kashe fitilu kafin ka rufe ɗakin.", "la haadhaa mustaḥeelun": "la haadhaa mustaḥeelun", "This is truly impossible": "Lalle wannan ba mai yiwuwa ba ne", "aṣbaḥa ḥaamidun mareeḍan": "aṣbaḥa ḥaamidun mareeḍan", "Hamid became sick": "Hamid ya zama mara lafiya", "awshakad-darsu an yantahiya": "awshakad-darsu an yantahiya", "The lesson is about to end": "Darasin ya kusa ƙarewa", "with a fatha) strengthens a sentence:": "mai fataha) yana ƙarfafa jumla:", "(became, or was in the morning) is a sister of": "(ya zama, ko ya wayi gari) 'yar'uwar", "(was about to) is also a sister of": "(ya kusa) shi ma ɗan'uwan", "+ a verb:": "+ fi'ili:", "Is this possible, Ali? No, this is truly impossible.": "Wannan yana yiwuwa, Ali? A'a, lalle wannan ba mai yiwuwa ba ne.", "And the reward of the Hereafter is greater.": "Kuma ladan Lahira shi ne mafi girma.", "How are you this morning, brothers? We are well this morning, praise Allah.": "Yaya kuka wayi gari, 'yan'uwa? Mun wayi gari lafiya, alhamdu lillah.", "He brought your hearts together, and you became brothers by His favour.": "Ya haɗa zukatanku, sai kuka zama 'yan'uwa da ni'imarSa.", "Now you come, when the lesson is about to end?": "Yanzu kake zuwa, lokacin da darasin ya kusa ƙarewa?", "a'ṭaytu ḥaamidan kitaaban": "a'ṭaytu ḥaamidan kitaaban", "I gave Hamid a book": "Na ba Hamid littafi", "wa law kaana ghaaliyan": "wa law kaana ghaaliyan", "even if it is expensive": "ko da yana da tsada", "li amrin maa": "li amrin maa", "for some reason": "saboda wani dalili", "two objects": "abubuwa biyu da aka yi wa aiki", "= even if:": "yana nufin ko da:", "after an indefinite noun =": "bayan suna nakira yana nufin", "some": "wani", "between two names loses its alif:": "tsakanin sunaye biyu yana rasa alif ɗinsa:", "Give me the absence sheet, Ya'qub.": "Ba ni takardar fashi, Ya'qub.", "Where did you get this beautiful Qur'an? The principal gave it to me.": "A ina ka sami wannan kyakkyawan Alƙur'anin? Shugaban makaranta ne ya ba ni shi.", "And Allah will perfect His light, even if the disbelievers dislike it.": "Kuma Allah zai cika haskenSa, ko da kafirai sun ƙi.", "Give it to the supervisor, for he wants it now for some reason.": "Ka ba mai kulawa ita, domin yana son ta yanzu saboda wani dalili.", "My name is Muhammad ibn William, and I am from Canada.": "Sunana Muhammad ɗan William, kuma ni daga Kanada nake.", "he became Muslim": "ya musulunta", "he put out (a light)": "ya kashe (fitila)", "he closed": "ya rufe", "he informed": "ya ba da labari", "it pleased": "ya burge, ya ƙayatar", "he praised": "ya yaba", "impossible": "abin da ba zai yiwu ba", "unique": "na musamman, maras tamka", "a letter": "wasiƙa, jawabi", "new to (something)": "sabon shiga (wani abu)", "aslama (yuslimu)": "aslama (yuslimu)", "aṭfa'a (yuṭfi'u)": "aṭfa'a (yuṭfi'u)", "aghlaqa (yughliqu)": "aghlaqa (yughliqu)", "akhbara (yukhbiru)": "akhbara (yukhbiru)", "a'jaba (yu'jibu)": "a'jaba (yu'jibu)", "athnaa 'alaa": "athnaa 'alaa", "mustaḥeelun": "mustaḥeelun", "fareedun": "fareedun", "khiṭaabun": "khiṭaabun", "ḥadeethu 'ahdin": "ḥadeethu 'ahdin", "even if": "ko da", "he became, it became morning": "ya zama, ya wayi gari", "it was about to": "ya kusa", "How are you this morning, brothers? Well, praise Allah. And how are you this morning, teacher? Well; I praise and thank Him.": "Yaya kuka wayi gari, 'yan'uwa? Lafiya, alhamdu lillah. Kai kuma yaya ka wayi gari, malam? Lafiya; ina gode wa Allah ina yabonSa.", "Put out the lights, Idris; there is no need now. Give me the absence sheet, Ya'qub. Here it is. Uthman did not come today; he has bad diarrhoea.": "Kashe fitilun, Idris; babu buƙatarsu yanzu. Ba ni takardar fashi, Ya'qub. Ga ta nan. Usman bai zo yau ba; yana fama da gudawa mai tsanani.", "Give it to the supervisor; he wants it now for some reason. If his office is closed, you will find him in the cultural activities supervisor's office.": "Ka ba mai kulawa ita; yana son ta yanzu saboda wani dalili. Idan ofishinsa a rufe yake, za ka same shi a ofishin mai kula da ayyukan al'adu.", "May I come in, honourable shaikh? Welcome. Come in and close the door. You seem to be a new student. Your name? Muhammad ibn William, from Canada.": "Zan iya shigowa, mai girma shehi? Barka da zuwa. Shigo ka rufe ƙofar. Kamar kai sabon ɗalibi ne. Sunanka? Muhammad ɗan William, daga Kanada.", "Are you new to Islam? Yes. Praise Allah who guided us to Islam. When did you become Muslim, brother? In 1981.": "Kai sabon shiga Musulunci ne? Ee. Godiya ta tabbata ga Allah wanda Ya shiryar da mu zuwa Musulunci. Yaushe ka musulunta, ɗan'uwa? A 1981.", "Did your father become Muslim? Not yet; may Allah guide him. My mother did, praise Allah. Here is the principal's letter. The principal praises you a lot. How did you find the university? I liked it a lot. It is a unique university.": "Babanka ya musulunta? Tukuna; Allah Ya shiryar da shi. Mahaifiyata ta musulunta, alhamdu lillah. Ga wasiƙar shugaban makaranta. Shugaban makaranta yana yaba maka sosai. Yaya ka ga jami'ar? Ta burge ni sosai. Jami'a ce maras tamka.", "They want to put out Allah's light with their mouths, but Allah refuses except to perfect His light, even if the disbelievers dislike it. Is that possible, Ali? No, it is truly impossible.": "Suna so su kashe hasken Allah da bakunansu, amma Allah Ya ƙi sai Ya cika haskenSa, ko da kafirai sun ƙi. Hakan yana yiwuwa, Ali? A'a, lalle wannan ba mai yiwuwa ba ne.", "The command starts with": "Umarni yana farawa da", "(a hamza with fatha).": "(hamza mai fataha).", "(a hamza with": "(hamza mai", "أُرْسِلَ → done-to": "أُرْسِلَ → wanda aka yi wa aiki", "أُغْلِقَ → done-to": "أُغْلِقَ → wanda aka yi wa aiki", "أُكْرِهَ → done-to": "أُكْرِهَ → wanda aka yi wa aiki", "أَرْسَلَ → doer": "أَرْسَلَ → mai aikatawa", "Sisters of": "'Yan'uwan", ", and": ", da", "for emphasis.": "don ƙarfafawa.", "Two objects, even if, some": "Abubuwa biyu da aka yi wa aiki, ko da, wani", "“Buy this dictionary even if it is expensive.”": "“Ka sayi wannan ƙamus ɗin ko da yana da tsada.”", "“Give me some book.”": "“Ba ni wani littafi.”", "The lesson is about to end.": "Darasin ya kusa ƙarewa.", "The principal gave it to me.": "Shugaban makaranta ne ya ba ni shi.", "أَسْلَمَ → doer": "أَسْلَمَ → mai aikatawa", "Listen, then write the word. (a letter)": "Saurara, sannan ka rubuta kalmar. (wasiƙa)", "✅ The lesson is about to end.": "✅ Darasin ya kusa ƙarewa.", "✅ The principal gave it to me.": "✅ Shugaban makaranta ne ya ba ni shi.", "✅ Write: a letter": "✅ Rubuta: wasiƙa", "✅ “Give me some book.”": "✅ “Ba ni wani littafi.”", "This is the final exam of Beginner 4 and of the whole course. It has forty questions from all seventeen lessons of Book 3, and you have thirty minutes. You need eighty five percent to pass and earn your certificate.": "Wannan ita ce jarrabawar ƙarshe ta Mafari 4 da ta dukan kwas ɗin. Tana da tambayoyi arba'in daga dukan darussa goma sha bakwai na Littafi na 3, kuma kana da minti talatin. Kana buƙatar kashi tamanin da biyar cikin ɗari don ka ci, ka sami takardar shaidarka.", "Book 3": "Littafi na 3", "Verb patterns": "Wazanan fi'ili", "Plural of طَالِبٌ (pattern فَعَلَةٌ)": "Jam'in طَالِبٌ (wazanin فَعَلَةٌ)", "The passive": "Majhuli", "“It was said to me”": "“An ce mini”", "The passive of كَتَبَ": "Majhulin كَتَبَ", "Sukun and conditions": "Sukun da sharuɗɗa", "Signs and the while و": "Alamomi da و na yayin da", "“Allah created the heavens”": "“Allah Ya halicci sammai”", "Derived nouns": "Sunayen da aka samo daga fi'ili", "Tool noun of كَنَسَ": "Sunan kayan aiki na كَنَسَ", "The 9th Islamic month": "Wata na 9 na Musulunci", "Definite, dual, both": "Ma'arifa, tasniya, duka biyun", "“Where are my two pens?”": "“Ina alƙalumana biyu?”", "Doer noun of سَرَقَ": "Sunan mai aikatawa na سَرَقَ", "The verbal noun of سَلَّمَ": "Masdarin سَلَّمَ", "Tell a man: Close the door!": "Ka gaya wa namiji: Rufe ƙofar!", "“Let him come in”": "“Bari ya shigo”", "Done-to noun of كُتِبَ": "Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki na كُتِبَ", "“If you work hard, you will pass”": "“Idan ka yi ƙoƙari, za ka ci jarrabawa”", "“Hamid's two notebooks”": "“Littattafan rubutun Hamid biyu”", "“My father died when I was small”": "“Babana ya rasu lokacin ina ƙarami”", "Doer noun of حَجَّ": "Sunan mai aikatawa na حَجَّ", "Doer noun of قَالَ": "Sunan mai aikatawa na قَالَ", "Which word is مَبْنِيٌّ (fixed)?": "Wace kalma ce مَبْنِيٌّ (mara canjawa)?", "The present of سَلَّمَ": "Mudari'in سَلَّمَ", "Sentences and time words": "Jumloli da kalmomin lokaci", "Find the time word: خَرَجْتُ لَيْلًا": "Nemo kalmar lokaci: خَرَجْتُ لَيْلًا", "“No one is to go out”": "“Kada wani ya fita”", "“Read it and you will understand it”": "“Karanta shi za ka fahimce shi”", "The verbal noun of أَسْلَمَ": "Masdarin أَسْلَمَ", "“Sit wherever you like”": "“Zauna duk inda kake so”", "Tool noun of فَتَحَ": "Sunan kayan aiki na فَتَحَ", "سَأَلَنِي الْمُدَرِّسُ → passive": "سَأَلَنِي الْمُدَرِّسُ → majhuli", "How do you say “The judge asked the lawyer”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Alƙalin ya tambayi lauyan”?", "The verbal noun of هَنَّأَ": "Masdarin هَنَّأَ", "“The teachers of fiqh came”": "“Malaman fiƙihu sun zo”", "Which is مَعْرِفَةٌ (definite)?": "Wanne ne مَعْرِفَةٌ (ma'arifa)?", "“These books are not sold”": "“Ba a sayar da waɗannan littattafan”", "“The two doors are closed”": "“Ƙofofin biyu a rufe suke”", "Which sentence is nominal?": "Wace jumla ce ismiyya?", "“We have a car”": "“Muna da mota”", "✅ Plural of طَالِبٌ (pattern فَعَلَةٌ)": "✅ Jam'in طَالِبٌ (wazanin فَعَلَةٌ)", "✅ “It was said to me”": "✅ “An ce mini”", "✅ The passive of كَتَبَ": "✅ Majhulin كَتَبَ", "✅ “Allah created the heavens”": "✅ “Allah Ya halicci sammai”", "✅ Tool noun of كَنَسَ": "✅ Sunan kayan aiki na كَنَسَ", "✅ The 9th Islamic month": "✅ Wata na 9 na Musulunci", "✅ “Where are my two pens?”": "✅ “Ina alƙalumana biyu?”", "✅ Doer noun of سَرَقَ": "✅ Sunan mai aikatawa na سَرَقَ", "✅ The verbal noun of سَلَّمَ": "✅ Masdarin سَلَّمَ", "✅ Tell a man: Close the door!": "✅ Ka gaya wa namiji: Rufe ƙofar!", "✅ “Let him come in”": "✅ “Bari ya shigo”", "✅ Done-to noun of كُتِبَ": "✅ Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki na كُتِبَ", "✅ “If you work hard, you will pass”": "✅ “Idan ka yi ƙoƙari, za ka ci jarrabawa”", "✅ “Hamid's two notebooks”": "✅ “Littattafan rubutun Hamid biyu”", "✅ “My father died when I was small”": "✅ “Babana ya rasu lokacin ina ƙarami”", "✅ Doer noun of حَجَّ": "✅ Sunan mai aikatawa na حَجَّ", "✅ Doer noun of قَالَ": "✅ Sunan mai aikatawa na قَالَ", "✅ Which word is مَبْنِيٌّ (fixed)?": "✅ Wace kalma ce مَبْنِيٌّ (mara canjawa)?", "✅ The present of سَلَّمَ": "✅ Mudari'in سَلَّمَ", "✅ Find the time word: خَرَجْتُ لَيْلًا": "✅ Nemo kalmar lokaci: خَرَجْتُ لَيْلًا", "✅ “No one is to go out”": "✅ “Kada wani ya fita”", "✅ “Read it and you will understand it”": "✅ “Karanta shi za ka fahimce shi”", "✅ The verbal noun of أَسْلَمَ": "✅ Masdarin أَسْلَمَ", "✅ “Sit wherever you like”": "✅ “Zauna duk inda kake so”", "✅ Tool noun of فَتَحَ": "✅ Sunan kayan aiki na فَتَحَ", "✅ سَأَلَنِي الْمُدَرِّسُ → passive": "✅ سَأَلَنِي الْمُدَرِّسُ → majhuli", "✅ How do you say “The judge asked the lawyer”?": "✅ Yaya ake cewa “Alƙalin ya tambayi lauyan”?", "✅ The verbal noun of هَنَّأَ": "✅ Masdarin هَنَّأَ", "✅ “The teachers of fiqh came”": "✅ “Malaman fiƙihu sun zo”", "✅ Which is مَعْرِفَةٌ (definite)?": "✅ Wanne ne مَعْرِفَةٌ (ma'arifa)?", "✅ “These books are not sold”": "✅ “Ba a sayar da waɗannan littattafan”", "✅ “The two doors are closed”": "✅ “Ƙofofin biyu a rufe suke”", "✅ Which sentence is nominal?": "✅ Wace jumla ce ismiyya?", "✅ “We have a car”": "✅ “Muna da mota”", "Arabiyyah Kids": "Arabiyyah na Yara", "Kids": "Yara", "Assalamu alaikum!": "Assalamu alaikum!", "▶ Start": "▶ Fara", "Not {0}–{1}? Change age": "Ba {0} zuwa {1} ba? Canja shekaru", "I am Nuri. Tap start to begin the lesson.": "Ni ne Nuri. Taɓa “fara” don mu fara darasin.", "We use": "Muna amfani da", "to point at something near us, like a book in your hand. It is for boy words. You will meet the girl word later.": "don nuna abin da yake kusa da mu, kamar littafi a hannunka. Na kalmomin maza ne. Za ka haɗu da kalmar mata nan gaba.", "See the two small marks at the end of": "Ka ga ƙananan alamomi biyu a ƙarshen", "? They say un, and they mean a. So": "? Suna cewa un, kuma suna nufin “wani”. Don haka", "means this is a house. Arabic does not need a word for is.": "yana nufin wannan gida ne. Larabci ba ya buƙatar kalmar “ne”.", "To ask about a thing or an animal, start with": "Don tambaya game da abu ko dabba, fara da", "means what is this?": "yana nufin mene ne wannan?", "Tap each word to hear it.": "Taɓa kowace kalma don ka ji ta.", "Practice": "Gwadawa", "Tap each word to hear it, and say it after Nuri.": "Taɓa kowace kalma don ka ji ta, ka faɗe ta bayan Nuri.", "Quiz": "Ƙaramin gwaji", "Well done!": "Madalla!", "8 of 8 right": "8 daga cikin 8 daidai", "✓ Finish": "✓ Gama", "points at something far away, like a car across the street.": "yana nuna abin da yake nesa, kamar mota a ƙetaren titi.", "Easy way to remember:": "Hanya mai sauƙi don tunawa:", "is near, here with you.": "yana kusa, nan tare da kai.", "is far, over there.": "yana nesa, can.", "Same as before:": "Kamar dā:", "asks about things and animals, and": "yana tambaya game da abubuwa da dabbobi, kuma", "asks about people.": "yana tambaya game da mutane.", "👉 It is far from you. Choose the right sentence.": "👉 Yana nesa da kai. Zaɓi jumla daidai.", "👇 It is near you. Choose the right sentence.": "👇 Yana kusa da kai. Zaɓi jumla daidai.", "means the. When you add it, the un ending becomes just u.": "yana nufin “-n” (sananne). Idan ka ƙara shi, ƙarshen un yana zama u kawai.", "is a house, and": "gida ne, kuma", "is the house.": "shi ne gidan.", "A simple sentence: the thing with": "Jumla mai sauƙi: abin da yake da", ", then what it is like.": ", sannan yadda yake.", "means the pen is broken. No word for is!": "yana nufin alƙalamin ya karye. Babu kalmar “ne”!", "means and. It sticks to the next word, like": "yana nufin “da”. Yana manne wa kalmar da ke biye, kamar", ", and the teacher.": ", da malamin.", "then what it is like.": "sannan yadda yake.", "and the teacher.": "da malamin.", "“The water is cold.”": "“Ruwan yana da sanyi.”", ", in, and": ", a ciki, da", ", on, the last sound changes to i.": ", a kan, sautin ƙarshe yana canjawa zuwa i.", "to say where. Answer with": "don faɗin a ina. Amsa da", "on, the last sound changes to i.": "a kan, sautin ƙarshe yana canjawa zuwa i.", "is he, for a man or a boy word.": "shi ne “shi”, ga namiji ko kalmar maza.", "is she, for a woman or a girl word. Words ending in ة are usually girl words.": "shi ne “ita”, ga mace ko kalmar mata. Kalmomin da suke ƙarewa da ة yawanci kalmomin mata ne.", "is she, for a woman or a girl word. Words ending in": "shi ne “ita”, ga mace ko kalmar mata. Kalmomin da suke ƙarewa da", "are usually girl words.": "yawanci kalmomin mata ne.", "To say whose something is, put the thing first, then the owner.": "Don faɗin na wane ne wani abu, sa abin a farko, sannan mai shi.", "is Muhammad's book. Arabic says book Muhammad!": "littafin Muhammad ne. Larabci yana cewa littafi Muhammad!", "The first word loses": "Kalma ta farko tana rasa", "and un. The second word ends in i.": "da un. Kalma ta biyu tana ƙarewa da i.", "After a word like": "Bayan kalma kamar", ", the name": ", sunan", "is the House of Allah.": "shi ne Gidan Allah.", "How do you say “Muhammad's book”?": "Yaya ake cewa “littafin Muhammad”?", "is for boy words, and": "na kalmomin maza ne, kuma", "is for girl words.": "na kalmomin mata ne.", ", this is a watch.": ", wannan agogo ne.", "Most girl words end in ة. Add it to make a word for a girl:": "Yawancin kalmomin mata suna ƙarewa da ة. Ƙara ta don yin kalma ga mace:", "is a male student,": "ɗalibi namiji ne,", "is a female student.": "ɗaliba mace ce.", "this is a watch.": "wannan agogo ne.", "Some girl words have no ة, like": "Wasu kalmomin mata ba su da ة, kamar", ", mother, and body parts that come in twos, like": ", uwa, da sassan jiki da suke zuwa biyu-biyu, kamar", "Most girl words end in": "Yawancin kalmomin mata suna ƙarewa da", "Add it to make a word for a girl:": "Ƙara ta don yin kalma ga mace:", "Some girl words have no": "Wasu kalmomin mata ba su da", "mother, and body parts that come in twos, like": "uwa, da sassan jiki da suke zuwa biyu-biyu, kamar", "هُوَ مُسْلِمٌ.Now say the same about هِيَ:": "هُوَ مُسْلِمٌ.Yanzu faɗi haka game da هِيَ:", ".Now say the same about": ".Yanzu faɗi haka game da", "الْأَبُ جَالِسٌ.Now say the same about الْأُمُّ:": "الْأَبُ جَالِسٌ.Yanzu faɗi haka game da الْأُمُّ:", "حَامِدٌ طَبِيبٌ.Now say the same about فَاطِمَةُ:": "حَامِدٌ طَبِيبٌ.Yanzu faɗi haka game da فَاطِمَةُ:", "points at a girl word that is far away.": "yana nuna kalmar mata da take nesa.", ", that is a car.": ", wancan mota ce.", "Both mean that.": "Dukansu suna nufin wancan.", "for boy words,": "na kalmomin maza,", "for girl words.": "na kalmomin mata.", "that is a car.": "wancan mota ce.", "Four pointing words: near,": "Kalmomin nuni huɗu: na kusa,", ". Far,": ". Na nesa,", "Far,": "Na nesa,", "👇 It is near. Choose the right sentence.": "👇 Yana kusa. Zaɓi jumla daidai.", "👉 It is far. Choose the right sentence.": "👉 Yana nesa. Zaɓi jumla daidai.", "Watch": "Kalla", "is a full sentence: this is a man.": "cikakkiyar jumla ce: wannan mutum ne.", "is only this man, waiting for more.": "“wannan mutumin” ne kawai, yana jiran ƙari.", "It works the same with": "Haka yake aiki da", "means this car.": "yana nufin wannan motar.", "means for or belongs to. Before": "yana nufin “na” ko “mallakar”. Kafin", ", for the merchant.": ", na ɗan kasuwar.", "for the merchant.": "na ɗan kasuwar.", "A describing word comes after the noun and copies its ending.": "Kalmar siffantawa tana zuwa bayan suna kuma tana kwaikwayon ƙarshensa.", ", a rich merchant.": ", ɗan kasuwa mai arziki.", "If the noun is a girl word, the describing word gets ة too.": "Idan sunan kalmar mata ce, kalmar siffantawa ita ma tana samun ة.", ", an easy language.": ", harshe mai sauƙi.", ", the new teacher.": ", sabon malamin.", "If the noun is a girl word, the describing word gets": "Idan sunan kalmar mata ce, kalmar siffantawa tana samun", "an easy language.": "harshe mai sauƙi.", "the describing word gets": "kalmar siffantawa tana samun", "the new teacher.": "sabon malamin.", "Add a small ending to say my, your, his or her:": "Ƙara ɗan ƙarshe don faɗin nawa, naka, nasa ko nata:", ". Then no": ". Sai babu", "and no un.": "kuma babu un.", "means what is your name? Answer": "yana nufin mene ne sunanka? Amsa", ", my name is. Words with ة change it to ت:": ", sunana. Kalmomi masu ة suna mayar da ita ت:", "Then no": "Sai babu", ", father, and": ", uba, da", ", brother, get a long u before an ending:": ", ɗan'uwa, suna samun dogon u kafin ƙarshe:", ". But my is short:": ". Amma “nawa” gajere ne:", "my name is. Words with": "sunana. Kalmomi masu", "change it to": "suna mayar da ita", "father, and": "uba, da", "brother, get a long u before an ending:": "ɗan'uwa, suna samun dogon u kafin ƙarshe:", "How do you say “her bed”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gadonta”?", "“I don't have a car.”": "“Ba ni da mota.”", "How do you say “your car”?": "Yaya ake cewa “motarka”?", "How do you say “her hand”?": "Yaya ake cewa “hannunta”?", "How do you say “your hand”?": "Yaya ake cewa “hannunka”?", "How do you say “his bed”?": "Yaya ake cewa “gadonsa”?", "Listen to the story about the house. Tap any sentence to hear it again.": "Saurari labarin gidan. Taɓa kowace jumla don ka sake jin ta.", "Remember: ة turns into ت before an ending.": "Ka tuna: ة tana komawa ت kafin ƙarshe.", ", a room, becomes": ", ɗaki, yana zama", ", my room.": ", ɗakina.", "means in it, for boy words.": "yana nufin a cikinsa, ga kalmomin maza.", "means in it, for girl words.": "yana nufin a cikinta, ga kalmomin mata.", "turns into": "tana komawa", "before an ending.": "kafin ƙarshe.", "a room, becomes": "ɗaki, yana zama", "my room.": "ɗakina.", "“I love my classmate.”": "“Ina son abokin ajina.”", "“I love my teacher.”": "“Ina son malamina.”", "How do you say “my teacher (ustadh)”?": "Yaya ake cewa “malamina (ustaz)”?", "with an i sound at the end.": "tare da sautin i a ƙarshe.", "Talking to a boy or man:": "Idan kana magana da yaro ko namiji:", ". Talking to a girl or woman:": ". Idan kana magana da yarinya ko mace:", "Add at to say she did it.": "Ƙara at don faɗin cewa ita ce ta yi.", "is he went,": "shi ne ya tafi,", "is she went.": "shi ne ta tafi.", "Talking to a girl or woman:": "Idan kana magana da yarinya ko mace:", "ذَهَبَ الْمُدَرِّسُ إِلَى الْفَصْلِ.Now say it about a woman:": "ذَهَبَ الْمُدَرِّسُ إِلَى الْفَصْلِ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da mace:", ".Now say it about a woman:": ".Yanzu faɗe shi game da mace:", "ذَهَبَ ابْنُكِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Now say it about a woman:": "ذَهَبَ ابْنُكِ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da mace:", "خَرَجَ مُحَمَّدٌ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ.Now say it about a woman:": "خَرَجَ مُحَمَّدٌ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da mace:", "For many people use": "Ga mutane da yawa yi amfani da", ", these, and": ", waɗannan, da", ", they. Many plurals change inside the word:": ", su. Jam'i da yawa suna canjawa a cikin kalmar:", "There is no single rule for these plurals, so learn each one together with its word.": "Babu ƙa'ida ɗaya ga waɗannan jam'in, don haka koyi kowanne tare da kalmarsa.", "they. Many plurals change inside the word:": "su. Jam'i da yawa suna canjawa a cikin kalmar:", "Some words for men just add uuna at the end:": "Wasu kalmomin maza suna ƙara uuna ne kawai a ƙarshe:", "Point to them: they are 👇 near.": "Nuna su: suna 👇 kusa.", "is you all, talking to a group of boys or men.": "shi ne “ku”, idan kana magana da gungun yara maza ko maza.", "is we, for anyone.": "shi ne “mu”, ga kowa.", "for your, to a group, and": "ga “naku”, ga gungu, da", "for our.": "ga “namu”.", "is our house.": "gidanmu ne.", "means you all went.": "yana nufin kun tafi.", "means we went.": "yana nufin mun tafi.", "أَنْتَ خَرَجْتَ مِنَ الْفَصْلِ.Now say it about a group:": "أَنْتَ خَرَجْتَ مِنَ الْفَصْلِ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da gungu:", ".Now say it about a group:": ".Yanzu faɗe shi game da gungu:", "أَنَا ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى السُّوقِ.Now say it about a group:": "أَنَا ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى السُّوقِ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da gungu:", "How do you say “our sister”?": "Yaya ake cewa “'yar'uwarmu”?", "is you all, talking to a group of girls or women. Their ending is": "shi ne “ku”, idan kana magana da gungun 'yan mata ko mata. Ƙarshensu shi ne", ", you went, to a boy.": ", ka tafi, ga yaro.", ", to a girl.": ", ga yarinya.", ", I went. Listen to the last sound!": ", na tafi. Saurari sautin ƙarshe!", "for boys,": "ga yara maza,", "for girls, and": "ga 'yan mata, da", "for we.": "ga “mu”.", "you went, to a boy.": "ka tafi, ga yaro.", "to a girl.": "ga yarinya.", "I went. Listen to the last sound!": "na tafi. Saurari sautin ƙarshe!", "“I went after the prayer.”": "“Na tafi bayan sallah.”", "أَبَيْتُكُمْ قَرِيبٌ يَا إِخْوَانُ؟Now ask some sisters:": "أَبَيْتُكُمْ قَرِيبٌ يَا إِخْوَانُ؟Yanzu tambayi wasu 'yan'uwa mata:", "For many people, use": "Ga mutane da yawa, yi amfani da", ". For many things or animals, Arabic uses the girl word": ". Ga abubuwa ko dabbobi da yawa, Larabci yana amfani da kalmar mata", ", these are books.": ", waɗannan littattafai ne.", "Even for many pens or books, we say": "Ko ga alƙaluma ko littattafai da yawa, muna cewa", "For many things or animals, Arabic uses the girl word": "Ga abubuwa ko dabbobi da yawa, Larabci yana amfani da kalmar mata", "these are books.": "waɗannan littattafai ne.", ", those are houses. For people far away, use": ", waɗancan gidaje ne. Ga mutane da suke nesa, yi amfani da", "those are houses. For people far away, use": "waɗancan gidaje ne. Ga mutane da suke nesa, yi amfani da", "Many things take a girl describing word with": "Abubuwa da yawa suna ɗaukar kalmar siffantawa ta mata mai", ", the doors are open.": ", ƙofofin a buɗe suke.", "People get a plural describing word:": "Mutane suna samun kalmar siffantawa ta jam'i:", ". Things get the girl word:": ". Abubuwa suna samun kalmar mata:", ", many, follows the same rule:": ", da yawa, yana bin ƙa'ida ɗaya:", ", many languages.": ", harsuna da yawa.", "Things get the girl word:": "Abubuwa suna samun kalmar mata:", "هٰذَا الدَّرْسُ سَهْلٌ.Make it plural:": "هٰذَا الدَّرْسُ سَهْلٌ.Mayar da shi jam'i:", ".Make it plural:": ".Mayar da shi jam'i:", "هٰذَا قَلَمٌ جَدِيدٌ.Make it plural:": "هٰذَا قَلَمٌ جَدِيدٌ.Mayar da shi jam'i:", "Arabic has a special form for two! Add aani:": "Larabci yana da siffa ta musamman ga abu biyu! Ƙara aani:", ", two books.": ", littattafai biyu.", "for two boy things,": "ga abubuwa biyu na maza,", "for two girl things.": "ga abubuwa biyu na mata.", "two books.": "littattafai biyu.", ", how many, use one word ending in an:": ", nawa, yi amfani da kalma ɗaya mai ƙarewa da an:", "how many, use one word ending in an:": "nawa, yi amfani da kalma ɗaya mai ƙarewa da an:", "هٰذَا الطَّالِبُ مِنَ الْهِنْدِ.Now say it about two:": "هٰذَا الطَّالِبُ مِنَ الْهِنْدِ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da biyu:", ".Now say it about two:": ".Yanzu faɗe shi game da biyu:", "هٰذِهِ مِسْطَرَةٌ.Now say it about two:": "هٰذِهِ مِسْطَرَةٌ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da biyu:", "هٰذِهِ السَّيَّارَةُ لِلْمُدِيرِ.Now say it about two:": "هٰذِهِ السَّيَّارَةُ لِلْمُدِيرِ.Yanzu faɗe shi game da biyu:", "These are the numbers three to ten for boy words. Tap each one and say it.": "Waɗannan su ne lambobi uku zuwa goma ga kalmomin maza. Taɓa kowace ɗaya ka faɗe ta.", "The number comes first, then the plural word ending in in:": "Lambar tana zuwa a farko, sannan kalmar jam'i mai ƙarewa da in:", ", three students.": ", ɗalibai uku.", "Ask with": "Tambaya da", "and one word ending in an. Answer with the number and the plural.": "da kalma ɗaya mai ƙarewa da an. Amsa da lambar da jam'in.", "How do you say “10 passengers”?": "Yaya ake cewa “fasinjoji 10”?", "With girl words, the number has no ة:": "Tare da kalmomin mata, lambar ba ta da ة:", ", three female students.": ", ɗalibai mata uku.", "It is the opposite rule! Boy word, number with ة. Girl word, number without": "Ƙa'ida ce ta saɓani! Kalmar maza, lamba mai ة. Kalmar mata, lamba babu", "With girl words, the number has no": "Tare da kalmomin mata, lambar ba ta da", "Listen to two students talking about their class.": "Saurari ɗalibai biyu suna magana game da ajinsu.", "It is the opposite rule! Boy word, number with": "Ƙa'ida ce ta saɓani! Kalmar maza, lamba mai", "Girl word, number without": "Kalmar mata, lamba babu", "How do you say “3 students”?One of them: طَالِبٌ": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai 3”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu: طَالِبٌ", "How do you say “3 students”?One of them:": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai 3”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu:", "How do you say “7 days”?One of them: يَوْمٌ": "Yaya ake cewa “kwana 7”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu: يَوْمٌ", "How do you say “7 days”?One of them:": "Yaya ake cewa “kwana 7”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu:", "How do you say “7 daughters”?One of them: بِنْتٌ": "Yaya ake cewa “'ya'ya mata 7”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu: بِنْتٌ", "How do you say “7 daughters”?One of them:": "Yaya ake cewa “'ya'ya mata 7”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu:", "How do you say “8 female teachers”?One of them: مُدَرِّسَةٌ": "Yaya ake cewa “malamai mata 8”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu: مُدَرِّسَةٌ", "How do you say “8 female teachers”?One of them:": "Yaya ake cewa “malamai mata 8”?Ɗaya daga cikinsu:", "Listen to the story about the school. Tap any sentence to hear it again.": "Saurari labarin makarantar. Taɓa kowace jumla don ka sake jin ta.", "is just another way to say": "wata hanya ce kawai ta faɗin", ", that.": ", wancan.", "Colours for boy words follow one pattern:": "Launuka na kalmomin maza suna bin tsari ɗaya:", ", red.": ", ja.", ", green.": ", kore.", ", blue.": ", shuɗi.", "Colours never take un. They end in just one u:": "Launuka ba sa taɓa ɗaukar un. Suna ƙarewa da u ɗaya kawai:", ", a red pen.": ", jan alƙalami.", "red.": "ja.", "green.": "kore.", "blue.": "shuɗi.", "Some words never take un: girls' names like": "Wasu kalmomi ba sa taɓa ɗaukar un: sunayen 'yan mata kamar", ", names with ة like": ", sunaye masu ة kamar", ", and words ending in aanu like": ", da kalmomi masu ƙarewa da aanu kamar", "names with": "sunaye masu", "and words ending in aanu like": "da kalmomi masu ƙarewa da aanu kamar", "How do you write “keys”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “mabuɗai”?", "How do you write “Muhammad”?": "Yaya ake rubuta “Muhammad”?", "most words end in in:": "yawancin kalmomi suna ƙarewa da in:", ". Words that never take un end in a instead:": ". Kalmomin da ba sa taɓa ɗaukar un suna ƙarewa da a maimakon haka:", "The same happens to all the words that never take un:": "Haka yake faruwa ga dukan kalmomin da ba sa taɓa ɗaukar un:", "Words that never take un end in a instead:": "Kalmomin da ba sa taɓa ɗaukar un suna ƙarewa da a maimakon haka:", "means give me or bring. The teacher says it when he wants something.": "yana nufin ba ni ko kawo. Malam yana faɗinsa idan yana son wani abu.", "Final": "Na ƙarshe", "Which question fits? 👨‍⚕️": "Wace tambaya ce ta dace? 👨‍⚕️", "How do you say “I am from Japan.”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ni daga Japan nake.”?", "How do you say “the man”?": "Yaya ake cewa “mutumin”?", "12 of 12 right": "12 daga cikin 12 daidai", "makes a sentence stronger, like indeed. The word after it ends in a:": "yana ƙarfafa jumla, kamar “lalle”. Kalmar da take bayansa tana ƙarewa da a:", "can join a pronoun:": "yana iya haɗuwa da wakilin suna:", "he,": "shi,", "she,": "ita,", "you,": "kai,", "means perhaps or I hope. It works just like": "yana nufin watakila ko ina fata. Yana aiki daidai kamar", ", I hope you are well.": ", ina fatan kana lafiya.", "الدَّرْسُ صَعْبٌ.Add إِنَّ:": "الدَّرْسُ صَعْبٌ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", ".Add": ".Ƙara", "هُوَ تَاجِرٌ.Add إِنَّ:": "هُوَ تَاجِرٌ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", "آمِنَةُ طَالِبَةٌ.Add إِنَّ:": "آمِنَةُ طَالِبَةٌ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", "الْمُدِيرُ فِي الْفَصْلِ.Add إِنَّ:": "الْمُدِيرُ فِي الْفَصْلِ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", "“Are you married or single?”": "“Kai mai aure ne ko gwauro?”", "أَنَا طَالِبٌ.Add إِنَّ:": "أَنَا طَالِبٌ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", "الْقُرْآنُ كِتَابُ اللهِ.Add إِنَّ:": "الْقُرْآنُ كِتَابُ اللهِ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", "means is not. The next word often gets": "yana nufin “ba … ba”. Kalmar da take biye sau da yawa tana samun", "and ends in i:": "kuma tana ƙarewa da i:", "changes with the person:": "yana canjawa bisa ga mutum:", "For you and me:": "Ga kai da ni:", "آمِنَةُ طَبِيبَةٌ.Make it negative:": "آمِنَةُ طَبِيبَةٌ.Mayar da shi korewa:", ".Make it negative:": ".Mayar da shi korewa:", "أَنْتُمْ جُدُدٌ.Make it negative:": "أَنْتُمْ جُدُدٌ.Mayar da shi korewa:", "نَحْنُ طُلَّابٌ.Make it negative:": "نَحْنُ طُلَّابٌ.Mayar da shi korewa:", "فِي جَيْبِي مِائَةُ رِيَالٍ.Add إِنَّ:": "فِي جَيْبِي مِائَةُ رِيَالٍ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", "فِي الْهِنْدِ أَنْهَارٌ كَثِيرَةٌ.Add إِنَّ:": "فِي الْهِنْدِ أَنْهَارٌ كَثِيرَةٌ.Ƙara إِنَّ:", "From 11 to 19 the number is two words, and the noun after it is one, ending in an:": "Daga 11 zuwa 19 lambar kalmomi biyu ce, kuma sunan da yake bayanta ɗaya ne, mai ƙarewa da an:", "To say taller or bigger, use": "Don faɗin “ya fi tsawo” ko “ya fi girma”, yi amfani da", "before a noun to say the most:": "kafin suna don faɗin “mafi”:", ", the tallest student.": ", ɗalibi mafi tsawo.", "the tallest student.": "ɗalibi mafi tsawo.", "هِيَ طَبِيبَةٌ.Join or add كَأَنَّ:": "هِيَ طَبِيبَةٌ.Haɗa ko ƙara كَأَنَّ:", ".Join or add": ".Haɗa ko ƙara", "الطُّلَّابُ كَثِيرٌ. الْفَصْلُ صَغِيرٌ.Join or add كَأَنَّ:": "الطُّلَّابُ كَثِيرٌ. الْفَصْلُ صَغِيرٌ.Haɗa ko ƙara كَأَنَّ:", "{0}How do you say it?": "{0}Yaya ake faɗinsa?", "Muhammad is a good student.Say it is the best / most:": "Muhammad ɗalibi ne nagari.Ka ce shi ne mafi:", "١٤ طَالِبًاWhich is correct?": "١٤ طَالِبًاWanne ne daidai?", "قَرِيبٌMore / -er:": "قَرِيبٌYa fi:", "كَبِيرٌMore / -er:": "كَبِيرٌYa fi:", "The past verb changes its ending for each person:": "Fi'ilin shuɗaɗɗen lokaci yana canja ƙarshensa ga kowane mutum:", "they,": "su,", "they girls.": "su 'yan mata.", "to a boy,": "ga yaro,", "to a girl,": "ga yarinya,", "to boys,": "ga yara maza,", "to girls.": "ga 'yan mata.", "is I went,": "shi ne na tafi,", "is we went. Listen closely:": "shi ne mun tafi. Saurara da kyau:", "differ only in the last sound.": "sun bambanta a sautin ƙarshe kaɗai.", "هُوَ …… مِنَ السُّوقِ.Choose the verb:": "هُوَ …… مِنَ السُّوقِ.Zaɓi fi'ilin:", ".Choose the verb:": ".Zaɓi fi'ilin:", "هُمْ …… مِنَ السُّوقِ.Choose the verb:": "هُمْ …… مِنَ السُّوقِ.Zaɓi fi'ilin:", "نَحْنُ …… إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Choose the verb:": "نَحْنُ …… إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Zaɓi fi'ilin:", "أَنْتُمْ …… إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Choose the verb:": "أَنْتُمْ …… إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Zaɓi fi'ilin:", "أَنْتُمْ …… مِنَ السُّوقِ.Choose the verb:": "أَنْتُمْ …… مِنَ السُّوقِ.Zaɓi fi'ilin:", "أَنَا …… إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Choose the verb:": "أَنَا …… إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ.Zaɓi fi'ilin:", "(they)": "(su)", "A verb sentence: first the verb, then the doer ending in u, then the object ending in a.": "Jumla fi'iliyya: da farko fi'ili, sannan mai aikatawa mai ƙarewa da u, sannan wanda aka yi wa aiki mai ƙarewa da a.", "If the verb comes first, it stays singular even with many doers:": "Idan fi'ili ya zo a farko, yana zama na mutum ɗaya ko da masu aikatawa suna da yawa:", "The object can stick to the verb as an ending:": "Wanda aka yi wa aiki yana iya manne wa fi'ili a matsayin ƙarshe:", ", I opened it.": ", na buɗe shi.", "سَمِعَ بِلَالٌ الْأَذَانَ.Which word is the object?": "سَمِعَ بِلَالٌ الْأَذَانَ.Wace kalma ce wanda aka yi wa aiki?", ".Which word is the object?": ".Wace kalma ce wanda aka yi wa aiki?", "الطَّبِيبَاتُ ذَهَبْنَ إِلَى الْمُسْتَشْفَى.Put the verb first:": "الطَّبِيبَاتُ ذَهَبْنَ إِلَى الْمُسْتَشْفَى.Sa fi'ilin a farko:", ".Put the verb first:": ".Sa fi'ilin a farko:", "قَتَلَ الرَّجُلُ الْحَيَّةَ.Which word is the object?": "قَتَلَ الرَّجُلُ الْحَيَّةَ.Wace kalma ce wanda aka yi wa aiki?", "الطَّالِبَاتُ دَخَلْنَ الْفَصْلَ.Put the verb first:": "الطَّالِبَاتُ دَخَلْنَ الْفَصْلَ.Sa fi'ilin a farko:", "شَرِبَتِ الْبَقَرَةُ الْمَاءَ.Which word is the object?": "شَرِبَتِ الْبَقَرَةُ الْمَاءَ.Wace kalma ce wanda aka yi wa aiki?", "قَتَلَ الرَّجُلُ الْحَيَّةَ.Which word is the doer?": "قَتَلَ الرَّجُلُ الْحَيَّةَ.Wace kalma ce mai aikatawa?", ".Which word is the doer?": ".Wace kalma ce mai aikatawa?", "كَتَبَ الْمُدَرِّسُ الدَّرْسَ.Which word is the object?": "كَتَبَ الْمُدَرِّسُ الدَّرْسَ.Wace kalma ce wanda aka yi wa aiki?", "Stick him, her or them to the verb:": "Manna shi, ita ko su ga fi'ilin:", "I saw him,": "na gan shi,", "I saw her,": "na gan ta,", "means that. It joins two sentences:": "yana nufin “cewa”. Yana haɗa jumloli biyu:", ", I think that he is sick.": ", ina tsammani cewa ba shi da lafiya.", "With girl words, 11 to 19 change:": "Tare da kalmomin mata, 11 zuwa 19 suna canjawa:", ", thirteen female students.": ", ɗalibai mata goma sha uku.", "thirteen female students.": "ɗalibai mata goma sha uku.", "١٨ رَاكِبًاWhich is correct?": "١٨ رَاكِبًاWanne ne daidai?", "هُمْ طُلَّابٌ.Begin with أَظُنُّ:": "هُمْ طُلَّابٌ.Fara da أَظُنُّ:", ".Begin with": ".Fara da", "١٧ طَبِيبَةًWhich is correct?": "١٧ طَبِيبَةًWanne ne daidai?", "١٦ شَقَّةًWhich is correct?": "١٦ شَقَّةًWanne ne daidai?", "To a group of boys:": "Ga gungun yara maza:", ". To a group of girls:": ". Ga gungun 'yan mata:", ". They answer:": ". Su suna amsawa:", ", we went.": ", mun tafi.", "When it joins": "Idan ya haɗu da", ", a و comes in between:": ", و yana shiga tsakani:", ", you all saw him.": ", kun gan shi.", "To a group of girls:": "Ga gungun 'yan mata:", "They answer:": "Su suna amsawa:", "means was. For a girl,": "yana nufin “ya kasance”. Ga mace,", ", the teacher was in the class.": ", malamar ta kasance a aji.", "you all saw him.": "kun gan shi.", "the teacher was in the class.": "malamar ta kasance a aji.", "مِنْ أَيِّ إِذَاعَةٍ …… الْأَخْبَارَ يَا بَنَاتِي؟Fill the gap:": "مِنْ أَيِّ إِذَاعَةٍ …… الْأَخْبَارَ يَا بَنَاتِي؟Cike gurbin:", "أَفَهِمْتُمُ الدَّرْسَ الْجَدِيدَ يَا أَبْنَائِي؟Say it to women:": "أَفَهِمْتُمُ الدَّرْسَ الْجَدِيدَ يَا أَبْنَائِي؟Faɗe shi ga mata:", "الْأَطِبَّاءُ فِي الْمُسْتَشْفَى.Say it was, earlier:": "الْأَطِبَّاءُ فِي الْمُسْتَشْفَى.Ka ce “sun kasance”, a da:", ".Say it was, earlier:": ".Ka ce “sun kasance”, a da:", "Review of he and they:": "Bitar “shi” da “su”:", ". She and they girls:": ". “Ita” da “su 'yan mata”:", "Review of you:": "Bitar “kai”:", "for boys.": "ga yara maza.", "for girls. And I and we:": "ga 'yan mata. Da “ni” da “mu”:", "She and they girls:": "“Ita” da “su 'yan mata”:", "In these verbs the ending tells you who did it:": "A cikin waɗannan fi'iloli ƙarshen yana gaya maka wanda ya yi:", "is I,": "shi ne “ni”,", "is they,": "shi ne “su”,", "is we.": "shi ne “mu”.", "أَيْنَ آمِنَةُ؟ خَرَجَتْ.Where is the doer of the last verb?": "أَيْنَ آمِنَةُ؟ خَرَجَتْ.Ina mai aikatawa na fi'ilin ƙarshe?", ".Where is the doer of the last verb?": ".Ina mai aikatawa na fi'ilin ƙarshe?", "دَخَلُواWhich part is the doer?": "دَخَلُواWane sashe ne mai aikatawa?", "خَرَجْتُWhich part is the doer?": "خَرَجْتُWane sashe ne mai aikatawa?", "To say how amazing!, use": "Don faɗin “abin mamaki!”, yi amfani da", "! How easy this lesson is!": "! Wannan darasin ya yi sauƙi!", "When calling someone with": "Idan ana kiran wani da", ", a one-word name ends in u:": ", suna mai kalma ɗaya yana ƙarewa da u:", ". A two-word name ends in a:": ". Suna mai kalmomi biyu yana ƙarewa da a:", "Plurals ending in aat never end in a as an object. They take i:": "Jam'i masu ƙarewa da aat ba sa ƙarewa da a a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki. Suna ɗaukar i:", ", I saw cars.": ", na ga motoci.", "a one-word name ends in u:": "suna mai kalma ɗaya yana ƙarewa da u:", "A two-word name ends in a:": "Suna mai kalmomi biyu yana ƙarewa da a:", "هٰذَا الْقَلَمُ رَخِيصٌ.Say “how …!”:": "هٰذَا الْقَلَمُ رَخِيصٌ.Ka ce “abin mamaki …!”:", ".Say “how …!”:": ".Ka ce “abin mamaki …!”:", "عَبْدُ اللهِCall him or her:": "عَبْدُ اللهِKira shi ko ita:", "النُّجُومُ جَمِيلَةٌ.Say “how …!”:": "النُّجُومُ جَمِيلَةٌ.Ka ce “abin mamaki …!”:", "…… (the heavens)": "…… (sammai)", "شَيْخٌCall him or her:": "شَيْخٌKira shi ko ita:", "هٰذَا الْمَاءُ بَارِدٌ.Say “how …!”:": "هٰذَا الْمَاءُ بَارِدٌ.Ka ce “abin mamaki …!”:", "for he and ends in u:": "ga “shi” kuma yana ƙarewa da u:", ", he went, becomes": ", ya tafi, yana zama", ", he goes.": ", yana tafiya.", "The middle vowel can be u, i or a:": "Wasalin tsakiya yana iya zama u, i ko a:", ". Learn it with each verb.": ". Koyi shi tare da kowane fi'ili.", "before a present verb to say does not:": "kafin fi'ili mudari'i don faɗin “ba ya”:", ", he does not go.": ", ba ya tafiya.", "Learn it with each verb.": "Koyi shi tare da kowane fi'ili.", "he does not go.": "ba ya tafiya.", "رَجَعَPresent:": "رَجَعَMudari'i:", "ذَهَبَPresent:": "ذَهَبَMudari'i:", "رَكَعَPresent:": "رَكَعَMudari'i:", "سَمِعَPresent:": "سَمِعَMudari'i:", "يَدْرُسُونَ (they study)": "يَدْرُسُونَ (suna karatu)", "سَـ (will)": "سَـ (zai)", "The present verb:": "Fi'ili mudari'i:", "is used for you and for she:": "ana amfani da shi ga “kai” da kuma “ita”:", "For I:": "Ga “ni”:", "For we:": "Ga “mu”:", "on the front of the present verb for the future.": "a gaban fi'ili mudari'i don nan gaba.", "I will go.": "Zan tafi.", "The verbal noun names the action:": "Masdari yana sunanta aikin:", "entering.": "shiga.", "going out.": "fita.", "sitting.": "zama.", "means as for, and the next part starts with": "yana nufin “amma … kuwa”, kuma sashe na gaba yana farawa da", "Ibrahim studies at the College of Commerce.": "Ibrahim yana karatu a Tsangayar Kasuwanci.", "My brothers all study at the university.": "'Yan'uwana duka suna karatu a jami'a.", "Zainab studies in the first year.": "Zainab tana karatu a shekara ta farko.", "they (f) study": "su (mata) suna karatu", "Present verbs for others:": "Fi'iloli mudari'i ga sauran mutane:", "Where do you study, brother? I study at Riyadh University.": "A ina kake karatu, ɗan'uwa? Ina karatu a Jami'ar Riyadh.", "In which college do you study? I study in the College of Engineering.": "A wace tsangaya kake karatu? Ina karatu a Tsangayar Injiniyanci.", "As for me, I live with a relative of mine.": "Ni kuwa, ina zaune tare da wani ɗan'uwana.", "you (m) go": "kai (namiji) kana tafiya", "she goes": "tana tafiya", "is for you, and also for she.": "na “kai” ne, kuma na “ita”.", "is for I, and": "na “ni” ne, kuma", "is for we.": "na “mu” ne.", "The principal will come back tomorrow.": "Shugaban makaranta zai dawo gobe.", "I will go to Makkah in a week, in sha Allah.": "Zan tafi Makka nan da mako ɗaya, in sha Allah.", "I will get off at the next stop.": "Zan sauka a tasha mai zuwa.", "he comes back": "yana dawowa", "he will come back": "zai dawo", "at the front for the future:": "a gaba don nan gaba:", ", I will go.": ", zan tafi.", "he studied": "ya yi karatu", "he lived (in a place)": "ya zauna (a wani wuri)", "he knew": "ya sani", "he thanked": "ya gode", "he got off, came down": "ya sauka", "he climbed": "ya hau", "he died": "ya mutu", "a card": "kati", "a garment, a thobe": "tufa, riga", "a station, a stop": "tasha", "next, coming": "mai zuwa, na gaba", "a barber": "wanzami", "a pharmacy": "kantin magani", "رَجَعَVerbal noun:": "رَجَعَMasdari:", "الْمُدَرِّسَةُ تَدْخُلُ الْفَصْلَ.Make it plural:": "الْمُدَرِّسَةُ تَدْخُلُ الْفَصْلَ.Mayar da shi jam'i:", "will (future)": "zai (nan gaba)", "تَفْعَلِينَ (you do, f)": "تَفْعَلِينَ (kina yi, mace)", "days of the week": "kwanakin mako", "To a woman the present verb ends in -": "Ga mace fi'ili mudari'i yana ƙarewa da -", "To men:": "Ga maza:", "To women:": "Ga mata:", "The group answers with": "Gungun suna amsawa da", "at the start of a sentence, and after": "a farkon jumla, da bayan", "after other verbs, like": "bayan sauran fi'iloli, kamar", "The days of the week:": "Kwanakin mako:", "What are you doing, Umm Ahmad? I am looking for the medicine.": "Me kike yi, Ummu Ahmad? Ina neman maganin.", "When are you going to the hospital? I will go in an hour.": "Yaushe za ki tafi asibiti? Zan tafi nan da awa ɗaya.", "Do you know the doctor you went to yesterday?": "Kin san likitar da kika je wurinta jiya?", "you go (m)": "kana tafiya (namiji)", "you go (f)": "kina tafiya (mace)", "To a girl, the present verb ends in iina:": "Ga yarinya, fi'ili mudari'i yana ƙarewa da iina:", "What are you doing?": "Me kike yi?", "What are you doing, my sons? We are writing the homework.": "Me kuke yi, 'ya'yana? Muna rubuta aikin gida.", "Do you understand the lessons well? Yes, we understand them well.": "Kuna fahimtar darussan sosai? Ee, muna fahimtarsu sosai.", "And what are you doing, my daughters? We are playing now.": "Ku kuma me kuke yi, 'ya'yana mata? Muna wasa yanzu.", "you go (m pl)": "kuna tafiya (maza)", "you go (f pl)": "kuna tafiya (mata)", "To boys:": "Ga yara maza:", ". To girls:": ". Ga 'yan mata:", ". The group answers with": ". Gungun suna amsawa da", "They say she is the best doctor in the hospital.": "Sun ce ita ce mafi ƙwarewa a cikin likitocin asibitin.", "I heard that she is the best doctor in the hospital.": "Na ji cewa ita ce mafi ƙwarewa a cikin likitocin asibitin.", "I bear witness that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah.": "Na shaida cewa Muhammad Manzon Allah ne.", "at the start, after قَالَ": "a farko, bayan قَالَ", "after other verbs": "bayan sauran fi'iloli", "at the start or after": "a farko ko bayan", ", said. Use": ", ya ce. Yi amfani da", "after other verbs like": "bayan sauran fi'iloli kamar", ", I heard.": ", na ji.", "To girls:": "Ga 'yan mata:", "a medicine": "magani", "homework": "aikin gida", "a neighbour": "maƙwabci", "a pupil": "ɗalibi (ƙarami)", "a telephone": "tarho, waya", "a number": "lamba", "work": "aiki", "the foreign minister": "ministan harkokin waje", "he laughed": "ya yi dariya", "he bore witness": "ya shaida", "said. Use": "ya ce. Yi amfani da", "I heard.": "na ji.", "أَنَا أَفْهَمُ الدَّرْسَ جَيِّدًا.Make it “we”:": "أَنَا أَفْهَمُ الدَّرْسَ جَيِّدًا.Mayar da shi “mu”:", ".Make it “we”:": ".Mayar da shi “mu”:", "like this": "kamar haka", "“Monday”": "“Litinin”", "مَتَى تَذْهَبُ إِلَى الْمُسْتَشْفَى يَا أَبِي؟Say it to a woman:": "مَتَى تَذْهَبُ إِلَى الْمُسْتَشْفَى يَا أَبِي؟Faɗe shi ga mace:", "Say it to a woman:": "Faɗe shi ga mace:", "أَيْنَ تَسْكُنُونَ يَا رِجَالُ؟Say it to women:": "أَيْنَ تَسْكُنُونَ يَا رِجَالُ؟Faɗe shi ga mata:", "مَاذَا تَأْكُلُ يَا مُحَمَّدُ؟Say it to a woman:": "مَاذَا تَأْكُلُ يَا مُحَمَّدُ؟Faɗe shi ga mace:", "أَنَا أَشْكُرُكَ يَا أُسْتَاذُ.Make it “we”:": "أَنَا أَشْكُرُكَ يَا أُسْتَاذُ.Mayar da shi “mu”:", "the present verb table (review)": "teburin fi'ili mudari'i (bita)", "The person spoken to always starts with": "Wanda ake magana da shi kullum yana farawa da", "Every present verb starts with one of four letters:": "Kowane fi'ili mudari'i yana farawa da ɗaya daga cikin haruffa huɗu:", "for I,": "ga “ni”,", "for we,": "ga “mu”,", "for he and they, and": "ga “shi” da “su”, da", "for you and she.": "ga “kai” da “ita”.", "is the doer. In": "shi ne mai aikatawa. A cikin", "Hamid, Ali and Hashim go.": "Hamid, Ali da Hashim suna tafiya.", "Aminah goes.": "Aminah tana tafiya.", "Review:": "Bita:", "for girls.": "ga 'yan mata.", "You (m) go.": "Kai (namiji) kana tafiya.", "You all (m) go.": "Ku duka (maza) kuna tafiya.", "You (f) go.": "Ke (mace) kina tafiya.", "When you talk to someone, the verb always starts with": "Idan kana magana da wani, fi'ilin kullum yana farawa da", ". I is": ". “Ni” shi ne", ", and we is": ", kuma “mu” shi ne", "we go": "muna tafiya", "the four present letters": "haruffa huɗu na mudari'i", "I is": "“Ni” shi ne", "and we is": "kuma “mu” shi ne", "a taxi": "tasi", "a row, a class": "sahu, aji", "last": "na ƙarshe", "he drinks": "yana sha", "he eats": "yana ci", "يَذْهَبُWhere is the doer?": "يَذْهَبُIna mai aikatawa?", "Where is the doer?": "Ina mai aikatawa?", "the يَ": "يَ", "يَ = he": "يَ = shi", "تَ = she": "تَ = ita", "تَ = you": "تَ = kai", "يَ = they": "يَ = su", "تَ = you or she": "تَ = kai ko ita", "اُكْتُبْ (write!)": "اُكْتُبْ (rubuta!)", "the command": "umarni", "To make a command, drop the": "Don yin umarni, cire", "end in a sukun, and add an alif at the start. If the middle letter has": "ka ƙare da sukun, kuma ka ƙara alif a farko. Idan harafin tsakiya yana da", "start with": "ka fara da", "If the middle letter has": "Idan harafin tsakiya yana da", "Two short commands to learn by heart:": "Gajerun umarni biyu da za a haddace:", "eat.": "ci.", "take.": "karɓa.", "The command changes with the person. To a man,": "Umarni yana canjawa bisa ga mutum. Ga namiji,", "The alif at the start of a command is read only at the start of speech. After another word it is silent:": "Alif ɗin da ke farkon umarni ana karanta shi ne kawai a farkon magana. Bayan wata kalma ba a furta shi:", "Write your lesson, Ali.": "Rubuta darasinka, Ali.", "Come in, Hamid.": "Shigo, Hamid.", "Look at that mountain.": "Duba wancan dutsen.", "you write": "kana rubutu", "write!": "rubuta!", "To give a command, drop the": "Don ba da umarni, cire", ", end with a sukun and add an alif:": ", ka ƙare da sukun ka ƙara alif:", ", write!": ", rubuta!", "Sit here, Bilal.": "Zauna nan, Bilal.", "Wash your face with soap.": "Wanke fuskarka da sabulu.", "Open the windows, Abdullah.": "Buɗe tagogin, Abdullahi.", "sit!": "zauna!", "go!": "tafi!", "If the middle vowel is i or a, start with": "Idan wasalin tsakiya i ne ko a, fara da", ", sit!": ", zauna!", ", go!": ", tafi!", "end with a sukun and add an alif:": "ka ƙare da sukun ka ƙara alif:", "Eat, my son.": "Ci, ɗana.", "Take this notebook of yours and write Surat al-Alaq in it.": "Karɓi wannan littafin rubutunka ka rubuta Suratul Alaq a cikinsa.", "Take this bag and open it.": "Karɓi wannan jakar ka buɗe ta.", "eat!": "ci!", "take!": "karɓa!", "Two short ones to learn by heart:": "Gajeru biyu da za a haddace:", ", eat! and": ", ci! da", ", take!": ", karɓa!", "a scorpion": "kunama", "a shoe": "takalmi", "a radio": "rediyo", "a voice, a sound": "murya, sauti", "a razor": "reza", "Paradise, a garden": "Aljanna, lambu", "a husband, a wife": "miji, mata", "a stranger": "baƙo", "sleepy": "mai jin barci", "dark": "duhu", "eat! and": "ci! da", "he kept quiet": "ya yi shiru", "he cut": "ya yanke", "he shaved": "ya aske", "تَشْكُرُCommand:": "تَشْكُرُUmarni:", "كُلْWhat kind of verb?": "كُلْWane irin fi'ili?", "…… وُجُوهَكُنَّ بِالصَّابُونِ. (wash)": "…… وُجُوهَكُنَّ بِالصَّابُونِ. (wanke)", ". (wash)": ". (wanke)", "يَا أَوْلَادُ، …… الْخُبْزَ. (eat)": "يَا أَوْلَادُ، …… الْخُبْزَ. (ci)", ". (eat)": ". (ci)", "تَلْعَبُCommand:": "تَلْعَبُUmarni:", "يَا مُوسَى، …… مِنَ الْفَصْلِ. (go out)": "يَا مُوسَى، …… مِنَ الْفَصْلِ. (fita)", ". (go out)": ". (fita)", "he collected": "ya tara", "تَفْتَحُCommand:": "تَفْتَحُUmarni:", "تَغْسِلُCommand:": "تَغْسِلُUmarni:", "To say don't, put": "Don faɗin “kada”, sa", "before the you verb and end it with a sukun:": "kafin fi'ilin “kai” ka ƙare shi da sukun:", ", don't go out!": ", kada ka fita!", "with a sukun means don't eat!": "mai sukun yana nufin kada ka ci!", "with u means you don't eat.": "mai u yana nufin ba ka ci.", "Two hamzas together become one long آ:": "Hamza biyu tare suna zama آ dogo ɗaya:", ", I eat.": ", ina ci.", "(take)": "(karɓa)", ". (get off)": ". (sauka)", ". (laugh)": ". (yi dariya)", ". (worship)": ". (bauta)", ". (take)": ". (karɓa)", "تَسْمَعُSay “don't”:": "تَسْمَعُKa ce “kada”:", "تَنْزِلُSay “don't”:": "تَنْزِلُKa ce “kada”:", "Call Ali.": "Kira Ali.", "How do you say “Why don't you eat?”": "Yaya ake cewa “Me ya sa ba ka ci?”", "glad": "mai farin ciki", "How do you say “Hamid is not a student”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Hamid ba ɗalibi ba ne”?", "How do you say “The students went” (verb first)?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ɗaliban sun tafi” (fi'ili a farko)?", "How do you say “I hope you are well”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ina fatan kana lafiya”?", "How do you say “The bell is about to ring”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Ƙararrawa ta kusa bugawa”?", "How do you say “I will go”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Zan tafi”?", ", he wants, starts with u:": ", yana so, yana farawa da u:", "Girl colours change pattern:": "Launukan mata suna canja tsari:", ", a red bag.": ", jar jaka.", "he wants, starts with u:": "yana so, yana farawa da u:", "means another, and for girl words it is": "yana nufin “wani”, kuma ga kalmomin mata shi ne", ", another surah.": ", wata sura.", "a red bag.": "jar jaka.", "another surah.": "wata sura.", ", to, the verb ends in a:": ", don, fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da a:", ", I want to go.": ", ina so in tafi.", "means in order to, and the verb ends in a too:": "yana nufin “domin”, kuma fi'ilin shi ma yana ƙarewa da a:", "to, the verb ends in a:": "don, fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da a:", "I want to go.": "ina so in tafi.", "means you can:": "yana nufin “kana iya”:", ", you can sit here.": ", kana iya zama nan.", "لِمَ خَلَقَنَا اللهُ؟ (worship)": "لِمَ خَلَقَنَا اللهُ؟ (bauta)", "(worship)": "(bauta)", ", the long forms lose their ن:": ", dogayen siffofi suna rasa ن ɗinsu:", "The girls' forms ending in": "Siffofin 'yan mata masu ƙarewa da", "the long forms lose their": "dogayen siffofi suna rasa", "join into": "suna haɗuwa su zama", ", please do not come in.": ", don Allah kada ka shigo.", "please do not come in.": "don Allah kada ka shigo.", "أَنْتِ تَذْهَبِينَ.Add يُرِيدُ أَنْ:": "أَنْتِ تَذْهَبِينَ.Ƙara يُرِيدُ أَنْ:", "أَنْتُمْ تَذْهَبُونَ.Add يُرِيدُ أَنْ:": "أَنْتُمْ تَذْهَبُونَ.Ƙara يُرِيدُ أَنْ:", "means will not, and the verb ends in a:": "yana nufin “ba zai …ba”, kuma fi'ilin yana ƙarewa da a:", ", I will not go.": ", ba zan tafi ba.", ", the long forms lose their ن too:": ", dogayen siffofi su ma suna rasa ن ɗinsu:", "I will not go.": "ba zan tafi ba.", "for now,": "ga yanzu,", "too:": "su ma:", "نَرْجِعُAdd لَنْ:": "نَرْجِعُƘara لَنْ:", "تَخْرُجُAdd لَنْ:": "تَخْرُجُƘara لَنْ:", "يَشْرَبُونَAdd لَنْ:": "يَشْرَبُونَƘara لَنْ:", "تَأْكُلِينَAdd لَنْ:": "تَأْكُلِينَƘara لَنْ:", "تَكْتُبِينَAdd لَنْ:": "تَكْتُبِينَƘara لَنْ:", "Two of something ends in aani when it does the action, and ayni otherwise:": "Abu biyu yana ƙarewa da aani idan shi ne yake yin aikin, da ayni idan ba haka ba:", ", but": ", amma", ", use one word ending in an:": ", yi amfani da kalma ɗaya mai ƙarewa da an:", "One of them and the other:": "Ɗaya daga cikinsu da ɗayan:", "use one word ending in an:": "yi amfani da kalma ɗaya mai ƙarewa da an:", "…… (two letters)": "…… (wasiƙu biyu)", "رَأَيْتُ …… (two teachers)": "رَأَيْتُ …… (malamai biyu)", "…… (two teachers)": "…… (malamai biyu)", "…… (two riyals)": "…… (riyal biyu)", "ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى …… (two teachers)": "ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى …… (malamai biyu)", ". (two words)": ". (kalmomi biyu)", "…… (two notebooks)": "…… (littattafan rubutu biyu)", "means did not, with a present verb ending in sukun:": "yana nufin “bai … ba”, tare da fi'ili mudari'i mai ƙarewa da sukun:", ", he did not go.": ", bai tafi ba.", "the long forms lose their ن:": "dogayen siffofi suna rasa ن ɗinsu:", ", they did not go.": ", ba su tafi ba.", "means not yet:": "yana nufin “har yanzu ba”:", ", I have not written yet.": ", har yanzu ban rubuta ba.", "they did not go.": "ba su tafi ba.", "I have not written yet.": "har yanzu ban rubuta ba.", "تَذْهَبِينَAdd لَمْ:": "تَذْهَبِينَƘara لَمْ:", "تَذْهَبُAdd لَمْ:": "تَذْهَبُƘara لَمْ:", "يَفْهَمُAdd لَمْ:": "يَفْهَمُƘara لَمْ:", "The present verb has three endings: u normally, a after": "Fi'ili mudari'i yana da ƙarshe uku: u a al'ada, a bayan", ", and sukun after": ", da sukun bayan", "The long forms keep the ن normally, and drop it after": "Dogayen siffofi suna riƙe ن a al'ada, kuma suna sauke shi bayan", "and sukun after": "da sukun bayan", "The girls' forms with": "Siffofin 'yan mata masu", "never change at all.": "ba sa canjawa ko kaɗan.", "normally, and drop it after": "a al'ada, kuma suna sauke shi bayan", "The plural uuna becomes iina as an object or after a small word like": "Jam'i mai uuna yana zama iina a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki ko bayan ƙaramar kalma kamar", "The tens work the same way:": "Goma-goma suna aiki haka nan:", ", twenty, becomes": ", ashirin, yana zama", "as an object.": "a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki.", "In a number like 53, both parts change their ending:": "A lamba kamar 53, sassan biyu duka suna canja ƙarshensu:", "twenty, becomes": "ashirin, yana zama", "……؟ (the engineers)": "……؟ (injiniyoyin)", "…… (the teachers)": "…… (malaman)", "…… (hardworking)": "…… (masu ƙoƙari)", "One and two come after the noun and match it:": "Ɗaya da biyu suna zuwa bayan suna kuma suna dacewa da shi:", "Three to ten do the opposite:": "Uku zuwa goma suna yin akasi:", "From 11 to 99, the noun is one, ending in an:": "Daga 11 zuwa 99, sunan ɗaya ne, mai ƙarewa da an:", "How do you say “21 students (m)”?": "Yaya ake cewa “ɗalibai maza 21”?", "makes the second word end in a:": "yana sa kalma ta biyu ta ƙare da a:", ", Hamid was sick.": ", Hamid ya kasance mara lafiya.", "means still, and works like": "yana nufin “har yanzu”, kuma yana aiki kamar", ", he is still sick.": ", har yanzu bai da lafiya.", "changes:": "yana canjawa:", "when he does something,": "idan shi ne yake yin wani abu,", "as an object,": "a matsayin wanda aka yi wa aiki,", "after a small word.": "bayan ƙaramar kalma.", "he is still sick.": "har yanzu bai da lafiya.", "الْمَكْتَبَةُ مُغْلَقَةٌ.Say “still”:": "الْمَكْتَبَةُ مُغْلَقَةٌ.Ka ce “har yanzu”:", ".Say “still”:": ".Ka ce “har yanzu”:", "(your brother)": "(ɗan'uwanka)", "عُمَرُ رَجُلٌ غَنِيٌّ.Add كَانَ:": "عُمَرُ رَجُلٌ غَنِيٌّ.Ƙara كَانَ:", "الْجَوُّ حَارٌّ.Say “still”:": "الْجَوُّ حَارٌّ.Ka ce “har yanzu”:", "الْمَاءُ بَارِدٌ.Add كَانَ:": "الْمَاءُ بَارِدٌ.Ƙara كَانَ:", "…… (your father)": "…… (babanka)", "…… (your brother)": "…… (ɗan'uwanka)", "Verbs starting with و drop it in the present:": "Fi'iloli masu farawa da و suna sauke shi a mudari'i:", ", he found, becomes": ", ya samu, yana zama", ", he finds.": ", yana samu.", "Their commands are very short:": "Umarninsu gajeru ne sosai:", ", stop!": ", tsaya!", ", put!": ", ajiye!", "Verbs starting with": "Fi'iloli masu farawa da", "drop it in the present:": "suna sauke shi a mudari'i:", "he found, becomes": "ya samu, yana zama", "he finds.": "yana samu.", "To make something small, use the pattern": "Don ƙanƙantar da abu, yi amfani da wazanin", ", a little boy.": ", ƙaramin yaro.", "تَقِفِينَCommand:": "تَقِفِينَUmarni:", "وَضَعَPresent:": "وَضَعَMudari'i:", "وَجَدَPresent:": "وَجَدَMudari'i:", "وَجَبَPresent:": "وَجَبَMudari'i:", "قَلَمٌSmall form:": "قَلَمٌƘaramar siffa:", "حَبِيبٌMore / -er:": "حَبِيبٌYa fi:", "جَبَلٌSmall form:": "جَبَلٌƘaramar siffa:", "Some verbs have a long vowel in the middle:": "Wasu fi'iloli suna da dogon wasali a tsakiya:", "With endings like": "Tare da ƙarshe kamar", "the long vowel gets short:": "dogon wasalin yana zama gajere:", ", I said.": ", na ce.", ", I sold.": ", na sayar.", ", I slept.": ", na yi barci.", "With a sukun at the end, it gets short too:": "Idan akwai sukun a ƙarshe, shi ma yana zama gajere:", "I said.": "na ce.", "I sold.": "na sayar.", "I slept.": "na yi barci.", "زَارَPresent:": "زَارَMudari'i:", "command: تَصُومُ": "umarni: تَصُومُ", "command:": "umarni:", "خَافَPresent:": "خَافَMudari'i:", "بَاعَPresent:": "بَاعَMudari'i:", "قَالَPresent:": "قَالَMudari'i:", "كَانَPresent:": "كَانَMudari'i:", "Some verbs end in a long vowel:": "Wasu fi'iloli suna ƙarewa da dogon wasali:", "the ending turns into": "ƙarshen yana komawa", ", I walked.": ", na yi tafiya.", ", I invited.": ", na gayyata.", ", in a command, or with": ", a umarni, ko tare da", "I walked.": "na yi tafiya.", "I invited.": "na gayyata.", "in a command, or with": "a umarni, ko tare da", "بَقِيَPresent:": "بَقِيَMudari'i:", "بَنَىPresent:": "بَنَىMudari'i:", "رَمَىPresent:": "رَمَىMudari'i:", "جَرَىPresent:": "جَرَىMudari'i:", "Some verbs have a double letter with a shadda:": "Wasu fi'iloli suna da harafi biyu mai shadda:", "the two letters split:": "haruffan biyu suna rabuwa:", "and in commands, they stay joined and end in a:": "da kuma a umarni, suna zama a haɗe kuma suna ƙarewa da a:", ", pull!": ", ja!", "means never for the past.": "yana nufin “ban taɓa ba” ga abin da ya wuce.", "means never for the future.": "yana nufin “har abada” ga nan gaba.", "حَجَّPresent:": "حَجَّMudari'i:", "مَرَّPresent:": "مَرَّMudari'i:", "ظَنَّPresent:": "ظَنَّMudari'i:", "جَرَّPresent:": "جَرَّMudari'i:", "For two people:": "Ga mutum biyu:", ", you two, and": ", ku biyu, da", ", they two.": ", su biyu.", "Past verbs for two:": "Fi'iloli na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci ga mutum biyu:", "for two boys,": "ga yara maza biyu,", "for two girls,": "ga 'yan mata biyu,", "they two.": "su biyu.", "Present for two:": "Mudari'i ga mutum biyu:", ". Command:": ". Umarni:", ", go, you two!": ", ku tafi, ku biyu!", "Five present forms end in aani, uuna or iina. They keep the ن normally and drop it after": "Siffofin mudari'i guda biyar suna ƙarewa da aani, uuna ko iina. Suna riƙe ن a al'ada kuma suna sauke shi bayan", "A describing word copies its noun in four ways: the ending, boy or girl, how many, and": "Kalmar siffantawa tana kwaikwayon sunanta ta hanyoyi huɗu: ƙarshe, namiji ko mace, adadi, da kuma", "Five present forms end in aani, uuna or iina. They keep the": "Siffofin mudari'i guda biyar suna ƙarewa da aani, uuna ko iina. Suna riƙe", "حَفِظْتُ سُورَتَيْنِ طَوِيلَتَيْنِ.Which is النَّعْتُ?": "حَفِظْتُ سُورَتَيْنِ طَوِيلَتَيْنِ.Wace ce النَّعْتُ?", ".Which is": ".Wace ce", "لَا تَكْتُبَا بِالْقَلَمِ الْأَحْمَرِ.Which is النَّعْتُ?": "لَا تَكْتُبَا بِالْقَلَمِ الْأَحْمَرِ.Wace ce النَّعْتُ?", "أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَشْرَبَ مَاءً بَارِدًا.Which is النَّعْتُ?": "أُرِيدُ أَنْ أَشْرَبَ مَاءً بَارِدًا.Wace ce النَّعْتُ?", "أَسْكُنُ فِي بَيْتٍ جَمِيلٍ.Which is النَّعْتُ?": "أَسْكُنُ فِي بَيْتٍ جَمِيلٍ.Wace ce النَّعْتُ?", "أَيْنَ الْمُدَرِّسُونَ الْجُدُدُ؟Which is النَّعْتُ?": "أَيْنَ الْمُدَرِّسُونَ الْجُدُدُ؟Wace ce النَّعْتُ?", "Which is": "Wace ce", "هُمْ رِجَالٌ صَالِحُونَ.Which is النَّعْتُ?": "هُمْ رِجَالٌ صَالِحُونَ.Wace ce النَّعْتُ?", "How do you say “They (f) will not go”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Su (mata) ba za su tafi ba”?", "How do you say “another surah”?": "Yaya ake cewa “wata sura”?", "Ask a woman: What do you want?": "Tambayi mace: Me kike so?", "Tell a man: Stop!": "Ka gaya wa namiji: Tsaya!", "How do you say “I invited”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na gayyata”?", "Tell a man: Don't be afraid.": "Ka gaya wa namiji: Kada ka ji tsoro.", "Some words change their ending, like": "Wasu kalmomi suna canja ƙarshensu, kamar", ". Others never change, like": ". Wasu kuma ba sa canjawa har abada, kamar", "The main endings for nouns are u, a and i. For present verbs they are u, a and sukun.": "Manyan ƙarshe na sunaye su ne u, a da i. Ga fi'iloli mudari'i su ne u, a da sukun.", "Others never change, like": "Wasu kuma ba sa canjawa har abada, kamar", "Some words use other signs: plurals with aat, names like": "Wasu kalmomi suna amfani da wasu alamomi: jam'i masu aat, sunaye kamar", ", and the plurals and twos you learned.": ", da jam'i da tasniya da ka koya.", "and the plurals and twos you learned.": "da jam'i da tasniya da ka koya.", "(the sukun sign)": "(alamar sukun)", "اِذْهَبْ إِلَى فِرْعَوْنَ (the -i sign)": "اِذْهَبْ إِلَى فِرْعَوْنَ (alamar -i)", "(the -i sign)": "(alamar -i)", "can mean while, telling how someone was:": "yana iya nufin “yayin da”, yana nuna halin da wani yake ciki:", ", I saw him while he was going in.": ", na gan shi yayin da yake shiga.", "has three jobs: and, while, and by in an oath like": "yana da ayyuka uku: “da”, “yayin da”, da rantsuwa kamar", "I saw him while he was going in.": "na gan shi yayin da yake shiga.", "can show hope for something good, or worry about something bad.": "yana iya nuna fatan abu mai kyau, ko tsoron abu mara kyau.", "When we don't say who did it, we use the passive:": "Idan ba mu faɗi wanda ya yi ba, muna amfani da majhuli:", ", the spy was killed. The object now ends in u.": ", an kashe ɗan leƙen asirin. Wanda aka yi wa aiki yanzu yana ƙarewa da u.", "Past passive: u on the first letter, i before the last:": "Majhuli na shuɗaɗɗen lokaci: u a kan harafin farko, i a gaban na ƙarshe:", ". Present passive: u first, a before the last:": ". Majhuli na mudari'i: u a farko, a a gaban na ƙarshe:", "the spy was killed. The object now ends in u.": "an kashe ɗan leƙen asirin. Wanda aka yi wa aiki yanzu yana ƙarewa da u.", "Use it every day:": "Yi amfani da shi kowace rana:", ", the restaurant opens.": ", ana buɗe gidan abincin.", ", I was asked.": ", an tambaye ni.", "Present passive: u first, a before the last:": "Majhuli na mudari'i: u a farko, a a gaban na ƙarshe:", "the restaurant opens.": "ana buɗe gidan abincin.", "سَأَلَنِي الْمُدَرِّسُ.Make it passive:": "سَأَلَنِي الْمُدَرِّسُ.Mayar da shi majhuli:", ".Make it passive:": ".Mayar da shi majhuli:", "the 7th month": "wata na 7", "يَشْرَحُ الْمُدَرِّسُ الدَّرْسَ مَرَّتَيْنِ.Make it passive:": "يَشْرَحُ الْمُدَرِّسُ الدَّرْسَ مَرَّتَيْنِ.Mayar da shi majhuli:", "سَرَقَ اللِّصُّ السَّاعَةَ.Make it passive:": "سَرَقَ اللِّصُّ السَّاعَةَ.Mayar da shi majhuli:", "حَفِظَPassive:": "حَفِظَMajhuli:", "the 8th month": "wata na 8", "The doer noun is on the pattern": "Sunan mai aikatawa yana kan wazanin", ", he stole, gives": ", ya yi sata, yana bayar da", ", a thief.": ", ɓarawo.", "The done-to noun is on the pattern": "Sunan wanda aka yi wa aiki yana kan wazanin", ", stolen.": ", abin da aka sata.", ", written.": ", abin da aka rubuta.", "he stole, gives": "ya yi sata, yana bayar da", ", I am not unaware.": ", ni ba gafali ba ne.", "كُسِرَDone-to noun:": "كُسِرَSunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", ". (not)": ". (ba)", "غُسِلَDone-to noun:": "غُسِلَSunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "فُتِحَDone-to noun:": "فُتِحَSunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "جَلَسَDoer noun:": "جَلَسَSunan mai aikatawa:", "Verbs with a long middle vowel make doer nouns with a hamza:": "Fi'iloli masu dogon wasali a tsakiya suna yin sunan mai aikatawa da hamza:", "Their passive:": "Majhulinsu:", ", it was said.": ", an ce.", ", it is sold.": ", ana sayar da shi.", "Verbs ending in a vowel:": "Fi'iloli masu ƙarewa da wasali:", ", one who calls, and": ", mai kira, da", ", invited.": ", wanda aka gayyata.", "it was said.": "an ce.", "one who calls, and": "mai kira, da", "بَنَىDoer noun:": "بَنَىSunan mai aikatawa:", "عُدَّDone-to noun:": "عُدَّSunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "…… (a server)": "…… (mai shayarwa)", "قَامَDoer noun:": "قَامَSunan mai aikatawa:", "دَعَاDoer noun:": "دَعَاSunan mai aikatawa:", "بِيعَDone-to noun:": "بِيعَSunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "نُسِيَDone-to noun:": "نُسِيَSunan wanda aka yi wa aiki:", "Nouns for a place or a time start with": "Sunayen wuri ko lokaci suna farawa da", ", an appointment.": ", lokacin alƙawari.", "If the present verb has a or u in the middle, use": "Idan fi'ili mudari'i yana da a ko u a tsakiya, yi amfani da", ", a playground.": ", filin wasa.", "an appointment.": "lokacin alƙawari.", "If it has i in the middle, or starts with و, use": "Idan yana da i a tsakiya, ko yana farawa da و, yi amfani da", "a playground.": "filin wasa.", "If it has i in the middle, or starts with": "Idan yana da i a tsakiya, ko yana farawa da", "وَقَفَ يَقِفُPlace / time noun:": "وَقَفَ يَقِفُSunan wuri / lokaci:", "وَعَدَ يَعِدُPlace / time noun:": "وَعَدَ يَعِدُSunan wuri / lokaci:", "سَعَى يَسْعَىPlace / time noun:": "سَعَى يَسْعَىSunan wuri / lokaci:", "لَعِبَ يَلْعَبُPlace / time noun:": "لَعِبَ يَلْعَبُSunan wuri / lokaci:", "طَبَخَ يَطْبُخُPlace / time noun:": "طَبَخَ يَطْبُخُSunan wuri / lokaci:", "جَلَسَ يَجْلِسُPlace / time noun:": "جَلَسَ يَجْلِسُSunan wuri / lokaci:", "دَخَلَ يَدْخُلُPlace / time noun:": "دَخَلَ يَدْخُلُSunan wuri / lokaci:", "Tool nouns name the thing we use:": "Sunayen kayan aiki suna sunanta abin da muke amfani da shi:", ", he opened, gives": ", ya buɗe, yana bayar da", ", a key.": ", mabuɗi.", "Three patterns:": "Wazanai uku:", ", a broom.": ", tsintsiya.", "he opened, gives": "ya buɗe, yana bayar da", "means woe to. Allah warns those who cheat when they weigh.": "yana nufin “bone ya tabbata ga”. Allah Yana gargaɗin masu cuta lokacin da suke aunawa.", "قَلَىTool noun:": "قَلَىSunan kayan aiki:", "كَنَسَTool noun:": "كَنَسَSunan kayan aiki:", "وَزَنَTool noun:": "وَزَنَSunan kayan aiki:", "غَرَفَTool noun:": "غَرَفَSunan kayan aiki:", "كَوَىTool noun:": "كَوَىSunan kayan aiki:", "A noun is known,": "Suna yana iya zama sananne,", ", or not known,": ", ko ba sananne ba,", ", a man.": ", wani mutum.", "Known words include pronouns like": "Kalmomi sanannu sun haɗa da wakilan suna kamar", ", names like": ", sunayen yanka kamar", ", pointing words like": ", kalmomin nuni kamar", ", and joining words like": ", da kalmomin haɗi kamar", "or not known,": "ko ba sananne ba,", "a man.": "wani mutum.", "Also known: words with": "Sanannu kuma: kalmomi masu", ", words joined to a known word like": ", kalmomin da aka rataya ga kalma sananniya kamar", ", and someone you call with": ", da wanda ka kira da", "names like": "sunayen yanka kamar", "pointing words like": "kalmomin nuni kamar", "and joining words like": "da kalmomin haɗi kamar", "words joined to a known word like": "kalmomin da aka rataya ga kalma sananniya kamar", "and someone you call with": "da wanda ka kira da", "(make it definite by joining)": "(mayar da shi ma'arifa ta hanyar ratayawa)", "(make it definite by calling)": "(mayar da shi ma'arifa ta hanyar kira)", "When two of something or a uuna plural is joined to another word, the ن drops:": "Idan aka rataya abu biyu ko jam'i mai uuna ga wata kalma, ن yana faɗuwa:", ", Hamid's two pens.": ", alƙaluman Hamid biyu.", "With my, two becomes": "Tare da “nawa”, biyu yana zama", "When two of something or a uuna plural is joined to another word, the": "Idan aka rataya abu biyu ko jam'i mai uuna ga wata kalma,", "Hamid's two pens.": "alƙaluman Hamid biyu.", "mean both:": "suna nufin duka biyun:", ", both of them are sick.": ", su duka biyun ba su da lafiya.", "both of them are sick.": "su duka biyun ba su da lafiya.", "……؟ (my two pens)": "……؟ (alƙalumana biyu)", "(of the school)": "(na makarantar)", "(my two eyes)": "(idanuna biyu)", ". (Hamid's)": ". (na Hamid)", ". (both m)": ". (duka biyun, maza)", "A noun sentence starts with a noun, with": "Jumla ismiyya tana farawa da suna, da", "A verb sentence starts with a verb. Some verbs need only a doer, like": "Jumla fi'iliyya tana farawa da fi'ili. Wasu fi'iloli suna buƙatar mai aikatawa kaɗai, kamar", ". Verbs like": ". Fi'iloli kamar", "need more.": "suna buƙatar ƙari.", "with a verb can be swapped for a verbal noun:": "tare da fi'ili ana iya musanya shi da masdari:", ", your going.": ", tafiyarka.", "Verbs like": "Fi'iloli kamar", "your going.": "tafiyarka.", "The subject is what we talk about, and the predicate tells us about it:": "Mubtada'i shi ne abin da muke magana a kansa, khabari kuma yana gaya mana game da shi:", "The subject can be not known if a place word comes first:": "Mubtada'i yana iya zama ba sananne ba idan kalmar wuri ta zo a farko:", ", we have a car.": ", muna da mota.", "A word can be left out when it is clear:": "Ana iya barin kalma idan ta bayyana:", "we have a car.": "muna da mota.", "عِنْدَنَا)Make a sentence:": "عِنْدَنَا)Yi jumla:", ")Make a sentence:": ")Yi jumla:", "مَا)Make a sentence:": "مَا)Yi jumla:", "A word ending in a can tell when or where:": "Kalma mai ƙarewa da a tana iya nuna yaushe ko a ina:", ", I arrived on Tuesday.": ", na iso ranar Talata.", "Some time and place words never change:": "Wasu kalmomin lokaci da wuri ba sa canjawa har abada:", "I arrived on Tuesday.": "na iso ranar Talata.", "Other words can stand in for time or place:": "Wasu kalmomi suna iya tsayawa a madadin lokaci ko wuri:", ", we travelled all day.": ", mun yi tafiya yini guda.", "we travelled all day.": "mun yi tafiya yini guda.", "before a present verb with a sukun makes a command for someone else:": "kafin fi'ili mudari'i mai sukun yana yin umarni ga wani:", ", let him come in.": ", bari ya shigo.", "that forbids works for others too:": "ta hani tana aiki ga wasu ma:", ", no one is to go out.": ", kada wani ya fita.", "Four little words give one verb a sukun:": "Ƙananan kalmomi huɗu suna ba fi'ili ɗaya sukun:", "for commands.": "don umarni.", "no one is to go out.": "kada wani ya fita.", "نَجْلِسُMake it “let …”:": "نَجْلِسُMayar da shi “bari …”:", "ظَهْرِيCry out in pain:": "ظَهْرِيYi kururuwar zafi:", "يَذْهَبُونَMake it “let …”:": "يَذْهَبُونَMayar da shi “bari …”:", "يَنْسَىMake it “let …”:": "يَنْسَىMayar da shi “bari …”:", "قَلْبِيCry out in pain:": "قَلْبِيYi kururuwar zafi:", "means when or if:": "yana nufin idan ko lokacin da:", "The answer starts with": "Amsa tana farawa da", "when it is a command, a don't, a question, or a noun sentence:": "idan umarni ce, hani, tambaya, ko jumla ismiyya:", "To say of or from, add": "Don faɗin “na” ko “daga”, ƙara", "and drop the ة:": "ka cire ة:", "and drop the": "ka cire", "means if, and gives both verbs a sukun:": "yana nufin idan, kuma yana ba fi'iloli biyu sukun:", ", if you work hard, you will pass.": ", idan ka yi ƙoƙari, za ka ci jarrabawa.", "Other if-words work the same:": "Sauran kalmomin “idan” suna aiki haka:", "whoever,": "duk wanda,", "whatever,": "duk abin da,", "whenever,": "duk lokacin da,", "if you work hard, you will pass.": "idan ka yi ƙoƙari, za ka ci jarrabawa.", "Most verbs have three root letters, like": "Yawancin fi'iloli suna da haruffan asali uku, kamar", ". Some have four, like": ". Wasu suna da huɗu, kamar", ". Some get extra letters, like": ". Wasu suna samun ƙarin haruffa, kamar", "Simple three-letter verbs follow six patterns, like": "Fi'iloli masu harafi uku tsirara suna bin wazanai shida, kamar", "Some have four, like": "Wasu suna da huɗu, kamar", "Some get extra letters, like": "Wasu suna samun ƙarin haruffa, kamar", "The pattern with a doubled middle letter:": "Wazanin da ake ninka harafin tsakiya:", "سَجَّلَPresent:": "سَجَّلَMudari'i:", "سَلَّمَVerbal noun:": "سَلَّمَMasdari:", "صُورَةٌPlural:": "صُورَةٌJam'i:", "سَبَّحَPresent:": "سَبَّحَMudari'i:", "دَخَّنَVerbal noun:": "دَخَّنَMasdari:", "وَزَّعَVerbal noun:": "وَزَّعَMasdari:", "سَلَّمَPresent:": "سَلَّمَMudari'i:", "→ doer": "→ mai aikatawa", ", he sent.": ", ya aika.", "Its doer is": "Mai aikatawarsa shi ne", ", the sender, and its done-to word is": ", mai aikawa, kalmar wanda aka yi wa aiki kuma ita ce", ", sent.": ", wanda aka aika.", "he sent.": "ya aika.", "makes a sentence strong:": "yana ƙarfafa jumla:", "means became, and works like": "yana nufin “ya zama”, kuma yana aiki kamar", "the sender, and its done-to word is": "mai aikawa, kalmar wanda aka yi wa aiki kuma ita ce", "تُخْبِرُCommand:": "تُخْبِرُUmarni:", "آمَنَVerbal noun:": "آمَنَMasdari:", "“I gave Hamid a book.”": "“Na ba Hamid littafi.”", "→ done-to": "→ wanda aka yi wa aiki", "أَجَابَVerbal noun:": "أَجَابَMasdari:", "أَقَامَVerbal noun:": "أَقَامَMasdari:", "أَسْلَمَPresent:": "أَسْلَمَMudari'i:", "تُطْفِئُCommand:": "تُطْفِئُUmarni:", "Tool noun of": "Sunan kayan aiki na", "Place noun of لَعِبَ يَلْعَبُ": "Sunan wuri na لَعِبَ يَلْعَبُ", "Place noun of": "Sunan wuri na", "The passive of يَفْتَحُ": "Majhulin يَفْتَحُ", "The passive of": "Majhulin", "The present of أَرْسَلَ": "Mudari'in أَرْسَلَ", "“I saw both men”": "“Na ga mutanen biyu duka”", "“Both of them are sick” (m)": "“Su duka biyun ba su da lafiya” (maza)", "(definite)?": "(ma'arifa)?", "I'm Nuri. Let's learn Arabic words!": "Ni ne Nuri. Mu koyi kalmomin Larabci!", "I am Nuri. Tap the big button to start!": "Ni ne Nuri. Taɓa babban maɓalli don mu fara!", "Listen and say": "Saurara ka faɗa", "🔊 Again": "🔊 Kuma", "Tap like this! Where is": "Taɓa kamar haka! Ina", "Tap the picture": "Taɓa hoton", "Where is": "Ina", "Listen. Which one did Nuri say?": "Saurara. Wanne ne Nuri ya faɗa?", "Masha'Allah! You did it!": "Masha'Allah! Ka iya!", "↻ Play again": "↻ Sake wasa", "You did it! Well done.": "Ka iya! Madalla.", "Tap the meaning": "Taɓa ma'anar", "How do you say “Hamzah's book”?": "Yaya ake cewa “littafin Hamza”?", "Ask some women: Where is your mother?": "Tambayi wasu mata: Ina mahaifiyarku?", "My sisters study at the middle school.": "'Yan'uwana mata suna karatu a makarantar sakandare ƙarama.", "he worshipped": "ya bauta", "Go out and play.": "Fita ka yi wasa.", "How do you say “they (men) study”?": "Yaya ake cewa “suna karatu (maza)”?", "How do you say “she studies”?": "Yaya ake cewa “tana karatu”?", "How do you say “Zainab is younger than her”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Zainab ta fi ta ƙuruciya”?", "The command of تَجْلِسُ": "Umarnin تَجْلِسُ", "The command of": "Umarnin", "How do you say “I went out to drink water”?": "Yaya ake cewa “Na fita don in sha ruwa”?", "Doer noun of": "Sunan mai aikatawa na", "an appointment": "lokacin alƙawari", "“When he comes, tell him”": "“Idan ya zo, ka gaya masa”", "Which is نَكِرَةٌ (indefinite)?": "Wanne ne نَكِرَةٌ (nakira)?", "(indefinite)?": "(nakira)?", "👨‍👩‍👧 For parents: sit with your child for the first lessons and tap together.": "👨‍👩‍👧 Ga iyaye: ku zauna tare da ɗanku a darussan farko ku taɓa tare.", "This one is for bigger children": "Wannan na manyan yara ne", "This lesson is for ages 6 and up. You can go on to the next lesson.": "Wannan darasin na yara masu shekara 6 zuwa sama ne. Kana iya wucewa zuwa darasi na gaba.", "✓ Go on": "✓ Ci gaba", "Change age": "Canja shekaru", "This lesson is for bigger children. Well done, you can go on!": "Wannan darasin na manyan yara ne. Madalla, kana iya ci gaba!", "Continue where you stopped": "Ci gaba daga inda ka tsaya", "Start again": "Sake farawa", "My voice": "Muryata", "We heard:": "Mun ji:", "Not quite. Listen again and repeat.": "Ba daidai ba sosai. Sake saurara ka maimaita.", "We couldn't check automatically. Compare your voice with the teacher's:": "Ba mu iya dubawa kai tsaye ba. Kwatanta muryarka da ta malam:", "Not yet. Review and try again": "Tukuna. Yi bita ka sake gwadawa", "Back to lessons": "Koma ga darussa", "Review the lesson": "Bitar darasin", ".steps button": ".steps button", "taa marbuutah": "taa marbuutah", "Take your time and read each question carefully. بِسْمِ اللهِ. Good luck.": "Ka ɗauki lokacinka ka karanta kowace tambaya da kyau. بِسْمِ اللهِ. Allah Ya ba da sa'a.", "We follow the famous book, Lessons in Arabic Language, by Dr. V. عَبْدِ الرَّحِيمْ, taught at the Islamic University of Madinah.": "Muna bin shahararren littafin nan, Darussan Harshen Larabci, na Dr. V. عَبْدِ الرَّحِيمْ, wanda ake koyarwa a Jami'ar Musulunci ta Madina.", "the first half of Book 2, lessons 1 to 15": "rabin farko na Littafi na 2, darussa 1 zuwa 15", "the second half of Book 2, lessons 16 to 31": "rabi na biyu na Littafi na 2, darussa 16 zuwa 31", "Listen carefully and repeat everything aloud. بِسْمِ اللهِ. Let's begin.": "Saurara da kyau ka maimaita komai da ƙarfi. بِسْمِ اللهِ. Mu fara.", "Book 1": "Littafi na 1", "Book 2, lessons 1 to 15": "Littafi na 2, darussa 1 zuwa 15", "Book 2, lessons 16 to 31": "Littafi na 2, darussa 16 zuwa 31", "wordStrip pop": "wordStrip pop", "Start the lesson": "Fara darasi", "maa · man": "maa · man", "what · who": "mene ne · wane ne", "along the way": "a kan hanya", "Lesson": "Darasi", "· XP added to your account": "· an ƙara XP a asusunka", "Write:": "Rubuta:", "Hello! How old are you? Tap your age.": "Sannu! Shekarunka nawa? Taɓa shekarunka.", "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. I am Nuri. Tap start to begin the lesson.": "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Ni ne Nuri. Taɓa “fara” don mu fara darasin.", "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. I am Nuri. Tap the big button to start!": "السَّلَامُ عَلَيْكُمْ. Ni ne Nuri. Taɓa babban maɓalli don mu fara!", "Let's try again": "Mu sake gwadawa", "· you need 70%": "· kana buƙatar 70%", "Good try! Let's try again.": "Ka yi ƙoƙari! Mu sake gwadawa.", "مَا شَاءَ اللهُ. You did it! Well done.": "مَا شَاءَ اللهُ. Ka iya! Madalla.", "English text": "Rubutun Turanci", "3. Read & repeat": "3. Karanta ka maimaita", "Fatha · Part 2 · رَ – عَ": "Fataha · Kashi na 2 · رَ – عَ", "are you there?": "kana nan?"};
